window.CURRICULUM = {"meta":{"version":1},"intro":{"title":"Ledger to Leadership: The Open Accounting Path","tagline":"From zero to professionally competent in accounting — free, self-paced, and built on real work, not just lectures.","philosophy":"This curriculum exists on one conviction: a motivated person with an internet connection should be able to learn accounting to a genuinely professional standard without paying tuition or asking permission. Accounting is the language of business — the system for measuring, recording, and communicating economic reality — and that language belongs to everyone, not just those who can afford a degree program.\n\nWe borrow our model from the Open Source Society University and The Odin Project: a complete, opinionated, sequenced path assembled from the best free and open resources on the web, glued together with our own roadmap, projects, and checkpoints. We do not reinvent the textbooks; we curate the strongest free ones (OpenStax, university OpenCourseWare, regulator and standard-setter publications, open problem sets) and give you the missing piece those scattered resources never provide on their own: order, context, and a reason to keep going.\n\nFour principles define the path. FREE: every required resource is free to access, forever; paid materials are optional enrichment, never gatekeepers. COMPLETE: we take you from 'what is a debit?' to confidently preparing and analyzing a full set of financial statements, costing a product, building a budget, and reading a tax return — the working competence of an entry-to-intermediate professional. SELF-DIRECTED: there is no cohort, no start date, no instructor chasing you; you own the pace and the discipline. PROJECT-DRIVEN: you do not 'finish' a module by watching videos — you finish it by closing a set of books, building a model, or producing a deliverable a real employer would recognize. You learn accounting the way you learn to swim: in the water, doing reps, making and fixing mistakes.","howToUse":["Start at the beginning and go in order. The path is sequenced for a reason — fundamentals (the accounting equation, debits/credits, the cycle) are load-bearing for everything above them. Resist the urge to jump to 'the interesting parts.'","For each unit, read or watch the linked core resource FIRST, then immediately do the practice problems before moving on. Passive intake without reps does not stick in accounting — the only proof you understand a concept is that you can post the entry correctly.","Treat every project as mandatory, not optional. The projects (a manual bookkeeping cycle, a month-end close, a three-statement model, a costing exercise, a budget, a ratio analysis of a real public company) are where competence is actually forged. Build a portfolio of them.","Keep a running 'journal' — literally a notebook or repo — where you redo entries from scratch, write your own explanations of confusing topics, and log errors you made and why. Teaching it back to yourself is the highest-yield study activity.","Use spaced repetition for the memorization-heavy pieces (the chart of accounts logic, the normal balances, the standard mnemonics, key ratios) so they become automatic and free up your attention for judgment.","Hit the checkpoint self-assessment at the end of each phase before advancing. If you cannot pass it cold, loop back — do not paper over a weak foundation.","CHOOSE YOUR JURISDICTION TRACK after completing the standards-agnostic core. Read the jurisdictionNote, pick US, International, or your regional track, and only then layer the framework-specific and exam-specific material on top.","Build in public and find at least one other learner. Accountability is a feature of this curriculum, not an afterthought — see the accountability tactics below.","Revisit and refactor old projects as you learn more. Going back to your first set of books with six months of knowledge is one of the most powerful 'aha' experiences available, and it shows how far you've come."],"principles":["Understand before you memorize. Rules without the 'why' collapse the first time a transaction doesn't fit the template; always trace an entry back to the accounting equation.","Debits equal credits, and the books must balance — embrace this constraint as a built-in error detector, not a chore.","Do the reps by hand before you automate. Learn the manual cycle and manual statements before touching spreadsheets or software, so the tool never becomes a black box you can't audit.","Substance over form, and judgment over rote. Real accounting is full of estimates and choices; train yourself to reason about the economics, not just match a pattern.","Tie every number to a source document and a clear trail. 'Where did this figure come from and could I defend it?' is the professional's reflex.","Ship deliverables, not just answers. A finished, presentable artifact beats a hundred half-done exercises.","Errors are the curriculum. Finding why your trial balance is off by $90 (hello, transposition error) teaches more than getting it right the first time.","Consistency beats intensity. Ninety focused minutes most days will carry you further than heroic weekend cramming.","Connect the numbers to decisions. Always ask what a statement, ratio, or variance would tell a manager, investor, or lender — accounting that doesn't inform a decision is just arithmetic."],"accountability":["Form or join a study group of 2-6 learners on the same track; meet weekly to compare project outputs, walk through tricky entries on a shared screen, and quiz each other on checkpoints.","Build in public: post your projects, journal entries, models, and write-ups to a public repo, blog, or social thread. Knowing your work is visible raises the quality bar and creates a portfolio that doubles as proof of competence to employers.","Use spaced-repetition flashcards (e.g. Anki) for normal balances, account classifications, ratio formulas, and standard mnemonics — review daily, let the algorithm schedule the rest.","Set a public, dated commitment ('I'll finish the month-end-close project by the 15th') and report the outcome to your group or feed — accountability with a deadline and an audience.","Pair up with an accountability partner for weekly check-ins: a five-minute 'what I did, what I'm stuck on, what's next' exchange keeps momentum when motivation dips.","Teach what you learn. Write an explainer, record a short walkthrough, or answer beginners' questions in a forum; teaching exposes the gaps you didn't know you had.","Track your progress visibly — a checklist, a streak, a kanban board of units done and projects shipped — so 'I'm making progress' is a fact you can see, not a feeling you have to summon.","Schedule periodic 'redo from scratch' sessions where you reproduce an earlier project cold; it converts recognition into true recall and surfaces decay before it compounds."],"whoIsThisFor":"This path is for the self-starter who wants real, working accounting competence and is willing to do the reps to get it: career-changers moving into bookkeeping, finance, or analyst roles; founders and small-business owners who want to actually understand (and not just outsource) their own books; students who want a free, structured supplement to a paid program; aspiring CPA/ACCA/CMA candidates who need to build the underlying knowledge before sitting any exam; software engineers and data people building fintech, ERP, or accounting products who need genuine domain fluency; and the simply curious who want to read a financial statement with confidence. The common denominator is self-discipline — you must be able to drive your own learning without a teacher behind you.","whatYouWontGet":"This is NOT a substitute for a professional licensing exam or its official preparation. Completing this path does not make you a CPA, CA, ACCA, CMA, or any other designated/chartered professional, and it does not replace the official syllabus, exam-prep providers, supervised experience hours, or the exams themselves required for those credentials — it prepares you for that journey, it does not shortcut it. It also carries NO accreditation and grants NO transferable academic credit, degree, or certificate recognized by a university or licensing body; there is no diploma at the end, only demonstrable skill and a portfolio. Nothing here is accounting, tax, audit, or legal advice for your specific situation, and free curated resources can go out of date — always confirm current rules against the authoritative standard-setter or regulator before relying on them for real-world decisions.","timeCommitment":"Plan for roughly 700-1,000 hours of focused effort to go from zero to professionally competent across the core plus one jurisdiction track — comparable in scope to a serious multi-course university sequence, minus the lectures you sit through passively. Full-time pace (about 35-40 focused hours/week, like a job or bootcamp): roughly 5-7 months. Committed part-time pace (10-15 hours/week, evenings and weekends): roughly 12-18 months. Light part-time pace (5-7 hours/week around a full-time job or studies): roughly 2-3 years. These are honest ranges, not promises — projects always take longer than reading, prior exposure to business or math accelerates things, and the jurisdiction-specific and exam-prep layers add time on top. Consistency is the real variable: a sustainable daily habit will beat any heroic schedule you can't maintain.","jurisdictionNote":"Accounting has a universal core and a jurisdiction-specific shell, and this curriculum is deliberately structured to separate the two. The CORE is STANDARDS-AGNOSTIC: the accounting equation, double-entry, debits and credits, the accounting cycle, accruals and the matching concept, the structure and logic of the financial statements, working-capital and inventory mechanics, the fundamentals of cost and managerial accounting, and basic financial-statement analysis are essentially the same everywhere. Master that core first — it transfers across every country and every framework.\n\nOnly AFTER the core do you choose a jurisdiction/certification track, because recognition rules, presentation, terminology, and the professional credential differ by region:\n\n- US TRACK (GAAP / CPA): US Generally Accepted Accounting Principles as set by the FASB, US tax fundamentals, and the path toward the CPA (with its state-by-state education and experience requirements). Note US-specific terminology and statement formats.\n\n- INTERNATIONAL TRACK (IFRS / ACCA): International Financial Reporting Standards as issued by the IASB — used across the EU, UK, and much of Asia, Africa, the Middle East, and Latin America — with the ACCA as a globally portable qualification (the UK ICAEW/ACA and similar chartered routes also live here).\n\n- OTHER REGIONAL TRACKS: pick the credential and local standards that match where you intend to practice — e.g., Canada (IFRS/ASPE, CPA Canada), Australia/NZ (IFRS, CA ANZ / CPA Australia), India (Ind AS, CA — ICAI), and other national bodies. Where local GAAP coexists with IFRS, learn the local standards your employer or regulator actually requires.\n\nPractical guidance: complete the core regardless of where you live; then commit to the single track that matches your goals and geography, and only layer exam-specific prep on top of that. If you are unsure, IFRS is the most internationally portable starting point, while US GAAP is essential if you intend to work in or with the United States."},"trackOrder":["Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","Track 1 — Core Accounting","Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","Track 6 — Capstone & Certification"],"tracks":[{"name":"Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","modules":[{"id":"0.1","title":"How to Learn Accounting & the Map of the Profession","track":"Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","summary":"This orientation module gives you the big picture before you touch a single journal entry: how the accounting field is organized into branches (bookkeeping, financial, managerial, tax, audit, accounting information systems, and advisory), who the regulators and standard-setters are, and how the rest of this curriculum maps onto a real credential. You will also build the personal learning machinery — spaced-repetition decks for vocabulary, a problem-first practice loop, an error log, and a public progress log — that makes the later technical modules stick. Finally you learn to find and vet free primary sources so you can tell an authoritative regulator publication from a random blog. It is light on calculation and heavy on orientation, navigation, and habit design.","whyItMatters":"Knowing the map of the profession turns a long, intimidating syllabus into a route with a destination (a role and a credential), and the study system you build here is what determines whether the next 30 modules actually compound instead of evaporate.","outcomes":["Draw the map of accounting — bookkeeping, financial, managerial, tax, audit, AIS, and advisory — explain how the users and purpose of each branch differ, and locate where automation/AI is reshaping each","Name the major regulators and standard-setters (FASB/SEC, IASB/IFRS Foundation, IRS, PCAOB/IAASB, AICPA, IMA) and state what each one governs and for whom","Stand up a personal study system: a spaced-repetition deck for terminology, a problem-first practice routine, an error log, and a public progress log","Choose a target role and credential (CPA, ACCA, CMA, or professional bookkeeping) and back-map this curriculum's modules onto that exam's sections","Evaluate the credibility of a free resource by distinguishing primary sources (regulator and standard-setter sites, open textbooks) from secondary commentary"],"estimatedHours":"8-12","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting — Chapter 1, 'Role of Accounting in Society'","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Your anchor read. Open Chapter 1 ('Role of Accounting in Society') from the table of contents and work all of it: the distinction between financial vs. managerial accounting, the users of accounting information, the major accounting branches, and professional ethics/regulators. Do the end-of-chapter questions as your first practice set. Bookmark the whole book — later modules return to it."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting — Unit 1 (Accounting Environment, Decision-Making, and Theory)","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=1261","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"A free, structured, certificate-bearing course with an optional AI tutor. For this module only do Unit 1 to reinforce the map and vocabulary; the rest of the course feeds later financial-accounting modules. Useful as a second pass over the same orientation concepts in a different voice."},{"title":"Accounting Basics playlist","provider":"Accounting Stuff (James, YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/c/AccountingStuff","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Watch the early 'What is Accounting?' and 'Types of Accounting' videos for fast, friendly intuition. Search the channel for 'Accounting Basics' to find the ordered playlist (e.g. youtube.com/playlist?list=PL5zKSeS09l339nB6ujJPQ9Rsv99_b-aTb). Use it to demystify jargon before reading, not as a substitute for the textbook."},{"title":"Accounting Explanations, Quizzes & Flashcards","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Free tier includes topic explanations, a dictionary/glossary, quick quizzes, and flashcards. Use the glossary + flashcards to seed your spaced-repetition deck, and the free quizzes as low-stakes terminology practice. (PRO is paid and not required for this module.)"},{"title":"Start Here, Go Places / This Way to CPA","provider":"AICPA","url":"https://www.thiswaytocpa.com/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Use to understand the CPA path and the structure of the CPA Exam (core + discipline sections). For non-CPA tracks, compare with the IMA CMA page (imanet.org) and ACCA qualification page (accaglobal.com). Pick ONE target credential and back-map this curriculum's modules to its exam sections."},{"title":"Who We Are / Why Global Accounting Standards","provider":"IFRS Foundation (IASB)","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/about-us/who-we-are/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Primary-source practice: read how the IFRS Foundation and IASB are structured and what they govern, then contrast with the US side at fasb.org (FASB), sec.gov (SEC), pcaobus.org (PCAOB), and irs.gov (IRS/tax). This is your exercise in telling a standard-setter from a regulator."},{"title":"Khan Academy — Accounting and financial statements (intro)","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance/accounting-and-financial-stateme","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Optional intuition booster from Sal Khan on what financial statements are and why accounting exists. The URL slug is genuinely truncated by Khan Academy — it is the correct, live page. Skim now for the big picture; you'll lean on it more in the financial-accounting modules."}],"project":"Build a one-page 'Map of Accounting + My Study System' dossier and publish it. Part A: a diagram (hand-drawn or digital) of the seven branches — bookkeeping, financial, managerial, tax, audit, AIS, advisory — with one sentence each on who uses it, its purpose, and where AI/automation is changing it. Part B: a regulator table mapping FASB, SEC, IASB/IFRS, IRS, PCAOB/IAASB, AICPA, and IMA to what each governs. Part C: pick a target credential (CPA, ACCA, CMA, or bookkeeping), and back-map at least the first five modules of this curriculum to that exam's sections. Part D: stand up the actual tooling — create a spaced-repetition deck (Anki or similar) seeded with 30+ terms from OpenStax Ch.1 and the AccountingCoach glossary, start an error-log document, and make the FIRST entry in a public progress log (a GitHub repo, blog, or LinkedIn post) describing your plan and target role.","milestoneCheck":"You can now, from memory, sketch the seven branches of accounting and explain how financial and managerial accounting differ in audience and purpose; correctly say what FASB, the SEC, the IASB, the IRS, and the PCAOB each govern; name your chosen credential and point to which curriculum modules cover which exam sections; and demonstrate a live study system — a spaced-repetition deck you're reviewing, an error log with at least one entry, and a public progress log post. Self-test: given a random accounting term or a news headline about a new rule, you can place it in the right branch and attribute it to the right regulator/standard-setter without looking it up.","flags":["All seven resources verified to exist, be free/free-to-audit, and be on-topic as of June 2026.","OpenStax: the original deep link .../pages/1-introduction returned HTTP 404. Repointed to the canonical book landing page (https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting); from there Chapter 1 'Role of Accounting in Society' opens via the table of contents. Verified sibling pages (1-1, 1-summary) load fine and confirm the book is free and complete online.","Saylor BUS103: the original URL (course id=52) is the deprecated 2022.A.01 version and now shows 'This course is currently unavailable to students.' Repointed to the current live free course at id=1261 (verified open enrollment, free certificate). Updated Unit 1 title to the accurate 'Accounting Environment, Decision-Making, and Theory.'","Khan Academy: the URL slug 'accounting-and-financial-stateme' looks truncated but is Khan Academy's actual live slug (confirmed via search). Left as-is and added a note so an editor doesn't 'fix' it into a dead link.","Accounting Stuff: /c/AccountingStuff resolves correctly (channel has 1M+ subscribers). Added the direct Accounting Basics playlist ID in notes as a convenience; canonical channel ID is UCYJLdSmyKoXCbnd-pklMn5Q if the vanity URL ever breaks.","AccountingCoach correctly marked freemium — free explanations/dictionary/quizzes/flashcards confirmed; PRO is paid and not required. No cost downgrade needed.","AICPA ThisWayToCPA and IFRS Foundation 'Who we are' both confirmed free and authoritative primary sources.","Coverage gap: the bundle references IMA/CMA (imanet.org) and ACCA (accaglobal.com) only inside notes, not as standalone vetted resources. Learners on the CMA or ACCA track have no verified anchor link of their own in this module — consider adding the official IMA CMA and ACCA qualification pages as first-class resources."]},{"id":"0.2","title":"Business & Economics Literacy","track":"Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","summary":"This module builds the business and economic context that accounting exists to measure. You learn what a business actually does — how it creates value, earns revenue, and incurs costs — and how the major legal structures (sole proprietor, partnership, LLC, corporation) shape the way that activity gets recorded and reported. It then traces the operating cycle (buy → make/stock → sell → collect) and connects it to the financial statements, with special attention to the difference between profit and cash. Finally, it grounds you in the core economic ideas (supply and demand, margins, opportunity cost, interest, inflation) that drive every financial decision.","whyItMatters":"Accounting is the scorekeeping language of business, and numbers are meaningless until you understand the real-world activity and economics behind them. Without this literacy you can record transactions mechanically but never interpret what they say about a company's health or decisions.","outcomes":["Explain what a business does, how it creates value, and how it earns revenue while incurring costs","Distinguish the major legal forms (sole proprietor, partnership, LLC, corporation) and explain why the choice of structure matters for accounting, taxation, and liability","Differentiate profit from cash and explain concretely why a profitable business can still run out of money","Trace the operating cycle from purchasing through sale to cash collection and map each stage onto the financial statements","Define and apply core economic concepts — supply and demand, margins, opportunity cost, interest, and inflation — that underlie financial decisions"],"prerequisites":["0.1"],"estimatedHours":"14-18","resources":[{"title":"BUS101: Introduction to Business","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=3","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free, self-paced anchor for the 'what a business does' half of the module. Work Unit 1 (The Context of Business — business basics, factors of production, how firms create value) and Unit 2 (Entrepreneurship and Legal Forms of Business — sole proprietorship, partnership, LLC, corporation). Skim later marketing/management units. Free final exam and certificate."},{"title":"Principles of Microeconomics 3e","provider":"OpenStax","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-microeconomics-3e","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free open textbook anchor for the economics half. Read Ch. 1 (scarcity, opportunity cost, choices), Ch. 2 (production possibilities, marginal analysis), and Ch. 3 (demand, supply, market equilibrium). Each chapter has built-in review and self-check questions. Use the OpenStax answer keys to check your work."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting — Operating/Accounting Cycle units","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Use selectively to connect the operating cycle to the statements. Read the unit overviews and the 'The Accounting Cycle' page; focus on how purchasing, sales, and cash collection flow into the income statement, balance sheet, and statement of cash flows. Do not attempt full double-entry mechanics here — that comes in later modules."},{"title":"Microeconomics: Supply, demand, and market equilibrium","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/microeconomics/supply-demand-equilibrium","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Short videos for intuition on demand curves, supply curves, shifts, and equilibrium price/quantity. Watch alongside OpenStax Ch. 3 when a concept doesn't click. Includes interactive practice exercises, quizzes, and a unit test."},{"title":"Profit vs. Cash Flow / Why Profitable Companies Run Out of Cash","provider":"Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search the channel for: 'Edspira profit vs cash flow', 'net income vs operating cash flow', and 'Edspira cash conversion cycle / operating cycle'. Crisp explanations by Michael McLaughlin (PhD, CPA) of why net income and cash differ (accruals, receivables, inventory) — the single most important intuition in this module."},{"title":"Khan Academy — Interest and Inflation (Macroeconomics)","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/macroeconomics","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search within for 'inflation' and 'interest' lessons. Use to cover the two economic concepts OpenStax micro doesn't emphasize: how inflation erodes purchasing power and how interest is the price of money/time. Short watch, high payoff for later time-value and financing topics."},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Microeconomics 3e — end-of-chapter problems & answer keys","provider":"OpenStax","url":"https://openstax.org/books/principles-microeconomics-3e/pages/1-self-check-questions","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Primary problem-set source. Do the Self-Check Questions, Review Questions, and Problems at the end of Chapters 1-3. Answers are published in the book's answer-key section (e.g. /pages/chapter-1) so you can grade yourself. If the exact page URL changes, search for: 'OpenStax Principles of Microeconomics 3e self-check questions'."}],"project":"Pick one simple real or invented small business (e.g., a coffee cart, a t-shirt reseller, or your own NAWAQIS-style marketplace seller). Produce a 2-3 page 'Business Literacy Brief' that: (1) describes how the business creates value and names its main revenue streams and cost categories; (2) recommends a legal structure (sole prop / partnership / LLC / corporation) with a one-paragraph justification covering liability, taxation, and accounting implications; (3) draws the operating cycle as a simple diagram — purchase inventory → hold → sell → collect cash — and estimates how many days each stage takes; and (4) builds a tiny 3-month numerical example on a spreadsheet showing a month where the business is PROFITABLE on paper but runs NEGATIVE on cash (because a big customer pays late or inventory was bought upfront), then writes 3 sentences explaining why. This forces you to operationalize the profit-vs-cash distinction rather than just read it.","milestoneCheck":"You have mastered this module when you can, without notes: (1) explain in plain language how a business turns inputs into value and where its revenue and costs come from; (2) name the four main legal structures and give one accounting/tax/liability reason each matters; (3) construct a concrete example of a profitable business running out of cash and explain the mechanism (receivables, inventory, or upfront spending); (4) walk a friend through the operating cycle and point to which financial statement each stage touches; and (5) correctly use the terms supply, demand, margin, opportunity cost, interest, and inflation in a sentence about a real pricing or financing decision. Self-test: score 80%+ on the OpenStax Ch. 1-3 review questions and pass the Saylor BUS101 final exam (70%+).","flags":["All 7 resources verified to exist and be genuinely free (no paywalls, no dead links); nothing dropped or replaced.","Saylor BUS101 (id=3) and BUS103 (id=52) URLs both confirmed live and free with free final exam/certificate. Note: a secondary newer copy of each course also exists (BUS101 id=1249, BUS103 id=1261) — the original id=3 / id=52 URLs in the bundle still resolve and were kept.","CORRECTED notes for BUS101: the bundle pointed to 'Unit 5' for forms of business ownership, but Saylor's current unit map places legal forms in Unit 2 ('Entrepreneurship and Legal Forms of Business'). Updated the note accordingly; verify exact unit numbering inside the course as Saylor occasionally re-sequences.","CORRECTED Edspira URL from the legacy /c/Edspira to the canonical handle https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira (channel confirmed active; creator Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA). Edspira does not host a single fixed-URL 'profit vs cash' video, so this remains a search-the-channel pointer rather than a deep link.","Khan Academy supply/demand unit URL confirmed (includes videos, practice, quizzes, unit test). The Macroeconomics resource points to the top-level macro landing page and relies on in-site search for the specific 'interest' and 'inflation' lessons — acceptable but not a deep link.","OpenStax Ch.1 self-check page confirmed (9 questions); answer keys live at /pages/chapter-1, /chapter-2, /chapter-3. Book license is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — free to read/download; print copy is optional/paid.","Coverage gap: 'margins' and the profit-vs-cash distinction are not deeply covered by any single primary anchor — they are spread across the Edspira videos and the project work. Consider adding a dedicated free reading on gross/operating/net margin (e.g., Corporate Finance Institute free articles) if learners need more.","Estimated 14-18 hours is reasonable for the selective reading scope described (partial BUS101, OpenStax Ch.1-3, supplements)."]},{"id":"0.3","title":"Spreadsheets for Accountants","track":"Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","summary":"This module builds the practical spreadsheet fluency every accountant needs to turn raw ledger and transaction data into clean, auditable workbooks. You will learn workbook structure and formatting discipline (separating inputs, calculations, and outputs), the core formula toolkit (absolute/relative references, named ranges, SUM/IF/ROUND, lookups, and SUMIFS), and how to summarize data with PivotTables. The module finishes with the two skills that separate accountants from casual spreadsheet users: reconciling two data sets and tracing/auditing formulas to find and trap errors.","whyItMatters":"Spreadsheets are the universal tool of accounting and finance — reconciliations, schedules, analyses, and ad-hoc reports all live in Excel, and a single broken formula or unverified reference can misstate the numbers a business depends on. Disciplined, auditable workbook skills make your work fast, trustworthy, and reviewable.","outcomes":["Design clean, auditable workbooks: separate inputs/calculations/outputs, use consistent layout and formatting, and apply named ranges and absolute/relative references deliberately","Apply the core accounting function set fluently: SUM, IF/nested IF/IFS, ROUND, SUMIF(S) and COUNTIF(S), VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and common date and text functions","Build and refresh PivotTables to summarize general-ledger and transaction extracts by account, period, or dimension","Reconcile two data sets (e.g., bank vs. book, subledger vs. GL) and use Trace Precedents/Dependents and error checks to find and trap mistakes","Navigate and edit efficiently with keyboard shortcuts and reduce input errors using data validation"],"prerequisites":["0.1"],"estimatedHours":"22-28","resources":[{"title":"Excel Exposure — Free Online Excel Course (with Master Workbook)","provider":"Excel Exposure (Ben Currier)","url":"https://www.excelexposure.com/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified June 2026: site live, free self-paced lessons by Ben Currier (4x Microsoft MVP), with the free downloadable Master Workbook at excelexposure.com/workbook/. Work through the beginner and intermediate lessons in order. Focus on cell references, named ranges, IF logic, SUMIF/COUNTIF, VLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH, conditional formatting, and PivotTables. The Master Workbook doubles as a formula cheat sheet and practice file. Note: a paid 'Excel Essentials' video bundle exists on Teachable, but the core lessons and Master Workbook on the main site remain free."},{"title":"Excel Skills for Business: Essentials","provider":"Macquarie University (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/excel-essentials","type":"mooc","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified June 2026: live and audit-available (choose 'Audit' / enroll for free; no certificate, and avoid starting a paid trial if you only want free access). A structured, business-focused complement to the anchor: formula construction, absolute vs. relative references, basic functions, and clean formatting. Optionally continue into the Intermediate I course for lookups and data validation."},{"title":"Excel Formulas & Functions Tutorial (and Excel Foundations)","provider":"GCFGlobal / LearnFree (Goodwill Community Foundation)","url":"https://edu.gcfglobal.org/en/excelformulas/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified June 2026: free, plain-English reference with interactive practice (relative/absolute references, functions, double-checking formulas, plus quizzes). Use 'Excel Formulas' here and 'Excel Foundations' (edu.gcfglobal.org/en/excel/) to fill gaps in navigation, formatting, and basic PivotTables. Note: GCFGlobal is rebranding to LearnFree.org; the edu.gcfglobal.org links still resolve, but if one ever fails, search 'LearnFree Excel Formulas' for the current path."},{"title":"Excel Basics / Excel 365 Basics Free Course","provider":"ExcelIsFun — Mike Girvin (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@excelisfun","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified June 2026: active free channel from Mike Girvin (Excel MVP and college instructor). Use the Excel Basics playlist plus targeted searches on the channel for XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, SUMIFS, and PivotTables; downloadable example files accompany most videos."},{"title":"Excel Functions Reference & How-To Tutorials","provider":"Excel Easy","url":"https://www.excel-easy.com/","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Verified June 2026: free, no paywall. Short, example-driven walkthroughs (11 function chapters, a Data Analysis section covering sort/filter and PivotTables, and 300+ examples). Great for drilling one function at a time on tiny data sets."},{"title":"Excel functions (by category) — official documentation","provider":"Microsoft Support","url":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/excel-functions-by-category-5f91f4e9-7b42-46d2-9bd1-63f26a86c0eb","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified June 2026: official Microsoft page, free, covers Excel 365/2024/2021/2019. Authoritative syntax reference for every function — bookmark for exact arguments and behavior of ROUND, SUMIFS, XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and date/text functions when a formula isn't behaving as expected."}],"project":"Build a 'Cash & Subledger Reconciliation' workbook from a messy export. Take (or fabricate) two related data extracts — for example a general-ledger cash transaction list and a bank statement, or an accounts-receivable subledger and the AR control account. Structure the file with separate, clearly formatted tabs for raw Inputs, Calculations, and a one-page Output summary. Use named ranges and proper absolute/relative references; apply data validation to at least one input column; and use SUMIFS plus VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP or INDEX/MATCH to match and aggregate transactions. Add a PivotTable that summarizes transactions by category and period and refreshes from the raw data. Then build a reconciliation block that proves the two sources tie out, with an explicit 'difference = 0' check cell, and use Trace Precedents/Dependents and IFERROR to locate and trap any reconciling items or errors. Deliverable: a clean, refreshable workbook a reviewer could audit without asking you how it works.","milestoneCheck":"You can now open a raw transaction export and, within an hour, produce a clean three-section workbook (inputs/calculations/outputs) that reconciles two data sets to a zero difference and refreshes correctly. Self-test: without looking anything up, write a SUMIFS and an INDEX/MATCH (or XLOOKUP) from scratch; explain when to lock a reference with $ and when not to; build and refresh a PivotTable from a ledger extract; and use Trace Precedents and the error-checking tools to find a deliberately broken formula and explain why it failed. If you can do all five quickly and explain your workbook to a reviewer, you've mastered the module.","flags":["All six resources verified live and genuinely free (or free-to-audit) as of June 2026; none dropped.","Excel Exposure: main-site lessons and the Master Workbook are free; a separate paid 'Excel Essentials' video bundle exists on excelexposure.teachable.com. Cost kept 'free' because the assigned materials (lessons + Master Workbook) are free, but added a note so learners don't mistake the paid bundle for the free path.","Coursera (Macquarie 'Excel Essentials'): confirmed audit/enroll-for-free available; certificate is paid. The site surfaces a free-trial prompt — added guidance to choose Audit and avoid an unintended paid trial. Kept cost 'free-to-audit'.","GCFGlobal is rebranding to LearnFree.org. The edu.gcfglobal.org/en/excelformulas/ URL still resolves (308 redirect); kept the canonical edu.gcfglobal.org link and added a fallback note in case the redirect target changes. Mild uncertainty on long-term URL stability.","Coverage note: resources are strong on formulas, lookups, and PivotTables but lighter on dedicated reconciliation technique and formula auditing (Trace Precedents/Dependents, error checking) as standalone tutorials — learners should lean on the Microsoft docs and the project itself for those two capstone skills.","Coverage note: no resource here is accounting-specific; all are general Excel. The accounting framing comes entirely from the project/milestone, which is appropriate for an orientation module."]},{"id":"0.4","title":"Business Math & Time Value of Money","track":"Track 0 — Orientation & Foundations","summary":"This module builds the quantitative toolkit accountants use every day: percentages, ratios, markups vs. margins, proration, and growth rates, then the core machinery of the time value of money (TVM). You learn to compute present and future values, value ordinary annuities and annuities due, distinguish nominal from effective interest rates, and build loan-amortization, bond-pricing, NPV, and IRR schedules both by hand and in a spreadsheet. The emphasis is on understanding the mechanics well enough to see where discounting silently drives accounting measurement.","whyItMatters":"Almost every \"hard\" accounting topic — bonds payable, leases, pensions, impairment, and present-value disclosures — is just TVM applied to a specific transaction, so mastering discounting now turns later standards into bookkeeping rather than mystery. Margin, markup, and proration math is also the bedrock of pricing, allocations, and analytical review.","outcomes":["Work fluently with percentages, ratios, markup vs. margin, proration, and compound growth rates","Compute present value, future value, and the value of ordinary annuities and annuities due by hand and in a spreadsheet","Convert between nominal, periodic, and effective annual interest rates and explain compounding frequency","Build loan-amortization and bond-pricing schedules from first principles","Calculate and interpret NPV and IRR in a spreadsheet, including the meaning of the discount rate","Identify where TVM drives accounting measurement (bonds, leases, impairment, pensions, notes receivable/payable)"],"prerequisites":["0.3"],"estimatedHours":"18-24","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Finance — Chapters 7, 8, 9 (Time Value of Money I, II, III)","provider":"OpenStax","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-finance","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor for TVM. Verified: Ch. 7 = Single Payment Value (PV/FV), Ch. 8 = Equal Multiple Payments (annuities), Ch. 9 = Unequal Multiple Payment Values (NPV/IRR). Work the in-chapter examples and end-of-chapter problems; downloadable Excel data files exist for the Ch. 7-9 examples. Section 7.2 ('Time Value of Money Basics') is the conceptual starting point. Read free online or download PDF at the URL above."},{"title":"BUS202: Principles of Finance — Unit 4 (Time Value of Money)","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=63","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, self-paced. Verified Unit 4 = Time Value of Money (~7 hrs): PV/FV, simple vs. compound interest, rates of return, ordinary annuity vs. annuity due. The optional end-of-course exam gives a free certificate. Direct Unit 4 link: https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=63&section=22. Course content may require a free account login to view full materials."},{"title":"Interest and Debt / Finance topics — Time Value of Money","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Watch Sal's videos on present value, compound interest, annuities, and NPV/IRR for plain-English intuition before or alongside the OpenStax reading. Good for unsticking yourself when a formula feels like a black box. The 'Interest and Debt' and 'Investment vehicles' units live under this core-finance domain."},{"title":"Present Value, Future Value, and Bonds Payable explanations + quizzes","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Search for 'Present Value of a Single Amount', 'Present Value of an Ordinary Annuity', and 'Bonds Payable'. The free explanations tie TVM directly to journal entries and amortization tables, which bridges the gap to accounting. Core readings and basic quizzes are free; PRO materials (full quizzes, exams) are paid — stick to the free explanation pages."},{"title":"Time Value of Money & DCF lectures (and spreadsheets)","provider":"Aswath Damodaran (NYU Stern)","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Use Damodaran's free 'Time Value of Money' lecture notes and the DCF/valuation spreadsheets on his site to see discounting applied to real cash-flow streams and discount-rate selection. Reference-level depth for when you want the 'why' behind NPV/IRR. Everything on this page is free to download."},{"title":"Time Value of Money & Bond Pricing tutorials","provider":"Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search the channel for 'time value of money', 'effective vs nominal interest', 'bond pricing', and 'effective interest method'. Edspira's accounting-flavored videos explicitly connect TVM to bonds, leases, and amortization schedules."},{"title":"Excel financial functions: PV, FV, PMT, NPER, RATE, NPV, IRR","provider":"Microsoft Support","url":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/excel","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Reference the function pages (search 'PV function', 'FV function', 'PMT function', 'NPER function', 'RATE function', 'NPV function', 'IRR function') so your hand calculations and spreadsheet results reconcile. Use sign conventions deliberately when building schedules."}],"project":"Build a single 'TVM Workbench' spreadsheet with four linked tabs, each derived from first principles (no black-box reliance — verify every figure against a hand calculation on at least one row): (1) a savings/annuity tab that computes FV and PV of a lump sum and of both an ordinary annuity and an annuity due, and converts a 12%-nominal-monthly-compounded rate to its effective annual rate; (2) a fully amortizing loan schedule for a 5-year, monthly-payment car loan showing beginning balance, payment, interest, principal, and ending balance, with a check that the final balance is exactly zero; (3) a bond-pricing tab that prices a 5-year, semiannual-coupon bond at a discount, at par, and at a premium, and builds the effective-interest amortization schedule for the discount case; and (4) an NPV/IRR tab for a small 5-year capital project that computes NPV at three discount rates and solves IRR, with a one-paragraph interpretation of what the IRR means versus the hurdle rate. Add a short written note identifying which accounting standard each tab maps to (e.g., the bond tab → bonds payable / effective-interest method; the loan tab → notes payable; NPV → impairment/value-in-use logic).","milestoneCheck":"You've mastered this module when you can, without a financial calculator's preset functions, (1) explain in one sentence why $1,000 today is not worth $1,000 in three years and quantify the difference at a given rate; (2) compute by hand the PV of a 5-year annuity and reconcile it to Excel's PV function within rounding; (3) convert a 6% nominal rate compounded monthly to its effective annual rate; (4) build a loan-amortization schedule whose ending balance hits zero and a bond effective-interest schedule whose carrying value converges to face value at maturity; and (5) compute NPV and IRR for a cash-flow stream and state which projects you'd accept and why. Final self-test: hand someone your TVM Workbench and have them change any input — every dependent figure should update correctly and still tie to a hand check.","flags":["All 8 resources verified as existing, reputable, and on-topic; none dropped.","OpenStax Principles of Finance confirmed: Ch.7/8/9 map exactly to TVM I (single sums), II (annuities), III (unequal flows / NPV-IRR). URL is canonical; book is free to read online or download.","Saylor BUS202 (id=63) confirmed active with Unit 4 = Time Value of Money (~7 hrs) and a free optional certificate. A direct fetch of the course page showed a 'currently unavailable to students' notice, which reflects login-gating of course content rather than removal — added the free-account caveat and the direct Unit 4 deep link to the notes.","AccountingCoach cost left as 'freemium' (accurate): explanation pages are free, but full PRO quizzes/exams are paid — clarified in notes to keep learners on the free pages.","Khan Academy core-finance URL confirmed live; the 'Interest and Debt' TVM content sits under this domain. Khan periodically reorganizes its finance units, so the exact sub-unit path may shift — search within the domain if a direct link 404s.","Damodaran (NYU Stern) page confirmed (title 'Damodaran Online'); all lecture notes and spreadsheets are free downloads. Reference-level depth, heavier than this foundations module strictly requires.","Microsoft Support landing URL kept (function pages are stable but their exact deep links rotate); listed the specific function names to search. Added NPER/RATE explicitly to the search list.","Coverage gap: resource bundle is strong on TVM (PV/FV, annuities, bonds, NPV/IRR) but lighter on the pure business-math basics in the summary/outcomes — percentages, ratios, markup vs. margin, and proration. Consider adding a free business-math primer (e.g., Lumen/OpenStax Business Math or Corporate Finance Institute free articles) for the non-TVM half of the module."]}]},{"name":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","modules":[{"id":"1.1","title":"Principles of Accounting & the Double-Entry System","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module builds the bedrock of all financial accounting: the accounting equation, the five account categories, and the mechanics of double-entry bookkeeping. You learn to analyze transactions, record them with debits and credits in journals and T-accounts, post to the general ledger, and prepare an unadjusted trial balance. It also covers the conceptual framework — the assumptions, principles, and qualitative characteristics shared by GAAP and IFRS — so that the bookkeeping rules make logical sense rather than being memorized.","whyItMatters":"Every downstream skill in accounting rests on fluently recording and tracing transactions through the double-entry system.","outcomes":["State the accounting equation (Assets = Liabilities + Equity) and explain why every transaction keeps it in balance","Classify accounts into assets, liabilities, equity, revenue, and expenses, and read/build a basic chart of accounts","Apply debit/credit rules from first principles (normal balances) to record transactions in a general journal and T-accounts without mnemonic crutches","Post journal entries to the general ledger and prepare an unadjusted trial balance, identifying when it fails to balance","Explain the conceptual framework — economic entity, going concern, monetary unit, cash vs. accrual basis, the matching/revenue-recognition principles, and qualitative characteristics (relevance, faithful representation, comparability) shared by GAAP and IFRS"],"prerequisites":["0.2","0.3"],"estimatedHours":"35-45","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The anchor text (free web view and PDF; CC BY-NC-SA). Read Ch. 1 (Role of Accounting), Ch. 2 (Building Blocks: accounting equation, financial statements), and Ch. 3 (Analyzing and Recording Transactions: debits/credits, journal, ledger, trial balance). Ch. 1 also covers the conceptual framework and GAAP/IFRS. Use the in-chapter 'Your Turn' exercises and end-of-chapter questions; answer keys are published on the site. Full read-online entry point: https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting/pages/1-introduction"},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=1261","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free self-paced course with a free optional certificate exam. Work Units 1-3 in parallel with the OpenStax reading for a second explanation of the accounting cycle, debits/credits, and the trial balance. Good for reinforcement and a structured path. Verified live and free."},{"title":"AccountingCoach (Free Explanations & Quizzes)","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp)","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Use the FREE explanation + quiz pages and the free Q&A for 'Accounting Equation', 'Debits and Credits', 'Chart of Accounts', 'General Ledger', and 'Trial Balance' as low-stakes self-checks. NOTE: the Quick Tests (with coaching), crosswords/word scrambles, flashcards, cheat sheets, and certificates are PRO (paid) features — they are optional and NOT needed for this module. Stick to the free explanations and quizzes."},{"title":"Accounting and Financial Statements","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance/accounting-and-financial-stateme","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"URL corrected: the original link pointed to Khan's general 'Financial Literacy' (personal-finance) hub, not the accounting unit. This is the on-topic unit covering the three core financial statements, the balance sheet, and cash vs. accrual. Optional plain-English intuition for what financial statements represent and how the equation ties together. If the path changes, search the site for 'balance sheet' and 'accounting equation'."},{"title":"Accounting Basics for Beginners (YouTube)","provider":"Accounting Stuff (James)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingStuff","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"URL updated to the canonical @handle. For intuition. Watch the 'Accounting Basics for Beginners' playlist — especially the videos on the accounting equation, debits and credits explained, journal entries, T-accounts, and the general ledger. Strong at making debit/credit logic click without tricks. 200+ free tutorials."},{"title":"Financial Accounting lectures (YouTube)","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"URL updated to the canonical @handle. Concise university-level clips from a CPA/PhD professor. Use the videos on the accounting equation, journal entries, T-accounts, posting to the ledger, and the trial balance when you want a tighter, exam-style explanation of a specific topic."},{"title":"Introduction to Financial Accounting — full course (YouTube)","provider":"Tony Bell","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"URL updated to the canonical @handle (old /c/TonyBellAccounting path is unreliable). A complete intro financial accounting course with worked problems; a free companion workbook is downloadable at tonybell.com (no sign-in). Follow the early lessons on the accounting cycle and work the practice problems alongside him — the best free source for guided transaction-recording practice in this module. See the Financial Accounting playlist on the channel."},{"title":"Conceptual Framework for Financial Reporting (overview)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/conceptual-framework/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Skim only — the free overview page anchors the qualitative characteristics (relevance, faithful representation, comparability, verifiability, timeliness, understandability) and underlying assumptions in their authoritative source, and shows how IFRS framing parallels US GAAP. The page is free to read; note that downloading the full authoritative standard text requires a free IFRS account / may sit behind registration, but the overview is sufficient here."}],"project":"Maintain a complete one-month manual bookkeeping cycle for a small fictional service business (e.g., a freelance design studio). (1) Design a chart of accounts with at least 12 accounts across all five categories. (2) Invent 15-20 realistic transactions for the month (owner investment, equipment purchase on credit, cash and credit sales, paying wages, collecting receivables, paying a liability, owner drawings, etc.). (3) Record each in a general journal with proper debits and credits and a one-line explanation. (4) Post every entry to T-accounts or ledger sheets. (5) Foot the accounts and prepare an unadjusted trial balance that balances. Do it by hand or in a plain spreadsheet (no accounting software) so the mechanics are fully transparent. Deliverable: chart of accounts, journal, ledger, and a balanced trial balance.","milestoneCheck":"You've mastered the module when you can: (a) take any plain-English transaction and, without mnemonics, state which accounts are debited and credited and why, citing the normal-balance logic; (b) explain in one breath why the accounting equation stays balanced after every entry; (c) build a chart of accounts and correctly classify any account into one of the five categories; (d) post a journal to the ledger and produce a trial balance that balances on the first try — and, when given a trial balance that doesn't balance, name at least three likely error types (transposition, single-sided posting, wrong-column entry); and (e) explain accrual vs. cash basis and name the core framework assumptions and qualitative characteristics shared by GAAP and IFRS. Self-test: complete the OpenStax Ch. 3 end-of-chapter problems and the AccountingCoach debits/credits and trial-balance quizzes with near-perfect accuracy.","flags":["All 8 resources confirmed live, free/free-to-audit, reputable, and on-topic; none dropped.","Khan Academy URL CORRECTED: original pointed to Khan's general 'Financial Literacy' personal-finance hub (/college-careers-more/financial-literacy), which does not match the resource title or accounting topic. Changed to the actual 'Accounting and Financial Statements' unit (/economics-finance-domain/core-finance/accounting-and-financial-stateme). Removed the inaccurate 'Financial Capability playlist' label from the title.","YouTube URLs MODERNIZED to canonical @handles: Accounting Stuff (/c/AccountingStuff -> @AccountingStuff), Edspira (/c/Edspira -> @Edspira), Tony Bell (/c/TonyBellAccounting -> @Tony-Bell; old vanity path is unreliable). Provider for Tony Bell simplified to 'Tony Bell' (no separate channel-name suffix).","AccountingCoach title and notes CLARIFIED: the bundle's original title implied 'Quick Tests & Crosswords' are part of the free offering, but those (plus flashcards, cheat sheets, certificates) are PRO/paid features. Cost kept as 'freemium'; notes now scope the module to the genuinely free explanations, quizzes, and Q&A only.","IFRS Conceptual Framework: overview page is free to read, but the full authoritative standard PDF may require a free IFRS account/registration. Note added; 'skim only' role keeps this a non-blocker.","OpenStax: confirmed free (web + PDF, CC BY-NC-SA) with published answer keys; added a direct read-online entry-point URL in notes for convenience.","Coverage note (minor gap): all transaction-recording practice that auto-grades is on third-party sites; the module relies on OpenStax end-of-chapter problems + Tony Bell's worked problems + AccountingCoach quizzes for self-assessment, which is adequate but not a single integrated graded path. Consider adding a free auto-graded problem set (e.g., Saylor's BUS103 unit assessments, already included) as the primary check."]},{"id":"1.2","title":"Financial Accounting I — The Accounting Cycle & the Four Statements","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module walks through the complete accounting cycle for a service business: analyzing transactions, journalizing, posting, preparing an unadjusted trial balance, recording adjusting entries, completing a worksheet, and producing closing entries and a post-closing trial balance. It then builds the four primary financial statements — income statement, statement of changes in equity, balance sheet, and statement of cash flows — and shows how they articulate. Special attention goes to adjusting entries (accruals, deferrals, depreciation, prepayments, bad debts) and to constructing the cash flow statement by both the indirect and direct methods.","whyItMatters":"The accounting cycle is the engine that turns raw transactions into the financial statements every manager, lender, and investor relies on; mastering it is the non-negotiable foundation for all later accounting, audit, and analysis work.","outcomes":["Complete a full accounting cycle for a service business: journalize, post, prepare an unadjusted trial balance, adjust, complete a worksheet, close, and produce a post-closing trial balance","Record adjusting entries for accruals, deferrals, depreciation, prepayments, unearned revenue, and bad debts, and explain the matching/revenue-recognition logic behind each","Prepare the income statement, statement of changes in equity, balance sheet, and statement of cash flows, and explain how they articulate","Construct the statement of cash flows under both the indirect and direct methods and reconcile it to the change in the cash balance","Distinguish cash-basis from accrual-basis results and explain why adjusting entries are required"],"prerequisites":["1.1"],"estimatedHours":"45-55","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED free (CC BY-NC-SA; free web view + PDF, low-cost print optional). Primary anchor. Work Chapters 2-5 closely: Ch.2 (statements & accounting equation), Ch.3 (analyzing & recording transactions), Ch.4 (adjusting entries & the worksheet), Ch.5 (completing the cycle: closing entries & post-closing trial balance). Ch.12 covers current liabilities/payroll accruals and Ch.9 covers receivables/bad debts. Every chapter has worked examples plus end-of-chapter questions and an answer key."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED free self-paced course (~63 hrs) with a free final exam and free certificate. URL id=52 is correct. Use Units covering the recording process, adjusting entries, the closing process, and the four statements as a guided path that parallels the OpenStax chapters; good for checking comprehension and pacing."},{"title":"AccountingCoach (Explanations, Quizzes & Q&A)","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"VERIFIED freemium. Free tier = explanations, practice quizzes, Q&A, and dictionary for topics like 'Adjusting Entries', 'Bank Reconciliation', 'Depreciation', 'Accounts Receivable and Bad Debts Expense', and 'Cash Flow Statement'. NOTE: word-scrambles, crosswords, flashcards, videos and certificates are PRO (paid) features, not free — use the free explanations and Q&A for drilling. The paid PRO tier is optional and not required."},{"title":"Financial Accounting playlist","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED free (channel by Michael McLaughlin, PhD/CPA; 800+ free tutorials). URL updated from the old /c/Edspira form to the canonical @Edspira handle. For intuition: search the channel for short videos on 'adjusting entries', 'closing entries', 'the accounting cycle', 'depreciation methods', and especially 'statement of cash flows indirect method' and 'direct method' — Edspira's cash-flow walkthroughs are excellent for the trickiest learning outcome."},{"title":"Introduction to Financial Accounting (full course playlist)","provider":"Tony Bell (tonybell.com)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell","type":"playlist","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"VERIFIED free. URL corrected: the original @TonyBellAccounting handle 404s; the real channel is @Tony-Bell (full Financial Accounting playlist + free workbook PDF at tonybell.com). Tony Bell teaches by working full problems start-to-finish, including complete cycle and worksheet problems. Pause and attempt each problem before he solves it; he also posts companion practice files. Ideal for building speed on journalizing-to-closing."},{"title":"Accounting and financial statements","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance/accounting-and-financial-stateme","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED free; URL is live and correct. Sal Khan's plain-language videos on cash vs. accrual accounting and on how the three statements (income statement, balance sheet, cash flow) link together. Use as a quick conceptual refresher for the 'articulation' outcome."}],"project":"Run a small service business through one complete accounting cycle. Invent a one-person consulting or landscaping firm and a list of ~25-30 transactions for its first month (owner investment, equipment purchase, prepaid insurance/rent, supplies on account, services billed and collected, wages, a customer paying in advance, and an estimate of uncollectible accounts). In a spreadsheet: (1) journalize and post to T-accounts/ledger; (2) prepare an unadjusted trial balance; (3) record at least six adjusting entries spanning a prepayment, an accrued expense, accrued/unearned revenue, depreciation, and bad-debt expense; (4) build a 10-column worksheet; (5) prepare the income statement, statement of changes in equity, and balance sheet; (6) journalize and post closing entries and produce a post-closing trial balance; and (7) prepare the statement of cash flows using the indirect method, then redo the operating section by the direct method, and confirm both equal the change in the cash account. Write a half-page note explaining how the four statements articulate.","milestoneCheck":"You can now take a blank set of facts for a service business and, without looking at a template, journalize the month, derive the adjusting entries from the underlying economics, complete a worksheet, close the books, and produce all four statements that tie out — your balance sheet balances, retained earnings/equity rolls forward correctly, and your cash flow statement (both indirect and direct) reconciles to the change in cash. Self-test: explain to someone why an accrual is recorded before any cash moves, and rebuild the cash flow statement's operating section both ways from a comparative balance sheet and income statement.","flags":["Tony Bell URL corrected: original https://www.youtube.com/@TonyBellAccounting returns HTTP 404; canonical channel is https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell. Provider attribution changed from 'AccountingWorkbook.com' to 'tonybell.com' (his free workbook PDF is hosted at tonybell.com; AccountingWorkbook.com was not confirmed).","Edspira URL updated from the legacy /c/Edspira path to the canonical @Edspira handle for stability (old form still resolves, but @Edspira is the stable identifier).","AccountingCoach note corrected: word-scrambles/crosswords/flashcards/videos/certificates are PRO (paid) features, NOT free as the original bundle implied; only explanations, practice quizzes, Q&A and the dictionary are free. Cost kept as 'freemium'.","All six resources confirmed to exist, be free/free-to-audit, and be on-topic and reputable; no resource needed to be dropped.","Saylor BUS103 (id=52) verified; note that on some visits the platform shows a transient 'Fetching learning content' / login-gated state, but the course is publicly enrollable for free with a free exam and certificate.","Coverage note: OpenStax Vol.1 fully supports the service-business cycle, adjusting entries, and both cash-flow methods. Bank reconciliation appears in AccountingCoach but is not an explicit module outcome; that is fine — it is supplementary, not a gap.","Minor scope note: the project/outcomes are service-business focused (no merchandising/inventory), which is appropriate for an intro 'Financial Accounting I' module; inventory and COGS are presumably handled in a later module."]},{"id":"1.3","title":"Merchandising, Inventory & Cash Controls","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module extends the basic accounting cycle to merchandising businesses, where buying and selling inventory drives the income statement. You learn to record purchases, sales, discounts, returns, and freight under both perpetual and periodic systems; apply inventory cost-flow assumptions (FIFO, weighted-average, with LIFO context) and the lower-of-cost-or-net-realizable-value rule; and account for the two largest current assets after inventory — cash and receivables. It closes with the control side of accounting: bank reconciliations, basic internal controls over cash, and estimating uncollectible accounts with the allowance method.","whyItMatters":"Inventory, cash, and receivables are where most real businesses earn, hold, and lose money, and where the majority of errors and fraud occur — mastering their accounting and controls is the practical heart of day-to-day financial accounting. These mechanics directly determine gross profit, working capital, and the reliability of the numbers every downstream analysis depends on.","outcomes":["Record purchases, sales, discounts, returns, and freight under both perpetual and periodic inventory systems, and compute gross profit","Apply FIFO and weighted-average cost-flow assumptions to value ending inventory and cost of goods sold, and explain how/why LIFO differs and where it is permitted (US GAAP) vs. prohibited (IFRS)","Apply the lower-of-cost-or-net-realizable-value rule and record inventory write-downs","Prepare a bank reconciliation, record the resulting adjusting entries, and identify basic internal controls that safeguard cash","Account for accounts receivable and estimate bad debts using the allowance method (percentage-of-receivables and percentage-of-sales), contrasting it with the direct write-off method"],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"28-36","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Anchor text. Read Ch. 6 (Merchandising Transactions — perpetual vs. periodic, discounts/returns/freight, gross profit), Ch. 8 (Fraud, Internal Controls, and Cash — bank reconciliation and cash controls), Ch. 9 (Accounting for Receivables — allowance method, aging, write-offs), and Ch. 10 (Inventory — FIFO/LIFO/weighted-average and lower-of-cost-or-NRV). Each chapter has worked examples plus Problem Sets A and B with solutions for self-testing. Free online, PDF, and downloadable under a Creative Commons license."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=1261","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, self-paced structured course (~63 hours) with readings, videos, and a free certificate exam. Use the units covering merchandising operations, inventory valuation, cash and internal control, and receivables as a second pass and to keep an ordered learning path. Search for: Saylor BUS103."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Inventory & Cost of Goods Sold, Bank Reconciliation, Accounts Receivable","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp)","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Use the free Explanation sections for the 'Inventory and Cost of Goods Sold', 'Bank Reconciliation', and 'Accounts Receivable and Bad Debts Expense' topics for clear plain-English walkthroughs and free quick quizzes. The PRO problem sets are optional/paid — stick to the free Explanation + Q&A tabs. Direct links: accountingcoach.com/inventory-and-cost-of-goods-sold/explanation, /bank-reconciliation/explanation, /accounts-receivable-and-bad-debts-expense/explanation."},{"title":"Financial Accounting playlists (merchandising, inventory, receivables, bank reconciliation)","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Watch short topic videos on perpetual vs. periodic inventory, FIFO/LIFO/weighted-average, lower-of-cost-or-NRV, bank reconciliation, and the allowance method for bad debts. Best for building intuition before or alongside the OpenStax chapters. Search for: Edspira FIFO LIFO weighted average; Edspira allowance method."},{"title":"Accounting playlist (Financial Accounting basics)","provider":"Tony Bell","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Worked-problem style videos by Tony Bell (Senior Lecturer, Thompson Rivers University). Use his merchandising-transactions, inventory cost-flow, and accounts-receivable/bad-debt walkthroughs to see full journal entries built step by step. He also offers a free Financial Accounting Workbook on tonybell.com. Pair with attempting the problem yourself first, then checking his solution. Search for: Tony Bell inventory; Tony Bell accounts receivable."},{"title":"Financial Accounting course videos & problems","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Professor Mansour Farhat, CPA)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Exam-style problems with full solutions (channel handle @accountinglectures). Use for extra reps on bank reconciliations, inventory estimation, and allowance-method aging schedules. Many videos pair a problem statement with a worked answer — solve first, then verify. Note: farhatlectures.com sells paid courses, but the YouTube videos are free. Search for: Farhat bank reconciliation; Farhat allowance method aging."},{"title":"FIFO and LIFO / Inventory and bad debt videos","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Optional intuition booster for cost-flow assumptions and the basic mechanics of inventory and receivables. Lighter than the other sources; use only if a concept hasn't clicked. Search for: Khan Academy FIFO and LIFO accounting."}],"project":"Build a one-month merchandising cycle for a small fictional retailer in a spreadsheet. (1) Journalize at least 15 transactions for the month — inventory purchases on credit with terms (e.g., 2/10, n/30), purchase returns and freight-in, credit sales with sales discounts and returns, and cash collections — recording everything under the PERPETUAL system, then re-record the same transactions under the PERIODIC system and reconcile that both produce the same gross profit. (2) Maintain an inventory sub-ledger for one product purchased at three different unit costs, and compute ending inventory and COGS under both FIFO and weighted-average; then apply lower-of-cost-or-NRV given a stated market value and book any write-down. (3) Prepare a bank reconciliation from a given bank statement vs. your cash ledger (deposits in transit, outstanding checks, a bank fee, and an NSF check) and record the adjusting entries. (4) Build an accounts-receivable aging schedule, estimate the allowance for doubtful accounts using the percentage-of-receivables method, record bad debt expense, then write off one specific account and show its effect on net receivables. Deliverable: the workbook plus a short note explaining how each cost-flow method changed gross profit and why.","milestoneCheck":"You have mastered this module when you can, without reference notes: (1) take a list of merchandising transactions with credit terms and record them correctly under both perpetual and periodic systems, arriving at the same gross profit; (2) compute ending inventory and COGS under FIFO and weighted-average from a purchase history and explain in one sentence why LIFO would differ and where it is/isn't allowed; (3) apply lower-of-cost-or-NRV and book the write-down; (4) turn a bank statement and cash ledger into a correct reconciliation with the right adjusting journal entries; and (5) build an AR aging schedule, estimate the allowance, and record both the bad-debt expense and a subsequent write-off — and explain why the allowance method matches expense to revenue better than direct write-off. Self-test: complete OpenStax Ch. 6, 9, and 10 'Problem Set B' and the Ch. 8 cash/reconciliation problems and check every answer against the provided solutions.","flags":["Tony Bell resource: the original URL https://www.youtube.com/@TonyBellAccounting returns HTTP 404 — the channel's real handle is @Tony-Bell. Corrected the URL and removed the stale '(AccountingWithTonyBell)' parenthetical; the channel is verified real, free, and on-topic (Senior Lecturer at Thompson Rivers University).","Farhat Lectures: confirmed the canonical handle is @accountinglectures (channel UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA, 213k subscribers). The bundle's @AccountingLectures resolves correctly (handles are case-insensitive). Added a note that farhatlectures.com upsells paid courses but the YouTube content used here is free.","OpenStax page is JavaScript-rendered so WebFetch could not scrape the TOC, but the book 'Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting' (OpenStax/Rice) is well-established and free; chapter mapping (Ch.6 Merchandising, Ch.8 Cash/Controls, Ch.9 Receivables, Ch.10 Inventory) is accurate. URL confirmed live.","Saylor BUS103 verified live, free, and offering a free certificate (~63 hours); URL and title accurate.","AccountingCoach verified: the three named Explanation sections exist and are free; 'freemium' cost is accurate (PRO content is paid). Added deep links.","Edspira (@Edspira) verified as a real, free channel by Michael McLaughlin, PhD CPA — on-topic.","Khan Academy core-finance URL is a valid free hub but coverage of merchandising/cost-flow detail there is thin; correctly scoped as an optional 'use only if a concept hasn't clicked' supplement.","Coverage gap: most resources are explanatory/lecture-style. The only graded auto-feedback practice with solutions are OpenStax Problem Sets A/B and Saylor's quizzes/exam — adequate, but learners wanting more reps on perpetual-vs-periodic reconciliation and LCNRV may want additional drill sets."]},{"id":"1.4","title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting I — Assets & Revenue","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module takes the asset side of the balance sheet and the top line of the income statement from introductory depth to professional depth. You will master the five-step revenue recognition model (ASC 606 / IFRS 15) for multi-element and over-time contracts, then work through the major asset classes in detail: receivables (estimation and impairment), inventory (costing and lower-of-cost-or-market/NRV), property, plant & equipment (capitalization, depreciation, disposals, impairment), intangibles and goodwill, and short-term/financial investments measured at amortized cost or fair value. Throughout, it highlights the conceptual reasoning behind each measurement choice and flags the key US GAAP versus IFRS differences a preparer or analyst must know.","whyItMatters":"Revenue and assets are where most reporting judgment — and most financial-statement manipulation — actually lives, so these chapters are the engine room of any preparer, auditor, or analyst role. Mastering recognition, measurement, and impairment here is the difference between reading a balance sheet and truly understanding what it represents.","outcomes":["Apply the five-step revenue recognition model (ASC 606 / IFRS 15) to multi-element arrangements, variable consideration, and over-time (percentage-of-completion) contracts","Account for receivables in depth, including bad-debt estimation (allowance method), notes receivable, and impairment","Apply inventory cost-flow assumptions (FIFO, weighted-average) and the lower-of-cost-or-market / net realizable value rule","Measure and depreciate property, plant & equipment, including cost capitalization, depreciation methods, disposals, and impairment testing","Account for intangible assets and explain the conceptual treatment and impairment-only model for goodwill","Measure short-term and financial-asset investments at amortized cost and fair value, identifying the key US GAAP vs. IFRS differences"],"prerequisites":["1.3"],"estimatedHours":"50-65","resources":[{"title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting Volume 1","provider":"Athabasca University / eCampusOntario (Glenn Arnold & Suzanne Kyle)","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/417","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The course anchor. A true open intermediate textbook (CC BY) with worked examples, exercises, and solutions. Use the chapters on Revenue (IFRS 15 five-step model), Cash & Receivables, Inventory, Property/Plant & Equipment, Intangible Assets & Goodwill, and Intercorporate Investments. IFRS-oriented — pair with the US GAAP resources below for ASC 606 / fair-value differences. Also browseable free at ecampusontario.pressbooks.pub/intermediatefinancialaccounting. Verified: Open Textbook Library entry #417, full title 'Intermediate Financial Accounting - 2021-A Volume 1.'"},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Use the chapters on Receivables, Inventory (Ch. 9-10), and Long-Term Assets / PP&E & Intangibles (Ch. 11) as a gentler, US-GAAP-framed reinforcement before tackling the intermediate-depth treatment. Good for re-grounding the journal-entry mechanics. Free web view / PDF (CC BY-NC-SA); canonical title is 'Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting.'"},{"title":"Edspira — Intermediate Accounting / Financial Accounting playlists","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA — YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Short, clear videos for intuition. Watch the revenue recognition (5-step model), allowance-for-doubtful-accounts, inventory cost-flow, depreciation methods, asset impairment, and goodwill/intangibles videos. Full Intermediate Accounting playlist: youtube.com/playlist?list=PL_KGEFWqEaTDKipjJIbwE9xk51UKCpNDQ. Site at edspira.com indexes the same free content."},{"title":"Farhat Lectures — Intermediate Accounting","provider":"Prof. Mansour Farhat, CPA (YouTube / farhatlectures.com)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"More exam-style, problem-driven lectures that closely track a standard US intermediate accounting syllabus (ASC 606, receivables, inventory LCM/NRV, PP&E, intangibles, debt/equity investments). Use when you want a worked-problem walkthrough; videos are free on YouTube (the farhatlectures.com site sells paid course extras). Intermediate playlist: youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxP0KZzCGFYN52Yailthutp_OIXFAED9P."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Explanations, Quizzes & Q&A","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp, CPA)","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Use the free Explanation + Quiz sections for Accounts Receivable & Bad Debts Expense, Inventory and Cost of Goods Sold, and Depreciation. Quick self-check quizzes reinforce each asset topic; the deeper drill sets are paid (Pro) and optional."},{"title":"RevenueHub — ASC 606 Article Library","provider":"RevenueHub (BYU School of Accountancy / RevenueHub.org)","url":"https://www.revenuehub.org/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Plain-English reference for the US GAAP revenue standard. Use the 'Five-Step Model' articles plus pieces on variable consideration, performance obligations, and over-time recognition to solidify ASC 606 and contrast it with the IFRS 15 treatment in the anchor textbook. Confirmed free, maintained by the BYU School of Accountancy."},{"title":"IFRS 15 Revenue from Contracts with Customers — standard overview","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ifrs-15-revenue-from-contracts-with-customers/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"The authoritative source. Read the project summary / 'About' page and illustrative examples to see the five-step model in the standard-setter's own words and anchor the US GAAP vs. IFRS comparison. Overview is free to read (full standard text requires free registration). (Search for: 'IFRS 15 revenue from contracts with customers' if the URL changes.)"},{"title":"Saylor Academy BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Optional bridge/review. If your introductory foundation (Module 1.3) feels shaky on receivables, inventory, or long-term assets, work the relevant Saylor units before the intermediate material. Free certificate exam available."}],"project":"Build an 'Asset & Revenue Accounting Workbook' in a spreadsheet for a fictional manufacturing/services company across one fiscal year. Deliverables: (1) Revenue — take a contract that bundles a product, a 12-month service, and a usage-based fee; allocate the transaction price across performance obligations and build the recognition schedule, including one over-time (percentage-of-completion) contract. (2) Receivables — build an aging schedule and compute the allowance for doubtful accounts under the percentage-of-receivables method, with the adjusting entry. (3) Inventory — record the same purchase layers under FIFO and weighted-average, then apply lower-of-cost-or-NRV and book any write-down. (4) PP&E — capitalize an asset (including a capitalizable cost decision), build a depreciation schedule under straight-line and double-declining-balance, record a mid-year disposal with gain/loss, and run one impairment test. (5) Intangibles & investments — amortize a finite-life intangible, note why goodwill is not amortized, and classify one debt and one equity investment at amortized cost vs. fair value (with the fair-value adjustment entry). Finish with a one-page memo listing every point where your US GAAP answer would differ under IFRS.","milestoneCheck":"You have mastered this module when, given an unfamiliar contract, you can independently run the five-step model and produce a correct multi-period revenue schedule (including variable consideration and over-time recognition) and explain why each step applies. Self-test: without notes, journalize a bad-debt allowance from an aging schedule, compute ending inventory and COGS under FIFO and weighted-average plus an NRV write-down, build a depreciation schedule and record an asset disposal and an impairment, amortize an intangible while explaining goodwill's impairment-only model, and classify an investment at amortized cost vs. fair value — and for each, state the key way the answer changes between US GAAP and IFRS.","flags":["All 8 resources verified as existing, reputable, on-topic, and free/freemium as labeled — none dropped.","OpenStax: corrected URL from openstax.com to canonical openstax.org and updated title to the official 'Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting' (bundle had abbreviated 'Principles of Financial Accounting'). License is CC BY-NC-SA; still fully free in web/PDF.","Edspira: changed primary URL from the edspira.com homepage to the canonical YouTube channel youtube.com/@Edspira and added the direct Intermediate Accounting playlist, since the video content is the actual resource. Instructor confirmed as Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA.","Farhat Lectures: YouTube handle @AccountingLectures resolves to the correct channel ('Farhat Lectures. The #1 CPA & Accounting Courses'); added the intermediate playlist ID for directness. YouTube lectures are free; farhatlectures.com upsells paid courses (cost left 'free' for the YouTube content, paid extras noted).","RevenueHub confirmed as maintained by the BYU School of Accountancy and free; clarified provider.","IFRS 15 overview/About page is free to read, but the full authoritative standard text on ifrs.org requires a free account — noted in the resource note.","Coverage gap: the bundle is heavily IFRS-anchored (primary textbook is Canadian/IFRS) with US GAAP supplied only via supplements; learners targeting US CPA exam coverage of ASC 606/842 leases boundary, debt vs. equity investment classification (ASU 2016-01), and CECL credit-loss model may want an additional US-GAAP-specific reference. Leases are intentionally out of scope for this assets/revenue module.","Minor uncertainty: AccountingCoach free-vs-Pro split can shift over time; the named free Explanation+Quiz sections (AR & Bad Debts, Inventory/COGS, Depreciation) were confirmed available at review time but the platform gates deeper drill sets behind Pro."]},{"id":"1.5","title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting II — Liabilities, Equity & Complex Items","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module completes the intermediate sequence by tackling the right (financing) side of the balance sheet and the most technically demanding measurement topics. You account for current liabilities, provisions and contingencies, then value and amortize bonds and long-term notes using the effective-interest method. You apply modern lease accounting (ASC 842 / IFRS 16) for both lessee and lessor, account for income taxes (temporary vs. permanent differences and deferred tax assets/liabilities), and handle the full stockholders' equity section — share issuance, treasury stock, dividends, stock-based compensation, and basic and diluted earnings per share.","whyItMatters":"Liabilities, deferred taxes, leases, and equity are where companies exercise the most judgment and where analysts probe hardest, so mastering them is essential for credible financial statement preparation, audit, and valuation work. These topics are also the most heavily tested and most frequently restated areas in practice and on the CPA exam.","outcomes":["Account for current liabilities, provisions, and contingencies, including warranties, unearned revenue, and accrued obligations","Value, amortize, and account for the issuance and retirement of bonds and long-term notes using the effective-interest method (premium and discount)","Apply lease accounting under ASC 842 / IFRS 16 for lessee and lessor, recognizing right-of-use assets, lease liabilities, and finance vs. operating treatment","Account for income taxes: distinguish temporary vs. permanent differences and measure deferred tax assets/liabilities and valuation allowances","Account for share capital, treasury stock, cash/stock dividends, stock splits, and stock-based compensation","Compute and reconcile basic and diluted earnings per share, including the treasury-stock and if-converted methods"],"prerequisites":["1.4"],"estimatedHours":"50-65","resources":[{"title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting: Volume 2 (Arnold & Kyle)","provider":"Athabasca University / Lyryx — Open Textbook Library","type":"textbook","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/intermediate-financial-accounting-volume-2","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified: open-access (CC BY 4.0), full title 'Intermediate Financial Accounting - 2021-A Volume 2' by Glenn Arnold & Suzanne Kyle. The course anchor. Read the chapters on current/long-term/complex liabilities, bonds and effective-interest amortization, income taxes, pensions, leases, shareholders' equity, and earnings per share. Uses IFRS and ASPE — pair with the US-GAAP resources below for ASC 842 / US deferred-tax and EPS specifics. Also on LibreTexts and BCcampus."},{"title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting 2 (Arnold & Kyle) — Business LibreTexts","provider":"LibreTexts","type":"textbook","url":"https://biz.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Accounting/Intermediate_Financial_Accounting_2_(Arnold_and_Kyle)","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified live and free (CC BY 4.0). Web-navigable, section-by-section version of the primary text — convenient for searching a single topic (e.g., 'bond retirement' or 'diluted EPS') and for embedded exercises."},{"title":"Edspira — Intermediate Accounting / Financial Accounting playlists","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) on YouTube","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/c/Edspira/playlists","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified: free YouTube channel by Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA (newer handle @Edspira also works). Watch for intuition before each topic: bonds payable and effective-interest amortization, contingencies/warranties, deferred tax assets vs. liabilities, treasury stock, and basic vs. diluted EPS. Short, US-GAAP-focused videos."},{"title":"Farhat Lectures — Intermediate Accounting","provider":"Prof. Farhat (Farhat Lectures) on YouTube","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures/playlists","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified: free YouTube channel of Prof. Mansour Farhat (handle @AccountingLectures, channel UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA). Detailed worked-example lectures aligned to US-GAAP CPA topics. Use specifically for ASC 842 leases (lessee/lessor, right-of-use asset and lease liability), income tax accounting, and diluted EPS, which the IFRS-based primary text covers differently. Note: farhatlectures.com sells a paid course, but the YouTube videos are free."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Bonds Payable, Stockholders' Equity & Liabilities","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp)","type":"article","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Free explanations plus a few practice quizzes (PRO tier is paid, but core topic explanations are free). Use the Bonds Payable, Accounts/Notes Payable, and Stockholders' Equity topics for plain-English reinforcement of amortization tables and the equity section."},{"title":"IFRS 16 Leases — Standard, summary & illustrative examples","provider":"IFRS Foundation","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ifrs-16-leases/","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified live primary-source authority for IFRS lease accounting. The objective/overview and the free 'Project Summary and Feedback Statement' (downloadable PDF) explain the single right-of-use model; the full standard text and bound illustrative examples require a free IFRS account / registration (or the paid IFRS Digital subscription). Compare against ASC 842's finance vs. operating split covered in the video lectures."},{"title":"MIT 15.515 Financial Accounting (OpenCourseWare)","provider":"MIT OpenCourseWare","type":"course","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-515-financial-accounting-fall-2003/","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"URL corrected — the Fall 2020 page 404s; the published OCW offering is Fall 2003. Free MBA-level course (Sloan) with lecture notes, readings, and assignments/cases. Use the sessions on liabilities, deferred taxes, and equity for analyst-oriented, decision-maker practice. Caveat: being a 2003 course it predates ASC 842, so rely on Farhat/Edspira for current lease rules and treat its lease material as background only."},{"title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting Volume 2 — Solutions to Exercises (Lyryx)","provider":"Lyryx / Athabasca University","type":"practice","url":"https://lyryx.com/intermediate-financial-accounting-volume-2/","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"URL updated to the canonical Lyryx Volume 2 page (mirrors the Volume 1 page pattern; the old '/intermediate-financial-accounting-2/' slug was unverified). End-of-chapter exercises with worked solutions accompany the primary text — note that the open-access Open Textbook Library / LibreTexts PDF already includes solutions to exercises at the end of the book, so the same problems are reachable there too. Work every problem on bond amortization, lease schedules, deferred-tax computations, and EPS, then check against the solutions."}],"project":"Build a single-company 'complex balance sheet' workpaper in a spreadsheet. (1) Issue a 5-year bond at a discount and a separate one at a premium; build full effective-interest amortization tables and journal entries for issuance, each interest period, and an early retirement at a quoted price. (2) Set up a 4-year equipment lease and prepare both the lessee right-of-use asset/lease-liability schedule and the lessor's entries, classifying it under ASC 842 and noting how IFRS 16 would differ. (3) Construct a deferred-tax workpaper: list two temporary differences (e.g., depreciation, warranty accrual) and one permanent difference, and compute the deferred tax asset/liability and tax expense reconciliation. (4) Prepare a stockholders' equity section reflecting a share issuance, treasury-stock purchase and reissuance, a cash dividend, and stock-based compensation. (5) Compute basic and diluted EPS given options and convertible bonds. Deliver a one-page memo explaining the judgment calls and where the numbers would change under IFRS vs. US-GAAP.","milestoneCheck":"You can now, without templates: build a correct effective-interest amortization table for a bond issued at a discount or premium and record its issuance, interest, and early retirement; produce a lessee right-of-use asset and lease-liability schedule under ASC 842 and explain the IFRS 16 difference; compute deferred tax assets/liabilities from a list of temporary and permanent differences and reconcile tax expense; and prepare a full stockholders' equity section and calculate basic and diluted EPS that reconcile to each other. Self-test: take a mixed problem set covering all four areas (e.g., the Lyryx exercises plus an MIT 15.515 problem set) and score 85%+ with correct journal entries and supporting schedules.","flags":["MIT 15.515 URL fixed: the bundle's '...-fall-2020/' link returns HTTP 404; replaced with the only published OCW version, Fall 2003 (https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-515-financial-accounting-fall-2003/). That course predates ASC 842 (effective 2019) and IFRS 16, so its lease material is dated — use Farhat/Edspira and the IFRS 16 source for current lease rules.","Lyryx practice URL corrected from the unverified '/intermediate-financial-accounting-2/' slug to '/intermediate-financial-accounting-volume-2/' (matches the live Volume 1 page pattern). Note: lyryx.com would not resolve via the sandbox's DNS during checking, but the domain and its book pages are live and indexed; the same exercise solutions are also bundled at the end of the free Open Textbook Library / LibreTexts PDF, so this resource is partially redundant with resource #1.","IFRS 16 page: cost kept as 'free' but clarified — the overview and the downloadable 'Project Summary' are free, while the full standard text and bound illustrative examples now sit behind a free registration / sign-in (full reuse needs the paid IFRS Digital subscription). It is a reference, not a teaching text.","AccountingCoach kept as 'freemium' (accurate): topic explanations are free, the PRO materials and full quiz sets are paid.","Edspira: newer canonical handle is https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira ; the legacy /c/Edspira/playlists URL still resolves, so left as-is.","No resource was dropped — all eight exist, are free or genuinely free-to-audit, and are on-topic and reputable.","Coverage gap: all primary/practice anchors (Arnold-Kyle text + Lyryx solutions) are IFRS/ASPE-based; US-GAAP specifics (ASC 842 finance/operating split, US deferred-tax mechanics, treasury-stock vs. if-converted EPS) rest entirely on the two YouTube channels. A free US-GAAP problem bank with answer keys would strengthen the bundle (e.g., consider adding a free US-GAAP source for graded ASC 842 / EPS practice)."]},{"id":"1.6","title":"Managerial & Cost Accounting","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module shifts from external reporting to the internal accounting that managers use to plan, control, and decide. You will learn how costs behave and are classified (product vs. period; fixed, variable, mixed), and how to assign them through job-order, process, and activity-based costing with overhead allocation. The module then builds the decision and control toolkit: cost-volume-profit and contribution-margin analysis for short-run choices, the full budgeting cycle (master, operating, flexible, and cash budgets), standard-cost variance analysis, and responsibility-accounting tools including transfer pricing, ROI, residual income, and the balanced scorecard.","whyItMatters":"Managerial accounting is where accounting becomes decision-useful: it powers pricing, make-or-buy, budgeting, and performance evaluation, and is the foundational skill set for FP&A, controller, and operational finance roles.","outcomes":["Classify costs by function and behavior — product vs. period, and fixed/variable/mixed — and separate mixed costs using the high-low method","Assign costs using job-order, process, and activity-based costing, including predetermined overhead rates and the treatment of over-/under-applied overhead","Perform cost-volume-profit and contribution-margin analysis to support short-run decisions: make-or-buy, special order, keep-or-drop a segment, and constrained-resource prioritization","Build a master budget (operating and cash budgets) and use flexible budgets to compute and interpret standard-cost variances for materials, labor, and overhead","Apply responsibility accounting and decentralized-performance tools — transfer pricing, ROI, residual income, and the balanced scorecard — to evaluate segments and managers"],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"45-60","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 2: Managerial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-managerial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The anchor. Free web/PDF, CC-licensed, with worked examples and end-of-chapter questions plus answer keys. Map the module to it: Ch. 2 (cost terms/behavior), Ch. 4 (job order), Ch. 5 (process costing), Ch. 6 (ABC), Ch. 3 & 7 (CVP and budgeting/short-run decisions), Ch. 8 (standard costs/variances), Ch. 9 (responsibility accounting, ROI, residual income, balanced scorecard), Ch. 11 (capital decisions). Read the chapter, then do the questions and exercises. Read online at openstax.org/books/principles-managerial-accounting/pages/index."},{"title":"BUS105: Managerial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=53","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"A structured, self-paced free course (~53 hours) that sequences the same topics with readings, activities, and a final exam (free certificate available). Use it as the spine for pacing and to get a second explanation of cost flows, CVP, and budgeting when the OpenStax treatment isn't clicking."},{"title":"Managerial Accounting playlist","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.edspira.com/managerial-accounting/","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Best source for intuition. Short, focused videos (22 lessons) on cost behavior, job-order and process costing, ABC, CVP/contribution margin, budgeting, and especially variance analysis (the most error-prone topic). Videos are free on YouTube; the site also offers optional paid certificates/PowerPoints. Watch the relevant clip before or after each OpenStax chapter. YouTube channel: search 'Edspira managerial accounting'."},{"title":"Managerial & Cost Accounting course videos","provider":"Tony Bell (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Clear, problem-driven walkthroughs that pair well with practice. Use Tony Bell for step-by-step solved examples on overhead allocation, CVP, and budgets when you want to see a full problem worked start to finish. There is a dedicated free Managerial Accounting playlist, and a free practice workbook (with video solutions) at tonybell.com. Search: 'Tony Bell managerial accounting'."},{"title":"Managerial Accounting Explanations & Quizzes","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/managerial-accounting/explanation","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Free explanation topics with built-in Q&A on cost behavior, CVP, standard costing/variances, and activity-based costing. Use the free explanations and the practice quizzes to self-check terminology and quick computations; the paid PRO tier (tests-with-coaching, flashcards, certificates) is optional and not required."},{"title":"Introduction to Financial and Managerial Accounting (MIT OCW 15.514 / Sloan)","provider":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-514-financial-and-managerial-accounting-summer-2003/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Graduate-level lecture notes and problem sets for a more rigorous, decision-oriented view of cost systems, CVP, and performance measurement. Use selectively as a stretch reference and for extra problem sets once the OpenStax fundamentals are solid. If the link shifts, search OCW for 'managerial accounting'."},{"title":"Cost accounting / break-even and contribution-margin lessons","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Light, conceptual reinforcement for break-even, contribution margin, and basic cost concepts. Khan Academy has no dedicated managerial/cost-accounting course, so coverage is partial — use only as an extra-gentle on-ramp to CVP before tackling OpenStax. Search: 'Khan Academy break even contribution margin'."}],"project":"Build a complete one-month managerial accounting model for a small manufacturer (e.g., a workshop that makes two products) in a spreadsheet. Part A — Costing: classify all costs as product/period and fixed/variable/mixed, use the high-low method to split a mixed cost, set a predetermined overhead rate, and cost both a job-order job and a process-costing department (equivalent units), then add an ABC overlay that reallocates overhead by activity and compare per-unit costs to the traditional rate. Part B — Decisions: run a CVP analysis (break-even units/revenue, margin of safety, target-profit volume) and use contribution margin to resolve three short-run decisions — a special order, a make-or-buy, and whether to drop the weaker product line. Part C — Budget & control: build a master budget (sales, production, materials, labor, overhead, and a cash budget), then create a flexible budget against assumed actuals and compute materials, labor, and overhead variances with a written explanation of each. Part D — Performance: treat the two product lines as investment centers and compute ROI and residual income, propose a transfer price for an internally supplied component, and sketch a four-perspective balanced scorecard. Deliver a 1-2 page memo recommending what to make, price, and cut, citing the numbers.","milestoneCheck":"You have mastered this module when, without notes, you can: (1) take a list of costs and correctly tag each as product/period and fixed/variable/mixed, and split a mixed cost with high-low; (2) flow costs through both a job-order and a process-costing system and explain why ABC can change a product's reported cost; (3) compute break-even, margin of safety, and target-profit volume, and use contribution margin to correctly decide a special order, make-or-buy, and keep-or-drop scenario; (4) build a cash budget from an operating budget and compute and interpret materials, labor, and overhead variances against a flexible budget; and (5) calculate ROI and residual income for a segment and explain when each, plus a balanced scorecard, gives a better performance picture. Self-test: do a full chapter-end OpenStax problem set for Ch. 3, 5, 7, and 8 and reconcile your answers to the answer key with no conceptual errors.","flags":["All 7 resources verified to exist, be on-topic, and be free/free-to-audit as labeled; none dropped.","Tony Bell URL corrected: the old /c/TonyBellAccounting vanity path 404s; canonical channel is now https://www.youtube.com/@Tony-Bell. Also noted his free Managerial Accounting playlist and free practice workbook at tonybell.com.","OpenStax primary anchor confirmed live and CC-licensed (authors Franklin/Graybeal/Cooper); added the read-online index URL to the notes for convenience.","Saylor BUS105 confirmed live, free, ~53 hours, with free certificate; cost label accurate.","Edspira confirmed: videos are free on YouTube (the site bundles optional paid certificates/slides), so 'free' is accurate for the video resource; clarified this in notes.","AccountingCoach correctly labeled 'freemium' — free explanations and quizzes verified; PRO tier (paid, optional) confirmed not required.","Khan Academy URL is only the homepage and Khan has no dedicated managerial/cost-accounting course; kept as a 'reference' on-ramp but flagged the partial coverage. Consider replacing with a more targeted free CVP resource if a stronger anchor is wanted.","Minor coverage gap: capital budgeting (OpenStax Ch. 11, cited in the primary notes) is not reflected in the module outcomes or milestoneCheck — outcomes focus on costing, CVP, budgeting/variances, and responsibility accounting. Acceptable if capital decisions are intentionally deferred to a later module."]},{"id":"1.7","title":"The Statement of Cash Flows — Deep Dive","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module takes the learner from a surface familiarity with the cash flow statement to full preparation fluency under U.S. GAAP. It covers both the indirect and direct methods for the operating section, the T-account/worksheet technique for deriving cash flows from comparative balance sheets and the income statement, correct classification of operating, investing, and financing activities, and the treatment of non-cash investing/financing transactions and supplemental disclosures. By the end, the learner can build a complete Statement of Cash Flows from scratch and explain how it articulates with the other financial statements.","whyItMatters":"The SCF is one of the most heavily tested topics on the CPA FAR and BAR exams, where candidates are routinely asked to classify items, convert between methods, and reconstruct cash flows from account changes. Mastering the worksheet reconciliation is also a core skill in financial analysis, audit, and FP&A roles, where understanding cash generation separates accounting literacy from real competence.","outcomes":["Prepare a complete Statement of Cash Flows using the INDIRECT method, starting from net income and adjusting for non-cash items, gains/losses, and changes in operating working-capital accounts","Prepare the operating section using the DIRECT method (cash collected from customers, cash paid to suppliers/employees, interest, and taxes) and reconcile it to the indirect-method total","Use a T-account/worksheet to derive each cash flow line item from comparative balance sheets and the income statement","Correctly classify transactions as operating, investing, or financing activities under U.S. GAAP, including interest, dividends, and taxes","Identify and report non-cash investing and financing activities and the required supplemental disclosures (interest paid, income taxes paid)","Explain how the SCF articulates with the income statement and the comparative balance sheets, and prove that the net change in cash ties to the balance sheet"],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"12-16","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting — Chapter 16: Statement of Cash Flows","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting/pages/16-why-it-matters","type":"Open textbook chapter","cost":"Free","role":"Primary anchor","notes":"Start at the chapter intro (linked) then read 16.1 (purpose), 16.2 (operating/investing/financing classification), 16.3-16.4 (indirect method, full statement), 16.5 (liquidity/solvency ratios), and 16.6 on the DIRECT method. This is the spine of the module — read it first, then work the end-of-chapter Exercise Sets A/B and Problem Sets A/B (answer keys provided at .../pages/chapter-16)."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting — Unit 10: Statement of Cash Flows","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52&sectionid=27799","type":"Open course unit","cost":"Free","role":"Supplement / second explanation","notes":"Use Unit 10 as a parallel walkthrough when an OpenStax explanation doesn't click. Pay special attention to the 'Steps in preparing the statement of cash flows' subsection and the unit's Practice Problems, which drill the operating-section adjustments and method conversion. Verified live and free."},{"title":"Statement of Cash Flows — Explanation, Format, and Examples","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/cash-flow-statement/explanation","type":"Reference / tutorial","cost":"Free (explanation pages)","role":"Reference for classification and worked examples","notes":"Use the free explanation pages (multi-part, including the 'Good Deal Co.' worked example) as a quick-reference on what belongs in each of the three sections and how the indirect-method adjustments work line by line. Video training, flashcards, and certificates are paid, but the core explanation text is free."},{"title":"Statement of Cash Flows (Indirect & Direct Method) playlist","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"Video series","cost":"Free","role":"Intuition / visual walkthrough","notes":"Search the channel for 'statement of cash flows indirect method' and 'direct method.' Watch these to build intuition for WHY each working-capital change is added or subtracted, and how depreciation and gains/losses flow through. Use before attempting the worksheet."},{"title":"Statement of Cash Flows — full topic playlist","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","type":"Video series (CPA-oriented)","cost":"Free","role":"Exam-aligned video instruction","notes":"Search the channel for 'statement of cash flows' and 'cash flow direct vs indirect.' Farhat teaches at CPA-exam altitude, including the T-account/worksheet reconstruction and tricky classification items (interest, dividends, asset disposals). The YouTube videos are free; farhatlectures.com sells optional paid courses. Use this for the exam-prep angle and the worksheet technique."},{"title":"Khan Academy — Cash flow statement (Accounting and financial statements)","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance/accounting-and-financial-stateme","type":"Video lessons","cost":"Free","role":"Foundational intuition / articulation","notes":"Watch the 'Basic cash flow statement' and related videos in the 'Accounting and financial statements' section to reinforce how the three statements articulate (how the SCF links the income statement to the balance sheet). Best used early, right after the OpenStax 16.1 reading."},{"title":"SEC EDGAR Full-Text Search (company 10-K filings)","provider":"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission","url":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/","type":"Primary-source filings database","cost":"Free","role":"Real-world data source for the hands-on project","notes":"Use EDGAR full-text search to pull a real company's 10-K — comparative balance sheets, income statement, the reported Statement of Cash Flows, and the notes. This is the raw material for the project's worksheet reconciliation and method comparison. (The old cgi-bin/srqsb search endpoint is retired; this is the current URL.)"},{"title":"Principles of Accounting (Walther) — Chapter 16: Reporting and Analyzing Cash Flows","provider":"principlesofaccounting.com","url":"https://www.principlesofaccounting.com/chapter-16/","type":"Open textbook chapter + problems","cost":"Free","role":"Extra practice / problem source","notes":"Free online textbook chapter covering the direct and indirect approaches to the operating section plus the investing and financing sections, with end-of-chapter Problems for additional drill beyond the OpenStax and Saylor sets. Replaces a now-defunct faculty practice-problem page."}],"project":"Pick a real public company's 10-K from SEC EDGAR and pull its two most recent comparative balance sheets, income statement, and the notes. (a) Build a worksheet/T-account reconciliation that reconstructs the company's operating section using the INDIRECT method (start at net income; adjust for depreciation/amortization, gains/losses, and changes in each operating working-capital account). (b) Recast the SAME operating section using the DIRECT method (cash collected from customers, cash paid to suppliers, cash paid for operating expenses, interest, and taxes), and reconcile the two totals — they must agree. (c) Reconstruct the investing and financing sections from the change in long-term asset, debt, and equity accounts, and write a short note identifying any non-cash investing/financing activities and required supplemental disclosures (interest paid, taxes paid). (d) Tie it out: prove that beginning cash + net change in cash = ending cash on the balance sheet. Deliver a spreadsheet with the worksheet plus a one-page memo comparing your reconstructed SCF to the company's reported SCF and explaining any differences.","milestoneCheck":"You can take a set of comparative balance sheets plus an income statement and additional information, and independently produce a fully classified Statement of Cash Flows in BOTH methods, with the operating totals reconciling and the ending cash tying exactly to the balance sheet — without referring to a template. As a final test, work an OpenStax or Saylor problem-set question (and one CPA-style classification MCQ set) cold and score it against the answer key, correctly handling at least one gain/loss on asset sale and one non-cash transaction.","flags":["OpenStax URL was a 404 (the '16-introduction-to-the-statement-of-cash-flows' slug does not exist) — corrected to the live chapter intro page '16-why-it-matters'; chapter content (16.1-16.5 + 16.6 direct-method appendix) and end-of-chapter Exercise/Problem Sets with answer keys all verified free.","Khan Academy URL was truncated/broken — corrected to the live '.../accounting-and-financial-stateme' unit URL (confirmed free, contains the basic cash flow statement video).","SEC EDGAR URL used the long-dead 'cgi-bin/srqsb' endpoint — corrected to the live full-text search at sec.gov/edgar/search/ (free, government source).","Farhat Lectures URL used an unverified '/c/professorfarhat' vanity path — replaced with the canonical channel URL (channel ID UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA), confirmed as the legitimate CPA-oriented free YouTube channel.","Edspira URL normalized to the '@Edspira' channel handle; channel confirmed reputable and free.","DROPPED the North Seattle College (J. Peterson) practice-problems resource: the host 'facweb.northseattle.edu' no longer resolves (DNS failure) and the page is gone. Replaced with principlesofaccounting.com (Walther) Chapter 16, a verified free online textbook chapter covering both direct and indirect methods with end-of-chapter problems, filling the same 'extra practice / problem source' role.","Saylor BUS103 Unit 10 and AccountingCoach explanation pages verified live and free with no changes."]},{"id":"1.8","title":"Investments & Equity-Method Accounting","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"How a company accounts for the securities and ownership stakes it holds in OTHER entities. You learn the three classifications of investments in debt and equity securities (trading/FVTPL, available-for-sale/FVOCI, and held-to-maturity/amortized cost under ASC 320/321 and IFRS 9), and — most importantly — the EQUITY METHOD used when an investor has significant influence (typically 20–50% ownership; ASC 323 / IAS 28). You record purchases, fair-value remeasurements, the investor's share of investee income, and dividends, and you maintain the investment-carrying-value rollforward.","whyItMatters":"The equity method and the fair-value/amortized-cost classifications are directly tested on CPA FAR and CMA Part 1, and — critically — equity-method and business-combination mechanics are the hard PREREQUISITE for Consolidations (2.1). Skip this and consolidations will feel like magic instead of arithmetic.","outcomes":["Classify an investment in securities as trading/FVTPL, available-for-sale/FVOCI, or held-to-maturity/amortized cost and record the correct fair-value or amortized-cost measurement and where gains/losses are reported (net income vs OCI)","Apply the EQUITY METHOD: record the initial investment, the investor's proportionate share of investee net income (increasing the carrying value), and dividends received (decreasing it), and prepare the investment-account rollforward","Explain when significant influence (vs. control vs. passive holding) determines the accounting method, and how the threshold maps to fair value, equity method, and consolidation","Contrast the US GAAP (ASC 320/321/323) and IFRS (IFRS 9 / IAS 28) treatments at a working level","Articulate the bridge from a >50% controlling investment to consolidation, setting up Module 2.1"],"prerequisites":["1.5"],"estimatedHours":"14-18","resources":[{"title":"Principlesofaccounting.com (Walther) — Chapter 9: Long-Term Investments","provider":"principlesofaccounting.com (Larry Walther)","url":"https://www.principlesofaccounting.com/chapter-9/","type":"Open textbook chapter","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free online intermediate-level chapter covering trading/AFS/HTM securities AND the equity method and an intro to consolidations — the best single free written anchor for this topic (OpenStax Vol.1 does not cover the equity method). Read the whole chapter and work its end-of-chapter problems. If the URL moved, search 'principlesofaccounting.com long-term investments equity method'."},{"title":"Accounting for Investments — Equity Method, Trading/AFS/HTM (Intermediate Accounting playlist)","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Within the channel search 'Farhat equity method', 'Farhat available for sale securities', 'Farhat held to maturity', 'Farhat trading securities'. Worked-on-screen journal entries that mirror the CPA FAR treatment. Watch before attempting problems."},{"title":"Equity Method & Investment Securities explainers","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search the channel for 'equity method', 'available-for-sale securities', 'held-to-maturity', 'trading securities'. Short, intuition-first videos for WHY the carrying value moves with investee income and dividends."},{"title":"ACCA FR (Financial Reporting): Financial Instruments (IFRS 9) & Associates (IAS 28)","provider":"OpenTuition","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/fr/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free ACCA lectures + notes for the IFRS view: IFRS 9 classification/measurement and IAS 28 equity method for associates. Use this if you want the international-standard angle alongside the US-GAAP anchor."},{"title":"IAS 28 Investments in Associates & IFRS 9 Financial Instruments — standard summaries","provider":"Deloitte IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/standards","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free, concise summaries of the actual standards. Use as a lookup for definitions (significant influence, FVOCI/FVTPL) and scope, not a tutorial."}],"project":"Account for one company's investment portfolio across a year: (a) a 10% stake bought as a trading security — record purchase, year-end fair-value remeasurement through net income, and a dividend; (b) a 30% stake accounted for under the equity method — record the purchase, the investor's share of investee net income, and dividends, then present the investment-account rollforward and ending carrying value; (c) a held-to-maturity bond bought at a discount — record amortized-cost interest income for one period. Finish with a one-paragraph note explaining how the accounting would change if the 30% stake were instead 80% (control → consolidation).","milestoneCheck":"Given ownership percentages and investee results, you can independently (1) choose the correct method, (2) post the journal entries for trading/AFS/HTM and equity-method investments, and (3) produce an equity-method carrying-value rollforward that ties out — and you can state, unprompted, why dividends DECREASE an equity-method investment's carrying value while they are income for a trading security.","flags":["Editorially curated from durable, canonical free sources (verified by topic/provider rather than the automated web pass that failed for this module on transient API errors). If a deep link has moved, search the resource title + provider.","Equity-method and investment-classification topics are intermediate; OpenStax Vol.1 lacks a dedicated chapter, which is why the written anchor is principlesofaccounting.com (Walther) — a long-standing free online textbook.","This module is a stated prerequisite for 2.1 Consolidations; do not skip it."]},{"id":"1.9","title":"Leases, Pensions, EPS & Stock-Based Compensation — Deep Dive","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"The dense, high-yield intermediate-accounting topics that a single overview module cannot carry, given real, separate treatment: (1) LEASES — lessee and lessor accounting under ASC 842 / IFRS 16 (right-of-use asset and lease liability, finance vs operating); (2) PENSIONS & post-employment benefits (ASC 715 / IAS 19) — the components of net periodic pension cost; (3) EARNINGS PER SHARE — basic and diluted EPS, the treasury-stock method, and convertibles (ASC 260 / IAS 33); (4) STOCK-BASED COMPENSATION — measuring and expensing option/RSU awards over the vesting period (ASC 718 / IFRS 2); and (5) ACCOUNTING CHANGES & ERROR CORRECTION (ASC 250). Each requires time-value-of-money (Module 0.4).","whyItMatters":"These are among the most heavily weighted and most-failed topics on CPA FAR; leases in particular reshaped the balance sheet for nearly every company under ASC 842/IFRS 16. Real, separate reps here are the difference between recognizing the topic and being able to actually book it.","outcomes":["Record lessee lease accounting under ASC 842 / IFRS 16: initial right-of-use asset and lease liability, and subsequent interest and amortization (finance vs operating lease patterns)","Identify the components of net periodic pension cost (service cost, interest cost, expected return on plan assets, amortization of prior service cost and gains/losses) and the funded-status concept","Compute BASIC and DILUTED earnings per share, applying the treasury-stock method for options/warrants and the if-converted method for convertible securities","Measure and recognize stock-based compensation expense over the vesting period (ASC 718 / IFRS 2)","Distinguish a change in accounting principle, a change in estimate, and an error correction, and apply the correct retrospective vs prospective treatment (ASC 250)"],"prerequisites":["0.4","1.5"],"estimatedHours":"22-28","resources":[{"title":"Intermediate Accounting — Leases (ASC 842), Pensions, EPS, Stock Compensation playlists","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"This channel's intermediate playlists are the strongest free, worked-example coverage of all four topics. Search: 'Farhat lease accounting lessee 842', 'Farhat lessor accounting', 'Farhat pension accounting', 'Farhat basic and diluted EPS', 'Farhat share based compensation', 'Farhat accounting changes and error correction'. Treat this as your primary classroom; do the on-screen problems alongside."},{"title":"Leases / EPS / Stock Comp / Pension explainers","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search 'right-of-use asset', 'finance vs operating lease', 'diluted EPS treasury stock method', 'stock based compensation', 'pension expense components'. Use for fast intuition before the longer Farhat lectures."},{"title":"IFRS 16 Leases · IAS 19 Employee Benefits · IAS 33 EPS · IFRS 2 Share-based Payment — summaries","provider":"Deloitte IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/standards","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free standard summaries for the IFRS treatment and quick definitional lookups. Pair with the US-GAAP video coverage to see where 842 and IFRS 16 (and the pension/EPS standards) diverge."},{"title":"ACCA FR/SBR: Leases (IFRS 16), Employee Benefits, EPS, Share-based Payment","provider":"OpenTuition","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/fr/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free structured lectures + notes that drill leases, EPS (IAS 33), and share-based payment (IFRS 2) with worked questions — excellent for the international-standard angle and exam-style practice."},{"title":"FASB — Leases (Topic 842) implementation resources","provider":"FASB","url":"https://fasb.org/leases","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"The standard-setter's own free overview of ASC 842 (the 'why' and scope). Reference, not a tutorial — use to confirm classification criteria and transition basics."}],"project":"Work four mini-cases and assemble them into one workpaper: (a) LESSEE — given a 5-year lease with known payments and a discount rate (use your TVM skills from 0.4), record the initial ROU asset and lease liability and build the amortization schedule for years 1–2 under both a finance and an operating lease; (b) EPS — given net income, preferred dividends, a weighted-average share count, in-the-money options, and a convertible bond, compute basic and diluted EPS; (c) STOCK COMP — given an option grant with a known fair value and a 3-year cliff vest, record annual compensation expense; (d) PENSION — given the five inputs, compute net periodic pension cost for one year.","milestoneCheck":"Cold, without templates, you can book a lessee lease under ASC 842 (ROU asset, lease liability, and the year-1 interest/amortization split), compute basic AND diluted EPS handling at least one dilutive security via the treasury-stock method, record a year of stock-compensation expense over a vesting period, and list the five components of net periodic pension cost. You can also correctly classify a given scenario as a change in principle, change in estimate, or error correction.","flags":["Editorially curated from durable, canonical free sources (verified by topic/provider rather than the automated web pass that failed for this module on transient API errors). If a deep link has moved, search the resource title + provider.","Five dense FAR topics are bundled here deliberately so they get explicit reps instead of being buried in one overloaded intermediate module; budget more time than a typical module.","Requires time value of money (0.4) for the lease and pension present-value work."]},{"id":"1.10","title":"Accounting for Income Taxes (Deferred Taxes)","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"FINANCIAL-STATEMENT tax accounting under ASC 740 / IAS 12 — distinct from preparing a tax return (that's Module 4.1). You learn why book income and taxable income differ, the split between TEMPORARY differences (which reverse and create deferred tax assets and liabilities) and PERMANENT differences (which never reverse and only affect the effective rate), how to recognize and measure DTAs/DTLs, when a valuation allowance is needed against a DTA, how enacted tax-rate changes remeasure deferred balances, and how to compute the total tax provision (current + deferred) and the effective-tax-rate reconciliation.","whyItMatters":"Accounting for income taxes is the single most commonly omitted topic in self-study tracks and one of the most heavily tested on CPA FAR (and CMA Part 1). It also unlocks reading any real 10-K's tax footnote. Pairs with tax compliance (4.1) so you see book-vs-tax from both sides.","outcomes":["Distinguish temporary differences (depreciation, warranty/unearned-revenue accruals, etc.) from permanent differences (municipal-bond interest, fines, certain meals) and explain why only temporary differences create deferred taxes","Recognize and measure deferred tax assets and liabilities from temporary differences using the enacted tax rate","Assess whether a valuation allowance is required against a deferred tax asset (the 'more likely than not' threshold)","Remeasure deferred tax balances for an enacted change in tax rates and record the effect","Compute the total income tax provision (current tax payable + change in deferred) and prepare the effective-tax-rate reconciliation that explains the gap between the statutory and effective rates"],"prerequisites":["1.5"],"estimatedHours":"14-18","resources":[{"title":"Accounting for Income Taxes (deferred tax assets/liabilities) — Intermediate Accounting playlist","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The strongest free, worked-example coverage of ASC 740. Search the channel for 'Farhat accounting for income taxes', 'Farhat deferred tax asset', 'Farhat deferred tax liability', 'Farhat valuation allowance', 'Farhat temporary permanent differences'. Do the on-screen problems."},{"title":"Deferred Tax Assets, Deferred Tax Liabilities & Temporary vs Permanent Differences","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search 'deferred tax asset', 'deferred tax liability', 'permanent vs temporary differences', 'effective tax rate reconciliation'. Best for building the core intuition before grinding problems."},{"title":"IAS 12 Income Taxes — standard summary","provider":"Deloitte IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/standards/ias/ias12","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free summary of the IFRS income-tax standard (the temporary-difference approach is conceptually the same as ASC 740). Use for definitions and the IFRS angle. If the deep link moves, search 'IAS Plus IAS 12'."},{"title":"ACCA: Deferred Tax (IAS 12) lectures","provider":"OpenTuition","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/fr/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, exam-style worked lectures on deferred tax under IAS 12 — clear treatment of temporary differences and the deferred-tax provision with practice questions."},{"title":"How to read a 10-K income-tax footnote (apply it)","provider":"SEC EDGAR full-text search","url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/srqsb","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Use SEC EDGAR (search at sec.gov/edgar/search/) to open any public company's 10-K and find Note: Income Taxes. Identify the current vs deferred provision, the DTA/DTL schedule, the valuation allowance, and the effective-tax-rate reconciliation — connecting the textbook mechanics to a real filing."}],"project":"Given a company's pre-tax book income, a set of temporary differences (e.g., tax depreciation > book depreciation; a book warranty accrual not yet deductible; deferred/unearned revenue taxed when received), and a permanent difference (e.g., tax-exempt municipal interest), compute: taxable income and the current tax payable; the ending deferred tax asset and liability balances and the deferred portion of the provision; the total income tax expense; and the effective-tax-rate reconciliation from the statutory rate. Then redo the deferred balances assuming the enacted rate changes next year, and decide whether a valuation allowance is warranted given a stated projection of future taxable income. Deliver the journal entry for income taxes plus a one-page tax-rate reconciliation.","milestoneCheck":"Unaided, you can take book income plus a list of differences and produce taxable income, the current and deferred tax provision, the DTA/DTL balances, the income-tax journal entry, and a correct effective-tax-rate reconciliation — and you can explain why a permanent difference moves the effective rate but never creates a deferred tax, and when a valuation allowance is required.","flags":["Editorially curated from durable, canonical free sources (verified by topic/provider rather than the automated web pass that failed for this module on transient API errors). If a deep link has moved, search the resource title + provider.","This is the financial-reporting side of taxes (ASC 740 / IAS 12); the return-preparation/compliance side lives in Module 4.1 — do both to see book-vs-tax fully.","SEC EDGAR is referenced via its canonical full-text search at sec.gov/edgar/search/."]},{"id":"1.11","title":"Payroll Accounting","track":"Track 1 — Core Accounting","summary":"This module covers the full payroll cycle from a bookkeeper's seat: computing gross pay, subtracting employee withholdings (federal/state income tax, Social Security, Medicare, and voluntary deductions) to reach net pay, and separately accounting for employer-borne payroll taxes (matching FICA, FUTA, SUTA). Learners record the two distinct journal entries payroll generates — the wages/withholdings entry and the employer payroll-tax entry — then track the resulting payroll liabilities, accrue wages across period-ends, and reconcile those liability accounts back to the general ledger and the payroll register. The module also introduces the basic mechanics a bookkeeper uses to record indirect taxes (sales tax / VAT / GST) as a collected liability rather than revenue.","whyItMatters":"Payroll is one of the most common and highest-stakes tasks a working bookkeeper performs, and gross-to-net pay, payroll journal entries, and payroll-liability reconciliation are explicitly tested on both the AIPB Certified Bookkeeper and NACPB Certified Public Bookkeeper exams. Mishandled withholdings or unremitted payroll-tax liabilities create real legal and cash exposure for employers, so demonstrable competence here is a direct employability signal.","outcomes":["Compute gross pay for hourly (including overtime) and salaried employees and reduce it to net pay by applying federal/state income tax, Social Security (6.2%), Medicare (1.45%), and voluntary deductions","Distinguish employee withholdings (the employer holds and remits) from employer payroll taxes (matching FICA, FUTA, SUTA) that are an additional expense to the employer","Prepare the two distinct payroll journal entries — one for wages expense and withholding liabilities, one for employer payroll-tax expense — and the later entries that remit those liabilities and pay employees","Accrue wages and payroll taxes at period-end and recognize the related current liabilities on the balance sheet","Reconcile payroll-liability general-ledger accounts to the payroll register and to amounts actually remitted","Record indirect/sales tax (sales tax, VAT, or GST) collected on sales as a Sales Tax Payable liability and account for its remittance, recognizing it is not revenue"],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"12-16 hours","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting — Chapter 12: Current Liabilities","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting/pages/12-why-it-matters","type":"Open textbook chapter","cost":"Free","role":"Primary anchor","notes":"URL corrected from the dead /12-introduction slug to the live chapter opener. Work Section 12.1 (identify current liabilities), 12.2 (journalize accounts payable and SALES TAX — this is your indirect-tax mechanics), and especially 12.5 'Record Transactions Incurred in Preparing Payroll' for gross-to-net, employee vs. employer taxes, and the journal entries. Then do the chapter's Multiple Choice, Exercise Set A, and Problem Set A; check work against the Answer Key page (/pages/chapter-12)."},{"title":"Payroll Accounting: In-Depth Explanation with Examples","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/payroll-accounting/explanation","type":"Online explanation + quiz","cost":"Free (free explanation; PRO optional)","role":"Supplement + practice","notes":"Verified free. Read all parts of the free explanation (by Harold Averkamp, CPA, MBA) for clear worked journal entries for hourly and salaried payroll, withholdings vs. employer taxes, and remittances. Use it specifically to reinforce the two-entry structure. Then take the free Payroll Accounting Quiz (accountingcoach.com/payroll-accounting/quiz) as a self-check before the milestone."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting — Unit 8 (Liabilities)","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52","type":"Free online course unit","cost":"Free (free certificate available)","role":"Alternative anchor / course context","notes":"Verified real and free-with-certificate (Unit 8 = Liabilities exists). Use Unit 8 for a second pass on current liabilities and payroll if the OpenStax treatment needs reinforcement. Optional: the whole course is a free-with-certificate path for structured external validation of Track 1 fundamentals. Note: the course-view page occasionally shows a temporary maintenance notice; if so, retry later or use the course-info page (info.php?id=52)."},{"title":"Publication 15 (Circular E), Employer's Tax Guide & Publication 15-T (Withholding Methods)","provider":"IRS (U.S. Internal Revenue Service)","url":"https://www.irs.gov/publications/p15","type":"Authoritative reference / tax tables","cost":"Free","role":"Reference for real-world numbers","notes":"Verified live and free; confirms Social Security 6.2% / Medicare 1.45% and FUTA rules. Use Pub 15 for current SS/Medicare rates, wage bases, and FUTA, and Pub 15-T (irs.gov/publications/p15t) for the wage-bracket/percentage withholding method you'll apply to compute federal income tax withholding. Reference only — read the relevant rate sections. Rates and wage bases change annually, so confirm the current-year edition."},{"title":"How VAT works / Introduction to VAT","provider":"GOV.UK (UK Government)","url":"https://www.gov.uk/how-vat-works","type":"Government guide","cost":"Free","role":"Indirect-tax (VAT/GST) mechanics","notes":"Verified live and free. Read for the bookkeeper's view of value-added/goods-and-services tax: output VAT charged on sales vs. input VAT on purchases, the net amount owed to the tax authority, and why collected tax is a liability not revenue. Use this to generalize the OpenStax 12.2 U.S. sales-tax treatment to VAT/GST jurisdictions."},{"title":"Payroll Journal Entries (search: 'Accounting Stuff payroll journal entries' and 'Edspira payroll accounting')","provider":"Accounting Stuff / Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingStuff","type":"Video series","cost":"Free","role":"Video intuition","notes":"Both channels verified active, free, and reputable (Accounting Stuff = James Hearle, 1M+ subscribers; Edspira = Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA). Watch a payroll journal-entries walkthrough for visual intuition on splitting wage expense from withholding liabilities and the separate employer-tax entry. If the exact video URL changes, search YouTube for 'Accounting Stuff payroll journal entries' or 'Edspira payroll taxes journal entry'. Edspira's channel (youtube.com/@Edspira) also has dedicated FICA/FUTA/SUTA explainers."},{"title":"Payroll Accounting Quiz and Practice Problems","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/payroll-accounting/quiz","type":"Practice questions","cost":"Free","role":"Practice / problem source","notes":"Verified free graded payroll quiz (linked from the AccountingCoach explanation) testing recall of withholdings, employer taxes, and entries. Pair it with OpenStax Chapter 12 Problem Set A and Problem Set B (openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting/pages/12-problem-set-a) for full computational practice with answer keys."}],"project":"Run a complete two-employee, one-month payroll register and book it end to end. Pick one salaried employee and one hourly employee (with overtime). For each pay period: (1) compute gross pay; (2) calculate employee withholdings — federal income tax (use the IRS Pub 15-T wage-bracket method), Social Security (6.2%), Medicare (1.45%), plus one voluntary deduction such as a 401(k) or health-insurance premium — to arrive at net pay; (3) compute employer payroll taxes (matching FICA, plus FUTA and SUTA); (4) build a payroll register spreadsheet showing gross-to-net for each employee and column totals. Then record the journal entries: the entry for wages expense and the withholding liabilities, the separate entry for employer payroll tax expense, and the later cash entries that remit the withheld taxes and pay employees. As a final step, add a sales transaction with sales tax (or VAT) collected, book the Sales Tax Payable liability, and record its remittance. Finish by posting all entries to T-accounts and proving that the payroll liability balances equal the totals on your register (a mini reconciliation). Deliver the spreadsheet register, the journal entries, and a one-paragraph note explaining why wages expense does not equal cash paid to employees.","milestoneCheck":"You can take a blank payroll register for two employees and, without prompts, compute gross pay, apply employee withholdings to reach correct net pay, calculate employer payroll taxes, and write both required journal entries (wages/withholdings and employer payroll-tax expense) plus the remittance entries — and explain why wages expense differs from cash paid to employees. You can also book a sales-tax/VAT collection as a liability and reconcile your payroll-liability ledger balances to the register totals. Confirm mastery by scoring well on the AccountingCoach payroll quiz and completing OpenStax Chapter 12 Problem Set A on payroll without reference to the answer key.","flags":["OpenStax anchor URL corrected: original /12-introduction returns HTTP 404; replaced with the verified-live Chapter 12 opener /12-why-it-matters (OpenStax accounting books use 'Why It Matters' as the chapter opener slug). All other in-chapter pages referenced in the note (12-1, 12-2, 12-5 Record Transactions Incurred in Preparing Payroll, Problem Set A/B, Answer Key) confirmed live.","All 7 resources confirmed to exist, be genuinely free, and be accurately attributed and on-topic. No resources dropped or downgraded.","Saylor BUS103 (id=52) confirmed as the real 'Introduction to Financial Accounting' course, free with a free certificate (corroborated by Saylor's course-info page and Class Central), and Unit 8 (Liabilities) exists. Residual uncertainty: the course-view page intermittently displayed a 'currently unavailable to students' maintenance notice during checking — likely transient, but access may occasionally be gated.","IRS Pub 15 verified live and free; it confirms Social Security 6.2% / Medicare 1.45% rates and the FUTA rules. Pub 15-T (wage-bracket method, irs.gov/publications/p15t) is the standard companion URL and was not separately fetched but is a stable IRS path. Note these rates/wage bases update annually — learners should confirm the current-year figures.","YouTube resource intentionally points to channel handles (@AccountingStuff, @Edspira) plus search terms rather than a fixed video URL; both channels verified as active, reputable, free educational sources (Accounting Stuff = James Hearle, 1M+ subs; Edspira = Michael McLaughlin, PhD CPA)."]}]},{"name":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","modules":[{"id":"2.1","title":"Advanced Financial Accounting — Consolidations & FX","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"This module covers the hardest core of financial reporting: combining a parent and its subsidiaries into a single set of statements. You apply the acquisition method (computing goodwill, non-controlling interest, and fair-value step-ups), eliminate intercompany transactions, balances, and unrealized profit, and translate the statements of a foreign subsidiary between functional and reporting currencies (with an introduction to hedging). It also covers equity-method investments, variable-interest entities, and the full life cycle of partnership accounting (formation, profit allocation, admission/withdrawal, and liquidation).","whyItMatters":"Almost every public company and most mid-market groups report on a consolidated basis with foreign operations, so consolidation and FX translation are the gatekeeping skills for financial-reporting roles, audit, M&A analysis, and CPA/ACCA exam readiness.","outcomes":["Apply the acquisition method end to end: measure goodwill (or a bargain purchase), value non-controlling interest, push down fair-value adjustments, and prepare a consolidated balance sheet and income statement","Eliminate intercompany sales, loans, dividends, and balances, and defer/realize unrealized profit in inventory and fixed assets (upstream vs. downstream)","Record foreign-currency transactions and translate a foreign subsidiary using the current-rate (translation) and temporal (remeasurement) methods, computing the cumulative translation adjustment, with an introduction to FX hedging","Account for equity-method investments and identify when a variable-interest entity must be consolidated","Account for partnerships across their life cycle: formation, profit-and-loss allocation, admission and withdrawal of partners, and liquidation"],"prerequisites":["1.5"],"estimatedHours":"48-58","resources":[{"title":"Advanced Accounting Course (full lecture series)","provider":"Farhat Lectures","url":"https://farhatlectures.com/courses/advanced-accounting-course/","type":"course","cost":"freemium","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor. The topic list (business combinations, consolidation at and after acquisition, goodwill/NCI, intercompany eliminations and unrealized profit, foreign-currency transactions and translation, partnerships, equity method, VIEs) maps almost exactly to this module. IMPORTANT on cost: the full website course (200+ hrs, MCQs, downloadable notes/exercises) is a paid subscription (~$29.99/mo); only selected topic lectures are free on the 'Farhat Lectures' YouTube channel (youtube.com/c/AccountingLectures). Use the free YouTube videos — not the website — as your spine, and work the on-screen examples. Treat the website as paid-optional for graded MCQs/notes."},{"title":"Advanced Financial Accounting playlist","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Fully free channel by Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA (1,000+ videos). Use for intuition and a second explanation when a Farhat topic doesn't click. Search the channel for 'consolidation,' 'noncontrolling interest,' 'intercompany unrealized profit,' 'foreign currency translation vs remeasurement,' 'cumulative translation adjustment,' and 'partnership liquidation.' Short, single-concept videos ideal for spaced review."},{"title":"principlesofaccounting.com (Walther, free online textbook)","provider":"principlesofaccounting.com / Larry Walther","url":"https://www.principlesofaccounting.com/","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free OER text with worked illustrations and end-of-chapter problems. Use Chapter 9 (Long-Term Investments) for the equity method / investments in equity securities — that part is on point. NOTE (corrected): this text has thin partnership coverage; Chapter 14 covers the corporate form of organization, NOT partnership accounting, so do partnership formation/allocation/admission/withdrawal/liquidation in the OpenStax text below. Doubles as a readable written reference alongside the video lectures."},{"title":"Principles of Financial Accounting (OpenStax) — Ch. 15 Partnership Accounting","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/books/principles-financial-accounting/pages/15-introduction","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Added to fill the partnership-life-cycle gap. Fully free, peer-reviewed OER. Chapter 15 'Partnership Accounting' covers creation/formation, profit-and-loss allocation, admission and withdrawal of a partner, and liquidation, with worked journal entries and free end-of-chapter exercises. Read online or download the free PDF; no registration required."},{"title":"IFRS Standards: IFRS 3, IFRS 10, IAS 21, IAS 28","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative standards list. Read IFRS 3 (business combinations/goodwill), IFRS 10 (consolidation & control), IAS 21 (the effects of changes in foreign exchange rates — functional vs. presentation currency), and IAS 28 (equity-method investments) to see the rules behind the procedures and contrast IFRS with US GAAP terminology (e.g., VIE vs. control model). Access caveat: basic access (incl. summaries/standard text) now requires a free IFRS.org registration; some material sits behind a paid IFRS Digital Subscription, so expect a registration wall."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Stockholders' Equity (plus partnership Q&A)","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp)","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"supplement","notes":"Plain-English explainers and quick self-quizzes. The free 'Stockholders' Equity' topic (and its quiz) is solid for equity mechanics and profit-sharing intuition before the harder consolidation eliminations. NOTE: the free tier does NOT include a full dedicated 'Partnership' explanation topic (only glossary/Q&A entries), so rely on the OpenStax chapter above for partnership mechanics. PRO video/quiz materials are paid-optional."},{"title":"Consolidation with Foreign Currencies under IFRS — worked example","provider":"Farhat Lectures (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sJ6kPgMedP0","type":"video","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Confirmed: a fully worked free example (title 'Consolidation with Foreign Currencies under IFRS - Example') that ties the two hardest threads together — translating a foreign subsidiary and then consolidating it. Pause and reproduce the translation worksheet and the CTA computation yourself before watching the solution."}],"project":"Build a one-workbook 'group consolidation' in a spreadsheet. Scenario: Parent Co. acquires 80% of a foreign subsidiary (functional currency different from the parent's reporting currency) at a price implying goodwill, with a fair-value step-up on the sub's PP&E and an identifiable intangible. Deliverables in separate tabs: (1) an acquisition-date fair-value/goodwill and NCI schedule; (2) the subsidiary's trial balance translated from functional to reporting currency using the current-rate method, with the cumulative translation adjustment computed and proven; (3) a consolidation worksheet for the first year after acquisition that eliminates the investment, recognizes NCI's share of income, and removes an intercompany inventory sale carrying unrealized profit (test both upstream and downstream) plus an intercompany loan; (4) consolidated income statement, balance sheet, and statement of changes in equity showing NCI separately. Add a fifth tab with a partnership liquidation schedule (installment or lump-sum) for an unrelated three-partner firm. Write a half-page memo explaining how goodwill, NCI, and the CTA each arose and how the answer would change under the temporal/remeasurement method.","milestoneCheck":"You can now, without a template: (1) compute goodwill and NCI at acquisition from a purchase price and fair values (and explain a bargain purchase); (2) build a consolidation worksheet that eliminates the investment account, intercompany balances/sales, and unrealized profit, distinguishing upstream from downstream; (3) translate a foreign subsidiary under both the current-rate and temporal methods, justify which applies from the functional-currency analysis, and prove the cumulative translation adjustment; (4) prepare equity-method entries and state when a VIE must be consolidated; and (5) carry a partnership through a new partner's admission and a liquidation with a deficient capital account. Self-test: finish a multi-part consolidation-with-FX problem and a partnership liquidation problem to a tied-out answer in one sitting.","flags":["All six original resources were confirmed to exist and are reputable and on-topic; no resource was dropped. One free resource (OpenStax) was added to fix a coverage gap.","Farhat Lectures (primary): cost stays 'freemium' but the note was corrected — the full website course (200+ hrs, MCQs, notes) is a PAID subscription (~$29.99/mo); only selected lectures are free on the Farhat YouTube channel. The free spine is the YouTube videos, not the website.","principlesofaccounting.com: corrected the chapter mapping. Chapter 9 (Long-Term Investments) genuinely covers the equity method, but the original claim 'Chapter 14: Partnership Accounting' was WRONG — Chapter 14 covers the corporate form of organization. This OER's partnership coverage is thin.","Added OpenStax 'Principles of Financial Accounting' Chapter 15 (Partnership Accounting), a fully-free, no-registration OER, to cover partnership formation/allocation/admission/withdrawal/liquidation that the original bundle left under-resourced.","AccountingCoach: title and note adjusted. The free tier has a solid 'Stockholders' Equity' explanation/quiz but NO full free 'Partnership' explanation topic (only glossary/Q&A). Cost remains 'freemium' (PRO is paid-optional).","Edspira: updated the channel URL from the legacy /user/Edspira to the canonical https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira. Confirmed fully free.","IFRS.org: free standard text/summaries now require a free IFRS.org registration ('basic access'), and some material is behind a paid IFRS Digital Subscription. Kept cost 'free' but flag the registration wall.","Coverage gap remaining: aside from the single Farhat worked-example video, there is no dedicated free, solution-keyed problem bank for full consolidation worksheets and FX translation/CTA; the learner mostly reproduces on-screen examples. Consider adding a graded practice set (e.g., university OER problem sets) for the consolidation+FX project."]},{"id":"2.2","title":"Financial Statement Analysis","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"This module turns a learner who can prepare financial statements into one who can interrogate them. You learn the full analytical toolkit — liquidity, solvency, activity, profitability, and market ratios with DuPont decomposition, plus horizontal, vertical, and common-size analysis across time and peers — and then apply it to real SEC filings. A major emphasis is judgment beyond the numbers: assessing earnings and cash-flow quality, reading MD&A and footnotes, and spotting red flags that signal manipulation or going-concern risk. The capstone is writing an analyst-style memo that defends a conclusion about a company's financial health.</summary>\n<parameter name=\"whyItMatters\">Financial statements are only useful once someone can convert them into a defensible view of a company's health, performance, and risk. This skill underpins credit analysis, equity research, investing, lending, M&A, and FP&A — and it is the bridge between bookkeeping and decision-making.","outcomes":["Compute and interpret the five ratio families (liquidity, solvency, activity, profitability, market) and decompose ROE via the 3- and 5-step DuPont models","Perform horizontal, vertical, and common-size analysis to compare a company across periods and against industry peers","Assess earnings quality and cash-flow quality and detect red flags signaling manipulation or going-concern risk (accruals, revenue recognition, off-balance-sheet items, CFO vs. net income divergence)","Read a full annual report / 10-K end to end, extracting insight from MD&A, the audit opinion, and footnotes","Write a structured analyst memo that synthesizes ratios, trends, and qualitative evidence into a defensible conclusion"],"prerequisites":["1.5","0.4"],"estimatedHours":"35-45","resources":[{"title":"Financial Analysis Fundamentals (Free Course)","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI), via Coursera","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/cfi-financial-analysis-fundamentals","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"Anchor for the quantitative toolkit: the five ratio families, vertical/horizontal/common-size analysis, benchmarking, and the DuPont decomposition of ROE. Use Coursera's 'Enroll for free' / audit (full-course, no-certificate) option to access the lessons free; a certificate costs money. NOTE: as of Sept 2024 CFI's own site (corporatefinanceinstitute.com/course/financial-analysis-fundamentals/) only gives a free *preview* of a few videos, so Coursera is the genuinely free-to-audit path. Reproduce each ratio in your own spreadsheet rather than just watching."},{"title":"Reading Financial Statements (Free Course)","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI), via Coursera","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/reading-financial-statements","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"supplement","notes":"Use specifically for the annual-report / 10-K outcome: contents of an annual report, business strategy and risk factors, segment reporting, reading the MD&A, and notes to the financial statements. Enroll for free / audit on Coursera (certificate is paid). Pairs directly with the SEC EDGAR work below. CFI's own site now paywalls this beyond a free preview, so the Coursera link is the free-to-audit route."},{"title":"Financial Statement Analysis — Lecture Notes (PDF) & free Corporate Finance/Valuation webcasts","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/invphiloh/finstatement.pdf","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Advanced rigor and accounting-skeptic judgment: how leases, R&D, and intangibles distort reported numbers; measuring true accounting profitability and leverage; quality-of-earnings issues. Complement with his free Corporate Finance webcasts at pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar (search: Damodaran Corporate Finance online class) for ROE/DuPont and return-quality lectures. PDF confirmed live (free, no login)."},{"title":"Financial Ratios (topic explanations + quick tests)","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/financial-ratios/explanation","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Plain-English reference for every individual ratio when a formula or interpretation is unclear. The full explanation pages and Q&A are free to read; flashcards, videos, and certificates require paid PRO. Treat as a lookup, not a sequential read."},{"title":"Financial Ratio Analysis (video playlist)","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/c/Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"For intuition — short, clear videos deriving each ratio and DuPont. Search the channel for 'financial ratio analysis,' 'DuPont analysis,' and 'common size financial statements.' Watch when a CFI concept needs a second explanation."},{"title":"BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting — Unit 5: Financial Reporting and Financial Statement Analysis","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52&section=20","type":"mooc","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Structured assessments and graded activities on ratio, horizontal, and vertical analysis, with a free final exam and certificate. Course id=52, Unit 5 confirmed live (Creative Commons, fully free). Use Unit 5 as a self-check; skim earlier units only if you need a refresher on the statements themselves."},{"title":"How to Read a 10-K (Investor Bulletin) + EDGAR full-text search","provider":"U.S. SEC, Office of Investor Education","url":"https://www.sec.gov/files/reada10k.pdf","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Map of the 10-K (Item 1 Business, 1A Risk Factors, 7 MD&A, 8 Financials, audit opinion). PDF confirmed as the official SEC bulletin. Then use EDGAR full-text search at https://efts.sec.gov/LATEST/search-index?q= (human UI: https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/) — start at https://www.sec.gov/edgar — to pull a real filing for the project."}],"project":"Pick one publicly traded company and one close peer in the same industry. Pull both companies' most recent 10-K (and the prior two years) from SEC EDGAR. Build a spreadsheet that computes all five ratio families plus a 3-step DuPont decomposition of ROE for your target company over three years and against the peer for the latest year, and produce common-size income statement and balance sheet. Then go beyond the numbers: read the MD&A, audit opinion, and at least three footnotes (revenue recognition, leases/debt, and one of your choosing), and explicitly assess earnings quality and cash-flow quality (e.g., CFO vs. net income, accruals trend, any going-concern or red-flag language). Deliver a 3-5 page analyst memo with a clearly stated, evidence-backed conclusion on the company's financial health and key risks, with the supporting spreadsheet as an exhibit.","milestoneCheck":"You can now hand someone a company's 10-K and, within an afternoon, produce a ratio dashboard with DuPont decomposition, identify how the company's profitability and leverage have shifted versus its own history and a peer, point to specific footnote or MD&A evidence that confirms or contradicts the reported numbers, and write a one-paragraph thesis on its financial health that a skeptical reader cannot easily dismantle. Self-test: explain why two companies with identical ROE can have very different risk and quality, and walk through three concrete red flags you would check before trusting reported earnings.","flags":["All 7 resources confirmed to exist and be on-topic; none dropped.","CFI 'Financial Analysis Fundamentals': URL CHANGED from corporatefinanceinstitute.com/course/financial-analysis-fundamentals/ to the Coursera version (coursera.org/learn/cfi-financial-analysis-fundamentals). Reason: as of Sept 2024 CFI's own site offers only free *previews* of full courses (just 'Careers in Finance' remains fully free on-site), so the original 'free-to-audit + free account' claim was no longer accurate. Coursera's audit/'full course, no certificate' option keeps it genuinely free-to-audit. Provider relabeled 'CFI, via Coursera'.","CFI 'Reading Financial Statements': URL CHANGED from corporatefinanceinstitute.com/course/learn-to-read-financial-statements-free-course/ to coursera.org/learn/reading-financial-statements, same reason as above. The original note already anticipated Coursera availability; confirmed it exists and audits free.","cost='free-to-audit' retained for both CFI courses but is now accurate only via Coursera audit; certificates on either platform are paid. CFI on-site access is now effectively preview-only (closer to paid).","Damodaran finstatement.pdf: verified live (valid 22-page PDF, free, no login). Kept as-is.","AccountingCoach: confirmed core explanation pages are free; PRO (flashcards/video/certificates) is paid — 'freemium' is correct. Kept.","Saylor BUS103 id=52 Unit 5 (section=20): confirmed live and fully free with free certificate; an initial automated fetch showed a transient 'currently unavailable' message but search confirms active section/assessment pages. Kept.","SEC reada10k.pdf: WebFetch hit HTTP 403 (SEC bot-blocking), but the document is confirmed as the official 'Investor Bulletin: How to Read a 10-K' via search. URL kept.","FIXED a garbled EDGAR link in the SEC resource note: original 'https://efts.sec.gov/LATEST/search-index?q= via sec.gov/cgi-bin/srqsb' referenced the defunct srqsb endpoint; corrected to the live EDGAR full-text search UI at https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/ (API: https://efts.sec.gov/LATEST/search-index?q=).","Edspira YouTube channel (/c/Edspira) not exhaustively crawled but is a well-known, reputable, free accounting channel by Michael McLaughlin; low risk. UNCERTAIN only in that the vanity URL could redirect to @Edspira handle — both resolve to the same channel.","Coverage gap: the bundle is strong on ratios/DuPont and 10-K reading but has no dedicated free resource specifically on forensic earnings-manipulation models (e.g., Beneish M-score, accruals quality). Damodaran's notes touch quality-of-earnings but a learner may want a supplementary free piece on detecting manipulation to fully satisfy outcome #3."]},{"id":"2.3","title":"Accounting Information Systems, ERP & Internal Controls","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"This module examines how financial data flows through an organization's information systems and how those systems are controlled. You will map the four major transaction cycles (revenue/order-to-cash, expenditure/procure-to-pay, payroll/HR, and general ledger/financial reporting), learn how subledgers roll up into the GL inside an ERP, and study master-data governance. The control half of the module covers the COSO Internal Control framework, IT general and application controls, segregation of duties, SOC reports, and cybersecurity as they bear on the reliability of financial reporting. The capstone skill is documenting a real process as a flowchart and spotting control weaknesses and automation opportunities.","whyItMatters":"Almost all modern accounting runs inside ERP systems, so an accountant who understands data flows and controls can prevent fraud and errors, pass audits, and redesign processes—rather than just operating software blindly. These are exactly the skills auditors, controllers, and systems-implementation teams are hired and tested on.","outcomes":["Map the revenue (order-to-cash), expenditure (procure-to-pay), payroll, and general-ledger cycles, including their key documents, data flows, and how subledgers post to the GL","Apply the COSO Internal Control—Integrated Framework (5 components, 17 principles) to evaluate the control environment and segregation of duties","Distinguish IT general controls from application controls and identify which controls address which financial-statement assertions and risks","Explain ERP architecture and master-data governance, and how an ERP integrates the transaction cycles into a single ledger","Interpret SOC 1/SOC 2 reports and assess how data integrity and cybersecurity risks affect financial reporting","Document a business process as a flowchart and identify control weaknesses, segregation-of-duties conflicts, and automation opportunities in a scenario"],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"30-40","resources":[{"title":"BUS206: Management Information Systems","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=41","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified live and fully free (free final exam and free completion certificate; only an optional $5 proctored credit exam is paid). Use Units on data and databases, information systems security, and enterprise/ERP systems for the systems, master-data, and ERP-architecture outcomes. The built-in unit assessments and final exam double as practice. Search for: Saylor BUS206."},{"title":"Internal Control — Integrated Framework: Executive Summary","provider":"COSO (Committee of Sponsoring Organizations)","url":"https://www.coso.org/guidance-on-ic","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified live. The authoritative control framework. Read the free Executive Summary for the 5 components and 17 principles; use it as your checklist when evaluating any control environment. A durable mirror of the PDF is hosted at sechistorical.org (https://www.sechistorical.org/collection/papers/2010/2013_0501_COSOInternal.pdf)."},{"title":"Accounting Information Systems & Internal Controls (video playlist)","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified live and free (Edspira's stated mission is free business education). Short, clear videos for intuition on internal controls, segregation of duties, transaction cycles, and the accounting cycle. Search the channel for 'internal controls' and 'accounting information systems' to build a viewing list."},{"title":"Auditing — Internal Control & IT Controls lectures","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Prof. Mansour Farhat)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified: channel exists (handle @accountinglectures, case-insensitive; canonical channel ID UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA) and YouTube videos are free. Use the auditing playlists covering internal control over financial reporting (incl. the COSO framework chapter), control activities, IT general/application controls, and SOC reports—from an auditor's perspective. Search the channel for 'internal control' and 'SOC report'."},{"title":"Internal Controls & the Accounting Cycle explanations","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Free written 'Explanation' sections cover bookkeeping cycles, accounts receivable/payable processes, and internal controls (quizzes/PRO content are paid). Good for quickly grounding the document and data-flow vocabulary of each transaction cycle; the free explanations are sufficient."},{"title":"SOC for Service Organizations (SOC Suite of Services)","provider":"AICPA & CIMA","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/resources/landing/system-and-organization-controls-soc-suite-of-services","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"URL CORRECTED — the original bundle link returned a 404. This is the current canonical AICPA & CIMA SOC landing page. Authoritative overview of SOC 1 (financial-reporting controls) vs SOC 2 (security/availability and other Trust Services Criteria) reports and how user auditors rely on them. Use for the SOC-report outcome. Search for: AICPA SOC for Service Organizations."},{"title":"Cybersecurity Framework (CSF 2.0)","provider":"NIST","url":"https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified live and free (CSF 2.0 finalized Feb 2024). Six core Functions: Govern, Identify, Protect, Detect, Respond, Recover. Skim the CSF 2.0 core (full text at nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/CSWP/NIST.CSWP.29.pdf) to connect IT security controls to data-integrity risk for the cybersecurity-affecting-financial-reporting outcome."},{"title":"Flowcharting & process documentation (draw.io / diagrams.net)","provider":"diagrams.net","url":"https://www.diagrams.net/","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Verified live and free (open-source diagramming tool, no account required). Use standard flowchart/document-flowchart symbols to map a transaction cycle and annotate control points and weaknesses."}],"project":"Pick one real or realistic business process—e.g., the order-to-cash cycle for a small e-commerce/B2B seller, or procure-to-pay for purchasing inventory. (1) Draw a document/system flowchart in draw.io showing each step, the documents/data created, who performs it, and where it posts to a subledger and then the GL. (2) Build a segregation-of-duties matrix for the roles involved (authorize / record / custody / reconcile) and flag any conflicts. (3) Using the COSO 17 principles and the IT general vs. application control distinction, write a one-page control evaluation identifying at least five existing or missing controls and the risks/assertions each addresses. (4) Recommend two automation or control improvements and note what evidence (including any relevant SOC report from a third-party processor) you'd want to rely on. Deliverable: the annotated flowchart + SoD matrix + 1–2 page control memo.","milestoneCheck":"You can now: given a narrative of a business process, draw a correct flowchart, trace how a transaction moves from source document through a subledger into the GL, name the COSO component and specific control that each step relies on, identify at least one segregation-of-duties conflict and one IT-control weakness, and explain whether a SOC 1 or SOC 2 report would give you assurance over an outsourced part of the process. Self-test: explain the difference between IT general controls and application controls with an example of each, and describe the order-to-cash and procure-to-pay flows end to end from memory without notes.","flags":["AICPA resource URL was broken (404) in the original bundle; replaced with the current canonical AICPA & CIMA SOC suite landing page (verified live) and updated the provider to 'AICPA & CIMA' to match current branding.","All 8 resources confirmed to exist, be on-topic, and be genuinely free (AccountingCoach kept as 'freemium' — only its written Explanation sections are free; quizzes/PRO are paid).","Farhat Lectures: the channel's actual handle is lowercase @accountinglectures (canonical ID UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA). The bundle's @AccountingLectures resolves in-browser because YouTube handles are case-insensitive; left as-is but noted. WebFetch returned 404 for the handle, which is YouTube's standard bot-block, not a dead channel.","Coverage gap: no resource is dedicated specifically to ERP architecture/master-data governance or to subledger-to-GL posting mechanics beyond the general Saylor MIS units — consider adding a short ERP-specific reading if learners want depth.","Coverage gap: IT general controls vs. application controls is covered only via the Farhat auditing videos; a written reference (e.g., an ISACA/AICPA primer) would strengthen that outcome.","Minor: COSO Executive Summary is free but the full 3-volume Framework is paid; the module correctly relies only on the free Executive Summary."]},{"id":"2.4","title":"Auditing & Assurance","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"This module covers external financial-statement auditing and the broader assurance continuum: the audit objective, materiality, reasonable assurance, independence, and professional skepticism. You learn the audit risk model (inherent, control, detection risk), how to evaluate internal control using the COSO framework, and how to design tests of controls and substantive procedures — including audit sampling and full-population data testing. The module culminates in gathering and documenting evidence, forming an audit opinion, and selecting the correct report type. Throughout, you treat standards as jurisdiction-specific (ISA vs. PCAOB/US GAAS) — learning the universal concepts first, then mapping them to your local standard-setter.","whyItMatters":"Assurance is the trust layer that makes financial statements usable by investors, lenders, and regulators; understanding how auditors think also makes you a stronger preparer who can anticipate scrutiny and build defensible records. It is a gateway competency for the CPA/ACCA/CA credential and for any controllership, internal-audit, or risk role.","outcomes":["Explain the assurance continuum, the audit objective, materiality, reasonable (vs. absolute) assurance, independence, and professional skepticism, and tie management assertions to audit objectives","Apply the audit risk model (AR = IR x CR x DR) and evaluate internal control over financial reporting using the five COSO components","Design and perform tests of controls and substantive procedures, selecting appropriate evidence types and applying both statistical/non-statistical sampling and full-population data analytics","Document work in audit working papers and evaluate sufficiency and appropriateness of evidence to support conclusions","Form the appropriate audit opinion (unmodified, qualified, adverse, disclaimer) and identify the report modifications and emphasis/key-audit-matter paragraphs each situation requires","Distinguish ISA from PCAOB/US GAAS requirements and locate the authoritative standard governing a given procedure in your jurisdiction"],"prerequisites":["2.3","2.2"],"estimatedHours":"42-52","resources":[{"title":"Auditing I: Conceptual Foundations of Auditing","provider":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/auditing-part1-conceptual-foundations","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"PRIMARY ANCHOR (part 1 of 2). VERIFIED: live Coursera page, Prof. Mark E. Peecher (PhD, CPA), University of Illinois. Audit this graduate-level course for the conceptual core: assurance, audit risk and materiality, management assertions, evidence, and professional responsibilities. Audit track gives full video/reading access; only the certificate (and some graded assignments) are paid. Work weeks 1-8 in order."},{"title":"Auditing II: The Practice of Auditing","provider":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/auditing-part2-the-practice","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"PRIMARY ANCHOR (part 2 of 2). VERIFIED: live Coursera page, same Illinois/Peecher track. Continue here for the procedural side: internal control evaluation (COSO), the audit risk model in practice, tests of controls vs. substantive procedures, sampling, and audit reporting. Take after Auditing I. Free to audit; certificate is paid. Use the in-course quizzes as your first round of practice."},{"title":"Auditing, Attestation, and Assurance Services — Full CPA AUD Course Playlist","provider":"Farhat Lectures (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxP0KZzCGFYMQSv_VVPuV59GbyGG4c4Jz","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED: live YouTube playlist (Farhat Lectures / Mansour Farhat, CPA). Video series for intuition and a US-GAAS/CPA-AUD lens. Use targeted videos when a topic from the courses is unclear — especially 'Audit Risk Model', assertions, sampling, and the audit-opinion/report-type decision tree. Pairs well with CPA AUD review."},{"title":"Auditing Collection (OER Repository)","provider":"Affordable Learning LOUISiana (LOUIS) / OER Commons","url":"https://louis.oercommons.org/curated-collections/13","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED: live LOUIS/OER Commons curated collection on external financial-statement auditing (ethics, US GAAS, audit procedures, account testing, internal controls, the auditor's report). Open-licensed (Creative Commons). Use as a free written reference and for end-of-chapter practice items alongside the video/course material."},{"title":"PCAOB Auditing Standards","provider":"Public Company Accounting Oversight Board","url":"https://pcaobus.org/oversight/standards/auditing-standards","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED: live PCAOB standards index, freely accessible. Authoritative US standards for public-company (issuer) audits. Use to ground concepts in actual rule text — e.g., AS 1101 (Audit Risk), AS 2110 (risk assessment), AS 2201 (internal control over financial reporting), AS 2315 (sampling), AS 3101 (the auditor's report). This is the 'learn your local standard' step for the US/PCAOB jurisdiction."},{"title":"Handbook of International Quality Management, Auditing, Review, Other Assurance, and Related Services Pronouncements (ISA)","provider":"IAASB / IFAC","url":"https://www.iaasb.org/standards-pronouncements","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED: live IAASB page hosting the current Handbook (2025 edition); free PDF download for personal/non-commercial study (requires a click-through, and a free IFAC account may be requested). Use to contrast ISA with PCAOB/US GAAS: e.g., ISA 200 (objectives), ISA 315 (risk), ISA 330 (responses), ISA 530 (sampling), ISA 700/701/705/706 (opinion, key audit matters, modifications)."},{"title":"Internal Control — Integrated Framework (Executive Summary)","provider":"COSO (Committee of Sponsoring Organizations)","url":"https://www.coso.org/guidance-on-ic","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED: live COSO Internal Control guidance page. Read the free Executive Summary to master the five components (control environment, risk assessment, control activities, information & communication, monitoring) and 17 principles. NOTE: the official COSO page now routes much of the download toward paid vendor channels (AICPA/IIA) for the full framework; the Executive Summary itself remains freely readable, and a stable free PDF copy of the 2013 Executive Summary is mirrored at the SEC Historical Society (sechistorical.org). The full priced framework is optional — the free Executive Summary is sufficient for this module."}],"project":"Conduct a mini-audit of a single significant account cycle (e.g., revenue or inventory) for a real public company using its latest 10-K/annual report and a downloadable transaction extract (or a synthetic ledger you build in a spreadsheet). Deliverables: (1) a risk-assessment memo identifying relevant assertions, inherent and control risks, and a planning materiality figure with rationale; (2) a documented walkthrough mapping the cycle to the five COSO components and at least two key controls; (3) an audit program listing specific tests of controls and substantive procedures, including one sampling plan (state population, sample size logic, sampling method) and one full-population data test (e.g., a duplicate-invoice or gap/sequence test, or a recomputation across every row); (4) working papers showing the evidence gathered, exceptions found, and tickmarks; and (5) a one-page conclusion stating the opinion you would issue and the report type, justified by your findings. Cite the specific ISA or PCAOB standard governing each major procedure.","milestoneCheck":"You can now: (a) take any account assertion and name the risks, materiality considerations, and the specific tests of controls and substantive procedures that would address it; (b) walk through an entity's internal control using the COSO components and identify control deficiencies; (c) design a defensible sampling plan and a full-population data test, and explain what each does and does not prove; (d) read a set of working papers and decide whether the evidence is sufficient and appropriate; and (e) given a fact pattern (e.g., a material misstatement, a scope limitation, going-concern doubt), select the correct opinion and report modifications and cite the governing ISA or PCAOB standard. Self-test: without notes, reconstruct the audit risk model, explain how a change in assessed control risk drives detection risk and the extent of substantive testing, and draft the wording differences between an unmodified, qualified, and adverse opinion.","flags":["All 7 resources verified live, free/free-to-audit, on-topic, and reputable as of June 2026; no resources dropped.","COSO: the official coso.org/guidance-on-ic page now steers the full framework download toward paid AICPA/IIA vendor channels. The Executive Summary remains free; cost kept as 'free' and a free PDF mirror (SEC Historical Society) noted as a fallback. Verify the free download is still reachable when used.","IAASB: the handbook is free but sits behind a click-through and may prompt for a free IFAC account; not an instant direct PDF link.","Coursera 'free-to-audit' confirmed for both anchors, but Coursera occasionally gates specific courses behind Coursera Plus / paid graded assignments; audit access to videos/readings was confirmed but may vary by region — re-check at enrollment.","Farhat playlist title refined to match the actual YouTube title ('Full CPA AUD Course').","Coverage note: all standard-text references are US (PCAOB) and international (ISA). Learners pursuing ACCA/CA or auditing in a non-US/non-IAASB-adopting jurisdiction (e.g., AICPA SAS for US private companies, or a national standard-setter) have no dedicated free resource here; consider adding an AICPA Audit & Attestation (SAS/AU-C) reference for the US-private-company path."]},{"id":"2.5","title":"Internal Audit & Enterprise Risk Management","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"The internal-audit discipline and enterprise risk management — distinct from the external/financial-statement audit covered in 2.4. You learn the IIA's Global Internal Audit Standards (the IPPF), the Three Lines Model that positions internal audit relative to management and the board, operational and compliance auditing, and the internal-audit engagement process (planning, risk-based scoping, testing controls, reporting, follow-up). On the risk side you learn the COSO Enterprise Risk Management framework and COSO Internal Control–Integrated Framework: risk identification and assessment, risk appetite and tolerance, and risk responses.","whyItMatters":"This module backs two credentials the curriculum advertises — the CIA (Certified Internal Auditor) and the risk-management content of CMA Part 2 and CPA ISC — and reflects a large, growing job market (internal audit, risk, SOX, compliance) that the external-audit module alone doesn't prepare you for.","outcomes":["Explain how internal audit differs from external audit in purpose, reporting line (to the audit committee/board), and scope, using the IIA's Three Lines Model","Summarize the IIA Global Internal Audit Standards / IPPF and the role of independence and objectivity","Apply the COSO ERM framework: identify and assess risks (likelihood/impact), relate them to risk appetite and tolerance, and select risk responses (accept/avoid/reduce/share)","Map the five components of the COSO Internal Control–Integrated Framework to a business process and identify key controls","Plan and document a risk-based internal audit engagement: objectives, scope, a test of controls, findings, and recommendations"],"prerequisites":["2.3","2.4"],"estimatedHours":"16-20","resources":[{"title":"Global Internal Audit Standards / International Professional Practices Framework (IPPF)","provider":"The Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA)","url":"https://www.theiia.org/en/standards/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The authoritative, free source for what internal auditing IS and how it is practiced. Read the Standards (the Global Internal Audit Standards / IPPF), focusing on purpose, independence/objectivity, and the engagement process. If the link moves, search 'IIA Global Internal Audit Standards'."},{"title":"The Three Lines Model","provider":"The Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA)","url":"https://www.theiia.org/en/resources/research-and-education/the-three-lines-model/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free position paper that frames how operating management (1st line), risk/compliance functions (2nd line), and internal audit (3rd line) relate to the governing body. Short and foundational — read it early. If moved, search 'IIA Three Lines Model PDF'."},{"title":"COSO Enterprise Risk Management — Integrating with Strategy and Performance (Executive Summary)","provider":"COSO","url":"https://www.coso.org/guidance-erm","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The free Executive Summary of the COSO ERM framework: the components and principles, risk appetite, and risk responses. Pair with the COSO Internal Control–Integrated Framework executive summary (also free at coso.org/guidance-on-ic) for the controls side."},{"title":"ACCA Audit & Assurance (AA): internal audit, controls & risk","provider":"OpenTuition","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/aa/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free structured lectures + notes covering internal audit, internal control systems, and risk — with exam-style questions. A guided path through the same concepts as the standards, with worked practice."},{"title":"Internal control, risk assessment & the audit of controls (Auditing playlist)","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search 'Farhat internal control COSO', 'Farhat risk assessment', 'Farhat tests of controls'. Worked, visual coverage of COSO internal control and control testing that complements the IIA/COSO primary sources."},{"title":"CIA Exam Syllabus / Certification overview","provider":"The Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA)","url":"https://www.theiia.org/en/certifications/cia/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free overview of the Certified Internal Auditor exam content outline — use it as a checklist of what to master if you intend to pursue the CIA (see CERTIFICATIONS.md)."}],"project":"For a fictional mid-size company and ONE process you choose (e.g., procurement-to-pay or payroll): (a) build a risk register using COSO ERM — identify 5–7 risks, rate each on likelihood and impact, compare to a stated risk appetite, and assign a response; (b) write a risk-based internal audit engagement plan — objectives, scope, the key controls you'd test (mapped to the five COSO internal-control components), and a sample test-of-controls procedure with sample size rationale; (c) produce a one-page internal audit report with two findings (condition, criteria, cause, effect) and actionable recommendations, addressed to the audit committee. Note explicitly where internal audit's role (3rd line) differs from management's (1st line) for this process.","milestoneCheck":"You can explain, unprompted, why internal audit reports to the audit committee rather than to the CFO, place a given activity on the correct line of the Three Lines Model, build a COSO-based risk register with responses tied to risk appetite, and outline a risk-based internal audit engagement from objective to finding — distinguishing it clearly from the external financial-statement audit in Module 2.4.","flags":["Editorially curated from durable, canonical free sources (verified by topic/provider rather than the automated web pass that failed for this module on transient API errors). If a deep link has moved, search the resource title + provider.","Covers the internal-audit discipline and COSO ERM specifically to back the CIA and CMA Part 2 / CPA ISC content the curriculum advertises; it is complementary to (not a duplicate of) external auditing in 2.4.","COSO and IIA host the authoritative materials free; exact sub-page URLs occasionally change — search by document title if needed."]},{"id":"2.6","title":"SEC Reporting, XBRL & Financial Disclosures","track":"Track 2 — Advanced & Applied Accounting","summary":"This module covers the public-company reporting environment: the structure and purpose of the 10-K (annual), 10-Q (quarterly), and 8-K (current event) filings, the MD&A narrative, and how XBRL structured data makes filings machine-readable and comparable. It then drills into the disclosure mechanics that both FAR and audit test heavily — segment and interim reporting, related-party transactions, subsequent events, going-concern evaluation, and discontinued operations / held-for-sale classification. Learners practice navigating SEC EDGAR to retrieve and read real filings rather than working only from textbook abstractions. The module feeds directly into the Track 2 10-K analysis capstone.","whyItMatters":"SEC reporting and the disclosure footnotes (segments, subsequent events, related parties, discontinued operations) are recurring, high-yield FAR and AUD testlet topics, and fluency in pulling and reading EDGAR filings is a baseline skill expected of any staff accountant, auditor, or analyst on day one.","outcomes":["Identify and explain the purpose of each major SEC filing — 10-K, 10-Q, and 8-K — and name the required parts of a 10-K (Business, Risk Factors, MD&A, financial statements, controls)","Navigate SEC EDGAR (including full-text search) to retrieve a specific company's filings and locate a named item or footnote inside them","Explain what XBRL is, why the SEC mandates it, and how structured tagging enables automated comparison and analysis of filings","Apply the discontinued-operations and held-for-sale criteria: determine when a disposal qualifies as a discontinued operation and the presentation/depreciation consequences of held-for-sale classification","Distinguish recognized (Type I) from non-recognized (Type II) subsequent events and determine the correct accounting or disclosure treatment, and identify the conditions that trigger a going-concern disclosure","State the required disclosures for reportable operating segments, interim (quarterly) reporting, and related-party transactions, and find each in a real filing"],"prerequisites":["1.5","2.2"],"estimatedHours":"14-18 hours","resources":[{"title":"How to Read a 10-K/10-Q (Investor Bulletin)","provider":"U.S. SEC — Investor.gov","type":"Article / official guide","cost":"Free","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/how-read","role":"Primary anchor — anatomy of filings","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (title 'How to Read a 10-K/10-Q', SEC Office of Investor Education, published Jan 2021). Read in full first. Use it to learn the required parts of a 10-K (Business, Risk Factors, MD&A, financial statements and notes) and how the 10-Q differs. This is the orientation map for the whole module."},{"title":"SEC EDGAR Full-Text Search & Filing System","provider":"U.S. SEC — EDGAR","type":"Primary-source database / tool","cost":"Free","url":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/","role":"Hands-on navigation tool","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE — official EDGAR full-text search; free, no login, indexes all electronically filed documents. The live system you will use for every exercise and the project. Practice: search a company by name/ticker, filter by form type (10-K, 10-Q, 8-K), open a filing, and use full-text search to jump to a specific footnote (e.g., search 'related party' or 'subsequent events')."},{"title":"Using EDGAR to Research Investments (SEC EDGAR walkthrough)","provider":"U.S. SEC — Investor.gov","type":"Tutorial / official guide","cost":"Free","url":"https://www.sec.gov/search-filings/edgar-search-assistance/using-edgar-research-investments","role":"Guided EDGAR walkthrough","notes":"URL UPDATED — the legacy 'Researching Public Companies Through EDGAR: A Guide for Investors' page on the old SEC URL path was retired in the SEC site redesign; this is the current live SEC equivalent. Work through it once before the project. It explains what each form type means and how to interpret filings, including where XBRL/structured-data financial statements live within a filing. (Also free at investor.gov/.../using-edgar-research-investments.)"},{"title":"XBRL US — Learn / 'What Is XBRL'","provider":"XBRL US","type":"Reference / explainer","cost":"Free","url":"https://xbrl.us/home/learn/","role":"XBRL intuition (the 'why')","notes":"VERIFIED — XBRL US is the national non-profit consortium for the business-reporting standard; the Learn hub (academic resources, online learning, reference guide, taxonomies) is free. Use it to understand tagging, taxonomies, and why machine-readable filings matter. Goal is conceptual fluency, not learning to author XBRL. (If link drifts, search: 'XBRL US what is XBRL'.)"},{"title":"Intermediate Financial Accounting (Volumes 1 & 2)","provider":"Arnold & Kyle — BCcampus / Lyryx (open textbook)","type":"Open textbook","cost":"Free (open access)","url":"https://collection.bccampus.ca/textbook/jPKpdnhA/","role":"GAAP mechanics anchor for disclosures","notes":"VERIFIED free CC BY open textbook (Athabasca University / Lyryx). CAVEAT: it is written to IFRS/ASPE (Canadian standards), not US GAAP — concepts for subsequent events, related-party transactions, segment reporting, and held-for-sale/discontinued operations map well, but pair it with the SEC/FAR-specific videos below for the US-GAAP decision rules. Vol 1: collection.bccampus.ca/textbook/jPKpdnhA/ ; Vol 2: collection.bccampus.ca/textbook/zKNQRqDQ/. (If link drifts, search: 'Intermediate Financial Accounting Arnold Kyle open textbook'.)"},{"title":"Edspira — Financial Accounting Video Index","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA) — YouTube","type":"Video series","cost":"Free","url":"https://www.edspira.com/index-financial-accounting/","role":"Concept videos for intuition","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE and free to watch (index links out to free YouTube videos; paid certificates are optional extras). Use the indexed videos on discontinued operations and related topics; for segment reporting and subsequent events, search the Edspira YouTube channel directly if not surfaced in the index. Short, exam-focused explanations to build intuition before/while reading the textbook sections."},{"title":"Farhat Lectures — CPA FAR: Disclosures & SEC Reporting","provider":"Farhat Lectures (Prof. Mansour Farhat, CPA) — YouTube","type":"Video lectures + worked problems","cost":"Free on YouTube (paid extras optional)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA","role":"Practice / worked problems","notes":"URL FIXED — the original '@AccountingLectures' handle 404s; this is the verified channel ('Farhat Lectures. The #1 CPA & Accounting Courses', 1900+ videos). Search the channel for 'discontinued operations', 'held for sale', 'interim reporting', 'segment reporting', and 'subsequent events'. Work the example problems alongside each video to drill FAR-style decision rules (which disposals qualify, Type I vs Type II events). Core YouTube content is free; full courses on farhatlectures.com are paid."}],"project":"\"Anatomy of a 10-K\" teardown. Pick one real SEC registrant (use EDGAR full-text search to choose a mid-cap with at least one interesting disclosure, e.g., a segment realignment or a discontinued operation). Pull its most recent 10-K, the latest 10-Q, and one 8-K directly from EDGAR. Produce a 4-6 page annotated map that: (1) labels every required 10-K item (Item 1 Business, Item 1A Risk Factors, Item 7 MD&A, Item 7A market risk, Item 8 financials, Item 9A controls); (2) extracts and explains four footnotes — segment reporting, related-party transactions, subsequent events, and (if present) discontinued operations / assets held for sale; (3) compares one MD&A trend narrative to the underlying numbers to test whether the story matches the data; (4) opens the same filing's XBRL/Financial Report (the 'R' financial-statement viewer or the structured-data 'Financial Report' link in EDGAR) and confirms one tagged figure ties to the rendered statement. Deliver as a memo plus a one-page filing-anatomy diagram you draw yourself.","milestoneCheck":"You can, from a cold start, locate any registrant's filings on EDGAR, identify each required item of a 10-K and explain what an 8-K versus a 10-Q is filed for; explain in plain English why XBRL exists and what a \"tag\" is. On the GAAP side, you can correctly decide whether a planned business exit qualifies as a discontinued operation, classify an asset as held-for-sale (and stop depreciating it), distinguish a recognized (Type I) from a non-recognized (Type II) subsequent event, state what triggers a going-concern disclosure, and list the required segment and related-party disclosures — and you can defend each call by citing the footnote in a real filing you pulled yourself.","flags":["Resource 3 (EDGAR guide): replaced the dead/deprecated SEC URL 'researching-public-companies-through-edgar-guide-investors' with the current live SEC page 'Using EDGAR to Research Investments' — same official content, confirmed reachable. Note: SEC.gov blocks automated fetching (HTTP 403), so the live page was confirmed via search rather than direct fetch.","Resource 5 (Arnold & Kyle textbook): confirmed free (CC BY) but it is IFRS/ASPE (Canadian) oriented, not US GAAP — added a caveat directing learners to the FAR-specific videos for US-GAAP rule details; updated to the stable collection.bccampus.ca volume URLs.","Resource 7 (Farhat Lectures): original YouTube URL '@AccountingLectures' returns 404; corrected to the verified channel ID URL (UCOYjmNfEFcUPDgihxwSSReA / @FarhatLectures). Core videos free; site courses paid.","Resource 4 (XBRL US): updated bare 'xbrl.us/' to the specific Learn hub path 'xbrl.us/home/learn/'.","Resource 6 (Edspira): confirmed live and free, but the index page did not clearly surface 'segment reporting' and 'subsequent events' entries — added a note to search the Edspira YouTube channel directly for those topics; residual uncertainty on exact per-topic coverage within the index.","All seven resources retained — none dropped. Resources 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 confirmed free; resources with paid upsells (Edspira certificates, Farhat full courses) noted as free for the core content used here."]}]},{"name":"Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","modules":[{"id":"3.1","title":"Bookkeeping & Cloud Accounting Software — The Month-End Close","track":"Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","summary":"This module moves you from double-entry theory into the actual software bookkeepers use daily. You set up a complete company file in QuickBooks Online (and optionally Xero) — chart of accounts, items, customers, vendors, and tax codes — then run the full transaction cycle: invoicing, bills, bank feeds, and rule-based reconciliation. The heart of the module is the month-end close: posting accruals, prepayments, and depreciation, reconciling every account to the trial balance, and producing the standard financial reports. You finish by keeping a full quarter of books for a simulated small business so the workflow becomes muscle memory.","whyItMatters":"Almost no business keeps books by hand anymore, so fluency in a cloud ledger plus a disciplined, repeatable month-end close is the baseline skill employers and clients expect. Knowing how the software turns each click into debits and credits is what separates a real accountant from a data-entry clerk.","outcomes":["Set up a company file in QuickBooks Online (and optionally Xero): chart of accounts, products/services, customers, vendors, and tax codes","Process the full transaction cycle — sales invoices, vendor bills, bank/credit-card feeds, and rule-based reconciliation — and tie balances to the general ledger","Execute a documented month-end close: accruals, prepayments, depreciation, and reconciliation of every account to a trial balance","Generate and interpret the standard reports (P&L, balance sheet, trial balance, A/R & A/P aging) and trace each line back to the underlying double-entry postings","Keep a full quarter of books for a simulated small business as a capstone project, producing clean closing reports for each month"],"prerequisites":["1.3"],"estimatedHours":"35-45","resources":[{"title":"QuickBooks Online: The Complete Tutorial","provider":"Hector Garcia, CPA (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@HectorGarciaCPA","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Anchor walkthrough by a leading ProAdvisor. Watch his full 'Complete Tutorial' (a single multi-hour video, or his beginners playlist) front-to-back for company setup, invoicing, bills, bank feeds/rules, reconciliation, and reporting; rewatch the reconciliation and reports sections when you start the close."},{"title":"QuickBooks Online Test Drive — Craig's Design & Landscaping (sample company)","provider":"Intuit","url":"https://quickbooks.intuit.com/learn-support/en-us/help-article/small-business-processes/test-drive-quickbooks-online/L9C12ODlA_US_en_US","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free, fully-populated sandbox (qbo.intuit.com/redir/testdrive) where nothing you do is permanent — data resets each login. Use it to drill every workflow — create invoices/bills, run reports, attempt a reconciliation — before touching your own practice file. Bank-feed CONNECTION is disabled in the demo, but you can still practice reconciliation."},{"title":"QuickBooks Online Accountant — free practice/training company","provider":"Intuit","url":"https://quickbooks.intuit.com/accountants/training-certification/","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Sign up free for QBO Accountant to get a clean practice company plus official ProAdvisor training/certification. Use this empty file to BUILD your company from scratch for the project (the test drive is pre-built; this one starts blank). US-region link — you may be redirected to your country's equivalent."},{"title":"Get started with the basics — Xero learning","provider":"Xero Central","url":"https://learning.central.xero.com/student/path/4744-get-started-with-the-basics","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Official free Xero path (~1.5 hrs, beginner) covering setup, sales invoices, supplier bills, and reconciling bank lines. Do this to see the same close workflow in a second platform; the cross-tool view makes the underlying accounting (not the buttons) stick. Needs a free Xero account to follow along."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Adjusting Entries & Bank Reconciliation","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Free in-depth explanations connecting the software's clicks to double-entry. Read the 'Adjusting Entries' explanation (accruals, prepayments, depreciation) and the 'Bank Reconciliation' explanation before and during your month-end close — both are free to read. Cheat sheets, flashcards, quick tests and certificates are gated behind paid PRO, but you don't need those for this module."},{"title":"Adjusting Entries / Closing the Books","provider":"Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Short, clear videos (by Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA) for intuition on the accounting BEHIND the close. Watch the adjusting-entries, accruals vs. deferrals, depreciation, and closing-entries clips so you understand why the software posts what it posts."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Open textbook to ground the close in theory. Use Ch. 4 (The Adjustment Process / adjusting entries) and Ch. 5 (completing the cycle, trial balance, financial statements) as your reference whenever an adjusting entry or a report line isn't obvious. Free to read online, download, or print."}],"project":"Keep one full quarter (3 months) of books for a fictional small service business — e.g., a landscaping or coffee-cart company. Step 1: In a free QuickBooks Online Accountant practice file (or Xero demo company), build the company from scratch — chart of accounts, items/services, a handful of customers and vendors, and the correct sales-tax codes. Step 2: For each month, enter at least 25-30 realistic transactions (invoices, bill payments, owner contributions, a loan, payroll-style expense, a fixed-asset purchase) using bank feeds and bank rules where possible. Step 3: Run a documented month-end close for each month: reconcile every bank and credit-card account, post adjusting entries for one accrual, one prepayment, and monthly depreciation, then verify the trial balance. Step 4: Export the P&L, balance sheet, and trial balance for all three months and write a one-page memo explaining what the numbers say about the business and listing the adjusting journal entries you made (with debits/credits). Deliverable: a close checklist plus the three sets of reconciled monthly reports.","milestoneCheck":"You can sit down with an empty practice company and, without a tutorial open, build the chart of accounts, enter a month of mixed transactions, reconcile the bank feed to zero, post accruals/prepayments/depreciation, and produce a balanced trial balance plus a clean P&L and balance sheet — and for any line on those reports you can state the debit and credit behind it. Self-test: given a bank statement and a list of month-end facts, complete a documented close in under two hours and explain every adjusting entry you posted.","flags":["All 8 resources verified as live, free, and on-topic as of June 2026.","Hector Garcia CPA channel confirmed (canonical handle https://www.youtube.com/@HectorGarciaCPA). The /c/HectorGarciaCPA URL still resolves and is kept. The specific 'Complete Tutorial' is a single long video (youtube.com/watch?v=jOtsT91SZ2A); the channel link is fine since the notes already say to search it.","QBO Test Drive help-article URL matches Intuit's canonical exactly; sandbox confirmed free and non-persistent (resets each login).","QBO Accountant training URL (US /accountants/training-certification/) is live; signup is genuinely free and gives a blank practice company plus free ProAdvisor certification. Note this is a US-region link — non-US learners may be redirected to a localized path (e.g., /ca/accountants/training/).","Xero path '4744-get-started-with-the-basics' confirmed live and published Oct 2025; Xero Central learning is free with a (free) Xero account.","Edspira URL updated from the legacy /user/Edspira format to the canonical handle https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira (old link still redirects). Channel confirmed free, run by Michael McLaughlin PhD CPA.","AccountingCoach: the assigned reading (Adjusting Entries and Bank Reconciliation in-depth EXPLANATIONS) is free to read; cost kept as 'free' but flagged freemium — flashcards, cheat sheets, quick tests and certificates are gated behind paid PRO. Direct free pages: accountingcoach.com/adjusting-entries/explanation and accountingcoach.com/bank-reconciliation/explanation.","OpenStax textbook confirmed free; adjusting process is Ch. 4 (The Adjustment Process) and completing the cycle/trial balance carries into Ch. 4–5 — the note's chapter pointers are accurate.","Coverage gap: no resource focuses specifically on a fixed-asset/depreciation-schedule setup or a payroll-style expense entry inside QBO (both required by the project); learners may need to lean on Hector Garcia's topical videos or AccountingCoach for those. Otherwise the bundle (one anchor video series, two QBO sandboxes, a second platform, two theory references) covers the module well."]},{"id":"3.2","title":"Data & Analytics for Accountants I — Modeling & Power Query","track":"Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","summary":"This module turns spreadsheet competence into professional financial-modeling and data-transformation skill. You learn the modern Excel toolkit (XLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH, nested logic, dynamic arrays, scenario and sensitivity tools), then build an assumption-driven, three-statement-aware model with linked supporting schedules and integrity checks. You also master Power Query to import, clean, and reshape messy accounting exports repeatably, and assemble a PivotTable-based management dashboard with error-trapping and documentation standards. The capstone is automating a recurring reporting task end-to-end so a monthly refresh requires no manual rework.","whyItMatters":"Modern accounting and FP&A roles are increasingly judged on the ability to build trustworthy models and clean, report-on data quickly and repeatably rather than reconcile by hand. A refreshable Power Query pipeline plus a well-structured model is the difference between hours of monthly copy-paste and a one-click close package.","outcomes":["Build robust lookups (XLOOKUP and INDEX/MATCH), nested logical tests, and dynamic-array formulas (FILTER, SORT, UNIQUE, SEQUENCE)","Construct an assumption-driven, three-statement-aware model with linked schedules (revenue, debt, depreciation) and built-in balancing/integrity checks","Use Power Query to import, clean, unpivot, merge, and transform messy accounting data into a refreshable query","Build scenario and sensitivity tools (data tables, scenario switches) and a PivotTable/PivotChart management dashboard","Apply error-trapping (IFERROR, validation flags), consistent formatting, and documentation/assumption standards to make models auditable","Automate a recurring reporting task end-to-end so a new data drop refreshes the report without manual rework"],"prerequisites":["0.3","1.5"],"estimatedHours":"32-42","resources":[{"title":"excelisfun (Mike Girvin) — Power Query and Excel Formula playlists","provider":"Mike Girvin, Highline College (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@excelisfun","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor. Work the 'Power Query (Get & Transform)' playlist (https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLrRPvpgDmw0m3ohSvgwoHvd0KO8QsQdiK) for import/clean/transform/merge/unpivot, plus the formula and dynamic-array playlists for XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and FILTER/SORT/UNIQUE. Every video has downloadable workbooks — use these as your built-in practice files."},{"title":"Power Query documentation (Get & Transform)","provider":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-query/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative reference for the query editor, the M language basics, merge vs append, data-type handling, and refresh behavior. Use it to look up specific transforms and to understand how query steps are recorded and re-applied on refresh."},{"title":"XelPlus (Leila Gharani) — Excel formulas & dynamic arrays","provider":"Leila Gharani (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@LeilaGharani","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Best for intuition on modern lookups and logic: XLOOKUP, nested IF vs IFS, dynamic-array spill behavior, and clean dashboard design. Use targeted videos when an excelisfun topic needs a second, slower explanation."},{"title":"Excel Fundamentals — Formulas for Finance (free playlist)","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLl3-0Xe_motTqWd79PcIMj-GVlafADbiF","type":"playlist","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Finance-oriented framing of Excel formulas and model structure conventions (inputs vs calculations vs outputs, color coding, sensible layout). Pair with CFI's free Financial Modeling Guide eBook (search for: CFI Excel eBook) for model-design standards. Note: CFI's full graded/certified courses are paid; only the YouTube playlist and free guides are needed here."},{"title":"Damodaran Online — spreadsheets, valuation tools and webcasts","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free downloadable three-statement, DCF, and sensitivity spreadsheets. Open and reverse-engineer one to see how a real linked model wires schedules together and where the balancing checks live before you build your own. (Spreadsheets live under the 'Spreadsheets' / 'Data, Tools, Webcasts' sections of the homepage.)"},{"title":"Excel Exposure — free online Excel course with homework","provider":"Ben Currier (excelexposure.com)","url":"https://www.excelexposure.com/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Self-paced lessons with downloadable practice workbooks and homework assignments. Use the lookup, logical-function, PivotTable, and data-cleaning units as graded-style problem sets to drill the mechanics before the capstone. Note: the original lesson set on excelexposure.com remains free; there is also an optional paid 'Excel Essentials' course on Teachable — the free site content is all you need here."}],"project":"Build a \"one-click monthly management pack\" for a small business. (1) Start from two or three messy raw exports (a general-ledger detail CSV, a sales-by-customer export, and a prior-month file) — deliberately include blank rows, merged headers, text-formatted numbers, and inconsistent account names. (2) In Power Query, import and clean each source, standardize account/customer names with a mapping table, unpivot where needed, and merge them into a single refreshable model — no manual edits to the loaded data. (3) Build an assumption-driven mini three-statement-aware model (or a budget-vs-actual model) with at least two linked schedules and a balance/integrity check cell that must read TRUE. (4) Add a scenario switch and a one-variable data-table sensitivity. (5) Build a PivotTable/PivotChart dashboard tab with XLOOKUP-driven summary KPIs, IFERROR trapping, and a documentation/assumptions tab. (6) Prove automation: drop in a fresh \"next month\" export, hit Refresh All, and confirm the entire pack updates with zero manual rework. Deliver the workbook plus a short README of assumptions and refresh instructions.","milestoneCheck":"You can now hand someone a folder of messy monthly exports and produce a refreshable, documented reporting pack without copy-paste. Self-test: (a) given a new data drop, your report updates correctly with a single Refresh All; (b) you can rebuild a lookup three ways (XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, and a Power Query merge) and explain when each is appropriate; (c) your model has a balance/integrity check that visibly breaks when an input is wrong and that you can trace and fix; (d) you can flip a scenario switch and read a sensitivity table and explain the output; and (e) a reviewer can open your workbook and understand the assumptions, inputs, and flow from your documentation alone.","flags":["All six resources verified live, free, and on-topic (June 2026); no resources dropped.","Verified the excelisfun 'Power Query (Get & Transform)' playlist URL resolves and is titled correctly; channel confirmed as Mike Girvin (Microsoft Excel MVP, Highline College).","Verified the CFI 'Excel Fundamentals — Formulas for Finance' free YouTube playlist URL resolves; clarified the note that CFI's full certified courses are paid while this playlist and free guides are not.","Excel Exposure: updated URL to canonical https://www.excelexposure.com/ (bare-domain fetch did not resolve, www does). Site is active; original lessons remain free, but an optional paid 'Excel Essentials' course now exists on Teachable — flagged so 'free' stays accurate for the assigned content.","XelPlus and Leila Gharani channel handle (@LeilaGharani) and Damodaran Online (NYU Stern) confirmed reputable and free; Damodaran homepage uses a frameset, so spreadsheets are reached via the in-page navigation sections rather than a direct deep link.","Coverage gap: resources are strong on Excel/Power Query mechanics and model structure but light on accounting-specific data-quality controls (e.g., trial-balance reconciliation logic, GL-to-subledger tie-outs). Consider adding a short accounting-control reading so learners connect the refreshable pipeline to audit/close-process integrity, not just spreadsheet hygiene.","Coverage note: no resource here covers VBA/Office Scripts; the 'automation' outcome is satisfied via Power Query Refresh All only, which is the intended (no-code) scope — confirm that matches the module's intent."]},{"id":"3.3","title":"Data & Analytics for Accountants II — SQL, Power BI & Python","track":"Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","summary":"This module takes the accountant from spreadsheet-level data work into the three tools that dominate modern finance analytics: SQL for pulling and joining transactional data straight from a database, Power BI for building governed, self-serve dashboards on top of a clean data model, and Python/pandas for cleaning, reconciling, and analyzing ledger files too large for Excel. It then layers analytical technique on top — trend and outlier analysis, Benford-style digit tests, and audit-style sampling — so the learner can hunt for anomalies rather than just report totals. It closes with a judgment lesson: where AI/LLM and low-code automation responsibly fit the close and review, and where a human control must stay in the loop.","whyItMatters":"Finance and audit are shifting from sampling and manual tick-and-tie to querying full transaction populations; accountants fluent in SQL, Power BI, and pandas self-serve answers instead of waiting on IT. Sound judgment about where AI and low-code automation can and cannot replace a control is now a core professional skill.","outcomes":["Write SQL (SELECT, WHERE, JOIN, GROUP BY, aggregates, basic window functions) to extract and summarize accounting data from a transactions database","Build an interactive Power BI report with a clean star-schema data model, relationships, and DAX measures that deliver self-serve KPIs","Use Python/pandas to import, clean, reconcile, and aggregate large ledger and sub-ledger files that exceed Excel's practical limits","Apply trend, outlier, and Benford-style digit tests plus audit-style sampling to surface anomalies in a transaction population","Evaluate where AI/LLM and low-code automation responsibly fit the close and review process — and where a human control or sign-off must remain"],"prerequisites":["3.2"],"estimatedHours":"40-50","resources":[{"title":"Mode / ThoughtSpot SQL Tutorial (Basic, Intermediate, Advanced)","provider":"ThoughtSpot (formerly Mode Analytics)","url":"https://www.thoughtspot.com/sql-tutorial","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary SQL anchor and practice in one: an in-browser editor runs real queries against sample data — no install. Work Basic (SELECT→ORDER BY), then Intermediate (aggregates, GROUP BY/HAVING, JOINs), then Advanced (subqueries, window functions). The 'SQL Analytics Training' section gives analyst-style business questions to practice translating a question into a query. (Mode was acquired by ThoughtSpot; the old mode.com/sql-tutorial URL now redirects here — same free interactive content.)"},{"title":"Databases: Relational Databases and SQL (Jennifer Widom)","provider":"Stanford Online (edX, free audit track)","url":"https://www.edx.org/learn/relational-databases/stanford-university-databases-relational-databases-and-sql","type":"mooc","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"supplement","notes":"Use to firm up the why behind SQL — relational model, joins, NULL handling, subqueries — when Mode's practical drills leave gaps. Audit track is free (a paid verified certificate is optional); the lecture videos are also on YouTube. Search for: 'Stanford Databases SQL Jennifer Widom'. Treat as reference, not a cover-to-cover requirement."},{"title":"Power BI learning paths: Get started, Prepare data, Model data, Visualize","provider":"Microsoft Learn","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/powerplatform/power-bi","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary Power BI anchor, free and official. Do the paths in order: Get started → Prepare/transform data with Power Query (clean/shape) → Model data (relationships, star schema, DAX measures) → Build visuals and reports. Focus DAX effort on measures (SUM, CALCULATE, time-intelligence) since those drive finance KPIs. Power BI Desktop is a free Windows download."},{"title":"Python for Data Analysis, 3rd Edition (Open Access)","provider":"Wes McKinney (pandas creator)","url":"https://wesmckinney.com/book/","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary Python/pandas anchor — full text free online, updated for pandas 2.0. For this module read Ch. 5 (Series/DataFrame), Ch. 6 (reading CSV/Excel files), Ch. 7 (cleaning & missing data), Ch. 8 (merge/join/reshape — the reconciliation chapter), and Ch. 10 (groupby aggregation). Companion notebooks at github.com/wesm/pydata-book."},{"title":"Kaggle Learn: Intro to SQL & Pandas micro-courses","provider":"Kaggle","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/learn","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Short hands-on exercises with auto-graded coding challenges (free Kaggle account required). Use 'Intro to SQL' to reinforce querying and 'Pandas' to drill DataFrame manipulation, filtering, grouping, and combining — the exact skills used to reconcile ledger files. A few hours each; free certificate on completion."},{"title":"Corey Schafer — Pandas Tutorial Playlist","provider":"Corey Schafer (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL-osiE80TeTsWmV9i9c58mdDCSskIFdDS","type":"playlist","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Clear, widely-trusted video walkthroughs for pandas intuition — loading data, filtering, groupby/aggregate, handling missing values, merging. Watch the install/setup, filtering, and groupby episodes alongside McKinney's chapters when a concept doesn't click on the page. Code snippets on the CoreyMSchafer GitHub."},{"title":"Alex The Analyst — Power BI & SQL for Data Analysts","provider":"Alex The Analyst (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AlexTheAnalyst","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Video intuition for the BI/SQL workflow end-to-end: building a Power BI dashboard from raw data, modeling, and DAX, plus SQL-for-analysts walkthroughs. Use the Power BI mini-series (part of the free Data Analyst Bootcamp) to see a full report built start to finish before attempting the project. Search for: 'Alex The Analyst Power BI full course'."}],"project":"Build a 'Close & Anomaly Review' analytics pipeline over a synthetic general-ledger dataset (e.g., a year of journal entries with account, date, amount, user, and entity — generate one or use a public sample GL/AdventureWorks transactions set). Step 1 (SQL): load the data into a free database (SQLite/DuckDB or Kaggle BigQuery) and write queries that produce a trial balance, top vendors/accounts by spend, and month-over-month movement by account. Step 2 (Python/pandas): import the same file, reconcile the sub-ledger total to the GL control account, flag entries posted on weekends/holidays or just under approval thresholds, and run a Benford's Law first-digit test on transaction amounts, charting expected vs. actual. Step 3 (Power BI): build a star-schema model (fact = journal lines, dims = account/date/entity) with DAX measures for net movement and YoY%, and a one-page interactive dashboard with a KPI header, trend chart, and a drill-through anomaly list. Step 4 (judgment, 1 page): document which review steps you would let an LLM/low-code bot automate (e.g., drafting the anomaly narrative, categorizing free-text memos) and which must keep a human sign-off (approving journal entries, concluding on a flagged item), with your reasoning.","milestoneCheck":"You can now: (1) take an unfamiliar transactions database and write SQL that joins and aggregates it into a trial balance or spend summary without exporting to Excel; (2) build a Power BI report from raw data — clean in Power Query, model as a star schema, write DAX measures, and ship an interactive dashboard a non-analyst can self-serve; (3) use pandas to reconcile two ledger files and output a list of exceptions; (4) run and correctly interpret a Benford first-digit test plus an outlier/trend scan to decide which items deserve follow-up; and (5) state, for a specific close task, where AI/automation belongs and where a human control cannot be removed. Self-test: given a raw GL extract you've never seen, produce a trial balance, a reconciliation exception list, and a one-page anomaly dashboard in a single working session, and defend why each flagged item is or isn't a real issue.","flags":["Mode SQL Tutorial: the canonical mode.com/sql-tutorial URL now 301-redirects to thoughtspot.com/sql-tutorial (Mode was acquired by ThoughtSpot). Updated URL and provider; the interactive in-browser tutorial remains free. Individual mode.com/sql-tutorial/... lesson sub-pages still load, but linking the live canonical page is safer.","Stanford Databases: replaced the generic edX topic URL (edx.org/learn/relational-databases) with the canonical course page. Confirmed free audit track; a verified certificate is the only paid option.","Alex The Analyst: updated channel URL from the legacy /c/AlexTheAnalyst to the canonical @AlexTheAnalyst handle (both resolve). Channel is free; it has no fixed playlist ID for the Power BI series, so a search hint is retained.","Python for Data Analysis (wesmckinney.com/book/) returned HTTP 403 to the automated fetcher (bot block), but the 3rd edition is well-established as a free open-access HTML book — not a paywall. Confirmed via prior knowledge and the book's known open-access status; low residual uncertainty.","Kaggle Learn SQL/Pandas micro-courses are free but require a (free) Kaggle account login to run exercises — noted in the resource.","Coverage note: resources are strong on SQL, Power BI, and pandas mechanics, but none directly teach Benford's Law / audit sampling theory or the AI-in-the-close judgment outcome — the learner meets those only through the project itself. Consider adding a short free reference on Benford's Law for fraud/audit and on AICPA/PCAOB guidance for AI in the audit to fully support outcomes 4 and 5.","All resource cost labels verified accurate (free / free-to-audit); no paywalls or dead links found, none dropped."]},{"id":"3.4","title":"Professional Communication & Staff-Accountant Workflow","track":"Track 3 — Tools, Data & Practice","summary":"This module bridges technical accounting knowledge and the day-to-day reality of a staff accountant: documenting work and communicating it clearly. Learners practice the genres real firms require — workpaper memos, management/audit letters, and PBC lists — alongside the mechanics of documentation standards (AS 1215), ticking and tying, cross-referencing, and reconciliations that drive the month-end close. It also rehearses the CPA-exam Written Communication Task format and adds a short career layer (accounting resume, behavioral interviewing, and what a realistic first 90 days looks like).","whyItMatters":"Written communication is graded on organization, development, and expression, while documentation and tie-out skills are exactly what distinguishes a hireable, retainable staff accountant — making this module a direct lever on first-job employability. (Note: the discrete CPA-exam Written Communication Task was retired in January 2024; clear professional writing remains valued on the job and is still assessed indirectly across exam simulations.)","outcomes":["Write a workpaper memo (purpose, procedures, results, conclusion) and a management/audit-style letter in correct professional format, judged on organization, development, and expression.","Apply audit-documentation standards from PCAOB AS 1215: prepare documentation detailed enough for an experienced reviewer with no prior connection to understand the work, and label and cross-reference workpapers.","Build and execute a tie-out: foot and cross-foot a schedule, agree balances to the general ledger and trial balance, trace items to source documents, and apply a consistent tickmark legend.","Draft a PBC (prepared-by-client) request list and sequence the recurring tasks of a real staff-accountant month-end close (accruals, prepaids, reconciliations, flux review).","Plan and write a CPA-exam-style Written Communication Task to format under time pressure, avoiding bullets/abbreviations and using a clear memo or letter structure.","Produce career-ready artifacts: an accounting-focused resume, STAR-format answers to behavioral interview questions, and a realistic first-90-days plan."],"prerequisites":["1.2"],"estimatedHours":"25","resources":[{"title":"Business Communication for Success (open textbook)","provider":"University of Minnesota Libraries Publishing / Open Textbook Library","type":"open textbook","cost":"Free (CC-licensed)","role":"Primary anchor — communication half","url":"https://open.lib.umn.edu/businesscommunication/","notes":"Read Ch. 4 (effective business writing), Ch. 9 (business writing in action: memos, emails, letters, reports) for memo/letter structure and audience, and Ch. 16 (interviewing, resumes) for the career layer. Conceptual backbone for every written deliverable. Verified CC BY-NC-SA 4.0; the site bot-blocks automated fetchers (HTTP 403) but pages and the full PDF download are live — if the UMN host is ever retired, the same text is mirrored free on LibreTexts and Saylor Academy."},{"title":"Professional & Technical Writing: Memos and Basic Business Letters","provider":"Purdue OWL (Online Writing Lab)","type":"reference + samples","cost":"Free","role":"Supplement — format templates","url":"https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/subject_specific_writing/professional_technical_writing/index.html","notes":"Use the Memos section (intro, Parts of a Memo, Sample Memo) and Basic Business Letters (Writing the Basic Business Letter + Sample Letters) as format templates when drafting the workpaper memo and management/audit letter. Quick mechanics reference, not a course. Verified live and free."},{"title":"AS 1215: Audit Documentation","provider":"PCAOB (Public Company Accounting Oversight Board)","type":"professional standard","cost":"Free","role":"Primary anchor — documentation standard","url":"https://pcaobus.org/oversight/standards/auditing-standards/details/AS1215","notes":"Read the paragraphs on the 'experienced auditor' understandability requirement and on documenting procedures, evidence, and conclusions. This defines the bar your workpaper memo and tie-out documentation must meet; pair conceptually with AU-C 230 for the non-issuer/private-company view. Verified: full standard is freely readable (amendments effective Dec 15, 2026 noted on the page)."},{"title":"CPA Exam Sample Tests (exam-format familiarization)","provider":"AICPA & CIMA","type":"practice / official simulator","cost":"Free","role":"Practice source — CPA exam format (see flag: Written Communication Task retired Jan 2024)","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/resources/article/get-familiar-with-the-cpa-exam-by-practicing-with-our-sample-tests","notes":"Verified free and official. IMPORTANT: the standalone Written Communication Task was removed from the CPA Exam in January 2024 (BEC retired under CPA Evolution); the current sample test covers AUD/FAR/REG/BAR/ISC/TCP and has NO WCT testlet. Use it to rehearse exam pacing and the task-based-simulation interface. For the module's timed memo/letter exercise (project item 4), treat 'WCT' as a self-imposed clear-writing-under-time drill graded on organization, development, and expression — not as a section of the live exam — and source any historical WCT prompts from archived prep materials."},{"title":"Edspira — Auditing & Accounting Cycle videos","provider":"Edspira (YouTube)","type":"video series","cost":"Free","role":"Video for intuition","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","notes":"Free tutorials by Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA. Watch videos on audit documentation/working papers, the accounting cycle, adjusting entries, and bank reconciliation. Search for: 'Edspira audit working papers' and 'Edspira adjusting entries'. Farhat Lectures on YouTube is an equally good free alternative for audit-documentation topics. URL updated to the canonical channel handle."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Adjusting Entries & Bank Reconciliation","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"explainer + practice","cost":"Free (core explanations)","role":"Supplement — close mechanics refresher","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","notes":"Use the Adjusting Entries (topic 8) and Bank Reconciliation (topic 15) topics to solidify accruals/prepaids and the reconciliation you will tie out in the project. Free explanations, Q&A, and quick-test items reinforce the entries; deeper video/flashcard content sits behind the optional one-time PRO upgrade. Verified."},{"title":"Month-End Close Process & Checklist","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI)","type":"article / workflow guide","cost":"Free (free articles)","role":"Supplement — month-end workflow","url":"https://corporatefinanceinstitute.com/resources/","notes":"Use the free resources library to map the real staff-accountant workflow and build your PBC list and close checklist. Search for: 'CFI month-end close process'. Read the close-steps and reconciliation overviews; ignore paid course/certification upsells. Verified live with free articles and templates."},{"title":"ThisWayToCPA — Career & Job-Search Resources","provider":"AICPA (ThisWayToCPA)","type":"career resource hub","cost":"Free","role":"Career layer — resume & interview","url":"https://www.thiswaytocpa.com/","notes":"Use the Work Experience sections (Find Your First Job, Resumes & Interviewing, Plan Your Career) to draft your accounting resume and prep behavioral (STAR) answers. Pair with Business Communication for Success Ch. 16. Indeed Career Guide ('accounting resume examples') is a free supplement for resume bullet phrasing. Verified as an official, free AICPA resource."}],"project":"Build a \"Month-End Close Packet\" for a fictional small company. (1) Given a trial balance and a short PBC (prepared-by-client) list you draft yourself, prepare 3-4 supporting workpapers in a spreadsheet: a bank reconciliation, an accrual/prepaid rollforward, and a revenue or AR tie-out. Add a tickmark legend and apply tickmarks (e.g., footed, agreed to GL, traced to bank statement), cross-reference each workpaper to the lead sheet, and tie every schedule back to the trial balance. (2) Write a one-page workpaper memo documenting the purpose, procedures performed, results, and conclusion for one account — written so an \"experienced reviewer with no prior connection\" could follow it (AS 1215 standard). (3) Write a short management/audit-style letter to the controller flagging one issue you found, in proper business-letter format. (4) Complete one AICPA sample-test Written Communication Task under a 25-minute timer. (5) Career capstone: draft a one-page accounting resume bullet set, answer three behavioral interview questions in writing (STAR format), and write a half-page \"my first 90 days as a staff accountant\" plan.","milestoneCheck":"You can take a trial balance plus a PBC list and independently produce a clean, cross-referenced workpaper set that ties to the TB with a coherent tickmark legend, accompanied by a memo a reviewer could follow without asking questions; you can complete an AICPA Written Communication Task within the time limit using proper structure; and you can articulate, in writing, your resume value and a credible first-90-days plan. Mastery is reaching the point where your documentation and memo would survive a senior's review with only minor notes.","flags":["MAJOR — AICPA CPA Exam Sample Test: verified live and free, but the discrete Written Communication Task (WCT) was ELIMINATED from the CPA Exam in January 2024 when the BEC section was retired under CPA Evolution. The current sample test (AUD/FAR/REG core + BAR/ISC/TCP disciplines) contains NO written-communication essay testlet. The resource is KEPT for exam-format familiarization, but its original 'written communication practice' role no longer holds, and project item (4) ('Complete one AICPA sample-test Written Communication Task') plus any claim that written communication is 'directly tested on the CPA exam' are outdated. Sourced WCT practice must now come from archived/historical materials; the WCT skill itself (clear memo/letter writing under time pressure) is still a valid learning goal, just not on the live exam.","CHANGED — Edspira URL updated from https://www.youtube.com/c/Edspira to the canonical handle https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira. Channel verified: free business/accounting tutorials by Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA; covers audit working papers, accounting cycle, adjusting entries, bank reconciliation. Farhat Lectures remains a valid free alternative.","VERIFY-CAVEAT — Business Communication for Success (open.lib.umn.edu): the site returns HTTP 403 to automated fetchers (bot block, NOT removal). Chapter pages and the full PDF download (open.lib.umn.edu/businesscommunication/open/download?type=pdf) remain live and indexed; CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 license and UMN Libraries Publishing attribution confirmed. Free-mirror fallbacks exist on LibreTexts and Saylor Academy should the UMN host ever be retired. Residual uncertainty: page body could not be rendered directly via automated fetch.","VERIFIED — Purdue OWL (memos/business letters), PCAOB AS 1215 (full standard freely readable; amendments effective Dec 15, 2026 noted), AccountingCoach (Adjusting Entries topic 8 / Bank Reconciliation topic 15; core explanations + quizzes free, PRO tier paid — cost label is accurate), CFI resources hub (free month-end-close articles/templates), and ThisWayToCPA (AICPA; free resume/interviewing/early-career sections) all confirmed live, free, reputable, and on-topic. No changes."]}]},{"name":"Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","modules":[{"id":"4.1","title":"Income Taxation Fundamentals (Jurisdiction-Specific)","track":"Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","summary":"This module builds working fluency in how an income tax system is structured and how it diverges from the financial accounting you learned earlier. You will compute individual income tax (including capital gains and property transactions), distinguish entity-level taxation of C corporations from pass-through taxation of S corporations and partnerships, and trace how consumption taxes (VAT/GST/sales tax) flow through the books via input/output mechanics. The anchor materials are US-based for concreteness, but the module is framed so the transferable concepts — book-tax differences, marginal vs. effective rates, pass-through vs. entity tax, and credit-method consumption tax — survive a swap to your own country's code.","whyItMatters":"Tax is where accounting income meets the law and cash leaves the business; accountants who cannot reconcile book to taxable income or explain how entity choice changes the tax bill are a liability to clients and employers.","outcomes":["Explain the structure of an income tax system (gross income, deductions, exemptions, credits, marginal vs. effective rates) and reconcile accounting income to taxable income via permanent and temporary book-tax differences","Compute individual income tax for common scenarios, including the treatment of capital gains/losses and basis in property transactions, in a chosen jurisdiction","Compute and contrast entity taxation across C corporations (entity-level tax plus shareholder-level tax on distributions), S corporations, and partnerships (pass-through), and identify each entity's filing obligations","Explain consumption taxes (VAT/GST/sales tax), the input/output credit mechanics, and how output tax payable and recoverable input tax are recorded and settled in the books","Adapt the framework to your own country's tax code, mapping local rules onto the universal concepts of base, rate, timing, and entity classification"],"prerequisites":["1.5"],"estimatedHours":"40-52","resources":[{"title":"Basic Income Tax (Kratzke) — eLangdell Open Casebook","provider":"CALI eLangdell Press / Open Textbook Library","url":"https://open.umn.edu/opentextbooks/textbooks/323","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified free CC BY-NC-SA PDF/eBook/Word by William P. Kratzke (Univ. of Memphis); also at kratzketax.lawbooks.cali.org. Use as the spine for individual taxation: chapters on gross income, the structure of the tax (rates, deductions, exemptions), capital gains and losses, and basis/realization in property transactions. Skim litigation/case detail; focus on rules, worked examples, and the embedded CALI drills. Note: NonCommercial license restricts redistribution for paid use."},{"title":"Corporate Tax (Kratzke) — eLangdell Open Casebook","provider":"CALI eLangdell Press","url":"https://www.cali.org/books/corporate-income-tax","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified free CC-licensed companion casebook by Kratzke for the entity-taxation outcome. Use the early chapters on the corporate income tax, the corporate vs. shareholder two-level tax, and distributions to ground C-corp mechanics; pair with the IRS pages below for S-corp and partnership pass-through treatment. If the cali.org page is briefly unavailable, the DRM-free PDF is also hosted at elangdell.cali.org."},{"title":"Taxation YouTube playlists (Individual + Business Entities)","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/c/Edspira/playlists","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"For intuition before/after reading. Watch 'Introduction to Income Tax for Individuals,' marginal vs. effective rate, deductions vs. credits, FICA, and the 'Taxation of Business Entities' playlist (C-corp, S-corp, partnership, Section 351). Search the channel for any specific topic you find dense in Kratzke. (If the /c/ path changes, the channel is also at youtube.com/@Edspira.)"},{"title":"Link & Learn Taxes (VITA/TCE e-learning + practice returns)","provider":"IRS","url":"https://apps.irs.gov/app/vita/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Verified free self-paced certification course that walks you through preparing real individual returns with practice scenarios and answer keys. This is your primary problem-set/hands-on source for individual tax — complete the Basic and Advanced scenarios and check your computed liability."},{"title":"Publication 17, Your Federal Income Tax + Forms & Instructions","provider":"IRS","url":"https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative plain-language reference for individuals plus the actual forms (Form 1040 and Schedules C/D/E, Form 1120 for C-corps, 1120-S for S-corps, 1065 + Schedule K-1 for partnerships). Use to see filing obligations and to sanity-check the textbook's rules against current numbers. (Pub 17 direct page: irs.gov/publications/p17.)"},{"title":"Tax Basics / TaxEDU explainers (incl. VAT, book vs. taxable income)","provider":"Tax Foundation","url":"https://taxfoundation.org/taxedu/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified free, nonpartisan explainers for conceptual glue: marginal vs. effective rates, deductions vs. credits, what a VAT is and how the credit-invoice method works, and why book income differs from taxable income. Good for the consumption-tax and book-tax-difference outcomes."},{"title":"ZATCA — VAT guidelines and taxpayer education (your-jurisdiction VAT/GST)","provider":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (Saudi Arabia)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/VAT/Pages/default.aspx","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"URL corrected — the old /RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/VAT.aspx now 404s; this verified VAT landing page works. Use to instantiate the 'adapt to your country' outcome and consumption-tax mechanics in your actual jurisdiction: input vs. output tax, registration thresholds, the VAT return, and the Implementing Regulations. KSA standard VAT rate is 15% (the landing page links to detailed guidelines/PDF rather than stating the rate inline). If outside KSA, substitute your national tax authority's VAT/GST guide and corporate income tax pages. (If the path shifts again, search 'ZATCA VAT general guideline'.)"}],"project":"Build a two-part 'Tax Reconciliation & Entity Choice' workbook (see project field).","milestoneCheck":"You can now, without notes: (1) walk a transaction from gross income to final tax owed for an individual, correctly handling a capital gain with basis and distinguishing a deduction from a credit and marginal from effective rate; (2) explain, with numbers, why the same profit is taxed differently under a C corp vs. an S corp vs. a partnership, and name the return each files; (3) reconcile accounting income to taxable income and classify differences as permanent or temporary; and (4) record a VAT/GST sale and purchase with correct input/output entries and compute the net remittance. Self-test: complete an IRS Link & Learn Advanced scenario and a multi-entity comparison and have your computed tax match the answer key within rounding — and then articulate which specific rules would change if you redid the whole exercise under your own country's code.","flags":["Verified all 7 resources exist, are free, and are on-topic and reputable (CALI/eLangdell, IRS, Tax Foundation, ZATCA, Edspira).","FIXED URL: ZATCA VAT link was a dead 404 (/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/VAT.aspx); replaced with the verified working canonical page https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/VAT/Pages/default.aspx. The new landing page does not state the 15% rate inline (it links out to guidelines/Implementing Regulations); KSA standard rate is 15% — added that note.","Corporate Tax (CALI) page returned a transient HTTP 500 during one fetch but is confirmed via search to be a live, free, CC-licensed eLangdell casebook by Kratzke; added the elangdell.cali.org PDF mirror as a fallback in notes.","Basic Income Tax license is CC BY-NC-SA (NonCommercial) — fine for learners but flagged because it constrains paid redistribution if this curriculum is ever sold.","Edspira /c/Edspira/playlists path verified; added @Edspira fallback in case YouTube migrates the legacy /c/ URL.","Anchor materials are US-federal; the 'adapt to your jurisdiction' outcome leans heavily on the learner doing their own mapping. Only the consumption-tax side has a non-US (KSA/ZATCA) anchor — there is no free non-US anchor for the individual/entity income-tax outcomes.","Coverage gap: deferred-tax/ASC 740 mechanics (the deeper accounting of temporary book-tax differences, deferred tax assets/liabilities) are only lightly touched by the Tax Foundation explainer; outcome 1's reconciliation depth may need a supplemental free source (e.g., an intermediate-accounting OER chapter on income taxes)."]},{"id":"4.2","title":"Business Law for Accountants (Jurisdiction-Specific)","track":"Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","summary":"This module builds a working command of the business law that accountants encounter in practice and on professional exams: contract formation, performance, breach and remedies; agency and the sale of goods under the UCC; the formation, liability, and governance trade-offs of different business entity types; debtor-creditor relationships, secured transactions, bankruptcy, and negotiable instruments; and the securities, anti-fraud, and professional-liability rules that bear directly on accountants and auditors. The treatment is common-law / US-oriented (UCC, federal securities law), and the module closes by having you map the equivalent regulatory bodies and rules in your own jurisdiction. The goal is legal literacy for accountants — enough to spot issues, read a contract or security agreement intelligently, and know when to involve counsel — not to make you a lawyer.","whyItMatters":"Accountants constantly act on legal facts — whether a contract is enforceable, who is liable in an LLC vs. a partnership, whether a creditor is perfected, when auditor liability attaches — and getting them wrong creates restatements, fraud exposure, and malpractice claims. It is also a heavily tested domain on the CPA REG exam, so mastering it pays off twice.","outcomes":["Explain contract formation, performance, breach, and remedies, and apply agency and UCC Article 2 sale-of-goods rules at a working level","Compare the major business entity types (sole proprietorship, partnership, LLC, corporation) on formation, liability, governance, and tax/exit consequences","Describe debtor-creditor relationships, the attachment and perfection of security interests under UCC Article 9, the basics of bankruptcy, and negotiable instruments","Summarize federal securities regulation (1933/1934 Acts), anti-fraud provisions, and the bases of accountants' professional and legal liability","Identify the regulatory bodies and statutes governing accountants and financial reporting in your own jurisdiction, mapping them to the common-law/US framework studied here"],"prerequisites":["0.2"],"estimatedHours":"26-36","resources":[{"title":"Business Law I Essentials","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/business-law-i-essentials","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor. Read sequentially: Ch. 6–8 (contracts: formation, performance, breach, remedies), Ch. 5 (criminal/civil & fraud context), Ch. 9 (agency), Ch. 12–13 (corporations and other business entities), and Ch. 14 (securities & related regulation). Do the end-of-chapter questions as you go. Use the LibreTexts mirror (biz.libretexts.org) if openstax.org is slow."},{"title":"BUS205: Business Law","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=89","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Full self-paced US course in 10 units (~42 hours). Use it as the structured backbone alongside OpenStax — especially the units on contracts, sales/UCC, negotiable instruments, secured transactions/creditors' rights, and business organizations. Work the unit assessments; the optional proctored final exam is the mastery checkpoint if you want a free certificate / Direct Credit."},{"title":"Business Law (CPA/CMA Exam) Playlist","provider":"Farhat Lectures (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxP0KZzCGFYPpcdJxq9h_7EZ8zm7AIIP2","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Watch for exam-focused intuition on contracts, agency, sales, secured transactions, negotiable instruments, business entities, and accountant liability. Framed around the CPA REG section, so it's the best bridge between general business-law theory and how accountants are actually tested. Search the channel for any specific topic you find thin in the textbook."},{"title":"Secured Transactions / Basics of Contract Law / Business Entities video courses","provider":"LawShelf Educational Media","url":"https://www.lawshelf.com/digitalbadges","type":"course","cost":"freemium","role":"supplement","notes":"Free to watch (you only pay if you want the optional proctored credit exam). Use the 'Basics of Contract Law', 'Secured Transactions' (UCC Article 9), 'Negotiable Instruments', and business-organizations courses for clearer, example-driven coverage of the debtor-creditor and commercial-paper topics OpenStax treats briefly. LawShelf is a project of National Paralegal College; courses are NCCRS-evaluated."},{"title":"Wex Legal Dictionary & Encyclopedia (UCC, securities, agency, bankruptcy)","provider":"Cornell Law School Legal Information Institute (LII)","url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative free reference for looking up doctrine and the actual statute text — e.g., UCC Article 2 (sales), Article 3 (negotiable instruments), Article 9 (secured transactions), Securities Act of 1933/Securities Exchange Act of 1934, and bankruptcy. Use it to verify any rule before you rely on it."},{"title":"Uniform CPA Examination Blueprints — REG (Regulation) section","provider":"AICPA","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/resources/download/learn-what-is-tested-on-the-cpa-exam","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free PDF blueprint (current 'CPA Exam Blueprints' covers all sections including REG) plus AICPA's sample/practice test. Use the Business Law portion of the REG blueprint as a self-audit checklist of every topic you should be able to answer, and work the released sample questions to practice exam-style application. Note: US-specific — if you sit a non-US qualification, substitute your jurisdiction's syllabus."}],"project":"Build a one-page 'Legal Issue-Spotter & Entity Decision Memo' for a fictional small company. Part A: draft a short memo recommending a business entity (LLC vs. S-corp vs. general partnership) for a startup, comparing formation steps, owner liability, governance, and exit/tax consequences, with a clear recommendation and the trade-offs you rejected. Part B: take a simple sample sales/supply contract (or write a 1-page one) and annotate it — identify offer/acceptance/consideration, a breach scenario and the remedy available, whether it falls under UCC Article 2, and one clause you'd renegotiate. Part C: write a half-page 'creditor & securities watch' noting how a lender would perfect a security interest in the company's equipment under UCC Article 9, and one federal anti-fraud/securities rule the company must respect if it later raises outside capital. Part D (jurisdiction map): in a short table, list the regulator(s) and statute(s) that would govern each of A–C in your own jurisdiction, flagging where they diverge from the US/common-law model.","milestoneCheck":"You can now read a contract or security agreement and correctly identify the formation elements, whether the UCC applies, the likely remedy for a given breach, and who bears liability — and you can recommend a business entity with the liability/governance/tax trade-offs articulated. Self-test: without notes, (1) list the elements of an enforceable contract and three remedies for breach; (2) explain attachment vs. perfection of a security interest and why perfection matters in bankruptcy; (3) distinguish liability exposure across sole proprietorship, GP, LLC, and corporation; (4) state the core purpose of the 1933 vs. 1934 Securities Acts and one basis on which an accountant can be held liable; and (5) name the bodies that regulate accountants and securities in your jurisdiction. If you can score well on the AICPA REG sample questions for the business-law topics and complete the project memo without major gaps, you've mastered the module.","flags":["All 6 resources were verified to exist, be reputable, on-topic, and free/free-to-audit as labeled; none were dropped.","FIXED URL — AICPA blueprint: the original link (aicpa-cima.com/resources/download/cpa-exam-blueprints) returned HTTP 404. Replaced with the live canonical download page aicpa-cima.com/resources/download/learn-what-is-tested-on-the-cpa-exam, which serves the current free 'CPA Exam Blueprints' PDF (all sections incl. REG). Note the file is now a single combined blueprint, not a REG-only PDF.","VERIFIED — OpenStax 'Business Law I Essentials' exists, is fully free (web/PDF, CC BY-NC-SA), 14 chapters, with end-of-chapter questions; LibreTexts mirror confirmed live.","VERIFIED — Saylor BUS205 is the correct course at id=89, free, 10 units (~42 hrs), optional free proctored exam/Direct Credit; added these details to notes.","VERIFIED — Farhat Lectures playlist (list ID PLxP0KZzCGFYPpcdJxq9h_7EZ8zm7AIIP2) is the channel's 'Business Law' playlist, free on YouTube, CPA/CMA-framed.","VERIFIED — LawShelf digitalbadges page confirms courses are free to watch with pay-only-for-proctored-exam model (cost 'freemium' is accurate); could not individually confirm a distinct 'Business Entities' course title but Contract Law, Secured Transactions, and Negotiable Instruments courses are confirmed live.","VERIFIED — Cornell LII Wex is live and free.","COVERAGE NOTE: The bundle is strongly US/common-law (UCC, 1933/34 Acts, CPA REG). Outcome 5 and Project Part D require the learner to source their own jurisdiction's materials — no non-US anchor resource is provided, which is an intentional but real gap for non-US users.","MINOR: OpenStax notes cite 'Ch. 5 (criminal/civil & fraud context)' and 'Ch. 14 (securities)'; chapter-to-topic mapping was not exhaustively verified against the live TOC, so confirm exact chapter numbers when building reading assignments."]},{"id":"4.3","title":"Corporate Finance Essentials","track":"Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","summary":"This module takes you from accounting numbers to value-based decision-making. You learn the time value of money and apply it to capital budgeting (NPV, IRR, payback, profitability index) with sensitivity/scenario analysis, then estimate a firm's cost of capital (WACC) and reason about capital structure and dividend policy. It rounds out with working-capital management (cash, receivables, inventory, short-term financing) and a first pass at business valuation using discounted cash flow and comparable companies, always tying financing and investing choices back to the financial statements and underlying value drivers.","whyItMatters":"Accountants who understand corporate finance can move beyond recording transactions to advising on which projects to fund, how to finance them, and what a business is worth — the skills that turn a bookkeeper into a finance business partner.","outcomes":["Apply time value of money to capital budgeting: compute and rank projects by NPV, IRR, payback, and profitability index, and stress-test results with sensitivity and scenario analysis","Estimate a company's weighted-average cost of capital (WACC), including cost of equity via CAPM and after-tax cost of debt, and explain capital-structure trade-offs and dividend-policy basics","Manage working capital — cash, accounts receivable, inventory, and short-term financing — using metrics like the cash conversion cycle","Build a basic discounted-cash-flow valuation and cross-check it with a comparable-company (multiples) analysis","Connect financing and investing decisions back to the financial statements and the firm's underlying value drivers"],"prerequisites":["2.2"],"estimatedHours":"30-40","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Finance","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-finance","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The free open-textbook anchor (CC BY; read free online or download PDF). Core chapters for this module: time value of money, capital budgeting (NPV, IRR, payback, PI), cost of capital (WACC, CAPM), valuation and risk/return, and working capital. Use the live table of contents to confirm exact chapter numbers. Read alongside the videos; do the end-of-chapter problems."},{"title":"Corporate Finance Online Class (lecture notes, webcasts & problem sets)","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/New_Home_Page/corpfin.html","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Full free corporate-finance course from a leading valuation authority: YouTube/webcast session videos, downloadable lecture-note PDFs, and exams/problem sets with solutions. Use the investment-decision (hurdle rate/WACC, NPV/IRR), financing, and dividend-policy sessions. Pair with his separate Valuation class (linked from his homepage) for the DCF/comps work."},{"title":"Finance and capital markets","provider":"Khan Academy","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/economics-finance-domain/core-finance","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Use for intuition before the textbook math: the 'Present value', 'Internal rate of return / NPV', 'Stocks and bonds', and 'Cost of capital / WACC' units. Short videos that build conceptual understanding."},{"title":"Principles of Finance (BUS202)","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=63","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"A structured, self-paced free course (~33 hours) covering TVM, financial statements, capital budgeting, cost of capital, capital structure, ratio analysis, and bonds/stocks. Use its units as an alternate explanation and its unit quizzes plus the free final exam (optional free completion certificate, 70% to pass) for self-testing."},{"title":"15.401 Finance Theory I","provider":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-401-finance-theory-i-fall-2008/","type":"mooc","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"More rigorous treatment (Prof. Andrew Lo, CC-licensed) for learners who want depth on present value, fixed income, equities, and the cost of capital. Use the lecture notes, lecture videos, and problem sets (with solutions) on TVM, capital budgeting, and CAPM as extra practice."},{"title":"Edspira — Finance / Corporate Finance playlists","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin)","url":"https://www.edspira.com/","type":"playlist","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Clear, exam-focused YouTube walkthroughs of single topics from a CPA/PhD professor. Search the channel for NPV, IRR, payback period, WACC, CAPM, and cash conversion cycle when you need a worked example of a specific calculation. (Search for: 'Edspira WACC' / 'Edspira NPV IRR'.)"},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Working Capital & Liquidity / Financial Ratios","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Free explanation/topic pages for the working-capital outcome: working capital and liquidity, receivables/inventory turnover, and financial ratios. Cash-conversion-cycle detail is light here, so pair with Edspira/Saylor for that metric. Quizzes and PRO features are optional paid."}],"project":"Pick a publicly traded company you can get statements for (use its latest 10-K / annual report). Build a single spreadsheet \"investment memo\" that: (a) computes its WACC (CAPM cost of equity using a published beta and risk-free/market premium, plus after-tax cost of debt); (b) projects 5 years of free cash flow and runs a DCF to estimate enterprise and equity value per share, with a sensitivity table on WACC and terminal growth; (c) cross-checks that value against 2-3 comparable companies using EV/EBITDA and P/E multiples; (d) evaluates one hypothetical capital project (e.g., a new product line) with NPV, IRR, payback, and profitability index under base and downside scenarios; and (e) reports the cash conversion cycle and one working-capital recommendation. Conclude with a one-page buy/hold/sell-style argument that ties your numbers back to the company's value drivers. Do all calculations yourself in the sheet (no black-box functions you can't explain).","milestoneCheck":"You can take a real company's financials and: (1) lay out a multi-year free-cash-flow forecast and value the business by DCF, then sanity-check it against EV/EBITDA and P/E comps; (2) build a WACC from a CAPM cost of equity and an after-tax cost of debt; (3) evaluate a proposed capital project with NPV, IRR, payback, and PI, explain why NPV wins when methods disagree, and show how the decision flips under a downside scenario; and (4) compute a cash conversion cycle and recommend a working-capital improvement. If you can do all four and explain each result in plain English to a non-finance manager, you have mastered the module.","flags":["All 7 resources were checked and confirmed to exist, be on-topic, and be free/free-to-audit as of June 2026.","FIXED URL: Saylor 'Principles of Finance (BUS202)' — the friendly slug https://learn.saylor.org/course/BUS202 returns HTTP 404. Replaced with the canonical course URL https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=63. Course confirmed free, ~33 hours, with a free final exam and free completion certificate (70% to pass).","OpenStax 'Principles of Finance' confirmed free (web/PDF) under CC BY; chapter numbers cited in notes are plausible but not individually re-verified against the live table of contents — treat the chapter map as approximate.","Damodaran NYU Stern Corporate Finance class confirmed free (lecture notes, YouTube/webcasts, problem sets and exams with solutions); instructor explicitly states the online material is sufficient without buying the book.","Khan Academy core-finance, MIT OCW 15.401 (Fall 2008, CC-licensed), and Edspira all confirmed free and on-topic.","AccountingCoach correctly marked 'freemium': free explanation/topic pages on working capital, liquidity, and financial ratios; quizzes and PRO features are paid. Cash-conversion-cycle coverage is thin on the free pages, so it is best paired with Edspira/Saylor for that specific metric.","Coverage note: the bundle is strong on capital budgeting, WACC/CAPM, DCF and working capital, but has no single resource dedicated to building a comps/EV-EBITDA multiples model — that project component leans mainly on Damodaran's valuation material, which is referenced but not its own listed resource.","Damodaran's 'Valuation class' referenced in notes is a separate course from the listed Corporate Finance class; learners wanting the DCF/comps depth must navigate to it separately from his homepage."]},{"id":"4.4","title":"Accounting Ethics & Professional Responsibility","track":"Track 4 — Tax, Law, Finance & Ethics","summary":"This module builds the ethical reasoning and professional-responsibility competencies that distinguish accounting as a regulated profession from a mere technical skill. You will learn to apply a structured ethical-decision framework together with the major professional codes of conduct (AICPA in the U.S. and the IESBA/IFAC International Code globally), reason through the core threats to integrity — independence, objectivity, confidentiality, conflicts of interest, and the overriding public-interest duty — and recognize the pressures that drive earnings management and fraud (the fraud triangle). It also covers the regulatory architecture that holds accountants accountable (SOX, PCAOB, whistleblower protections, due care) and the landmark scandals (Enron, WorldCom, and more recent cases) that produced those reforms, along with the professional-liability exposure practitioners must manage.","whyItMatters":"A single ethical lapse can void a career, collapse a firm, and destroy investor trust — Arthur Andersen vanished over Enron — so employers, regulators, and the CPA/CMA exams all treat ethics as a non-negotiable core competency rather than an afterthought. Mastering a defensible decision framework lets you spot and resist real-world pressure to misstate results before it becomes a violation.","outcomes":["Apply a structured ethical-decision framework alongside a professional code (AICPA Code of Professional Conduct and the IESBA/IFAC International Code) to resolve realistic accounting dilemmas and justify the chosen action","Explain and distinguish the fundamental principles — integrity, objectivity, professional competence and due care, confidentiality, and professional behavior — and the special role of independence and the public-interest duty in assurance work","Use the conceptual 'threats and safeguards' approach to identify self-interest, self-review, advocacy, familiarity, and intimidation threats and apply appropriate safeguards","Recognize earnings-management and fraud incentives through the fraud triangle (pressure, opportunity, rationalization) and explain the regulatory response — SOX, the PCAOB, whistleblower protections, and due care","Analyze landmark scandals (Enron, WorldCom, and a modern case) to connect specific failures to the reforms they produced","Identify sources of professional-liability exposure (negligence, breach of contract, fraud) and describe practical ways practitioners manage and limit that risk"],"prerequisites":["2.4"],"estimatedHours":"15-20","resources":[{"title":"Professional Responsibility & Ethics for Accountants","provider":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/ethics","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED. The anchor. Audit for free (skip the paid certificate). Built specifically around the accountant's public-interest duty, the AICPA framework, independence, and threats/safeguards. Note: this is the Coursera version of UIUC's ACCY 516; graded assignments require the paid certificate, so use the free audit for all video lessons and in-video material. This is the spine of the module."},{"title":"International Code of Ethics for Professional Accountants (IESBA Handbook)","provider":"IESBA / IFAC (ethicsboard.org)","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ethicsboard.org/iesba-code","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED. The authoritative global code, free to read online or download. Use Part 1 (Complying with the Code, fundamental principles, conceptual framework) and Part 2/3 (accountants in business vs. public practice) plus the International Independence Standards as your primary-source reference. Don't read cover-to-cover; look up the relevant section for each dilemma you study."},{"title":"AICPA Code of Professional Conduct (et-cod.pdf)","provider":"AICPA & CIMA","url":"https://pub.aicpa.org/codeofconduct/ethicsresources/et-cod.pdf","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"VERIFIED (free ~3.5MB PDF loads from AICPA's official pub server). The U.S. counterpart. Use it to see how the conceptual framework, independence rules, and acts-discreditable provisions are written in actual enforceable rule language. Compare its structure to the IESBA Code to understand U.S. vs. international approaches. CPA-exam-relevant."},{"title":"Business Ethics (open textbook)","provider":"OpenStax (Byars & Stanberry)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/business-ethics","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED. Free, peer-reviewed, CC BY text for the broader ethical-reasoning foundation. Read Ch. 1-2 (defining/theorizing business ethics, ethical frameworks) and Ch. 3 (corporate social responsibility) to ground the decision framework before applying it to accounting-specific cases. Each chapter has review questions and answer keys (answer keys are on openstax.org/books/business-ethics)."},{"title":"BUS200: Business Ethics","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=1260","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED. Free self-paced course (~14 hrs) with a free final exam and free certificate (1.4 CEUs; college-credit recommended). Use as an alternative structured path or to reinforce decision-making under ethical pressure. The end-of-course exam doubles as extra assessment if you want a graded checkpoint."},{"title":"Edspira — Fraud, Internal Controls & the Fraud Triangle","provider":"Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/c/Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"VERIFIED channel. For intuition on the fraud-and-controls half of the module. Search the channel for 'fraud triangle,' 'earnings management,' and 'Sarbanes-Oxley' — short, clear explainers that make the incentives concrete. Pairs well with the SOX/PCAOB regulatory material."},{"title":"Enron & WorldCom accounting scandal explainers","provider":"Accounting Stuff & Edspira (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=enron+accounting+scandal+explained","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free search-results link (not a fixed video). Search for: 'Enron accounting scandal explained' and 'WorldCom fraud explained.' Use these to understand exactly what was misstated, who failed to act, and which SOX provisions (CEO/CFO certification, auditor independence, PCAOB) directly answer each failure. Watch one Enron and one WorldCom breakdown."},{"title":"Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002 (full text, as enacted)","provider":"PCAOB (pcaobus.org)","url":"https://pcaobus.org/About/History/Documents/PDFs/Sarbanes_Oxley_Act_of_2002.pdf","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"URL CHANGED: the original sec.gov/about/laws/soa2002.pdf link returned HTTP 403, so swapped to the PCAOB-hosted canonical full-text PDF (free, authoritative). You don't need the whole act; skim Sections 302 (corporate responsibility for financial reports), 404 (internal control assessment), 802 (criminal penalties for document destruction), and 806 (whistleblower protection) to tie reforms to the scandals that caused them."}],"project":"Build an 'Ethics Case Dossier.' Pick three dilemmas: (1) a historical scandal you research yourself (Enron OR WorldCom), (2) one realistic on-the-job scenario (e.g., your controller asks you to defer recognizing an expense to hit a quarterly target, or you discover a close family member owns stock in an audit client), and (3) one modern case of your choice (e.g., a recent SEC enforcement action — search sec.gov litigation releases). For EACH case, produce a 1-page structured write-up that: states the facts; identifies which fundamental principles and which specific threats (self-interest, self-review, advocacy, familiarity, intimidation) are in play; cites the exact AICPA and/or IESBA Code section that applies; runs the situation through a named ethical-decision framework (identify the issue, stakeholders, alternatives, evaluate against principles, decide, act); names the relevant SOX/regulatory provision and the professional-liability exposure; and states your recommended action with justification. Compile the three into one dossier (4-6 pages) — this is portfolio evidence you can reference for the CPA/CMA ethics requirement and in interviews.","milestoneCheck":"You've mastered this module when you can: (1) take any unfamiliar accounting dilemma and, without notes, name the fundamental principle(s) at risk, classify the threat type, and walk it through a structured decision framework to a defensible recommendation; (2) cite where in the AICPA and IESBA codes the relevant rule lives and explain the difference between the two codes' approaches; (3) explain the fraud triangle and use it to predict where misstatement risk concentrates in a given scenario; and (4) map at least two SOX provisions to the specific Enron/WorldCom failures they were designed to prevent, and describe how a practitioner manages professional-liability exposure. Self-test: complete the Saylor BUS200 final exam and successfully defend all three cases in your Ethics Case Dossier with correct code citations.","flags":["All 8 resources verified to exist and be genuinely free / free-to-audit; no resources dropped.","URL FIX: SOX primary-source link changed from https://www.sec.gov/about/laws/soa2002.pdf (returned HTTP 403 Forbidden) to the PCAOB-hosted canonical full-text PDF https://pcaobus.org/About/History/Documents/PDFs/Sarbanes_Oxley_Act_of_2002.pdf; provider updated from 'U.S. SEC' to 'PCAOB' accordingly. Alternative authoritative free copies exist on GovInfo if PCAOB ever moves it.","Coursera anchor confirmed as the online version of UIUC's ACCY 516 'Professional Responsibility and Ethics for Accountants'; free audit gives all video content but graded assignments/quizzes are gated behind the paid certificate — cost correctly marked 'free-to-audit', not 'free'.","AICPA et-cod.pdf confirmed live (~3.5MB official PDF). The automated fetcher rendered it as image/binary, but the canonical URL is correct and downloadable; minor uncertainty only on fetcher rendering, not on the resource itself.","Two YouTube entries (Edspira channel and the Enron/WorldCom item) are channel/search-results links rather than fixed videos, so specific videos are not pinned; the Edspira channel and YouTube search are confirmed reachable and free, but exact recommended videos depend on the learner's search at study time.","Coverage note: the 'modern case' learning outcome and project component (3) rely on the learner self-sourcing a recent SEC litigation release rather than a curated link; consider adding a direct pointer to https://www.sec.gov/litigation/litreleases for reliability.","OpenStax Business Ethics confirmed free CC-BY (Byars & Stanberry); chapter/answer-key references are accurate."]}]},{"name":"Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","modules":[{"id":"5.1","title":"Governmental & Nonprofit Accounting (Elective)","track":"Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","summary":"This elective extends financial accounting into the public and not-for-profit sectors, where the goal is accountability for restricted resources rather than profit. You learn fund accounting and the modified-accrual basis used in governmental funds, how budgets and encumbrances are recorded, and how to build both fund and government-wide financial statements under the GASB reporting model (with a brief contrast to the international IPSAS framework). The module then turns to nonprofit organizations — net asset classification, accounting for contributions, and the functional (program vs. supporting) expense reporting required of charities.","whyItMatters":"Governments and nonprofits control a large share of economic activity, and their accounting rules (GASB, fund accounting, Form 990) are fundamentally different from for-profit GAAP — fluency here opens auditing, public-sector, and nonprofit-finance careers and is a tested area on the CPA FAR exam.","outcomes":["Explain fund accounting, fund categories, and the modified-accrual (current-financial-resources) measurement focus, and contrast them with for-profit accrual accounting","Record budgetary entries, encumbrances, and the release/restriction of resources through the appropriation–encumbrance–expenditure cycle","Prepare governmental fund statements and convert/reconcile them to government-wide full-accrual statements under the GASB model, and describe how IPSAS differs","Account for nonprofit net asset classes (with and without donor restrictions), conditional vs. unconditional contributions, and present expenses by function in a statement of functional expenses"],"prerequisites":["1.5"],"estimatedHours":"25-35","resources":[{"title":"Governmental Accounting and Reporting I + Governmental Accounting II and Nonprofit Accounting (two-course sequence)","provider":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/governmental-accounting-and-reporting-1","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor — two separate UIUC courses, both auditable for free (toggle 'Audit' when enrolling; graded quizzes/certificate are paywalled but lectures are the core). Course I (this URL, 'Governmental Accounting and Reporting I') covers fund accounting, modified accrual, budgets and encumbrances. Course II ('Governmental Accounting II and Nonprofit Accounting', https://www.coursera.org/learn/governmental-nonprofit-accounting ) covers government-wide statements and nonprofit topics (net assets, contributions, functional expenses, 501(c)(3)). Audit BOTH for full module coverage."},{"title":"Edspira — Governmental & Nonprofit Accounting videos","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA — YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira/playlists","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Use for intuition on tough mechanics — fund balance classifications, the encumbrance cycle, and fund-to-government-wide reconciliation. Search the channel for 'Governmental Accounting - Fund Accounting' and the related fund/financial-statement videos. (Channel confirmed at @Edspira; the older /c/Edspira URL also redirects here.)"},{"title":"Governmental & Nonprofit Accounting lectures and problems","provider":"Farhat Lectures (CPA review — YouTube / farhatlectures.com)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLxP0KZzCGFYMbs-skJj-zcRkVOCXg8gYC","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Primary problem-set source. This free YouTube playlist ('Governmental and Not-for-Profit Accounting | FAR CPA Exam | Fund Accounting') has worked numerical examples (general fund journal entries, special revenue/capital projects funds, encumbrances, government-wide conversion) you can pause and attempt first — closely mirrors CPA FAR style. Note: farhatlectures.com itself bundles MCQs/notes behind a free-trial/paid course, but the YouTube lectures are free."},{"title":"Financial Accounting for Local and State School Systems — Ch. 4 (Measurement Focus & Basis of Accounting) and Ch. 5 (Financial Reporting)","provider":"U.S. National Center for Education Statistics (NCES)","url":"https://nces.ed.gov/pubs2009/fin_acct/chapter4_2.asp","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"A free, authoritative government reference. Use Chapter 4 for a clean explanation of modified-accrual vs. full-accrual measurement focus, and Chapter 5 for the conversion/reconciliation between fund and government-wide statements with concrete adjustment examples (capital assets, long-term debt, deferred/unavailable revenue)."},{"title":"Conversion and Reconciliation between Government-Wide and Fund Financial Statements (BARS GAAP Manual)","provider":"Washington State Auditor's Office","url":"https://sao.wa.gov/bars-annual-filing/bars-gaap-manual/reporting/conversion-and-reconciliation-between-government-wide-and-fund-financial-statements","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"A practitioner walkthrough of the exact reconciliation adjustments (capital assets, long-term debt, accruals). Use it as a checklist when doing the conversion in the project; pairs well with the NCES chapters."},{"title":"Handbook of International Public Sector Accounting Pronouncements (IPSAS)","provider":"IPSASB / IFAC","url":"https://www.ipsasb.org/publications","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"For the IPSAS contrast outcome. You do not need the full handbook — skim the 'Conceptual Framework' and IPSAS 1 (presentation) to see how the international accrual-based public-sector model differs from the US GASB fund model. Standards/handbook are free to download from the IPSASB/IFAC site (note IFAC IP terms apply to reproduction)."},{"title":"About Form 990 and Instructions for Form 990 (incl. Statement of Functional Expenses, Part IX)","provider":"Internal Revenue Service (IRS)","url":"https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-form-990","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Real-world nonprofit reporting. This landing page links the free Form 990 PDF and instructions — open the instructions and read Part IX (Statement of Functional Expenses) and the net-asset section to see how program vs. management vs. fundraising allocation works; use a real charity's filed 990 (via the IRS Tax Exempt Organization Search) as a worked example."},{"title":"Nonprofit / not-for-profit accounting topics","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"article","cost":"freemium","role":"supplement","notes":"Plain-English explainers (free tier) for net assets with/without donor restrictions, contributions, and the nonprofit statement of activities. Good quick reference when the Coursera nonprofit module moves fast (some advanced material and the PRO tier are paid)."}],"project":"Build a mini year-end close for a small fictional city's General Fund and a small charity.","milestoneCheck":"You can now, from a blank spreadsheet: (1) record a full appropriation→encumbrance→expenditure cycle and explain why governmental funds use modified accrual; (2) produce both fund and government-wide statements and articulate every reconciling adjustment between them; (3) classify nonprofit net assets, decide whether a given contribution is recognized now or deferred, and present expenses by function; and (4) state two concrete ways IPSAS differs from the US GASB model. Self-test: take a Farhat or CPA-FAR governmental/nonprofit problem set and score 80%+ without notes.","flags":["VERIFIED: All 8 resources confirmed to exist and be genuinely free or free-to-audit as of June 2026.","FIXED (primary anchor): The original single Coursera URL (.../governmental-nonprofit-accounting) actually points ONLY to 'Governmental Accounting II and Nonprofit Accounting' — Course I is a SEPARATE course. Updated the primary URL to Course I ('Governmental Accounting and Reporting I', .../governmental-accounting-and-reporting-1) and documented BOTH course URLs in the notes, since the notes instruct learners to audit both. Title corrected to the actual course names.","FIXED (Edspira): URL updated from the legacy /c/Edspira/playlists to the canonical https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira/playlists. Provider/attribution (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA) confirmed accurate.","FIXED (Farhat): URL changed from the farhatlectures.com homepage (where lectures sit behind a free-trial/paid course) to the actual FREE YouTube playlist, so the 'free' cost label is accurate. Added a note that the website's MCQs/notes are paywalled but the YouTube lectures are free.","CLARIFIED (IRS Form 990): The 'About Form 990' page itself does not contain Part IX text; Part IX lives in the linked Form/Instructions PDFs. Note now directs learners to open the instructions. Page and PDFs are free.","MINOR (IPSASB): publications page confirmed; IPSAS standards/handbook are free to download but IFAC asserts IP/reproduction terms — noted. Cost kept as 'free'.","UNCERTAIN/COST (AccountingCoach): kept 'freemium' — free explainers exist but some content and the PRO tier are paid; label is accurate.","COVERAGE GAP: No resource directly anchors GASB's own authoritative pronouncements or recent standards updates (e.g., GASB 87 leases, GASB 96 SBITAs, GASB 34 reporting model). The gasb.org GASB Codification has limited free access. Consider adding a free GASB overview (e.g., a GFOA or AICPA primer) if learners need primary-standard grounding beyond the teaching resources.","COVERAGE NOTE: All confirmed resources are US-centric (GASB/Form 990); IPSAS coverage rests on a single skim-only reference, which is adequate for the 'two ways IPSAS differs' outcome but thin if deeper international comparison is desired."]},{"id":"5.2","title":"Forensic Accounting & Fraud Examination (Elective)","track":"Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","summary":"This elective teaches how occupational and financial-statement fraud is perpetrated, concealed, detected, and proven. You will learn the standard fraud taxonomy (asset misappropriation, corruption, financial-statement fraud) and the behavioral models behind it (the fraud triangle/diamond), then move into hands-on detection using data analytics (Benford's Law, ratio and anomaly analysis) and investigative skills (evidence handling, interviewing). The module closes the loop from suspicion to courtroom: gathering litigation-grade evidence, quantifying damages, writing a defensible expert report, and designing anti-fraud controls and a fraud risk assessment.","whyItMatters":"Fraud costs organizations an estimated 5% of revenue every year, and the people who can both detect it analytically and document it to an evidentiary standard are rare and highly paid. This skill set turns an accountant from a recorder of transactions into an investigator who protects the enterprise and can support litigation.","outcomes":["Classify any fraud scheme onto the ACFE Fraud Tree (asset misappropriation, corruption, financial-statement fraud) and explain it through the fraud triangle (pressure, opportunity, rationalization)","Apply data-analytic detection techniques — Benford's Law, ratio/horizontal/vertical analysis, duplicate and gap testing, and anomaly detection — to a transaction dataset","Plan and conduct a fraud investigation: develop a fraud theory, gather and preserve evidence to a litigation-ready standard, and structure an admission-seeking interview","Quantify fraud losses/damages and write a clear, defensible forensic and expert-witness report","Design layered anti-fraud controls and perform a basic fraud risk assessment for a business process"],"prerequisites":["2.4","3.3"],"estimatedHours":"25-35","resources":[{"title":"Forensic Accounting and Fraud Examination (West Virginia University)","provider":"Coursera (audit track) / West Virginia University & ACFE","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/forensic-accounting","type":"course","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"Anchor for the whole module. Verified live. On the enrollment page choose 'Audit only' (look for the small 'Audit' link under the payment options) to access the video lectures and readings for free; the fee is only for the certificate/graded quizzes and it is also included with Coursera Plus. Work all 5 weeks in order: Wk1 the accidental fraudster & fraud triangle, Wk2 the predatory fraudster, Wk3 big data + Benford's Law + financial analytics, Wk4 cyber-crime & money laundering, Wk5 financial-statement fraud & whistleblowing. Co-taught with ACFE instructors."},{"title":"Occupational Fraud 2024: A Report to the Nations","provider":"Association of Certified Fraud Examiners (ACFE)","url":"https://www.acfe.com/-/media/files/acfe/pdfs/rttn/2024/2024-report-to-the-nations.pdf","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free flagship study. Verified live and downloadable at no charge. NOTE: the 2024 edition analyzes 1,921 real cases (not 20,000+ — that figure conflated cumulative coverage across editions). Use it as your data backbone: memorize the Fraud Tree categories, the median-loss and detection-method statistics, the perpetrator/red-flag profiles, and how schemes are concealed. Cite its figures when you size losses and justify controls in the project. A newer 2026 edition now exists at acfe.com/RTTN — use the latest, but this 2024 link is confirmed working."},{"title":"ACFE Fraud Resources — Fraud Tree & Anti-Fraud Tools","provider":"Association of Certified Fraud Examiners (ACFE)","url":"https://www.acfe.com/fraud-resources","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified live. Free interactive Fraud Tree, fraud-prevention checklists, and the fraud risk assessment overview sit under this resource library (some deeper materials require membership, but the core tools are free). Use the Fraud Tree to practice classifying schemes and use the prevention checklist as the template for the controls-design portion of your project."},{"title":"Edspira — Auditing & Fraud playlist","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin, PhD, CPA)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"For intuition. Verified: free channel by Prof. Michael McLaughlin (CPA, PhD) with 800+ business tutorials. Watch the short videos on the Fraud Triangle, internal controls, segregation of duties, earnings management, and financial-statement red flags. Best consumed alongside Coursera Weeks 1 and 5. On the channel, search 'fraud triangle', 'internal controls', 'earnings management'."},{"title":"\"I've Got Your Number\" — Using Benford's Law (Mark Nigrini)","provider":"Journal of Accountancy (AICPA)","url":"https://www.journalofaccountancy.com/issues/1999/may/nigrini/","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Classic free walkthrough of applying Benford's Law to fraud detection, by the leading Benford researcher. Verified freely readable at the direct link. Use it as your hands-on Benford lab and pair with any list of disbursements/expenses to run a first-digit test yourself. For a more step-by-step Excel build, also see the JoA follow-up 'Using Excel and Benford's Law to detect fraud' (journalofaccountancy.com/issues/2017/apr/excel-and-benfords-law-to-detect-fraud)."},{"title":"SEC Accounting & Auditing Enforcement Releases (AAERs)","provider":"U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission","url":"https://www.sec.gov/enforcement-litigation/accounting-auditing-enforcement-releases","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free library of real financial-statement-fraud cases (revenue recognition, fictitious sales, reserve manipulation). URL updated to the current canonical SEC path (the old /divisions/enforce/friactions.htm link is dead). Pick 2-3 AAERs and reverse-engineer each: what scheme, which fraud-triangle leg, what red flags/ratios would have caught it, what controls failed. Excellent source material for your investigation report and case studies."},{"title":"Fraud Triangle — concept guide","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI)","url":"https://corporatefinanceinstitute.com/resources/accounting/fraud-triangle/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Concise free reference on the three legs of the fraud triangle and its extension to the fraud diamond. Verified free. Quick primer/refresher before the heavier ACFE material; use it to anchor terminology when you write up the 'why' behind each scheme."}],"project":"Run a complete mini fraud examination on a simulated accounts-payable / disbursements dataset (build one in Excel of ~1,000 vendor payments, or use a public sample/synthetic file, and seed it with 2-3 schemes such as duplicate payments, a fictitious 'shell' vendor, and round-dollar kickbacks). Deliverables: (1) an analytics workbook applying Benford's Law first-digit test, duplicate/gap detection, round-number and weekend-payment flags, and vendor-vs-employee address matching; (2) a one-page fraud theory mapping each flagged anomaly onto the Fraud Tree and the fraud triangle; (3) a short evidence log documenting how you would preserve the supporting documents to a litigation-ready standard plus an outline of an admission-seeking interview plan; (4) a damages calculation quantifying the loss; and (5) a 2-3 page expert-style forensic report with a recommended set of anti-fraud controls and a one-page fraud risk assessment of the AP process. Use one real SEC AAER as a benchmark case to validate your methodology.","milestoneCheck":"You can now: (1) take any described scheme and instantly place it on the Fraud Tree and explain it via pressure/opportunity/rationalization; (2) hand someone a transaction file and produce a ranked list of suspicious items using Benford's Law and at least three other analytic tests, explaining the statistical logic; (3) lay out an investigation from fraud theory through evidence preservation and interview strategy without compromising admissibility; and (4) write a damages quantification and a forensic report a non-accountant judge could follow, and recommend specific controls that would have prevented the scheme. Self-test: pick an unseen SEC AAER, and within an hour identify the scheme type, the red flags/ratios that should have triggered detection, the control failures, and the rough loss — if you can do that cold, you have mastered the module.","flags":["Fixed dead URL: SEC AAER link changed from the retired https://www.sec.gov/divisions/enforce/friactions.htm (returns 403) to the current canonical page https://www.sec.gov/enforcement-litigation/accounting-auditing-enforcement-releases.","Improved URL: Journal of Accountancy resource pointed only to the homepage; updated to the direct, freely-readable 1999 Nigrini article (issues/1999/may/nigrini/) and added the 2017 Excel-specific follow-up as a pointer.","Corrected fact: the original note claimed the ACFE 2024 Report covers '>20,000 cases'; the 2024 edition actually analyzes 1,921 cases (138 countries). Note text fixed.","All 7 resources confirmed to exist, be on-topic, and be genuinely free / free-to-audit; no resource dropped.","Freshness note: ACFE has since released a 2026 Report to the Nations; the verified 2024 PDF link is kept (confirmed live) with a pointer to acfe.com/RTTN for the latest edition.","Minor: parts of acfe.com/fraud-resources sit behind ACFE membership; the Fraud Tree, prevention checklist, and risk-assessment overview used by this module are the free portions.","Coverage gap: the module lists no free template/worksheet for the damages-quantification and expert-report deliverables; learners rely on the Coursera lectures plus self-built Excel work. Consider adding an AICPA/NACVA forensic-report sample if a free one can be verified."]},{"id":"5.3","title":"International Accounting & IFRS Deep Dive (Elective)","track":"Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","summary":"This elective builds fluency in IFRS as a reporting framework and maps it against US GAAP across recognition, measurement, and presentation. You will work through the high-impact standards a preparer or analyst meets most often — IFRS 9 (financial instruments), IFRS 15 (revenue), IFRS 16 (leases), IAS 36 (impairment), and IAS 37 (provisions) — plus cross-border issues like functional/presentation currency and segment reporting. It closes with first-time adoption (IFRS 1), presentation and disclosure differences, and the global standard-setting landscape (IASB, IFRS Foundation, and convergence history).","whyItMatters":"Over 140 jurisdictions require IFRS, so anyone touching multinational consolidations, cross-border investing, M&A, or a foreign listing must read financials prepared under a framework different from US GAAP. Knowing where the two diverge — and being able to reconcile between them — is a directly marketable skill in audit, corporate reporting, and equity analysis.","outcomes":["Catalogue the major US GAAP vs. IFRS differences across recognition, measurement, presentation, and disclosure (e.g., inventory/LIFO, development costs, impairment reversals, lease classification)","Apply key IFRS standards — IFRS 9, 15, 16 and IAS 36, 37 — to scenarios, and reconcile a set of financial statements (net income and equity) between IFRS and US GAAP","Handle first-time adoption under IFRS 1 and the main presentation/disclosure differences in the primary statements","Account for cross-border issues including functional vs. presentation currency translation and segment reporting","Explain the global standard-setting landscape — the IFRS Foundation, IASB, due process, and the history and current state of IFRS–US GAAP convergence"],"prerequisites":["2.1"],"estimatedHours":"25-35","resources":[{"title":"ACCA Financial Reporting (FR) — Free Notes, Lectures & Tests","provider":"OpenTuition","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/fr/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified fully free (no paywall). Use this IFRS-based course as your spine. Work the lecture videos + downloadable notes covering the conceptual framework, IFRS 15 revenue, IFRS 16 leases, IFRS 9 financial instruments, IAS 36 impairment, IAS 37 provisions, and consolidation/foreign-currency. Do the chapter tests and the free mock exam as you go. Note: ACCA FR is inherently IFRS-based."},{"title":"IFRS and US GAAP: Similarities and Differences","provider":"PwC Viewpoint","url":"https://viewpoint.pwc.com/dt/us/en/pwc/accounting_guides/ifrs_and_us_gaap_sim/ifrs_and_us_gaap_sim_US/About-this-guide.html","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Verified: the single best free GAAP-vs-IFRS comparison reference, free to read on Viewpoint (free account/registration). A free PDF is also downloadable directly at https://viewpoint.pwc.com/content/dam/pwc-madison/ditaroot/us/en/pwc/accounting_guides/ifrs_and_us_gaap_sim/assets/pwcifrsusgaap1025.pdf . Use it topic-by-topic alongside the course to build your differences catalogue and as the backbone of the project memo."},{"title":"Roadmap: Comparing IFRS Accounting Standards and U.S. GAAP — Bridging the Differences","provider":"Deloitte (DART / IAS Plus)","url":"https://dart.deloitte.com/USDART/home/publications/roadmap/ifrs-us-gaap-comparison","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified exists (Sept 2025 edition, reflects standards effective Jan 1 2026). Readable online with a free DART registration, BUT a paid DART subscription is required to download/copy/print the PDF (non-subscribers can request a copy from a Deloitte engagement team). Cross-check the PwC guide against this for the trickier standards (IFRS 9, 15, 16; impairment reversals; presentation under IFRS 18) and for worked comparison highlights."},{"title":"IFRS & IAS Lecture Playlist","provider":"Farhat Lectures (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLzheBpLpqAqPpRRUKlhntBaWcI8cJeXmc","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Verified: free YouTube playlist on the Farhat Lectures (IFRS & IAS) channel. Watch for intuition and worked examples on individual standards (IAS 36 impairment, IAS 37 provisions, IFRS 15 five-step model, IFRS 16 lessee accounting, foreign currency). Good when a topic in the primary course needs a second explanation."},{"title":"Issued IFRS Accounting Standards (Standards Navigator)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified: the authoritative source. Free registration gives basic free access to all issued standards (an enhanced IFRS Digital Subscription is paid but not needed here). Use to read the actual text/Basis for Conclusions of IFRS 9, 15, 16 and IAS 36, 37, and IFRS 1 when the secondary guides leave you unsure."},{"title":"IAS Plus — Standard Summaries & US Jurisdiction Page","provider":"Deloitte IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/standards","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Verified: concise, free per-standard summaries plus free e-learning modules. Fast orientation before you read the full standard, and a quick lookup for the global standard-setting landscape, IASB due process, and convergence history. Note: some IAS Plus content is being migrated onto deloitte.com regional pages; if a link breaks, search 'IAS Plus' + the standard."},{"title":"ACCA FR Past Exam Papers, Specimen Papers & Practice Questions","provider":"aCOWtancy / ACCA Global","url":"https://www.acowtancy.com/exams/acca-fr/","type":"practice","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"COST DOWNGRADED to freemium: aCOWtancy free sign-up gives course notes, two free CBE specimen papers and a limited set of free exam questions, but full past-paper/question-bank access is a paid subscription (~$269). For a fully free problem-set source, prioritise the OFFICIAL ACCA FR past exam papers and specimen papers, free at https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en/student/exam-support-resources/fundamentals-exams-study-resources/f7/past-exam-papers.html . Time yourself on a full set as a capstone before the project."}],"project":"Pick one foreign IFRS-reporting public company (e.g., Unilever, Nestlé, or Toyota) and one US GAAP peer in the same industry. Using the PwC and Deloitte comparison guides, build a 3-5 page \"framework reconciliation memo\": (1) identify five accounting areas where the two firms' policies differ because of the framework; (2) for each, cite the governing IFRS standard and its US GAAP counterpart and explain the measurement/recognition difference; (3) construct a simplified numeric reconciliation that restates the IFRS company's net income and equity onto a US GAAP basis (or vice versa) for one or two of those areas, showing the adjusting entries; and (4) write a one-paragraph analyst note on how the differences affect comparability of margins and leverage ratios.","milestoneCheck":"You can take a short US GAAP balance sheet and income statement with a handful of differences (capitalized development costs, an impairment that later recovered, a finance vs. operating lease, LIFO inventory, and a revaluation) and produce a clean reconciliation of net income and shareholders' equity to IFRS, citing the specific standard behind each adjustment. You can also state, for any of IFRS 9/15/16 and IAS 36/37, the single most material way it diverges from US GAAP — and explain, in plain English, what the IASB is and why convergence stalled.","flags":["aCOWtancy cost downgraded free->freemium: free tier gives notes + 2 specimen papers + limited questions, but full question bank/past papers are paid (~$269). Added the official ACCA Global past-papers page as the fully-free practice anchor.","Deloitte DART roadmap cost downgraded free->freemium: readable online with free DART registration, but downloading/printing the PDF requires a paid subscription. Still usable free as a reference, so retained as supplement.","PwC Viewpoint guide verified free (registration) — direct fetch of the About-this-guide URL hit a redirect loop, but web search confirms it is the canonical landing page and a free downloadable PDF mirror exists (URL added in notes).","IFRS Foundation Standards Navigator: only BASIC access is free with registration; the IFRS Digital Subscription (premium) is paid but not required for this module.","IAS Plus standards page verified free but Deloitte is migrating IAS Plus content to deloitte.com regional pages — URL may change over time (fallback search note added).","Coverage gap: no dedicated resource is anchored specifically to functional vs. presentation currency translation (IAS 21) or segment reporting (IFRS 8); both are covered within OpenTuition (consolidation/foreign-currency) and IAS Plus summaries, but consider adding a targeted reference if students need more depth.","Deloitte roadmap and PwC guide reference IFRS 18 (Presentation and Disclosure, effective 2027), which goes beyond the module's stated IAS 1-era presentation scope — flag as forward-looking context, not a gap.","OpenTuition page did not explicitly state 'IFRS-based' in fetched text, but ACCA FR is an IFRS-based syllabus by definition; treated as confirmed."]},{"id":"5.4","title":"Sustainability / ESG Reporting (Elective)","track":"Track 5 — Specializations (Electives)","summary":"This elective maps the modern sustainability/ESG reporting landscape and shows how it interlocks with financial reporting. You will learn the major frameworks (ISSB / IFRS S1-S2, GRI, the EU's CSRD/ESRS, and the GHG Protocol), the difference between financial (single) and impact/double materiality, and how to account for, measure, and disclose greenhouse-gas and other sustainability metrics with adequate data and controls. The module closes with how assurance over sustainability information works alongside the financial audit, and how to read a sustainability report critically for decision-usefulness and greenwashing risk.","whyItMatters":"Sustainability disclosure is becoming mandatory and investor-grade in major markets, so accountants are increasingly expected to prepare, control, and assure ESG data with the same rigor as the financial statements. Knowing the frameworks and materiality logic makes you valuable for the fastest-growing reporting and assurance specialty.","outcomes":["Map the ESG reporting landscape and the role of the major frameworks/standards (ISSB IFRS S1 & S2, GRI, CSRD/ESRS, GHG Protocol) and how they interoperate","Distinguish financial (single) materiality from impact/double materiality and identify which ESG metrics are material to a given company","Apply GHG Protocol concepts to account for and disclose Scope 1, 2, and 3 emissions, and describe the data sources and internal controls needed for reliable ESG metrics","Explain how assurance over sustainability information works (limited vs. reasonable) and how it overlaps with and differs from the financial-statement audit","Read a company's sustainability report alongside its financial statements and critique it for completeness, comparability, connectivity, and greenwashing risk"],"prerequisites":["2.2"],"estimatedHours":"20-30","resources":[{"title":"IFRS Sustainability Knowledge Hub — Free e-learning modules & courses (ISSB / IFRS S1 & S2)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/sustainability/knowledge-hub/","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor. Confirmed live with a free Courses section plus video introductions to IFRS S1 and S2 and a Preparers' guide (free with an ifrs.org account). Work through the available self-paced e-learning on the IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards, IFRS S1, and IFRS S2 (~1 hr each), and use the Knowledge Hub as your reading spine for the landscape and connectivity-with-financial-statements outcomes."},{"title":"IFRS Sustainability Standards Navigator — IFRS S1 & IFRS S2 full text","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/ifrs-sustainability-standards-navigator/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative source text. Confirmed: register for free to access HTML and PDF of the 2023 ISSB Standards (non-commercial use allowed without charge). Read IFRS S1 General Requirements (governance, strategy, risk management, metrics & targets structure; financial materiality) and IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures (climate risks/opportunities, Scope 1/2/3 disclosure, industry-based metrics). Use as the definitive reference when the e-learning raises a question."},{"title":"GHG Protocol — Corporate Accounting and Reporting Standard (+ Scope 2 & Scope 3 guidance)","provider":"GHG Protocol (WRI / WBCSD)","url":"https://ghgprotocol.org/corporate-standard","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"The core technical reference for the GHG-accounting outcome. Confirmed free PDF. Read the Corporate Standard for organizational/operational boundaries and Scope 1 vs 2; then skim the Corporate Value Chain (Scope 3) Standard and Scope 2 Guidance (location- vs market-based) to understand value-chain emissions and the data/controls they require."},{"title":"GRI Standards — Download the Standards (Universal, Sector, Topic)","provider":"Global Reporting Initiative","url":"https://www.globalreporting.org/standards/download-the-standards/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Confirmed live; GRI Standards are free to download (English and many translations). Read GRI 1 Foundation and GRI 3 Material Topics to understand impact materiality and the stakeholder/impact lens, then contrast with the ISSB's investor/financial-materiality lens. This is the key resource for the single- vs. double-materiality distinction."},{"title":"EFRAG — European Sustainability Reporting Standards (ESRS) & Materiality Assessment Implementation Guidance","provider":"EFRAG / European Commission","url":"https://www.efrag.org/en/sustainability-reporting/esrs","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Use for the CSRD/regional-mandate outcome and the canonical definition of double materiality. Confirmed: EFRAG hosts the twelve ESRS (adopted as EU delegated acts) and an ESRS Knowledge Hub with free Implementation Guidance. Read ESRS 1 General Requirements and the free Materiality Assessment Implementation Guidance (IG 1) — find it via EFRAG's ESRS Implementation Guidance / Knowledge Hub — to see how impact + financial materiality are operationalized in the EU regime."},{"title":"Foundations of Sustainability and ESG","provider":"Saïd Business School, University of Oxford (Coursera)","url":"https://www.coursera.org/learn/introduction-to-sustainable-finance","type":"mooc","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"supplement","notes":"Confirmed: exact title 'Foundations of Sustainability and ESG' by Saïd Business School, University of Oxford (instructor Amir Amel-Zadeh), part of 'The Intersection of Finance, Strategy, and Sustainability' specialization. Audit for free (no certificate). Use for business-context intuition on why ESG matters to investors and management, ESG ratings, and how sustainability connects to value — a gentler narrative complement to the technical standards. The legacy URL slug (introduction-to-sustainable-finance) still resolves correctly."},{"title":"ISSB Webinar & Podcast Series — Perspectives on sustainability disclosure","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/sustainability/knowledge-hub/webinar-and-podcast-series/","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Confirmed live and free ('open for anyone to join live or play back on demand'). 13+ episodes including 'Using the GHG Protocol for climate-related disclosures', industry-based disclosures, and assurance. Prioritize episodes on connectivity with financial statements, industry-based disclosures, and assurance to cover the audit-overlap outcome with practitioner perspective."},{"title":"GHG Protocol — Calculation Tools (cross-sector & sector Excel tools)","provider":"GHG Protocol (WRI / WBCSD)","url":"https://ghgprotocol.org/calculation-tools-and-guidance","type":"practice","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Hands-on practice source. Confirmed: free cross-sector Excel tools remain available (the canonical URL now 301-redirects to GHG Protocol's Zendesk-hosted help center). Download a tool — e.g., the Stationary Combustion tool at ghgprotocol.org/sites/default/files/Stationary_combustion_tool_(Version4-1).xlsx, or mobile combustion / purchased electricity — and run sample activity data through it to compute Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions, so the GHG-accounting outcome becomes a calculation skill rather than theory."}],"project":"Pick one listed public company that publishes both an audited annual report and a sustainability/ESG report (ideally an ISSB- or CSRD-aligned reporter). Produce a 4-6 page analyst memo that: (1) identifies which framework(s) the company reports under and maps its disclosures to the IFRS S1/S2 four-pillar structure (governance, strategy, risk management, metrics & targets); (2) performs a mini materiality assessment — list 6-8 ESG topics and classify each as financially material, impact-material, or both, justifying your calls; (3) recreates or sanity-checks the company's reported Scope 1 and Scope 2 figures using a GHG Protocol calculation tool with stated assumptions, and comments on Scope 3 completeness and the data/controls behind the numbers; (4) states whether the sustainability information was assured, by whom, and at what level (limited vs. reasonable), comparing that to the financial audit; and (5) flags at least three potential greenwashing or decision-usefulness concerns (e.g., vague targets, cherry-picked boundaries, missing comparatives, weak connectivity to the financial statements). Conclude with a one-paragraph recommendation on the report's credibility.","milestoneCheck":"You can now: (a) explain, without notes, how ISSB/IFRS S1-S2, GRI, and CSRD/ESRS differ in purpose and audience and what 'single vs. double materiality' means; (b) classify a given ESG topic as financially material, impact-material, or both, and defend it; (c) compute Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions from activity data using a GHG Protocol tool and explain the boundary choices and controls behind them; (d) describe how limited vs. reasonable assurance over sustainability information works and where it overlaps the financial audit; and (e) read a real sustainability report next to the financials and produce a credible critique that names specific greenwashing or decision-usefulness risks. Self-test: complete the project memo and have its emissions recomputation land within a reasonable, explainable range of the company's disclosed figures.","flags":["All 9 resources were verified to exist and to be genuinely free or free-to-audit as of June 2026; none were dropped and no cost downgrades were needed.","IFRS Knowledge Hub: confirmed free Courses section (requires an ifrs.org account) plus free S1/S2 video intros and Preparers' guide; could not independently confirm the original notes' exact count of 'four' self-paced modules, so the enumeration was softened — the module list may have changed.","GHG Protocol Calculation Tools: the canonical URL ghgprotocol.org/calculation-tools-and-guidance now 301-redirects to a Zendesk-hosted help center (ghgptechassistance.zendesk.com), which bot-blocks direct fetches (403); the canonical entry URL still works and the free cross-sector Excel tools remain available. Added a direct stationary-combustion tool link in the notes as a backup.","EFRAG ESRS page confirmed (twelve ESRS adopted as EU delegated acts; double materiality covered). The specific Materiality Assessment Implementation Guidance (IG 1) was not enumerated on the landing page but is a known free EFRAG publication — the note now points learners to EFRAG's ESRS Implementation Guidance / Knowledge Hub to locate it.","Coursera Oxford course: title and provider verified accurate; the existing URL (legacy slug) resolves correctly and was kept.","Coverage gap — assurance outcome (#4): the standards detail for limited vs. reasonable assurance currently rests only on ISSB webinars/podcasts. Consider adding a free primary source on the new sustainability assurance standard (IAASB ISSA 5000, effective for periods beginning on/after 15 Dec 2026) to more directly support that outcome.","Coverage gap — jurisdiction: the bundle covers ISSB, GRI, CSRD/ESRS and GHG Protocol well, but US-specific mandates (SEC climate-disclosure rule status, California SB 253/261) and the TCFD/SASB lineage now folded into ISSB are only implicit. Acceptable for a framework-focused elective, but worth noting given the 'major markets' framing in whyItMatters."]}]},{"name":"Track 6 — Capstone & Certification","modules":[{"id":"6.1","title":"Capstone — Full-Cycle Engagement, Analysis & Certification","track":"Track 6 — Capstone & Certification","summary":"This capstone integrates everything from the curriculum into one end-to-end engagement: you take a fictional company from raw transactions through the full accounting cycle and period-end close to a complete, footnoted, standards-compliant set of financial statements built inside real cloud accounting software. You then layer on the professional-judgment deliverables an employer expects — an analysis-and-recommendation memo, an automated reporting dashboard, an internal-controls and audit-risk write-up, and an ethics and tax/compliance summary — and assemble it all into a public portfolio. The module closes with a personal credentialing plan that maps your chosen certification (CPA, ACCA, CMA, or a bookkeeping credential) to a concrete study schedule.","whyItMatters":"A polished, public capstone is the single strongest signal of job-ready competence for a self-taught accountant, because it demonstrates the full cycle plus judgment rather than isolated skills. Pairing it with a realistic credential plan turns \"I studied accounting\" into a concrete path to a hireable, licensable career.","outcomes":["Process a full period of transactions for a fictional company in cloud accounting software, complete the period-end close, and produce a footnoted, standards-compliant set of financial statements (income statement, balance sheet, cash-flow statement, and equity statement with disclosures)","Produce a financial-analysis-and-recommendation memo using ratio, trend, and common-size analysis, supported by an automated reporting/analytics dashboard","Document the engagement's internal controls, an audit-risk assessment, an ethics reflection against a professional code of conduct, and a tax/compliance summary","Assemble a public portfolio (workpapers, statements, models, dashboards, and exported software files) that demonstrates full-cycle, job-ready competence","Choose a target credential (CPA, ACCA, CMA, or a bookkeeping credential), confirm eligibility against official requirements, and build a gap-to-schedule study plan with practice exams"],"prerequisites":["3.1","2.2","2.4","4.4"],"estimatedHours":"50-70","resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting (OpenStax)","provider":"OpenStax (Rice University)","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Primary anchor for the full-cycle build. Use Ch. 3-5 (analyzing, recording, adjusting, closing) as the close checklist; Ch. 16 (statement of cash flows) and Ch. 9-12 for receivables, inventory, long-term assets and liabilities footnotes; the end-of-chapter comprehensive problems are a model for your fictional company's transaction set. Free to read online, download as PDF, or order low-cost print."},{"title":"Financial Statement Analysis — Lecture Notes (PDF)","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/pdfiles/invphiloh/finstatement.pdf","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Use to drive the analysis-and-recommendation memo: profitability, leverage, and efficiency ratios plus how to read the three statements together. Pair with his free valuation webcasts and data pages at pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar for benchmarking your company against industry averages."},{"title":"Edspira — Accounting Cycle, Adjusting Entries & Financial Statements (YouTube)","provider":"Edspira / Michael McLaughlin, CPA","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Watch for intuition while you build: accounting-cycle, adjusting/closing entries, and statement-of-cash-flows (indirect method) videos. Short, exam-aligned explanations to unstick you mid-engagement. Videos are free on YouTube (edspira.com offers some paid certificate courses). Also useful: Farhat Lectures and Accounting Stuff on YouTube."},{"title":"Saylor Academy BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52","type":"course","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free, self-paced full-cycle course with a graded final exam and an optional free certificate of completion. Use its units and assessments as a structured practice/problem-set backbone and to self-test your close before you trust your own numbers. (Free account sign-in required to take the final exam and earn the certificate.)"},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Bookkeeping, Financial Statements & Ratio Analysis","provider":"AccountingCoach","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"reference","cost":"freemium","role":"reference","notes":"Free explanations, quick tests, and Q&A for any topic you stall on during the build (adjusting entries, depreciation methods, cash-flow classification, financial ratios). Core explanations across all topics and many quizzes are free; the PRO lifetime-access materials (videos, cheat sheets, certificates) are optional and paid."},{"title":"Wave — Free Cloud Accounting Software","provider":"Wave Financial","url":"https://www.waveapps.com/accounting","type":"tool","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free cloud platform to actually process the engagement: create the company, enter transactions, reconcile, and export trial balance and financial statements as your workpapers. Wave's free Starter Plan covers unlimited bookkeeping, invoicing, and reports; the paid Pro Plan adds automatic bank-feed connections. Alternatives: a free trial of Xero/QuickBooks Online, or the free GnuCash desktop app if you want full inventory."},{"title":"This Way to CPA — Licensure & State Requirements","provider":"AICPA","url":"https://www.thiswaytocpa.com/licensure/state-requirements/","type":"article","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Use for the CPA credential plan: confirm 120/150-hour education rules, the four-section (3 core + 1 discipline) CPA Evolution exam structure, and ethics requirements by jurisdiction. For other paths use ACCA at accaglobal.com (Applied Knowledge/Skills), IMA's CMA at imanet.org, and AIPB (aipb.org) or NACPB (nacpb.org) for bookkeeping credentials."},{"title":"IFRS Foundation — Issued Standards (Accounting Standards Navigator)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/","type":"reference","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Reference for footnote disclosures and to make your statements standards-compliant. Map your chosen framework: IAS 1 (presentation), IAS 7 (cash flows), IAS 2 (inventory). Free access to standards for non-commercial use requires a free IFRS.org registration; some enhanced features are behind a paid Digital Subscription. For a US-GAAP company, cross-check against the FASB Codification basic view (free registration) at asc.fasb.org."}],"project":"Run a complete engagement for a fictional small business of your choosing (e.g., \"Cedar & Co.\", a small wholesaler or services firm). (1) Write a one-page company brief and a chart of accounts, then generate a realistic 1-3 month transaction set (40-80 transactions covering sales, purchases, payroll, inventory or prepaids, a loan, and depreciation). (2) Enter everything in Wave (or Xero/QuickBooks trial), reconcile the bank, record adjusting and closing entries, and export a trial balance plus the four financial statements. (3) Write footnotes/disclosures for accounting policies, inventory, fixed assets, and debt, mapped to a stated framework (IFRS or US GAAP). (4) Build an automated dashboard (Google Sheets or Excel linked to your exported data) showing revenue/expense trends and a ratio panel — liquidity, profitability, leverage, efficiency — and write a 2-3 page analysis-and-recommendation memo benchmarking against industry data (Damodaran's pages). (5) Document a one-page internal-controls narrative, an audit-risk assessment (3-5 risks with assertions and planned procedures), a short ethics reflection against the AICPA Code or IESBA Code, and a tax/compliance summary. (6) Publish the whole package — workpapers, statements, model, dashboard, and exported software file — to a public portfolio (GitHub, Google Drive, or a simple site). (7) Produce a personal credential plan: pick CPA/ACCA/CMA/bookkeeping, confirm eligibility against the official requirements page, list your gaps, and build a dated study schedule with at least one practice-exam milestone.","milestoneCheck":"You've mastered this module when you can hand a stranger a single link and they can see, with no further explanation, that you took a company from raw transactions to a footnoted, standards-compliant statement set in real software — and the numbers tie (your exported financial statements reconcile to your trial balance, and the cash-flow statement's ending cash equals the balance-sheet cash). Self-test: can you (a) explain every adjusting and closing entry you made and why, (b) defend two recommendations in your memo using specific ratios and a benchmark, (c) name three audit risks in your engagement and the assertion each threatens, and (d) state your target credential's exact eligibility requirements and the date of your first planned practice exam? If yes to all four, you're job-ready and certification-bound.","flags":["All 9 resources verified to exist and be free/freemium as labeled (June 2026).","Saylor BUS103: original URL (learn.saylor.org/course/BUS103) returned HTTP 404. Fixed to the canonical course page https://learn.saylor.org/course/view.php?id=52 and corrected the title to the official 'BUS103: Introduction to Financial Accounting'. Final exam + free certificate confirmed; free sign-in required.","Wave: original note claimed 'Wave Mobile Money is the free tier' — that is inaccurate (Mobile Money is a separate Africa-only product). Corrected to reflect Wave's free Starter Plan (bookkeeping/invoicing/reports) vs. the paid Pro Plan (auto bank feeds). cost=free retained.","Edspira: changed type label and URL to point directly at the free YouTube channel (the canonical free resource); edspira.com itself sells some paid certificate courses, so the YouTube link better matches the 'free' claim. Provider attributed to founder Michael McLaughlin, CPA.","Damodaran: PDF confirmed live (314KB, served from NYU Stern). Reclassified type from 'course' to 'article' since it is a standalone lecture-notes PDF, not a course.","IFRS Foundation: page confirmed but access to the standards now requires a free IFRS.org registration (and some features sit behind a paid Digital Subscription). Kept cost=free with that caveat added to notes.","AccountingCoach freemium status confirmed (free explanations/quizzes/Q&A; paid PRO lifetime access).","OpenStax, This Way to CPA, and Damodaran confirmed free and on-topic; OpenStax note expanded to mention free online/PDF access.","Coverage gap: the bundle has strong full-cycle, analysis, and IFRS coverage but thin US-GAAP-specific and payroll/tax-compliance anchors — the FASB Codification (asc.fasb.org, free registration) is only mentioned in a note, not a standalone resource; consider adding it and an IRS Small Business / payroll-tax reference for the tax-compliance deliverable.","Minor: CPA exam structure described as '3 core + 1 discipline' reflects the 2024 CPA Evolution model — accurate as of 2026; verify against the live AICPA page since jurisdiction rules evolve."]},{"id":"6.2","title":"Exam Readiness & Practice Simulations","track":"Track 6 — Capstone & Certification","summary":"This module converts accumulated subject knowledge into pass-readiness for the certifications this curriculum advertises (CPA, CMA, EA, ACCA, and bookkeeping certificates). Learners locate the official free sample tests, blueprints, and retired-question banks published by each exam body, then learn to build a topic-to-blueprint study plan and sit full mock exams under realistic timed conditions. It covers the distinct question formats — timed MCQ, CPA task-based simulations (TBS), CMA essays, and EA representation scenarios — and emphasizes diagnosing wrong answers by root cause. EA candidates additionally practice Circular 230 representation and practitioner-conduct questions.","whyItMatters":"Knowing the material and passing a timed, format-specific professional exam are different skills, and the credential — not the coursework — is what employers and state boards recognize. Deliberate timed simulation against the official blueprint is the single highest-leverage predictor of a first-attempt pass.","outcomes":["Locate and download the official, free blueprint/content outline and sample test for at least one target credential (CPA, CMA, EA, ACCA, or a bookkeeping certificate) and map every tested area back to the curriculum modules that cover it","Build a dated, hours-budgeted study plan that sequences weakest-area-first and schedules at least two full mock sittings before the exam date","Sit a full sample/mock exam under strict timed, single-session, closed-note conditions and pace MCQs to the per-question time budget","Work the non-MCQ formats: complete a CPA task-based simulation, draft a CMA essay response, and answer an EA representation scenario","Apply Circular 230 rules to representation questions — who may practice before the IRS, the scope of EA representation, and practitioner duties/sanctions","Diagnose every missed question by root cause (knowledge gap vs. misread vs. timing) and convert the diagnosis into a targeted remediation list","Score a mock against the official passing standard and write a defensible go/no-go readiness decision"],"prerequisites":["6.1"],"estimatedHours":"40-55","resources":[{"title":"CPA Exam Sample Tests and Tutorial","provider":"AICPA & CIMA (ThisWayToCPA)","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/resources/article/get-familiar-with-the-cpa-exam-by-practicing-with-our-sample-tests","type":"official sample exam / interactive practice","cost":"Free","role":"Primary anchor — official timed mock and format trainer","notes":"Verified live and free. Use the free official sample test, which runs in the same software as the real test center and includes MCQ testlets, task-based simulations (TBS), and written communication tasks (WCT) across AUD, FAR, REG, ISC, BAR, and TCP. Sit it once cold for a baseline (up to ~2 hours), then again after remediation. This is your authoritative format-and-timing reference for the CPA path; pair it with the blueprint resource below."},{"title":"Uniform CPA Examination Blueprints (2026) + Free CPA Prep Resources","provider":"AICPA & CIMA / ThisWayToCPA","url":"https://www.thiswaytocpa.com/exam/articles/passing-exam/free-stuff/","type":"blueprint / study-plan reference","cost":"Free","role":"Study-plan backbone — map topics to tested skills","notes":"Verified live and free. Download the current Blueprints booklet (content areas, representative tasks, and skill levels per section) and the exam booklet/FAQs. Use it to build your topic-to-blueprint tracker and to sequence study weakest-area-first. For the blueprint PDF specifically, search for: 'AICPA CPA Exam Blueprints 2026'."},{"title":"Sample Special Enrollment Examination (SEE) Questions & Answers","provider":"IRS (Internal Revenue Service)","url":"https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/enrolled-agents/sample-special-enrollment-examination-questions-and-answers","type":"official sample questions","cost":"Free","role":"EA practice source — official MCQ samples","notes":"Verified live and free (official IRS). Work the IRS's official sample SEE questions across all three parts (Individuals; Businesses; Representation, Practices & Procedures). Note: effective March 1, 2026 the SEE is administered by PSI Services (not Prometric) — confirmed accurate; visit PSI's SEE page for the current test-drive/interface tutorial and updated sample resources (search for: 'PSI Special Enrollment Examination sample test')."},{"title":"Treasury Department Circular No. 230 (Regulations Governing Practice before the IRS)","provider":"IRS","url":"https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/office-of-professional-responsibility-and-circular-230","type":"primary source / reference","cost":"Free","role":"EA representation & conduct practice","notes":"URL corrected to the verified canonical IRS page (the bundle's original slug redirected here). For the full regulation text, read the PDF at irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/pcir230.pdf — Subparts A and B for SEE Part 3 (who may practice before the IRS, scope and limits of EA representation, due-diligence and conduct duties) and Subpart C (sanctions). Use it to answer representation scenarios and to self-check Circular 230 MCQs. Search for: 'IRS Circular 230 PDF'."},{"title":"CMA Practice Quiz + Sample MCQ and Essay Questions","provider":"IMA (Institute of Management Accountants)","url":"https://www.imanet.org/ima-certifications/cma-certification/prepare/resources","type":"official sample exam / question bank","cost":"Free","role":"CMA practice source — MCQ + essay format","notes":"Verified live and free. Use IMA's free CMA Practice Quiz (ten randomly drawn retired questions), the Prometric interface/exam simulator, and the downloadable sample multiple-choice and essay PDFs for Parts 1 and 2. Practice the essay/constructed-response format here, not just MCQ. Search for: 'IMA CMA examination sample questions and essays'."},{"title":"ACCA CBE Practice Platform & Specimen Exams","provider":"ACCA Global","url":"https://www.accaglobal.com/us/en/student/exam-support-resources/practice-tests.html","type":"official specimen exams / practice platform","cost":"Free (with free myACCA account)","role":"ACCA practice source — live-format specimen exams","notes":"Verified: the CBE Practice Platform is free for all registered ACCA students across Applied Knowledge, Applied Skills, and Strategic Professional. Log in with a myACCA account to sit specimen and past-exam content in the real exam layout, then self-mark against the published marking guides and sample answers. Direct specimen site: specimen.accaglobal.com. Use the Applied Knowledge/Skills specimens that match your target exam."},{"title":"AccountingCoach — Quizzes, Crosswords & Q&A","provider":"AccountingCoach (Harold Averkamp)","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","type":"practice problems / quizzes","cost":"Free (Pro tier optional)","role":"Supplement — drilling fundamentals and bookkeeping-certificate readiness","notes":"Verified: core quizzes, Q&A, and explanations are free (Pro upgrade optional). Use the free topic quizzes and Q&A to shore up bookkeeping and financial-accounting fundamentals before timed drills, and as a stand-in question bank for bookkeeping-certificate (AIPB/NACPB-style) prep. Best for closing red/amber topics flagged in your tracker, not for full timed simulation."},{"title":"Farhat Lectures — CPA / CMA / EA Exam Walkthroughs","provider":"Prof. Mansour Farhat (YouTube)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","type":"video series","cost":"Free","role":"Video series for intuition and worked exam questions","notes":"Verified channel; provider name corrected (instructor is Mansour Farhat, not 'Hisham'). Use the free YouTube playlists for exam-style worked problems and concept refreshers tied to CPA/CMA/EA topics. Watch targeted videos on your weakest blueprint areas and to see how to attack TBS-style and computational questions; do not substitute passive watching for timed practice. Search for: 'Farhat Lectures CPA exam'."}],"project":"Run a four-week \"exam simulation block.\" (1) Pick the certification you are actually targeting (CPA section, CMA part, EA part, ACCA exam, or a bookkeeping certificate). (2) Download that body's official blueprint/content outline and map each tested area to where you studied it in this curriculum, scoring yourself red/amber/green per topic in a tracker. (3) Build a written, dated study plan that allocates hours by weakest-area-first and schedules at least two full mock sittings. (4) Sit the official free sample test once cold (baseline) under strict timed, single-session, no-notes conditions; record your raw score, time per question, and every wrong answer with the reason (knowledge gap vs. misread vs. timing). (5) Remediate the top gaps for two weeks using the MCQ banks and at least three task-based/essay simulations (CPA TBS, CMA essay, or EA representation scenario applying Circular 230 rules on who may practice and conduct/sanctions). (6) Sit a second full timed mock, re-score, and write a one-page \"go / no-go\" readiness memo comparing the two attempts against the passing standard (e.g., CPA scaled 75, CMA ~360/500, EA scaled 105) and stating your decision and remaining gaps. Deliverables: the topic-to-blueprint tracker, the dated study plan, two scored mock logs, and the go/no-go memo.","milestoneCheck":"You can take the official free sample test for your target credential cold, under timed single-session conditions, and score at or above the passing standard (e.g., CPA scaled ~75, CMA ~360/500, EA scaled ~105) — and on a second timed mock your score improves and your per-question pacing stays within budget. You can explain, for any missed item, whether it was a knowledge gap, a misread, or a timing failure, and point to where the topic sits in the official blueprint. For EA, you can correctly answer a Circular 230 representation/conduct scenario and state who may represent a taxpayer and in what scope.","flags":["All 9 resources verified to exist, be free (or free-to-audit), accurately attributed, reputable, and on-topic as of June 2026; none dropped.","FIXED URL — Circular 230: the bundle's slug irs.gov/tax-professionals/circular-230-tax-professionals redirects to the canonical IRS page; updated to the verified canonical URL irs.gov/tax-professionals/office-of-professional-responsibility-and-circular-230. The full-text PDF (irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/pcir230.pdf, Rev. 6-2014) remains the best source for reading Subparts A/B/C and is referenced in the notes.","FIXED PROVIDER — Farhat Lectures: instructor's first name was wrong in the bundle ('Prof. Hisham Farhat'). The channel (youtube.com/@AccountingLectures) is run by Prof. Mansour Farhat; corrected. Channel and CPA/CMA/EA exam-question content confirmed.","VERIFIED CLAIM — EA SEE: the bundle's note that the SEE moved from Prometric to PSI Services effective March 1, 2026 is accurate; candidates should consult PSI's SEE page for the current interface tutorial. The IRS official sample-questions page itself remains live and free.","MINOR — CPA sample test: the AICPA sample test includes MCQ, task-based simulations (TBS), AND written communication tasks (WCT) across AUD, FAR, REG, ISC, BAR, TCP; bundle omits WCT but this does not affect accuracy of the resource.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — secondary deep-link paths (specimen.accaglobal.com, quiz.ima.ninja) were not individually fetched but the primary provider pages and free-access model for ACCA (free with myACCA account) and IMA were confirmed."]}]}],"saudi":{"title":"The Saudi Track: Mastering Accounting for the Kingdom (SOCPA Overlay)","tagline":"Learn accounting the world over — then make it count in the Kingdom. A free, open path from global fundamentals to fully SOCPA-, ZATCA- and Vision 2030-ready practice.","intro":"This track is the Saudi Arabia (KSA) jurisdiction overlay for the Open Accounting Curriculum — a free, OSSU/Odin-Project-style path to becoming a working accountant. It does NOT replace the standards-agnostic global core; it layers on top of it. The global core teaches universal principles (the accounting equation, double-entry, the IFRS conceptual framework, audit logic, professional ethics). This overlay teaches what a Saudi accountant must do differently to apply those principles legally and competitively inside the Kingdom.\n\nWhy a separate track? Saudi Arabia does not adopt raw IFRS — it applies \"IFRS as endorsed in KSA\" through the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA), which runs a structured endorsement process (translation plus technical, Sharia and legal review) before any IASB standard becomes binding, sometimes adding local disclosures. Tax is unusual too: the Kingdom runs a dual system of Zakat (a 2.5% Islamic levy on the zakat base for Saudi/GCC-owned shares) and a 20% Corporate Income Tax (on non-Saudi/foreign-owned shares), both administered by the Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA, formed in 2021 by merging GAZT with the General Authority of Customs). On top of that sit 15% VAT (since 1 July 2020), mandatory e-invoicing (the FATOORAH program, Phase 1 from December 2021 and Phase 2 integration in waves from January 2023), a new Companies Law (effective 19 January 2023), and a payroll regime built on GOSI social insurance, the Wage Protection System (WPS) and end-of-service benefits under the Labor Law.\n\nAll of this is accelerating under Vision 2030, which is professionalizing the finance function, deepening the Saudi Exchange (Tadawul) capital market, and driving demand for Saudis who hold the SOCPA Fellowship. This overlay is your map to that opportunity. Each Saudi module names the global core module(s) you should finish first, then tells you exactly what changes in the Saudi context.","howToUse":["Start with the global core. Do not begin a Saudi overlay module until you have completed the global module(s) it pairs with (listed in the Overlay Map). The global core gives you the standards-agnostic foundation the overlay assumes.","Find your global module in the Overlay Map, then open the matching Saudi (SA.x) module. Read the one-line 'whatChanges' first so you know the single most important difference before you dive in.","Layer, do not relearn. In each overlay module you only study the KSA-specific delta — what SOCPA endorsed, what ZATCA requires, what the Companies Law mandates — not the underlying concept you already learned globally.","Always confirm rules against primary sources. Saudi rules change fast (VAT moved to 15% in 2020; ZATCA was created in 2021; the Companies Law took effect in 2023; e-invoicing rolls out in waves). Use the Regulators list to check the live rate, threshold, or e-invoicing wave before relying on any number.","Sequence the tax and payroll modules early if you intend to work in KSA practice: SA.3 (Zakat/CIT/WHT), SA.4 (VAT & FATOORAH) and SA.6 (GOSI/WPS/EOSB) are the day-one survival skills for any Saudi finance role.","Use SA.10 (Arabic resources) in parallel throughout — official filings, ZATCA portals and SOCPA exams operate in Arabic, so build the bilingual vocabulary as you go rather than at the end.","Finish with SA.9 to map your path to the SOCPA Fellowship and professional certification, the credential that unlocks signing/audit roles in the Kingdom."],"overlayMap":[{"saudiModule":"SA.1 The Saudi Accounting Landscape & SOCPA","pairsWithGlobal":["0.1 Orientation to Accounting","1.1 Foundations of Financial Accounting"],"whatChanges":"You map the Kingdom's regulatory ecosystem (SOCPA, ZATCA, CMA, MoC) and learn that the standard-setter and professional body is SOCPA, not the IASB or a Western institute."},{"saudiModule":"SA.2 IFRS as Endorsed in KSA & the SOCPA Endorsement Framework","pairsWithGlobal":["1.4 The IFRS Conceptual Framework","1.5 Financial Statement Presentation (IAS 1)","5.3 Advanced IFRS Topics"],"whatChanges":"You apply 'IFRS as endorsed in KSA' — IASB standards filtered through SOCPA's translation, technical, Sharia and legal review, with SOCPA-added local disclosures, plus IFRS for SMEs as the default for non-PIEs."},{"saudiModule":"SA.3 Saudi Taxation I — Zakat, Corporate Income Tax & Withholding Tax (ZATCA)","pairsWithGlobal":["4.1 Introduction to Taxation","1.10 Income Taxes (IAS 12)"],"whatChanges":"You compute the dual system: 2.5% Zakat on the zakat base for Saudi/GCC ownership, 20% Corporate Income Tax on foreign ownership, and 5%-20% withholding tax — all filed with ZATCA."},{"saudiModule":"SA.4 Saudi Taxation II — VAT & E-Invoicing (FATOORAH)","pairsWithGlobal":["1.11 Accounting for Sales Taxes & VAT","4.1 Introduction to Taxation"],"whatChanges":"You apply the 15% standard VAT and produce compliant e-invoices under ZATCA's FATOORAH program (Phase 1 generation, Phase 2 integration/clearance via the Fatoora platform)."},{"saudiModule":"SA.5 Saudi Business & Companies Law","pairsWithGlobal":["4.2 Business Law & Forms of Organization"],"whatChanges":"You work under the new Saudi Companies Law (effective 19 January 2023) and its single framework for all entity types, registering and filing through the Saudi Business Center and Ministry of Commerce."},{"saudiModule":"SA.6 Saudi Payroll — GOSI, WPS, End-of-Service & Labor Law","pairsWithGlobal":["1.11 Payroll & Employee Benefits Accounting"],"whatChanges":"You run KSA payroll: GOSI social-insurance contributions (Saudi vs. non-Saudi rates, SANED), the Wage Protection System, and end-of-service benefit accruals under the Labor Law."},{"saudiModule":"SA.7 Auditing & Assurance in KSA (ISA as Endorsed)","pairsWithGlobal":["2.4 Audit & Assurance Fundamentals","2.5 Internal Controls"],"whatChanges":"You audit under ISA as endorsed by SOCPA, applying SOCPA licensing, quality-control and local reporting requirements rather than a generic ISA baseline."},{"saudiModule":"SA.8 Public-Sector & Government Accounting in KSA","pairsWithGlobal":["5.1 Governmental & Non-Profit Accounting"],"whatChanges":"You follow the Kingdom's transition to accrual-based public-sector accounting (IPSAS-aligned) led by the Ministry of Finance, instead of a generic government model."},{"saudiModule":"SA.9 SOCPA Fellowship & Professional Certification Roadmap","pairsWithGlobal":["6.1 Professional Certification Pathways","6.2 Accounting Careers & Continuing Education"],"whatChanges":"You target the SOCPA Fellowship and KSA certification/CPD route as your primary credential, mapping how global certs (ACCA/CPA/CMA) interact with SOCPA requirements."},{"saudiModule":"SA.10 Arabic-Language Resources for Saudi Accountants","pairsWithGlobal":["0.1 Orientation to Accounting"],"whatChanges":"You build the bilingual (Arabic/English) accounting vocabulary and learn to navigate Arabic-language regulator portals, filings and the SOCPA exam, which the global core does not cover."}],"regulators":[{"name":"SOCPA — Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants","role":"National accounting & auditing standard-setter and professional body; runs the IFRS/ISA endorsement process and the SOCPA Fellowship/certification.","url":"https://socpa.org.sa"},{"name":"ZATCA — Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority","role":"Administers Zakat, Corporate Income Tax, Withholding Tax, 15% VAT, Customs and the FATOORAH e-invoicing program (formed 2021 by merging GAZT and Customs).","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa"},{"name":"CMA — Capital Market Authority","role":"Regulates the Saudi capital market, listed (public-interest) entities and securities disclosure.","url":"https://cma.org.sa"},{"name":"Saudi Exchange (Tadawul)","role":"The Kingdom's stock exchange; sets listing and continuous financial-reporting obligations for listed companies.","url":"https://www.saudiexchange.sa"},{"name":"Ministry of Commerce (MoC)","role":"Oversees company registration and the Companies Law; supervises SOCPA; operates the Saudi Business Center.","url":"https://mc.gov.sa"},{"name":"Ministry of Human Resources & Social Development (HRSD)","role":"Administers the Labor Law, Wage Protection System (WPS), Saudization (Nitaqat) and end-of-service rules.","url":"https://hrsd.gov.sa"},{"name":"GOSI — General Organization for Social Insurance","role":"Runs social-insurance and SANED unemployment contributions, pensions and occupational-hazard coverage.","url":"https://www.gosi.gov.sa"},{"name":"Ministry of Finance (MoF)","role":"Sets fiscal policy and leads public-sector (government) accounting reform, including the move to accrual/IPSAS-aligned reporting.","url":"https://www.mof.gov.sa"},{"name":"SAMA — Saudi Central Bank","role":"Regulates banks, insurance and finance companies and their specialized financial-reporting requirements.","url":"https://www.sama.gov.sa"}],"keyFacts":["Currency: the Saudi Riyal (SAR), pegged at SAR 3.75 per USD.","Standards framework: 'IFRS as endorsed in KSA' for public-interest entities and IFRS for SMEs for other entities, endorsed and supplemented by SOCPA (not raw IASB adoption).","Professional body & standard-setter: SOCPA — the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants, which also confers the SOCPA Fellowship.","VAT: standard rate 15%, in force since 1 July 2020 (raised from 5%), administered by ZATCA; zero-rated and exempt categories apply.","Zakat vs. Corporate Income Tax: Zakat is 2.5% of the zakat base on Saudi/GCC-owned shares, while a 20% Corporate Income Tax applies to foreign-owned shares; withholding tax ranges 5%-20% — all under ZATCA (formed 2021 from GAZT + Customs).","E-invoicing (FATOORAH): mandatory under ZATCA — Phase 1 (generation) from 4 December 2021 and Phase 2 (integration/clearance via the Fatoora platform) rolled out in waves from 1 January 2023.","Companies Law: the new Saudi Companies Law took effect on 19 January 2023, providing a single framework for all entity types (with a bylaw-alignment compliance deadline that ran to January 2025).","Payroll/social insurance: GOSI contributions plus the SANED unemployment scheme, the Wage Protection System (WPS) and statutory end-of-service benefits under the Saudi Labor Law govern employment costs."],"modules":[{"id":"SA.1","title":"The Saudi Accounting Landscape & SOCPA","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This overlay orients the learner to how accounting actually works in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia before any technical standard is studied. It covers SOCPA — the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (renamed from \"Certified Public Accountants\" in 2021) — which translates, reviews for Sharia/legal compatibility, and endorses IFRS for use in KSA, plus the regulator map every Saudi accountant must navigate: ZATCA (VAT, Zakat, customs, e-invoicing), CMA and the Saudi Exchange/Tadawul for listed entities, the Ministry of Commerce (commercial registration and the Companies Law), MHRSD and GOSI (labor and social insurance), the Ministry of Finance, and SAMA for banks and insurers. It ties the whole field to Vision 2030 and the rapid professionalization of Saudi accounting. The goal is a working mental model of \"who requires what,\" not deep mechanics — those come in later modules.","whyItMatters":"Anyone doing accounting in Saudi Arabia must know which regulator owns which obligation: filing the wrong return, missing the 120-day Zakat deadline, or mis-stating that statements follow plain IFRS rather than \"IFRS as endorsed in KSA\" creates real compliance and audit exposure. The SOCPA Fellowship exam — the credential to sign audit reports in the Kingdom — assumes fluency in the SOCPA endorsement mechanism, Zakat/tax administration, and the local legal framework, so this landscape is foundational to both employment and certification. Because the rules changed fast (VAT to 15% in 2020, ZATCA formed in 2021, e-invoicing/FATOORAH from 2021, new Companies Law in 2023, the new GOSI social-insurance system from July 2024), knowing where the live official source lives matters more than memorizing any single figure.","outcomes":["Explain SOCPA's mandate and history, including its 2021 rename from the Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants to the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants, and its role as standard-setter, endorser, and certifier.","Describe what 'IFRS as endorsed in KSA' means — IFRS as issued by the IASB plus SOCPA additions/disclosures and a Sharia-and-legal compatibility review — and identify who must apply full endorsed IFRS (publicly accountable / listed entities) versus IFRS for SMEs.","Draw the Saudi regulator map and match each body to its obligation: ZATCA (VAT, Zakat, customs, e-invoicing), CMA + Saudi Exchange/Tadawul (listed-company disclosure), Ministry of Commerce (commercial registration & Companies Law), MHRSD + GOSI (labor & social insurance), Ministry of Finance, and SAMA (banks & insurers).","State the headline current parameters and verify them against the official source: 15% standard VAT (since 1 July 2020), ~2.5% Zakat with a 120-day filing window, 20% corporate income tax on the foreign-owned share, the Companies Law in force since 19 January 2023, and FATOORAH e-invoicing phased from December 2021 (Phase 2 integration from January 2023).","Distinguish Zakat (Saudi/GCC-owned share, ~2.5%) from corporate income tax (foreign-owned share, 20%) and explain how mixed-ownership entities are assessed.","Connect the professionalization of Saudi accounting — SOCPA Fellowship, IFRS adoption, e-invoicing, ZATCA digitization, the 2024 GOSI reform — to Vision 2030 economic-diversification goals."],"estimatedHours":"5-7","resources":[{"title":"SOCPA — Official Website (About, Standards & Media Center)","provider":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/socpa/home.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"Official primary source / website","cost":"Free","role":"Anchor primary source for SOCPA's mandate, history, and the IFRS endorsement process","notes":"VERIFIED loads in English (June 2026). Read the 'About us' page (socpa.org.sa/Socpa/About-Socpa/About-us.aspx?lang=en-us) for SOCPA's role and the 2021 rename (formerly Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants). Use the Media Center / News section for the latest endorsed IFRS editions. Bilingual site — switch the lang toggle; some technical standards and exam content is Arabic-only (note for non-Arabic learners). Search for: 'SOCPA About us' and 'SOCPA endorsed IFRS'."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — IFRS Jurisdiction Profile","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/saudi-arabia/","type":"Official primary source (standard-setter)","cost":"Free","role":"Authoritative neutral confirmation of how IFRS is applied in KSA and who must use full IFRS vs. IFRS for SMEs","notes":"VERIFIED current (June 2026). Confirms IFRS is required for all publicly accountable entities and permitted for SMEs, that SOCPA endorses IFRS plus local additions/disclosures with a technical/legal/Sharia compatibility review, and that those additions do not impair an IFRS-compliance assertion. A downloadable PDF profile is linked from the page. English. Preferred over IAS Plus for the current endorsement picture."},{"title":"ZATCA — Official Portal (E-Invoicing/FATOORAH, VAT & Zakat Guidelines)","provider":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Official primary source / regulator","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source to verify the 15% VAT rate, Zakat rules, and the FATOORAH e-invoicing phases/waves","notes":"VERIFIED loads, free (June 2026). ZATCA was formed in 2021 by merging GAZT and the General Authority of Customs. E-Invoicing page confirms FATOORAH Phase 1 (Generation, from 4 Dec 2021) and Phase 2 (Integration, from 1 Jan 2023, rolling waves). For Zakat, use the Guidelines hub (https://zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx) and the current 'Implementing Regulations for Zakat Collection 1445H/2024' (https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Documents/ZAKAT%20COLLECTION.pdf) to confirm the ~2.5% rate, the sources-of-funds Zakat base, and the 120-day filing deadline. NOTE: the older 'Zakat General Simplified Guideline' direct PDF intermittently 404s — use the hub/regulations links instead. English available; the filing portal and many detailed guidelines are Arabic-first."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — Worldwide Tax Summaries","provider":"PwC","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia","type":"Reputable free secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"One-stop plain-English reference for VAT, Zakat, corporate income tax, withholding tax, and GOSI, kept current","notes":"VERIFIED free and current (June 2026). Best single secondary source to cross-check every rate and the Zakat-vs-CIT split for Saudi/GCC (2.5% Zakat) vs. foreign (20% CIT) ownership. Use the 'Corporate' and 'Individual — Other taxes' tabs. Always re-verify a headline figure against ZATCA/GOSI before quoting. English."},{"title":"Financial Reporting Framework in Saudi Arabia","provider":"Deloitte — IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/jurisdictions/asia/saudi-arabia","type":"Reputable free secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Secondary explainer of the SOCPA endorsement mechanism and the IFRS transition history","notes":"VERIFIED free (June 2026) but DATED — the page still uses SOCPA's old name ('Certified Public Accountants') and centers on the pre-2017 IFRS-convergence transition. Useful for historical context, but treat the IFRS Foundation jurisdiction profile as the authority on the current endorsement model. English."},{"title":"GOSI — General Organization for Social Insurance (Official)","provider":"General Organization for Social Insurance (GOSI)","url":"https://www.gosi.gov.sa/en/","type":"Official primary source / regulator","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for social-insurance contribution rates and the contribution base used in payroll","notes":"VERIFIED exists, free (June 2026; JS-heavy, loads bilingually). Use to confirm contribution mechanics for the project's GOSI calculation. Current context (verify on the site/calculator): two parallel schemes for Saudi nationals — the pre-3-July-2024 'existing' scheme vs. the new system for entrants from 3 July 2024 whose rates ramp annually (uplifts began July 2025, e.g. ~10.25% employee / 12.25% employer in 2025); expats covered only by the occupational-hazards branch at 2% employer-only; SAR 45,000 monthly contributory-salary cap. GOSI is the collecting body. Some pages and the calculator are Arabic-first."},{"title":"Companies Law in Force from 19 January 2023 (News & Regulations)","provider":"Ministry of Commerce, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia","url":"https://mc.gov.sa/en/mediacenter/News/Pages/19-01-23-01.aspx","type":"Official primary source / regulator","cost":"Free","role":"Primary confirmation of the commercial-registration regime and the Companies Law effective date","notes":"VERIFIED canonical MoC URL (top official result, June 2026). Confirms the new Companies Law (replacing the 2015 Companies Law and 2019 Professional Companies Law) took effect 19 Jan 2023, including the Simple/Simplified Joint Stock Company form and a two-year grace period for existing entities. NOTE: automated fetch hit a TLS certificate-chain error; the page loads normally in a browser. Bilingual — toggle to English; the official law text is Arabic."}],"project":"\"KSA Regulator Map + Mini-Compliance File.\" Pick one real Saudi company type (e.g., a Riyadh-based LLC trading company, Saudi-owned). Deliverable in three parts: (1) Build a one-page regulator map naming every body the company interacts with and the exact filing/obligation each requires — SOCPA-endorsed IFRS financial statements; ZATCA for the 15% VAT return and the annual Zakat return (filed within 120 days of year-end, ~2.5% of the Zakat base); Ministry of Commerce for the commercial registration (CR) under the Companies Law in force since 19 Jan 2023; GOSI for monthly social-insurance contributions; MHRSD for labor/Saudization; and (if listed) CMA + Saudi Exchange/Tadawul. (2) Compute a simplified Zakat base from a given mini-balance sheet using ZATCA's 'sources of funds' approach (adjusted equity + long-term liabilities − long-term/deductible assets), apply ~2.5%, and compare against the 'cannot be less than adjusted net profit' floor. (3) Compute one employee's monthly GOSI contribution split (Saudi national, existing pre-3-July-2024 scheme vs. new scheme with annual rate uplifts that began ramping in July 2025; expat at 2% employer-only occupational-hazards) using the SAR 45,000 cap, and state which body collects it. Cite the official source you used for each rate.","milestoneCheck":"Without notes, the learner can: (1) name SOCPA and explain in two sentences what 'IFRS as endorsed in KSA' adds to IASB IFRS; (2) correctly assign at least six obligations (VAT return, Zakat return, commercial registration, social-insurance contributions, listed-company disclosure, bank/insurer supervision) to the right regulator (ZATCA, ZATCA, Ministry of Commerce, GOSI, CMA/Tadawul, SAMA); (3) state the current 15% VAT rate and ~2.5% Zakat rate and name the official source where each is verified; and (4) complete the project's Zakat-base and GOSI computations with each rate cited to an official page.","flags":["VERIFIED — VAT 15% (standard rate since 1 July 2020), Zakat ~2.5% on the Zakat base, 120-day filing window, and corporate income tax 20% on the foreign/non-GCC-owned share. Confirmed via ZATCA and PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries (June 2026). Mixed-ownership entities: Saudi/GCC share assessed for Zakat, foreign share for 20% CIT.","VERIFIED — SOCPA was renamed in 2021 from 'Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants' to 'Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants' (the acronym SOCPA is retained); the 2021 framework was formalized via the Law of the Profession of Accounting and Auditing (Royal Decree M/59, 2021) and related ordinance. Confirmed via IFAC, my.gov.sa, and the SOCPA site.","VERIFIED — New Companies Law in force since 19 January 2023, replacing the 2015 Companies Law and 2019 Professional Companies Law, and introducing the Simple/Simplified Joint Stock Company. Confirmed via Ministry of Commerce news page and multiple law-firm summaries. NOTE: the official MoC URL (mc.gov.sa/.../19-01-23-01.aspx) is canonical and appears as the top MoC result, but the page returned a TLS certificate-chain error on automated fetch — it loads in a normal browser; left as-is.","VERIFIED — ZATCA formed in 2021 (merger of GAZT and the General Authority of Customs). FATOORAH e-invoicing: Phase 1 (Generation) from 4 December 2021; Phase 2 (Integration) rolling waves from 1 January 2023. Confirmed on ZATCA's E-Invoicing page (loads, free).","FIXED — The 'Zakat General Simplified Guideline' direct PDF (zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Documents/Zakat%20General%20Simplified%20Guideline.pdf) returned a 404 on automated fetch (still appears in ZATCA's search index, so it may be intermittently moved). Updated the ZATCA resource notes to anchor on the stable Guidelines hub (zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx) and the current 'Implementing Regulations for Zakat Collection 1445H (2024)' (zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Documents/ZAKAT%20COLLECTION.pdf), which is the most up-to-date primary source for the 2.5% rate, the sources-of-funds base, and the 120-day deadline.","VERIFIED with UPDATE — GOSI: a new Social Insurance System took effect 3 July 2024 for new labor-market entrants with no prior GOSI/civil-pension contributions; pre-3-July-2024 subscribers stay on the old scheme. The new-scheme contribution rates ramp annually and the increases began in July 2025 (e.g., ~10.25% employee / 12.25% employer in 2025, rising ~0.5pt/year through 2028). The SAR 45,000 monthly contributory-salary cap and the expat 2% employer-only (occupational-hazards branch) are confirmed. Project text adjusted to reflect that the new-scheme uplifts started in July 2025. GOSI collects the contributions. Confirmed via GOSI updates and PwC; learners should pull the exact current-year split from gosi.gov.sa.","DATED-BUT-FREE — Deloitte IAS Plus Saudi Arabia jurisdiction page still uses the old SOCPA name ('Certified Public Accountants') and describes the pre-2017 IFRS-convergence transition; kept as a free secondary explainer but flagged as outdated — prefer the IFRS Foundation jurisdiction profile for the current endorsement picture.","VERIFIED — All eight resources exist and are free (no paywalls). SOCPA, IFRS Foundation, ZATCA, PwC Tax Summaries, IAS Plus, GOSI, and the MoC news page all load (MoC via browser per TLS note above). PwC remains a secondary cross-check; learners are directed to re-verify any headline figure against ZATCA/GOSI before quoting.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — Specific GOSI new-scheme percentages and SANED/unemployment components change on an annual uplift schedule, and the exact split for the project's 'existing vs new scheme' computation should be read off the live GOSI calculator at fire/use time rather than memorized."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["0.1","1.1"]},{"id":"SA.2","title":"IFRS as Endorsed in KSA & the SOCPA Endorsement Framework","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"SOCPA (the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants, renamed from the former \"Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants\") is the body that endorses accounting standards in KSA under the Ministry of Commerce. It requires publicly accountable entities (listed and other large entities) to apply \"IFRS that are endorsed in the Kingdom\" — full IFRS as issued by the IASB plus a small set of additional Saudi disclosures and pronouncements for matters not covered by IFRS — effective for periods beginning 1 January 2017, while non-publicly-accountable entities apply \"IFRS for SMEs as endorsed in KSA\" from 1 January 2018. This module explains the endorsement mechanism (translation plus technical, Sharia and legal review), the transition timeline, the few points where endorsed KSA practice diverges from pure IFRS, and how zakat — a 2.5% religious levy on a net-worth zakat base assessed by ZATCA — is presented in IFRS financial statements.","whyItMatters":"Almost every set of audited financial statements you will prepare, audit, or analyze in Saudi Arabia is signed off as complying with \"IFRS as endorsed in SOCPA,\" not plain IFRS — so a practitioner must know exactly what the endorsement adds and removes, or risk an incorrect compliance assertion. The SOCPA Fellowship exam tests the endorsement framework, the 2017/2018 transition dates, the publicly-accountable-entity scoping that drives full-IFRS-vs-IFRS-for-SMEs, and the distinctly Saudi treatment of zakat in the primary statements. Getting the zakat presentation and the SOCPA-specific disclosures right is a frequent differentiator between a generic IFRS preparer and someone genuinely competent in the KSA reporting environment.","outcomes":["Explain SOCPA's role and the endorsement mechanism (translation, then technical, Sharia and legal review with public consultation) and state precisely what 'IFRS that are endorsed in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia' means relative to IFRS as issued by the IASB.","Apply the publicly-accountable-entity test to determine whether an entity reports under full endorsed IFRS or under IFRS for SMEs as endorsed in KSA, and cite the transition dates (listed/publicly accountable entities: periods beginning 1 January 2017; other entities: 1 January 2018).","Identify at least three specific ways endorsed KSA practice can differ from pure IFRS — SOCPA-added disclosures for Sharia or local-law reasons, pronouncements covering matters not addressed by IFRS (notably zakat), and transition-period measurement constraints — and confirm these additions do not by themselves prevent an IFRS-compliance assertion.","Describe how zakat is presented in KSA IFRS financial statements (historically within the income-tax/levy caption and the open IFRS 18 presentation debate) and distinguish a 2.5% zakat charge on a net-worth zakat base from income tax on accounting profit.","Locate and cite the authoritative sources for a compliance conclusion: the SOCPA professional-standards pages, the IFRS Foundation jurisdiction profile, and ZATCA guidance on zakat.","Draft a SOCPA-compliant basis-of-preparation and zakat disclosure note for a Saudi entity."],"estimatedHours":"7","resources":[{"title":"Use of IFRS Standards by Jurisdiction — Saudi Arabia (Jurisdiction Profile)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/use-around-the-world/use-of-ifrs-standards-by-jurisdiction/view-jurisdiction/saudi-arabia/","type":"reference","cost":"Free","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026). Authoritative starting point. Confirms SOCPA requires 'IFRS Accounting Standards that are endorsed in Saudi Arabia and other standards and pronouncements that are endorsed by SOCPA', that endorsement = full IFRS as issued by the IASB plus SOCPA-added disclosures (mainly for Sharia or local law), that entities in liquidation use a separate basis, and that the additions do not prevent an IFRS-compliance assertion. The downloadable Saudi Arabia IFRS Profile PDF (https://www.ifrs.org/content/dam/ifrs/publications/jurisdictions/pdf-profiles/saudi-arabia-ifrs-profile.pdf) gives the formal jurisdiction answers."},{"title":"Overview of Professional Standards / Accounting Standards","provider":"SOCPA (Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Professional-standards/Overview-of-standards.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"reference","cost":"Free","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026), English view loads. The standard-setter's own page; confirms one-go IFRS adoption with 1 Jan 2017 (listed) and 1 Jan 2018 (others) effective dates and the IFRS-for-SMEs alternative. SOCPA also publishes the full updated IFRS text and endorsement news (e.g., IFRS 18 and IFRS 19 adoption announced 2025). Much deeper material and the binding master texts are Arabic-only — flag that the binding standards are issued in Arabic. If a sub-link breaks, start from socpa.org.sa and search 'endorsed standards' / 'IFRS'."},{"title":"The Document of Endorsement of IFRSs and IFRS for SMEs for Adoption in Saudi Arabia","provider":"SOCPA (Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Professional-standards/Accounting-standards.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"reference","cost":"Free","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026) — points to SOCPA's Accounting-standards page (the Overview page above is also valid). This is the formal endorsement framework naming the two endorsed frameworks (full IFRS for publicly accountable entities; IFRS for SMEs for others) plus the additional SOCPA requirements. The core endorsement texts are issued in Arabic — flag as Arabic-language; use the English IFRS Foundation profile above as the working-language summary. Search SOCPA's site for 'Document of Endorsement of IFRSs and IFRS for SMEs'."},{"title":"Financial Reporting Framework in Saudi Arabia","provider":"Deloitte — IAS Plus","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/jurisdictions/asia/saudi-arabia","type":"article","cost":"Free","role":"secondary","notes":"Page is live but JavaScript-heavy (did not fully render in a plain fetch on Jun 2026 — load in a browser). Best concise free secondary summary of the timeline: listed entities report under endorsed IFRS for periods beginning 1 January 2017; unlisted entities under IFRS for SMEs from 1 January 2018; SOCPA removes some options, adds disclosures, and issues extra pronouncements for matters relevant in KSA (e.g., for religious reasons)."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — Corporate: Taxes on Corporate Income (Zakat & CIT rates)","provider":"PwC — Worldwide Tax Summaries","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia/corporate/taxes-on-corporate-income","type":"reference","cost":"Free","role":"secondary","notes":"URL CORRECTED (Jun 2026): the original '/other-taxes' page does NOT carry the zakat rate; this Taxes-on-Corporate-Income page does. Verified verbatim: 'Zakat is charged on the company's Zakat base at 2.5%. Zakat base represents the net worth of the entity as calculated for Zakat purposes' and 'The rate of income tax is 20% of the net adjusted profits' (oil/hydrocarbon 50%-85%). Saudi/GCC ownership is generally subject to zakat while non-GCC ownership is subject to 20% income tax; mixed-ownership entities split. Authoritative free rate source — do not quote rates from memory. ZATCA administers; cross-check the 'Overview' page."},{"title":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA) — Zakat guidance / Help Center","provider":"ZATCA (Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority, formed 2021 by merging GAZT and Customs)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/","type":"reference","cost":"Free","role":"primary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026) — official .gov.sa government site for the authority that assesses and collects zakat. Use the English Help Center / guidelines for the official zakat-base computation rules and the IFRS-transition manuals ZATCA publishes. Some detailed guides and the binding regulations are Arabic-only — flag as partly Arabic. Navigate from the homepage to Help Center > Guidelines and search 'Zakat'."},{"title":"SOCPA's Perspective — Presentation of Zakat Expense (ASAF agenda paper AP10, March 2026)","provider":"IFRS Foundation / SOCPA (Accounting Standards Advisory Forum)","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/content/dam/ifrs/meetings/2026/march/asaf/ap10-socpa-presentation-zakat.pdf","type":"article","cost":"Free","role":"secondary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026) — PDF downloads (~869 KB). Standard-setter-level paper explaining why and how zakat is presented in KSA IFRS statements: SOCPA's standard requires zakat expense as a separate line, and the live IFRS 18 debate is whether zakat can sit in the income-taxes category (IFRS 18 para 67 ties that category to IAS 12 income taxes only). Read this to ground Part C. NOTE: the IFRS 19 reference in the original outcomes was trimmed — the distinctive zakat-presentation debate is an IFRS 18 issue."}],"project":"Build a one-page \"KSA reporting framework decision memo\" plus a zakat-presentation note for a fictional Saudi entity. Part A: Given three entities — (1) a Tadawul-listed manufacturer, (2) a non-listed family LLC with SAR 40m revenue and 30 staff, and (3) a small services startup — decide for each whether it applies \"IFRS as endorsed in SOCPA\" (full IFRS) or \"IFRS for SMEs as endorsed in SOCPA,\" citing the publicly-accountable-entity test and the 2017/2018 transition dates. Part B: For the listed manufacturer, compute a simplified zakat charge: take a given zakat base of SAR 10,000,000 and apply the 2.5% rate (verify the rate against PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries; show SAR 250,000). Part C: Draft a SOCPA-style disclosure note (8-12 lines) stating that the financials comply with \"IFRS that are endorsed in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and other standards and pronouncements endorsed by SOCPA,\" and present the zakat charge — show it as a separate line on the face of profit or loss / within the tax-and-zakat caption, and add a note explaining that zakat is a religious levy assessed by ZATCA on a zakat base (net-worth basis) rather than on accounting profit, flagging that its presentation differs from pure IFRS practice. Part D: List two specific examples of where \"IFRS as endorsed in KSA\" differs from pure IFRS (e.g., SOCPA-added disclosures for Sharia/local-law reasons; pronouncements for matters not covered by IFRS such as zakat; the historical liquidation-basis and cost-model transition rules).","milestoneCheck":"Learner can, without notes: (1) state that KSA financials comply with 'IFRS that are endorsed in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia and other standards and pronouncements endorsed by SOCPA' and explain how that differs from pure IFRS; (2) correctly route a listed entity vs a small family LLC to full endorsed IFRS vs IFRS for SMEs and cite the 2017/2018 transition dates; (3) compute a 2.5% zakat charge on a given zakat base and explain why zakat differs from income tax; and (4) produce a basis-of-preparation note plus a zakat-presentation note that an examiner would accept as SOCPA-compliant.","flags":["VERIFIED (Jun 2026): zakat rate 2.5% on net-worth zakat base, and CIT 20%, confirmed verbatim on PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries (Saudi Arabia, Taxes on Corporate Income). Part B arithmetic SAR 10,000,000 x 2.5% = SAR 250,000 is correct.","CORRECTED RESOURCE URL: the PwC resource originally pointed to '/saudi-arabia/corporate/other-taxes', which does NOT state the 2.5% zakat rate (only a passing mention of zakat). Changed to '/saudi-arabia/corporate/taxes-on-corporate-income', which carries both the 2.5% zakat rate and the 20% CIT rate. Title and notes updated accordingly.","CORRECTED SUMMARY: original text read 'recently renamed the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants' — a tautology giving SOCPA's current name on both sides of 'renamed'. Corrected to note the rename was FROM the former 'Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants' TO 'Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants'.","VERIFIED transition dates: 1 January 2017 (listed / publicly accountable entities) and 1 January 2018 (IFRS for SMEs / other entities) confirmed on both the SOCPA Overview-of-standards page and IAS Plus.","VERIFIED endorsement wording: 'IFRS Accounting Standards that are endorsed in Saudi Arabia and other standards and pronouncements that are endorsed by SOCPA' confirmed on the IFRS Foundation Saudi Arabia jurisdiction profile.","VERIFIED ZATCA: zatca.gov.sa/en/ is the live official government site of the Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (formed 2021 by merging GAZT and Customs). Date and authority correct.","VERIFIED ASAF zakat paper: the AP10 March-2026 PDF on ifrs.org exists and downloads. Confirms SOCPA presents zakat as a separate line and the open IFRS 18 (para 67 / IAS 12) classification debate. Title clarified to AP10 / March 2026.","TRIMMED 'IFRS 19' reference in one outcome: the distinctive KSA zakat-presentation debate is an IFRS 18 matter (IFRS 19 is the subsidiaries-without-public-accountability disclosure standard and is not the locus of the zakat-presentation issue); changed 'IFRS 18/IFRS 19 presentation debate' to 'IFRS 18 presentation debate'.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY: the IAS Plus jurisdiction page is live but JavaScript-rendered and did not return content in a plain server-side fetch; verified as existing via search index. A browser visit is recommended. All other resources confirmed live and free.","NOTE (not changed): all resources confirmed FREE — no downgrades or drops needed. SOCPA binding master texts and parts of the ZATCA guidance are Arabic-only; this is already flagged in the resource notes."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["1.4","1.5","5.3"]},{"id":"SA.3","title":"Saudi Taxation I — Zakat, Corporate Income Tax & Withholding Tax (ZATCA)","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This module is the Saudi replacement for the US-centric direct-tax content in global module 4.1. It covers the Saudi direct-tax system administered by ZATCA (the Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority, formed in 2021 by merging GAZT and the General Customs Authority): zakat at 2.5% on the zakat base for the Saudi/GCC-owned share of an entity, corporate income tax at 20% of net adjusted profit on the foreign/non-GCC-owned share, and the mixed-ownership split that allocates a single company between the two regimes. It also covers withholding tax (5%–20%) on payments to non-residents, the arm's-length transfer-pricing rules, and the filing/assessment cycle. Learners read the global accounting-for-income-tax and conceptual-framework modules first, then layer this Saudi-specific overlay on top.","whyItMatters":"Direct tax is the single most jurisdiction-specific topic an accountant faces in Saudi Arabia: there is no US-style income tax on individuals or fully Saudi-owned firms — instead a Sharia-based zakat and a separate income tax on foreign ownership coexist inside the same entity, a structure found almost nowhere else. Anyone preparing financial statements, computing a tax/zakat provision, or advising on inbound investment in KSA must split ownership, build a zakat base, gross up withholding on cross-border payments, and meet ZATCA filing deadlines. For the SOCPA fellowship exam, the zakat/CIT/WHT framework and ZATCA compliance are core examinable content and cannot be answered from US (4.1) knowledge alone.","outcomes":["Explain why a Saudi entity can be subject to zakat, corporate income tax, or both, and allocate taxable income/zakat base between the Saudi-GCC ownership share (zakat at 2.5%) and the foreign/non-GCC share (CIT at 20%) in a mixed-ownership company","Compute a zakat base from a trial balance: start from equity/owners' capital, add long-term financing and provisions (sources of funds), deduct fixed assets, investments and deferred costs, then compare against adjusted net profit as the minimum base","Calculate the 20% corporate income tax on net adjusted profit, identifying common book-to-tax adjustments (non-deductible provisions, disallowed expenses, depreciation differences)","Apply withholding tax to payments to non-residents at the correct domestic rate (5% dividends/interest/rent, 15% royalties/payments to head office, 20% management fees, 5-20% technical/consulting services) and explain how a double-tax treaty can reduce the rate","Describe the arm's-length principle and ZATCA transfer-pricing obligations (Controlled Transaction Disclosure Form, Local/Master file, Country-by-Country Report) and the relevant thresholds","Map the ZATCA compliance cycle: registration, annual return filing within 120 days of year-end, WHT monthly remittance within 10 days, assessment, objection and appeal"],"estimatedHours":"14","resources":[{"title":"Implementing Regulations for Zakat Collection 1445H (2024)","provider":"ZATCA (Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority)","type":"Regulation / primary source","cost":"Free","role":"Primary authority for zakat","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/ZakatRegulations.aspx","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026). The current zakat bylaws (Minister of Finance Decision No. 1007, dated 19/8/1445H), effective for fiscal years starting on/after 1 Jan 2024, superseding the prior Decision No. 2216. Use as the authoritative source for what is added to and deducted from the zakat base and the 2.5% rate. Page links to the full English PDF, also reachable directly at https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Documents/ZAKAT%20COLLECTION.pdf (verified loads, ~652KB). Read the zakat-base articles; skim sector-specific rules. Arabic is the governing language — English PDF is a translation."},{"title":"Income Tax Law and Implementing Regulations","provider":"ZATCA","type":"Statute / primary source","cost":"Free","role":"Primary authority for CIT and WHT","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/IncomeTaxlaw.aspx","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026). Source for the 20% corporate income tax, the foreign-ownership scope, the withholding-tax articles, and Article 63/64 (related-party/arm's-length adjustment). Use to confirm taxable scope and WHT obligations. Arabic text is authoritative; English version provided for reference. NOTE: ZATCA has published proposed amendments to the Income Tax Law on the Istitlaa public-consultation platform — confirm whether any amended/unified income-tax law has been enacted before relying on specific article numbers (see flags)."},{"title":"ZATCA Guidelines and Manuals — Help Center (Zakat guidelines hub)","provider":"ZATCA","type":"Official guide (hub page)","cost":"Free","role":"Plain-language walkthrough","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx","notes":"REPLACED dead link (Jun 2026). The previously cited 'Zakat General Simplified Guideline' PDF (zatca.gov.sa/.../Zakat%20General%20Simplified%20Guideline.pdf) now returns HTTP 404. This verified-live Guidelines & Manuals hub is the official source for ZATCA's plain-language zakat walkthroughs (how the zakat base is built: sources of funds added, deductions subtracted, comparison to adjusted profit). From here open the current zakat general guideline / zakat-base guideline. If a specific PDF link 404s, navigate from this hub or search ZATCA Help Center for 'Zakat' guideline."},{"title":"Transfer Pricing Guidelines (Third Edition, 2024)","provider":"ZATCA","type":"Official guide (PDF)","cost":"Free","role":"Transfer-pricing reference","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Documents/Transfer%20Pricing%20Guidelines_Final_Manual.pdf","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (Jun 2026, ~7.6MB PDF). ZATCA released the third edition of the TP Guidelines on 24 June 2024. Use for the arm's-length principle, accepted methods, the Controlled Transaction Disclosure Form (filed with the income-tax/zakat return within 120 days, with a licensed-auditor affidavit), and the Master file / Local file / Country-by-Country Report documentation thresholds. Skim — focus on disclosure obligations and thresholds, not full methodology."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — Corporate (Taxes on corporate income, Withholding taxes, Tax administration)","provider":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","type":"Secondary reference","cost":"Free","role":"Best structured free overview","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia/corporate/taxes-on-corporate-income","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE and free; last reviewed 14 Jan 2026. Use as the one-stop summary of the zakat-vs-CIT split, the 20% rate, the mixed-ownership rule, and the WHT rate table (dividends 5%, interest 5%, royalties 15%, management fees 20%, technical/consulting services 5-20%). Also read the sibling 'Withholding taxes' (https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia/corporate/withholding-taxes) and 'Tax administration' pages for rates and deadlines."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia issues new Executive Regulations for Zakat Collection — Tax Alert","provider":"EY","type":"Secondary reference / news alert","cost":"Free","role":"Context on the 2024 zakat rules","url":"https://www.ey.com/en_gl/technical/tax-alerts/saudi-arabia-issues-new-executive-regulations-for-zakat-collecti","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE and free (Jun 2026). Use to understand what changed under the 2024 zakat regulations (approved by the Minister of Finance 21 March 2024, effective fiscal years on/after 1 Jan 2024, with an optional early-adoption application window of 60 days, and alignment of the base with financial-statement closing balances). Good orientation before reading the regulation itself."},{"title":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","provider":"SOCPA","type":"Professional body / exam authority","cost":"Free","role":"Exam scope and standards anchor","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/socpa/home.aspx?lang=en-us","notes":"URL FIXED (Jun 2026): the previous https://socpa.org.sa/en returned HTTP 404; the canonical English site is the home.aspx?lang=en-us form (verified live). Confirm how zakat/tax disclosure ties to SOCPA-endorsed IFRS and the fellowship-exam (Saudi-specific) syllabus. Use to align study with examinable requirements. Much of the standards/guidance content is Arabic-only — navigate the Arabic site for the full standards library."}],"project":"Take a mock mixed-ownership Saudi LLC (e.g., 60% owned by a Saudi/GCC shareholder, 40% by a non-GCC foreign investor) with a one-page trial balance: owners' equity, retained earnings, a long-term loan, provisions, fixed assets, investments, and net profit before tax. Deliverable in three parts: (1) compute the full zakat base — start from equity, add the sources of funds (long-term financing, opening provisions), deduct fixed assets and investments, then compare to adjusted net profit as the floor — and apply zakat at 2.5% to the Saudi/GCC 60% share; (2) compute corporate income tax at 20% of net adjusted profit on the foreign 40% share, showing at least two book-to-tax adjustments; (3) on a SAR 100,000 management fee and a SAR 50,000 royalty paid to a non-resident parent, calculate withholding tax (20% and 15% respectively), state the monthly remittance deadline (within 10 days of the month-end following payment), and note how a tax treaty could reduce it. Conclude with a short note stating the annual ZATCA filing deadline (within 120 days of year-end) and one SOCPA-style financial-statement disclosure of the zakat/tax provision.","milestoneCheck":"Given a trial balance and an ownership split for a Saudi entity, the learner can independently (a) determine which portion is subject to zakat versus CIT, (b) build a defensible zakat base and apply 2.5%, (c) compute 20% CIT on the adjusted-profit foreign share, (d) apply the correct WHT rate to a cross-border payment and state the remittance deadline, and (e) cite the correct ZATCA annual filing deadline — explaining at each step how the Saudi treatment differs from the US approach in global module 4.1.","flags":["RATES VERIFIED CURRENT (Jun 2026): zakat 2.5%; CIT 20% on non-Saudi/non-GCC share; WHT — dividends 5%, interest 5%, rent 5%, royalties 15%, payments to head office 15%, management fees 20%, technical/consulting services 5-20%. Confirmed against PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries (last reviewed 14 Jan 2026). No change needed.","DATES VERIFIED: ZATCA formed 2021 (GAZT + General Customs Authority merger) — correct. Annual zakat/CIT return due within 120 days of fiscal year-end — correct. WHT remitted within 10 days of the month-end following the payment — correct (added the precise wording to the project step).","DEAD LINK FIXED: 'Zakat General Simplified Guideline' PDF (zatca.gov.sa/.../Zakat%20General%20Simplified%20Guideline.pdf) returns HTTP 404 (verified twice). Several other ZATCA guideline PDFs (e.g., General Manual of Zakat) also 404'd at verification — ZATCA reorganizes the Help Center frequently. Replaced with the verified-live ZATCA Guidelines & Manuals hub (zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx), which still serves the official plain-language zakat walkthrough.","DEAD LINK FIXED: SOCPA https://socpa.org.sa/en returned HTTP 404; corrected to the canonical English portal https://socpa.org.sa/socpa/home.aspx?lang=en-us (verified live).","RESOURCE UPDATED: ZATCA Transfer Pricing Guidelines confirmed live and canonical; updated title/note to reflect that the current version is the THIRD EDITION released 24 June 2024 (was generically dated). CTDF is filed with the return within 120 days and now requires a licensed-auditor TP affidavit — added.","ALL RESOURCES FREE: no paywalled items found; no downgrades or drops required. The two ZATCA primary-source HTML pages (Zakat Regulations, Income Tax Law), the ZAKAT COLLECTION.pdf, the TP Guidelines PDF, PwC, and EY all verified to load and be free.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — pending income-tax-law reform: ZATCA has published proposed amendments to / a possible new unified Income Tax Law on the Istitlaa public-consultation platform. As of Jun 2026 the existing Income Tax Law (Royal Decree M/1 of 1425H/2004) and the 20% CIT rate remain in force, but specific Income Tax Law article numbers (e.g., the arm's-length/related-party article) and the WHT article structure could shift if a new law is enacted. Re-verify article citations before exam use.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — WHT services rate band: the 5-20% range for technical/consulting and 'other services' payments depends on payee relationship and category; PwC lists services generally at 5% but related-party/other services up to 15-20%. Treat the band as correct but confirm the specific category rate per transaction.","TRANSLATION CAVEAT (unchanged but worth noting): for zakat regs, income tax law, and SOCPA standards the Arabic text is legally governing; English PDFs are reference translations only."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["4.1","1.10"]},{"id":"SA.4","title":"Saudi Taxation II — VAT & E-Invoicing (FATOORAH)","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This overlay covers Saudi Value Added Tax (VAT), administered by the Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA), at the standard rate of 15% in force since 1 July 2020, including registration thresholds, output/input VAT mechanics, zero-rated and exempt supplies, and periodic return filing. It also introduces the basics of excise tax and, centrally, ZATCA's mandatory e-invoicing system (FATOORAH) — the Generation phase (live since 4 December 2021) and the phased Integration phase (rolling out in waves since 1 January 2023, still ongoing into 2026). The emphasis is on the day-to-day bookkeeping and compliance an accountant in KSA must execute: recording VAT on transactions, issuing compliant tax invoices, and meeting ZATCA filing and integration obligations.","whyItMatters":"VAT and e-invoicing are the most frequent and unavoidable compliance touchpoints for any business operating in Saudi Arabia, and accurate VAT accounting and FATOORAH compliance are core expectations of any accountant, controller, or auditor working in the Kingdom. ZATCA penalties for late filing, incorrect returns, or non-compliant invoices are significant, so practical fluency directly protects employers and clients. Indirect taxation is also a recurring topic in SOCPA professional examinations and in the local tax knowledge expected of licensed Saudi accountants, making this overlay essential for both employability and exam readiness.","outcomes":["Determine whether a Saudi business must register for VAT (mandatory threshold SAR 375,000; voluntary SAR 187,500 of annual taxable supplies) and explain group registration and non-resident rules.","Classify supplies as standard-rated (15%), zero-rated, or exempt, and calculate net VAT payable as output VAT minus deductible input VAT for a filing period.","Record VAT correctly in the books — VAT control/payable and recoverable accounts — and reconcile them to the ZATCA VAT return before filing monthly or quarterly.","Prepare and file a mock ZATCA VAT return, applying the reverse-charge mechanism on imported services and adjusting for bad debts, credit notes, and corrections.","Explain ZATCA e-invoicing (FATOORAH): the Generation phase versus the phased Integration phase, the difference between standard and simplified tax invoices, and the XML/QR-code, cryptographic stamp, and clearance/reporting requirements an accountant must ensure the invoicing system meets.","Outline the scope of Saudi excise tax: tobacco and energy drinks are taxed at 100% of retail price, while the former 50% flat rate on soft/carbonated and sweetened drinks was replaced from 1 January 2026 by a four-tier, sugar-content-based charge levied per litre (SAR 0 for tiers 1–2, SAR 0.79 for tier 3, SAR 1.09 for tier 4); identify which businesses (producers/importers) must register and remit it."],"estimatedHours":"16","resources":[{"title":"ZATCA — Value Added Tax (VAT) Rules & Regulations","provider":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/VAT/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Official primary source / regulations portal","cost":"Free","role":"Authoritative reference for the VAT Law, rate (15%), registration thresholds and taxpayer obligations","notes":"Start here for the official statement of the law and rates. Use to confirm the standard rate (15% since 1 July 2020) and the registration thresholds. Site is bilingual; switch to the Arabic version for the legally binding text (the English is a courtesy translation). Note: the landing page links out to the Law and Implementing Regulations PDFs rather than stating the 15% rate inline."},{"title":"VAT Implementing Regulations of the VAT Law (PDF)","provider":"ZATCA","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Documents/Implmenting%20Regulations%20of%20the%20VAT%20Law_EN.pdf","type":"Official primary source (regulation text)","cost":"Free","role":"Detailed rules on supplies, registration, invoicing, deduction of input tax and returns","notes":"Use as the rulebook for the technical mechanics: what is zero-rated vs exempt, input tax deduction rules, invoice content and return timing. English translation of the Arabic original; cross-check the Arabic if a point is contentious. If the deep PDF link breaks (ZATCA reorganises its document store periodically), reach it from the VAT Rules & Regulations landing page."},{"title":"ZATCA E-Invoicing (FATOORAH) Portal","provider":"ZATCA","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Official primary source / programme hub","cost":"Free","role":"Defines the Generation phase (from 4 Dec 2021) and the phased Integration phase (from 1 Jan 2023), wave criteria and compliance obligations","notes":"The home base for FATOORAH. Use to understand the two phases, the integration wave schedule (waves continue into 2026 — wave 24 covers taxpayers above SAR 375,000 in revenue, with integration deadlines through mid-2026), and the list of compliant solution providers. Bilingual."},{"title":"E-Invoicing Simplified Guideline & Detailed Guidelines (PDFs) — Educational Library","provider":"ZATCA","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/E-Invoicing/Introduction/Guidelines/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Official primary source (guidance / educational library)","cost":"Free","role":"Plain-language and technical explanation of e-invoice types, XML, QR codes, cryptographic stamps and clearance/reporting","notes":"Read the Simplified Guidelines first, then dip into the Detailed Guidelines and Detailed Technical Guideline for the standard vs simplified tax invoice distinction and the technical fields an accountant must verify. Some documents are Arabic-only; the core guides have English versions."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — Corporate: Other Taxes (VAT, excise, customs, RETT)","provider":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia/corporate/other-taxes","type":"Reputable free secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Concise, regularly updated professional summary of VAT, excise tax rates and other Saudi indirect taxes","notes":"Use for a fast, exam-friendly overview and to confirm excise tax scope. IMPORTANT: as of 1 January 2026 the 50% flat excise on soft/sweetened drinks was replaced by a four-tier, sugar-based per-litre charge; tobacco and energy drinks remain at 100%. Verify any figure used for real filing against ZATCA, as secondary summaries can lag regulatory changes."},{"title":"ZATCA — Goods Subject to Excise Tax","provider":"ZATCA","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Taxes/Pages/excise-tax.aspx","type":"Official primary source","cost":"Free","role":"Authoritative scope, rates and registration/remittance rules for excise goods","notes":"Use to confirm which goods are excisable and the registration/return duties on producers and importers (bi-monthly returns). Reflects the amended Executive Regulations effective 1 January 2026 for sweetened beverages. Bilingual; if the exact URL has changed, go to zatca.gov.sa and search for: Excise Tax."},{"title":"ZATCA — Help Center: VAT Guidelines (e.g., Input Tax Deduction)","provider":"ZATCA","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Official primary source (taxpayer guidance)","cost":"Free","role":"Topic-specific worked guidance on input tax deduction, returns and common VAT scenarios","notes":"Use the Input Tax Deduction and VAT return guidelines to practise the bookkeeping mechanics before attempting the project. Mix of English and Arabic PDFs; if a direct link breaks, search the Help Center for: VAT guideline."}],"project":"Take a small fictional Riyadh-based trading company (annual taxable supplies of about SAR 2 million, so above the SAR 375,000 mandatory threshold) and process one monthly VAT period. Given a list of ~15 transactions — domestic sales, a zero-rated export, an exempt financial fee, standard-rated purchases, and one imported service subject to the reverse charge — (1) record each transaction's VAT in a VAT control/payable and an input VAT recoverable ledger; (2) compute total output VAT, total deductible input VAT, and net VAT payable to (or refundable from) ZATCA; (3) complete a mock ZATCA VAT return form mapping your figures to the standard return boxes; and (4) for two sample sales, draft a compliant FATOORAH tax invoice — one standard and one simplified — listing every mandatory field (seller/buyer VAT number, invoice timestamp, line items, 15% VAT, QR code and the cryptographic stamp/UUID requirements) and state which e-invoicing phase obligations apply. Write a one-page memo explaining your treatment of the zero-rated, exempt, and reverse-charge items.","milestoneCheck":"Learner can, without aids, state the Saudi VAT rate (15%) and the mandatory (SAR 375,000) and voluntary (SAR 187,500) registration thresholds; correctly classify a given supply as standard-rated, zero-rated, or exempt and explain the bookkeeping difference; compute net VAT payable from output and input VAT including a reverse-charge item; and explain the difference between the FATOORAH Generation and Integration phases and list the mandatory contents of a compliant tax invoice. Verified by a correct mock VAT return and two compliant draft e-invoices in the project.","flags":["VERIFIED (unchanged): VAT standard rate 15% in force since 1 July 2020; mandatory registration threshold SAR 375,000; voluntary threshold SAR 187,500. Confirmed via ZATCA and multiple 2026 sources.","VERIFIED (unchanged): FATOORAH Generation phase live 4 December 2021; Integration phase began 1 January 2023 and continues in waves into 2026 (wave 24 covers taxpayers with VAT-subject revenue above SAR 375,000, with integration deadlines through mid-2026). Confirmed on ZATCA E-Invoicing portal.","CORRECTED (material): Excise tax on sweetened/soft drinks. Outcome 6 and the PwC resource note previously stated 'soft and sweetened drinks at 50%'. Effective 1 January 2026 the 50% flat rate on soft/carbonated and sweetened drinks was REPLACED by amended Executive Regulations with a four-tier, sugar-content-based excise levied per litre: SAR 0/litre (tiers 1–2: artificial sweeteners or <5g sugar/100ml), SAR 0.79/litre (tier 3: 5–7.99g/100ml), SAR 1.09/litre (tier 4: ≥8g/100ml). Carbonated drinks were folded into the 'sweetened beverages' category. Tobacco and energy drinks REMAIN at 100% of retail price. Sources: ZATCA, SPA (N2478517), KPMG, Grant Thornton, AHYSP, vatupdate (Jan 2026).","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY: Treatment of energy drinks under the Jan 2026 reform. ZATCA still lists energy drinks at 100%, but some commentary notes energy drinks containing added sugar may also fall within the new sweetened-beverage tiering. The module keeps energy drinks at 100% (the headline ZATCA position); learners filing real excise returns should confirm the specific product classification against the current ZATCA Executive Regulations.","URL UPDATED: Excise resource changed from the previous '.../Pages/ExciseTax.aspx' to the current canonical '.../Pages/excise-tax.aspx' (lowercase, hyphenated). Both currently resolve, but the lowercase-hyphen form is the live canonical link and reflects the Jan-2026 amendments.","VERIFIED: All eight... (seven) resource URLs load and are free (no paywalled or downgraded items). PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries is a free secondary source and is retained as such. No resources were dropped.","TITLE CLARIFIED: The e-invoicing guidelines resource title now reads 'Educational Library' to match ZATCA's current page title; URL unchanged and confirmed live (last updated 12 Jan 2026).","NOTE: The bundle does not reference zakat (2.5%), CIT (20%) or GOSI rates, so no correction was needed for those; the only Saudi rate/date requiring correction was the excise sweetened-beverage regime."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["1.11","4.1"]},{"id":"SA.5","title":"Saudi Business & Companies Law","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This overlay replaces the US business-law content of Module 4.2 with the Saudi legal environment that accountants must master. It covers the new Companies Law (Royal Decree M/132, effective 19 January 2023 / 26-6-1444H) and its entity types — the LLC, the joint stock company (JSC), and the newly introduced simplified joint stock company (SJSC) — plus commercial registration under the Ministry of Commerce (modernized by the 2024 Commercial Register Law that took effect 3 April 2025), and the CMA/Saudi Exchange (Tadawul) listing and continuing-disclosure regime for public companies. The goal is to recognize which legal form a client uses, what its governance and capital rules are, and what financial-reporting and disclosure obligations flow from that form.","whyItMatters":"Every engagement in the Kingdom sits on a specific entity type whose capital, reserves, governance, and reporting duties are fixed by the Companies Law; an accountant who misreads the form mis-states equity and required disclosures. The SOCPA Fellowship exam tests Business Law (Commercial Legislation) as one of its five subjects, and listed-company work additionally demands fluency in current CMA and Tadawul disclosure deadlines.","outcomes":["Distinguish the main Saudi entity types under the 2023 Companies Law (LLC, JSC, simplified joint stock company / SJSC, general and limited partnership, professional company) and identify the capital, shareholder-number, and governance rules that differentiate them.","Explain the role of the Ministry of Commerce and the commercial registration (CR) regime, including the unified national commercial register introduced by the 2024 Commercial Register Law (effective 3 April 2025) that abolished regional sub-registries.","Trace how an entity's legal form drives its accounting and reporting obligations — statutory reserve, distributable profits, board/shareholder approval of financial statements, and the duty to apply SOCPA-endorsed IFRS.","Describe the CMA and Saudi Exchange (Tadawul) framework for public companies: the Capital Market Law, the Rules on the Offer of Securities and Continuing Obligations, the Corporate Governance Regulations, and the Main Market vs. Nomu (Parallel Market) listing routes.","State the key continuing-disclosure duties of a listed issuer, including immediate disclosure of material developments and the deadlines for interim and annual financial statements filed through the Tadawul/Efsah disclosure platform.","Identify which legal events (incorporation, capital increase, conversion of form, related-party transactions, dividend distribution) trigger specific accountant or auditor involvement."],"estimatedHours":"12","resources":[{"title":"Companies Law (Royal Decree M/132) — Official English Translation","provider":"Ministry of Investment Saudi Arabia (MISA)","type":"primary law (PDF)","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source — the statute itself","url":"https://misa.gov.sa/app/uploads/2025/07/Companies-Law.pdf","notes":"Verified live (1.8 MB government-hosted PDF). Read the chapters defining each entity type: LLC, joint stock company (JSC), and the new simplified joint stock company (SJSC), plus partnerships and professional companies. Focus on capital, statutory reserve, and approval-of-accounts provisions. This is the English translation; the binding original is Arabic (see mc.gov.sa for the Arabic text)."},{"title":"Ministry of Commerce — Official Portal (Companies Law & Commercial Registration)","provider":"Ministry of Commerce, Saudi Arabia","type":"government regulator portal","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for registration and entity rules","url":"https://mc.gov.sa/en","notes":"Use for the commercial registration (CR) process, the unified national commercial register, trade-name rules, and implementing regulations of the Companies Law. Search the site for 'Companies Law' and 'Commercial Register'. Bilingual; some implementing regulations are Arabic-only. (Note: automated fetch tools may hit a TLS/certificate warning, but the site loads normally in a browser.)"},{"title":"Saudi Arabia's New Commercial Registration Law and Trade Name Law","provider":"Clyde & Co (law firm guide)","type":"secondary explainer (article)","cost":"Free","role":"Plain-English context on the 2024/2025 CR reform","url":"https://www.clydeco.com/en/insights/2024/09/saudi-arabia-s-new-commercial-registration-law","notes":"Verified live and free (published 27 Sept 2024). Use to understand the 2024 Commercial Registration Law (effective 3 April 2025) that replaced regional registration with one national register, abolished sub-registries (with a five-year grace period to April 2030 for restructuring branches), and reformed trade-name rules. English."},{"title":"Capital Market Law & Rules on the Offer of Securities and Continuing Obligations","provider":"Capital Market Authority (CMA)","type":"primary regulator rules","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for listed-company disclosure","url":"https://cma.gov.sa/en/RulesRegulations/Regulations/Pages/default.aspx","notes":"Verified live; the Rules on the Offer of Securities and Continuing Obligations (OSCO) are listed here, and the Capital Market Law (Royal Decree M/30) and Corporate Governance Regulations are reachable from the same Laws & Regulations menu. Focus on continuing-obligation disclosure duties and financial-statement filing deadlines. CMA's official domain is cma.gov.sa (old cma.org.sa links redirect). English provided; Arabic is authoritative."},{"title":"Saudi Exchange (Tadawul) — Listing Rules & Issuer Resources","provider":"Saudi Exchange (Tadawul)","type":"market-operator rules","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for listing mechanics","url":"https://www.saudiexchange.sa/wps/portal/saudiexchange/rules-guidance/capital-market-overview/listing-rules","notes":"Free public portal. Use for the difference between the Main Market (e.g., SAR 4bn min market cap threshold, 200+ public shareholders) and Nomu/Parallel Market (lighter requirements, qualified investors), admission requirements, and exchange disclosure. The deep link sometimes returns a 403 to automated tools / can change — if it fails, start at saudiexchange.sa and navigate Rules & Guidance > Capital Market Overview, or search 'Listing Rules'. English available."},{"title":"Worldwide Tax Summaries — Saudi Arabia","provider":"PwC","type":"secondary reference","cost":"Free","role":"Cross-reference of legal form to tax/zakat treatment","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia","notes":"Verified live and free (confirms standard VAT 15%, headline corporate income tax 20%; zakat is levied at 2.5% on the zakat base for Saudi/GCC ownership). Use the 'Corporate' sections to connect entity legal form (resident company, branch, mixed ownership) to zakat vs. corporate income tax exposure under ZATCA. Confirm the 'last reviewed' date when you read it."},{"title":"SOCPA Fellowship — General Rules & Program Information","provider":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","type":"exam/standards body","cost":"Free","role":"Maps this module to the SOCPA exam","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Fellowship-Authority/General-Rules.aspx?lang=en-us","notes":"Verified live; page confirms the Fellowship exam consists of five subjects — Accounting, Auditing, Zakat and Tax, Jurisprudence, and Business Law — each scored out of 100 with a 60% pass mark. Use to calibrate exam depth. Bilingual site; some technical resources are Arabic-only."}],"project":"Pick a real Saudi-listed company on the Main Market (e.g., from saudiexchange.sa) and a hypothetical small private firm. Part A: classify the legal form of each (JSC vs. LLC/SJSC) and write a one-page memo stating, for each, the governing Companies Law rules on minimum capital, statutory reserve, and who must approve the annual financial statements. Part B: for the listed company, draft a SOCPA/CMA-style continuing-disclosure note — identify a triggering material event (e.g., a board-approved dividend or a >10% capital change), cite the relevant Rules on the Offer of Securities and Continuing Obligations provision, and state the filing deadline and the Tadawul/Efsah channel used. Part C: for the private firm, outline the commercial-registration steps under the current unified national CR regime and note one obligation that changed versus the pre-2025 system.","milestoneCheck":"Given a short fact pattern describing an entity (shareholders, capital, whether shares are publicly traded), the learner can correctly name the legal form under the 2023 Companies Law, state its statutory reserve and accounts-approval rule, and — if it is listed — identify at least one CMA continuing-disclosure obligation with its correct filing deadline, citing the applicable primary source.","flags":["VERIFIED: Companies Law Royal Decree M/132 confirmed — issued 1/12/1443H (30 June 2022), effective 26/6/1444H = 19 January 2023; it replaced the 2015 Companies Regulation and introduced the simplified joint stock company (SJSC). Date in bundle is correct.","VERIFIED: SJSC is genuinely a new entity type under the 2023 law (no minimum capital, flexible governance, can issue ordinary/preference/redeemable shares) — bundle's 'newly introduced' framing is accurate.","VERIFIED/REFINED: 2024 Commercial Registration Law confirmed — approved 17 Sept 2024, published 4 Oct 2024, effective 180 days later = 3 April 2025 (bundle said 'April 2025'; refined to the exact date). It creates a unified national CR, abolishes branch/regional sub-registries, and gives a five-year grace period (to April 2030) for restructuring existing sub-registers. Added grace-period detail to the Clyde & Co note.","VERIFIED: SOCPA Fellowship exam = five subjects (Accounting, Auditing, Zakat and Tax, Jurisprudence, Business Law), each /100 with 60% pass. Bundle's 'one of five subjects' claim is correct; clarified that 'Commercial Legislation' is the topic mapped to the 'Business Law' subject.","VERIFIED: Tax facts cross-checked on PwC — VAT standard rate 15% (since 1 July 2020), corporate income tax 20%, zakat 2.5% of the zakat base. These are current as of June 2026. No rate in the bundle text was wrong.","VERIFIED: CMA official domain is cma.gov.sa (old cma.org.sa redirects); regulations page loads and lists the Rules on the Offer of Securities and Continuing Obligations (OSCO). Capital Market Law = Royal Decree M/30, reachable from the same menu.","RESOURCES: All 7 resources confirmed live and free; none downgraded or dropped. The MISA PDF URL (uploads/2025/07/) is current and loads. Changed the Companies Law resource 'provider' to MISA only (the file is MISA-hosted), keeping the cross-reference to mc.gov.sa for the binding Arabic text.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — Saudi Exchange listing-rules deep link returned HTTP 403 to the automated fetch tool. This is consistent with bot-blocking rather than a dead page (the saudiexchange.sa portal path structure is valid and the page is publicly reachable in a browser). Kept the URL but strengthened the fallback navigation note. If it 404s in future, navigate from saudiexchange.sa.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — mc.gov.sa/en triggered a TLS certificate warning in the automated fetch tool; the site is genuine and operational in normal browsers. Added a note so learners aren't alarmed.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY — Companies Law implementing regulations and CMA/Tadawul disclosure deadlines (e.g., interim FS within ~30 days, annual within ~3 months of period-end) shift via regulator amendments; learners must confirm exact current deadlines against the live OSCO rules and Tadawul/Efsah filing calendar at the time of study rather than relying on a fixed figure."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["4.2"]},{"id":"SA.6","title":"Saudi Payroll — GOSI, WPS, End-of-Service & Labor Law","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This overlay replaces the US FICA/FUTA payroll mechanics of global module 1.11 with the Saudi statutory payroll stack. Learners master GOSI social-insurance contributions on a basic-plus-housing wage capped at SAR 45,000. For Saudis who first contributed BEFORE 3 July 2024 (the \"old system\"), the long-standing combined rate is 21.5%, split employee 9.75% (9% annuities + 0.75% SANED unemployment) / employer 11.75% (9% annuities + 2% occupational hazard + 0.75% SANED). Under the 2024 Social Insurance Law reform, NEW labor-market entrants (no GOSI/pension contributions before 3 July 2024) follow a higher schedule whose annuities branch steps up 0.5% each July from July 2025 (9% → 9.5% in 2025, 10% in 2026, 10.5% in 2027, 11% by 2028): the combined rate is 22.5% for Jan–Jun 2026 (employee 10.25% / employer 12.25%) and 23.5% from 1 July 2026 (employee 10.75% / employer 12.75%). Non-Saudis carry only the flat 2% employer-only occupational-hazard contribution (SANED and annuities do not apply). Learners also master the Wage Protection System (WPS) enforced through the Mudad platform, and End-of-Service Benefit (EOSB) accrual and computation under Labor Law Articles 84–85. The Saudization/Nitaqat framework ties WPS and GOSI compliance to a firm's ability to hire and renew visas.","whyItMatters":"Every private-sector employer in KSA must register with GOSI, pay wages through WPS/Mudad on time, and accrue EOSB — these are the bread-and-butter payroll obligations a Saudi accountant touches monthly, and getting the GOSI splits (including the date-sensitive old-vs-new-entrant schedule) or the EOSB resignation tiers wrong creates real liabilities and Nitaqat penalties. For the SOCPA exam and IFRS-as-adopted-in-KSA reporting, EOSB is a defined-benefit-style obligation under IAS 19 that must be measured and disclosed, while GOSI and WPS underpin the payroll cycle, internal controls, and compliance testing an auditor is expected to understand. US payroll mechanics (FICA, FUTA, W-2 withholding) simply do not apply, so a KSA learner needs this overlay to make 1.11 usable.","outcomes":["Compute the GOSI contributory wage (basic + housing, SAR 45,000 cap) and correctly split employee vs employer contributions for an OLD-system Saudi national (21.5% total; employee 9.75% incl. 0.75% SANED / employer 11.75% incl. 2% occupational hazard + 0.75% SANED) versus the 2% employer-only occupational-hazard contribution for a non-Saudi employee.","Explain the 2024 Social Insurance Law reform — the annuities branch rising in 0.5% annual steps each July from July 2025 (9.5% in 2025 → 11% by 2028) for new labor-market entrants — apply the period-correct combined rate (22.5% Jan–Jun 2026, employee 10.25% / employer 12.25%; 23.5% from 1 July 2026, employee 10.75% / employer 12.75%), and identify which employees fall under the old (first contribution before 3 July 2024) versus new schedule.","Prepare and interpret a Wage Protection System (WPS) wage file, describe how Mudad matches it against GOSI records and contracted salaries, and state the 'pay/disburse within 10 days of period end' deadline and the Nitaqat consequences of non-compliance.","Calculate End-of-Service Benefit (EOSB) under Labor Law Articles 84–85 for both employer-termination and resignation, applying the half-month-per-year (first 5 years) / full-month-per-year (thereafter) formula on the last full wage and the resignation tiers (nothing < 2 yrs, one-third for 2–5 yrs, two-thirds RECEIVED for 5–10 yrs, full at 10+ yrs).","Book the monthly payroll and EOSB accrual journal entries and explain how EOSB is presented as an employee-benefit obligation under IFRS (IAS 19) as adopted by SOCPA.","Describe the Saudization/Nitaqat color-band system (Platinum/Green/Yellow/Red) and how GOSI registration, WPS compliance, and Saudi-headcount ratios interact to govern an establishment's visa and hiring privileges."],"estimatedHours":"8","resources":[{"title":"GOSI Official Portal — Contributors FAQ (Contributions, Rates & SANED)","provider":"General Organization for Social Insurance (GOSI)","url":"https://www.gosi.gov.sa/GOSIOnline/FAQ_Contributor&locale=en_US","type":"Official primary source / government portal","cost":"Free","role":"Authoritative source for current contribution rates and rules","notes":"FIXED LINK: the previously listed /GOSIOnline/Individuals?locale=en_US landing returns HTTP 404; this Contributors-FAQ page is the live, English-toggle equivalent and covers the annuities (18% combined old-system), occupational-hazard (2%) and SANED branches and eligibility (SANED is Saudi-nationals only). The SAR 45,000 contributory-wage cap and the new-entrant rate schedule are also confirmable from the GOSI site (try gosi.gov.sa home if a sub-page moves). Bilingual; some detailed circulars are Arabic-only (flagged). Treat GOSI as the rate-of-record over any third-party summary."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia — Individual: Other Taxes (Social Security / GOSI)","provider":"PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries","url":"https://taxsummaries.pwc.com/saudi-arabia/individual/other-taxes","type":"Reputable secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Concise, exam-friendly statement of the GOSI rate split","notes":"VERIFIED: confirms Saudi total 21.5% (employee 9.75% = 9% insurance + 0.75% SANED; employer 11.75% = 9% + 2% occupational hazard + 0.75% SANED), the 2% employer-only rate for non-Saudis, and the SAR 45,000 cap on basic + housing. NOTE: PwC states the OLD/existing-employee 21.5% rate and does NOT yet reflect the rising new-entrant schedule — cross-check the post-July-2025 new-entrant figures against GOSI or the Mercans alert."},{"title":"Mudad Business — Wage Protection System Platform","provider":"Mudad (semi-governmental, with MHRSD, GOSI & Saudi Central Bank)","url":"https://mudad.com.sa/","type":"Official primary source / government-affiliated platform","cost":"Free to browse","role":"Operational reference for WPS file upload and compliance","notes":"VERIFIED live (Arabic-first single-page app, English support; flagged). Use to understand the monthly wage-file (CSV) upload, how Mudad matches paid wages against GOSI-registered contracted salaries, the real-time compliance percentage, and the deadline (wages disbursed within 10 days of period end). Practical anchor for the project's WPS file step."},{"title":"Ministry of Human Resources & Social Development — Labor Law & Wage Protection","provider":"Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development (MHRSD/HRSD)","url":"https://www.hrsd.gov.sa/en","type":"Official primary source / government ministry","cost":"Free","role":"Source of the Labor Law text and WPS regulatory basis","notes":"VERIFIED. The consolidated Labor Law PDF (Royal Decree M/51) is downloadable from this domain (e.g. hrsd.gov.sa/sites/default/files/2023-02/Labor.pdf). Read EOSB Articles 84 (computation), 85 (resignation tiers) and 87 (exceptions) directly. Arabic text is authoritative; English translations are flagged."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia: GOSI Contribution Rates & SANED Unemployment Fund 2026 (statutory alert)","provider":"Mercans (global payroll provider)","url":"https://mercans.com/resources/statutory-alerts/saudi-arabia-gosi-contribution-rates-saned-unemployment-fund-2026/","type":"Reputable secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Plain-language walkthrough of the post-July-2025 GOSI new-entrant rates","notes":"VERIFIED live and free. Confirms the two parallel systems for 2026: existing/old system unchanged at 21.5%; new system (post-3-July-2024 entrants) at 22.5% for Jan–Jun 2026 and 23.5% from 1 July 2026 under annual 0.5% July uplifts. NOTE: this alert is rate-focused and does not deeply explain the new-entrant definition or the 2028 endpoint — use Mercans' GOSI glossary page for that background, and confirm any figure against GOSI before relying on it."},{"title":"How to Calculate End-of-Service Benefits (Gratuity) in KSA","provider":"Payroll Middle East","url":"https://payrollmiddleeast.com/how-to-calculate-end-service-benefits-in-ksa/","type":"Reputable secondary source / worked tutorial","cost":"Free","role":"Step-by-step EOSB worked examples","notes":"VERIFIED live and free (no paywall). Fully worked numeric EOSB examples covering termination vs resignation and the half-month / full-month and one-third / two-thirds / full tiers, plus an interactive calculator. Validate your own project calculation against it; legal authority remains Labor Law Articles 84–85 on the HRSD site."},{"title":"Qiwa — Saudi Labor Market & Nitaqat (Saudization) Services","provider":"Qiwa (HRSD national labor platform)","url":"https://qiwa.sa/en","type":"Official primary source / government platform","cost":"Free to browse","role":"Context for Saudization/Nitaqat and its link to payroll compliance","notes":"VERIFIED live (Arabic-first SPA with English; flagged). Use to understand the Nitaqat color bands (Platinum/Green/Yellow/Red) and how Saudi-headcount ratios plus WPS and GOSI compliance affect visa issuance and renewals — establishing why payroll accuracy is a hiring-privilege issue, not just a cost issue."}],"project":"Run a full monthly payroll for a mock Riyadh-based private-sector establishment with three employees: (a) a Saudi national hired before July 2024 on SAR 18,000 (basic 12,000 + housing 3,000 + transport allowance 3,000), who therefore stays on the OLD GOSI schedule (total 21.5%; employee 9.75% / employer 11.75%), (b) a Saudi national who is a NEW labor-market entrant (no GOSI/pension contributions before 3 July 2024, joined after July 2025), who therefore falls under the NEW rising schedule, and (c) a non-Saudi employee on SAR 9,000. For each, compute the GOSI contributory wage (basic + housing, capped at SAR 45,000), split the employee vs employer GOSI/SANED/occupational-hazard contributions at the correct CURRENT rates (for the new entrant, use the period-correct rate — 22.5% total for Jan–Jun 2026, i.e. employee 10.25% / employer 12.25%, stepping to 23.5% total, i.e. employee 10.75% / employer 12.75%, from 1 July 2026), and total the cash net pay and the employer cost. Then build the WPS wage file fields (employee ID/IBAN/basic/housing/other/deductions) you would upload to Mudad and state the payment deadline (wages disbursed within 10 days of the end of the pay period). Finally, compute the End-of-Service Benefit (EOSB) for employee (a) under two scenarios — (i) employer-terminated after exactly 7 years, and (ii) the employee resigns after 7 years — applying Labor Law Articles 84 and 85 (half-month wage per year for the first 5 years, full-month per year thereafter, on the last full wage; and for resignation the tiered entitlement: nothing under 2 years, one-third for 2–5 years, TWO-THIRDS of the award for 5–10 years — note the worker RECEIVES two-thirds, not loses two-thirds — and the full award at 10+ years). Present the result as a one-page payroll register plus a short EOSB accrual journal entry (Dr EOSB expense / Cr EOSB provision) showing the period accrual a SOCPA-reporting employer would book under IAS 19.","milestoneCheck":"Learner can, for a mixed Saudi/non-Saudi payroll, independently produce a correct monthly payroll register showing GOSI contributory wages (basic+housing capped at SAR 45,000), the correct employee/employer GOSI-SANED-occupational-hazard splits at current rates for BOTH an old-system Saudi (21.5%) and a new-entrant Saudi (period-correct 22.5%/23.5% in 2026) plus the 2% non-Saudi rate, a valid WPS wage-file layout with the 10-day Mudad payment deadline, and a correct EOSB figure for both termination and resignation under Articles 84–85 (with the 5–10-year resignation worker RECEIVING two-thirds of the award) — and can post the payroll and IAS 19 EOSB accrual journal entries while explaining the Nitaqat compliance link.","flags":["LINK FIX: GOSI resource URL https://www.gosi.gov.sa/GOSIOnline/Individuals?locale=en_US returns HTTP 404 (confirmed in both ? and & query-separator forms). Replaced with the live English Contributors-FAQ page https://www.gosi.gov.sa/GOSIOnline/FAQ_Contributor&locale=en_US, which covers the same contributions/SANED/cap content. If GOSI reorganizes again, fall back to the gosi.gov.sa home page.","RATE VERIFIED (old system): 21.5% combined for Saudis first contributing before 3 July 2024 — employee 9.75% (9% annuities + 0.75% SANED), employer 11.75% (9% annuities + 2% occupational hazard + 0.75% SANED); non-Saudi 2% employer-only occupational hazard; SAR 45,000 cap on basic+housing. Confirmed via PwC Worldwide Tax Summaries and GOSI. Correct as written for employee (a).","MATERIAL ADDITION (new-entrant rates were missing): the original bundle named employee (b) a 'new labor-market entrant' and asked for 'correct current rates' but never stated them. Verified (Mercans 2026 statutory alert + multiple payroll sources): new-system entrants (no GOSI/pension contribution before 3 July 2024) pay 22.5% combined for Jan–Jun 2026 (employee 10.25% / employer 12.25%) and 23.5% from 1 July 2026 (employee 10.75% / employer 12.75%), because the annuities branch steps up 0.5% each July (9% pre-reform → 9.5% Jul-2025 → 10% Jul-2026 → 10.5% Jul-2027 → 11% by 2028). Added these explicit figures to the project, summary, outcomes and milestone.","DATE-SENSITIVITY WARNING: the curriculum's 'current' date is 30 June 2026 — one day before the 1 July 2026 new-entrant uplift. Employee (b)'s split changes from 22.5% to 23.5% literally the next day. Learners (and any auto-grader) must use the rate for the actual pay-period month: 22.5% for June 2026, 23.5% for July 2026 onward. This is the single highest-risk number in the module.","NEW-ENTRANT DEFINITION clarified: the trigger for the new schedule is 'no contribution period under the Civil Pension Law or Social Insurance Law before 3 July 2024' (the law's reference date), NOT simply 'hired after July 2025' as the original project loosely implied. Anyone hired after July 2025 with no prior contributions qualifies, so the example still works, but the project/summary now state the precise 3-July-2024 cutoff.","EOSB WORDING CORRECTED: the original project said 'the two-thirds reduction for resignation between 5 and 10 years,' which reads as 'reduced BY two-thirds' (i.e. receive one-third) — that is WRONG. Verified against Labor Law Article 85 (HRSD Royal Decree M/51): a worker resigning with 5–10 years' service is entitled to (RECEIVES) two-thirds of the full Article-84 award. Reworded to 'receives two-thirds.' For employee (a) at 7 years: full award = (0.5×5 + 1×2) = 4.5 months × 18,000 = SAR 81,000 on termination; resignation = 2/3 × 81,000 = SAR 54,000.","VERIFIED (unchanged, correct): EOSB Article 84 formula (half-month wage per year first 5 years, full-month per year thereafter, on last full wage including fixed allowances); Article 85 resignation tiers (< 2 yrs nothing, 2–5 yrs one-third, 5–10 yrs two-thirds, 10+ yrs full); WPS deadline 'wages disbursed within 10 days of the end of the pay period' (MHRSD/Mudad); SAR 45,000 contributory-wage cap.","RESOURCES: all 7 resources verified live and FREE (no paywalls, no downgrades needed). PwC, Mercans, Mudad, HRSD, Qiwa, Payroll Middle East and the GOSI FAQ page all load; Mudad and Qiwa are Arabic-first single-page apps (English available) — already flagged in notes. No resource dropped.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY: the exact post-2026 annuities steps (10.5% Jul-2027, 11% Jul-2028) and whether any future amendment alters the 0.5% cadence should be re-confirmed against GOSI each July, as these are forward-dated reform figures. The SAR 45,000 cap is current as of mid-2026 but is a policy lever that GOSI can revise — re-verify before exam cycles.","SCOPE NOTE: this is a payroll/labor module, so the broader KSA tax constants referenced in the verification brief (VAT 15%, zakat 2.5%, CIT 20%, ZATCA formed 2021, Companies Law effective Jan 2023) do not appear in this bundle and required no correction here; they are spot-checked as still current but are out of this module's scope."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["1.11"]},{"id":"SA.7","title":"Auditing & Assurance in KSA (ISA as Endorsed)","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"External audit in Saudi Arabia is governed by SOCPA (the Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants), which operates under Ministry of Commerce supervision per the Law of the Profession of Accounting and Auditing (Royal Decree M/59, dated 27/07/1442H, corresponding to 11 March 2021; Council of Ministers approval 9 March 2021). SOCPA endorses the IAASB's International Standards on Auditing (ISA), the International Standards on Quality Management (ISQM 1 & 2, ISA 220 Revised) and the IESBA International Code of Ethics for application to all mandatory audits in the Kingdom, with limited local additions (notably audit-documentation retention of at least 10 years under ISA 230 and required footnotes in the audit report). To sign a statutory audit report a practitioner must hold a SOCPA practising licence, and auditors of CMA-listed entities need additional CMA registration; firms are subject to SOCPA's mandatory quality-assurance review cycle (at least every three years for firms auditing public companies, banks and independent governmental organizations, and every five years for other firms). This module layers that Saudi institutional and statutory framework on top of the global auditing (2.4) and professional-ethics/independence (2.5) modules.","whyItMatters":"Auditing is one of the six examinable SOCPA Fellowship subjects, and the exam tests the KSA-endorsed framework — not vanilla ISA — including the local additions and the statutory audit/exemption rules of the Companies Law (Royal Decree M/132, in force 19 January 2023). Anyone working in assurance, finance, or controllership in KSA must know which companies are legally required to be audited, who is licensed to sign the report, the exact framework reference an auditor cites, and how SOCPA quality review and the ethics/independence code constrain firms. This is foundational for working in or contracting with audit firms, listed companies, and ZATCA/CMA-regulated entities.","outcomes":["Explain how SOCPA endorses ISA, ISQM 1 & 2, ISA 220 (Revised) and the IESBA International Code of Ethics for mandatory audits in KSA, and name the two key local additions (at least 10-year ISA 230 documentation retention and required audit-report footnotes).","Determine whether a given Saudi entity is legally required to appoint a statutory auditor under the 2023 Companies Law, applying the micro/small exemption (2 of 3: revenue ≤ SAR 10m, assets ≤ SAR 10m, ≤ 49 employees) and its carve-outs (foreign entities, debt issuers, 10%-partner request, articles of association).","Describe the licensing pathway to practise — SOCPA Fellowship → full member practitioner — and the additional CMA registration required to audit listed (Tadawul) entities.","Outline SOCPA's mandatory quality-assurance review system and its legal basis (Law of the Profession, RD M/59), including the more frequent review cycle (at least every three years) for auditors of public-interest entities, banks and independent governmental organizations versus every five years for other firms.","Draft an ISA 700-style independent auditor's report worded for the framework as endorsed in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, including the opinion and basis-for-opinion paragraphs and an ethics/independence statement.","Map global ISA risk/assurance concepts (module 2.4) and ethics/independence rules (module 2.5) onto the Saudi regulatory architecture of SOCPA, the Ministry of Commerce and the CMA."],"estimatedHours":"10","resources":[{"title":"SOCPA — Auditing Standards & Media Center (adoption announcements)","provider":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/","type":"Official standard-setter website","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source","notes":"Verified live (homepage loads; Professional Standards and Media Center > News sections present, Arabic-first). Authoritative source for which ISA/ISQM standards SOCPA has endorsed and the local-addition adoption documents. English news pages exist (append ?lang=en-us). Use it to confirm the current endorsed framework and the two local additions (10-year ISA 230 retention; audit-report footnotes)."},{"title":"Accountant's Regulations / Law of the Profession of Accounting and Auditing (RD M/59)","provider":"SOCPA","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/About-Socpa/Accountant-s-Regulations.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"Primary law / regulation","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source","notes":"Verified live. NOTE: this English page currently renders the older Certified Public Accountants' Regulations (Royal Decree M/12, 13/05/1412H); the new controlling statute is the Law of the Profession of Accounting and Auditing, RD M/59 dated 27/07/1442H (11 March 2021), whose full Arabic text is the controlling version. For the current law text, also see SOCPA Media Center > News (2021) 'Saudi Council of Ministers Adopts the New Accounting and Auditing Profession Law'. Use to ground the licensing, code of ethics, and mandatory QA-review outcomes; flag as Arabic-primary."},{"title":"Licensed Accountants — Registration & Licensing (Licenses and Quality)","provider":"SOCPA","url":"https://www.socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Licenses-and-Quality/Licensed-Accountants/Registration.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"Official guidance page","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source","notes":"Verified live but renders in Arabic ('ترخيص مزاولة مهنة المحاسبة والمراجعة') even with ?lang=en-us. Use to map the route to becoming a licensed practitioner (Fellowship → member practitioner) and firm-licensing requirements. If the link shifts, search SOCPA for 'Licenses and Quality'."},{"title":"IFAC Member Organization Profile — Saudi Arabia (SOCPA)","provider":"International Federation of Accountants (IFAC)","url":"https://www.ifac.org/about-ifac/membership/profile/saudi-arabia","type":"Regulatory summary","cost":"Free","role":"Secondary — best plain-English overview","notes":"Verified live. Concise English summary confirming KSA's 'Adopted' status for ISA, ISQM 1 & 2, and the IESBA Code, the two local additions (10-year ISA 230 retention; report footnotes), and the QA-review cycle (at least every three years for firms auditing public companies, banks and independent governmental organizations; every five years for others). Use this first to orient before reading the Arabic primary sources."},{"title":"Handbook of International Quality Management, Auditing, Review, Other Assurance and Related Services Pronouncements (the ISA texts)","provider":"IAASB / IFAC","url":"https://www.iaasb.org/publications","type":"Standards (full text)","cost":"Free (download/registration)","role":"Primary source (global standards)","notes":"Verified live publications hub. The actual ISA, ISQM 1 & 2, and ISA 220 (Revised) texts that SOCPA endorses — read ISA 200, 230, 700, 701, 705 and ISQM 1 here. Free PDF download but may require a free login/registration. SOCPA adopts these as issued, so the global text plus SOCPA's adoption document = the KSA framework. Search the IAASB site for 'ISA 700' and 'ISQM 1' if the listing page paginates."},{"title":"International Code of Ethics for Professional Accountants (including Independence Standards)","provider":"IESBA / IFAC (ethicsboard.org)","url":"https://www.ethicsboard.org/international-code-ethics-professional-accountants","type":"Code of ethics (full text)","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source (ethics — overlays 2.5)","notes":"Verified live. The current edition / handbook is free to download as PDF (a paid print/marketplace version also exists, but the digital text is free). SOCPA has adopted this IESBA Code; use it for the independence, conflicts, and confidentiality content that module 2.5 introduces and that the SOCPA exam tests. Read the fundamental principles and the independence sections for audit engagements."},{"title":"Capital Market Authority (CMA) — Saudi Arabia","provider":"Capital Market Authority (CMA)","url":"https://cma.gov.sa/en/Pages/default.aspx","type":"Regulator website","cost":"Free","role":"Secondary — listed-entity layer","notes":"URL CORRECTED: the old cma.org.sa address now 301-redirects permanently to cma.gov.sa (verified live; title 'Capital Market Authority | Home'). Use to confirm the additional registration/approval regime for auditors of CMA-listed (Tadawul) entities, which sits on top of the SOCPA licence. Search the CMA site for 'registered auditors' / 'audit firms'."}],"project":"Take a one-page fact pattern for a fictional Saudi limited liability company (\"Nakheel Trading LLC\": SAR 28m revenue, SAR 9m total assets, 35 employees, wholly Saudi-owned, no debt instruments) plus a variant that is foreign-owned. (1) Apply the 2023 Companies Law exemption test to decide, for each variant, whether a statutory auditor must be appointed, and state who appoints the auditor and at which meeting. (2) Assuming an audit is required, draft a complete ISA 700-style independent auditor's report (Opinion, Basis for Opinion, Responsibilities of Management and Those Charged with Governance, Auditor's Responsibilities) worded with the correct KSA framework reference — \"International Standards on Auditing that are endorsed in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia\" — and an independence/ethics statement citing the IESBA Code as adopted by SOCPA. (3) In a short note, identify the two SOCPA local additions that distinguish this report and working papers from a plain-ISA engagement, and state whether the engagement partner would also need CMA registration if the client later lists on Tadawul.","milestoneCheck":"You can (a) state the exact audit-framework reference a KSA auditor must cite and name the two SOCPA local additions to ISA; (b) correctly decide, for a given Saudi company, whether it must be audited under the 2023 Companies Law and who appoints the auditor; (c) explain the SOCPA practising-licence pathway plus the extra CMA registration for listed-company auditors; and (d) produce a compliant mock opinion and basis-for-opinion paragraph — demonstrating you can layer Saudi statutory/regulatory requirements onto the global ISA framework.","flags":["VERIFIED: RD M/59 (Law of the Profession of Accounting and Auditing) dated 27/07/1442H = 11 March 2021; Council of Ministers approval 9 March 2021 (25 Rajab 1442H). Bundle's '11 March 2021' is correct — added the hijri date and Council approval date for precision.","VERIFIED: SOCPA adoption status 'Adopted' for ISA, ISQM 1 & 2, ISA 220 (Revised) and the IESBA Code (IFAC profile + SOCPA news).","VERIFIED: the two SOCPA local additions — (i) audit documentation (ISA 230) retained at least 10 years, and (ii) footnotes required in audit reports — confirmed via IFAC SOCPA profile.","VERIFIED: 2023 Companies Law audit exemption — not required if 2 of 3 met (annual income/revenue ≤ SAR 10m, assets ≤ SAR 10m, ≤ 49 employees), with carve-outs for foreign entities, debt-instrument issuers, a 10%-of-capital partner request, or articles of association. Multiple legal sources confirm.","VERIFIED/REFINED: Companies Law is RD M/132 (1/12/1443H), in force 19 January 2023. Some secondary sources cite 19 February 2023; the widely-cited and correct effective date is 19 January 2023 (180 days after issuance). Bundle text only says '2023 Companies Law', which is accurate; added the RD number and effective date in whyItMatters.","VERIFIED/REFINED QA cycle: at least every three years for firms auditing public companies, banks and independent governmental organizations; every five years for other firms (IFAC profile). Bundle's 'more frequent review cycle for PIEs and banks' is correct — added the explicit 3-year/5-year figures.","URL FIX: CMA homepage changed from cma.org.sa to cma.gov.sa (verified 301 Moved Permanently). Old link still redirects but the .gov.sa address is now canonical.","RESOURCE NOTE: the SOCPA 'Accountant's Regulations' English page currently displays the older CPA Regulations (RD M/12, 1412H) rather than the new RD M/59 text; flagged in the resource note with the correct current-law pointer. Page is live and free, so retained.","RESOURCE NOTE: IESBA Code page is free to download (digital PDF); a paid print/marketplace edition also exists but does not affect the free digital access — cost kept as Free.","RESOURCE NOTE: IAASB Handbook/standards are free but download may require a free registration/login — cost kept as 'Free (download/registration)'.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY: SOCPA's Arabic homepage title now reads 'الهيئة السعودية للمراجعين والمحاسبين' (Saudi Organization for Auditors and Accountants); the official English brand remains 'Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants' (acronym SOCPA unchanged). No change needed, but naming may evolve.","No resources dropped; all seven verified live and free. No paid items required downgrading."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["2.4","2.5"]},{"id":"SA.8","title":"Public-Sector & Government Accounting in KSA","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"Saudi government accounting is undergoing one of the largest public-sector reforms in the region: a phased transition (the conversion program began in 2017 under Royal Decree No. 13059, issued 16 Rabi al-Awwal 1438H) from traditional cash-basis budgeting toward full accrual-basis accounting aligned with International Public Sector Accounting Standards (IPSAS), led by the Accrual Accounting Center at the Ministry of Finance (MoF). This module overlays the global governmental/nonprofit module (5.1) by showing how IPSAS-aligned recognition of assets, liabilities, revenue, and depreciation differs from the cash-only view, and how the digital backbone — the Etimad platform — runs government budgeting, tendering, contracting, and payments. It ties the reform to Vision 2030 goals of fiscal transparency, accountability, and better decision-making across state entities.","whyItMatters":"Anyone working in or auditing a Saudi government entity, a Vision 2030 program, a public university/hospital, or a contractor that bids through Etimad must understand the cash-to-accrual shift — it changes what gets recognized, when, and how it is disclosed. The SOCPA exam expects candidates to distinguish private-sector IFRS from public-sector IPSAS, to know that SOCPA technically supports the MoF reform, and to reason about transparency mandates. Practically, the private sector touches this every time it sells to government: invoicing, contract management, and getting paid all flow through Etimad, so the accountant who understands the public-sector ledger and the platform that feeds it is far more employable in KSA's public-finance ecosystem.","outcomes":["Explain the legal and institutional basis of Saudi public-sector accounting reform (Royal Decree No. 13059, the MoF Accrual Accounting Center) and the rationale linking it to Vision 2030 fiscal transparency","Contrast cash-basis and accrual-basis (IPSAS-aligned) treatment of the same government transactions, identifying which items appear under accrual (receivables, payables, PP&E, depreciation, accrued expenses) that are invisible under cash","Describe the phased IPSAS adoption approach used by KSA government entities and the main implementation challenges (asset registers, opening balances, system change, capacity building)","Navigate the role of the Etimad platform across the government financial lifecycle — budget, tenders/procurement, contracts/awards, and payments — and trace a single procurement through it","Differentiate public-sector IPSAS from the IFRS-for-private-sector and SOCPA-endorsed framework used elsewhere in the Saudi track, and articulate SOCPA's supporting role in the reform","Draft an IPSAS-style disclosure note (e.g., property, plant and equipment or revenue) appropriate to a Saudi government entity's accrual financial statements"],"estimatedHours":"9","resources":[{"title":"Etimad Platform (official government finance & procurement portal)","provider":"Saudi Ministry of Finance / Etimad","url":"https://portal.etimad.sa/en-us","type":"website/platform","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source — the live system","notes":"Explore the public tenders/procurement section to see how government budgeting, tendering, contracting, and payments are operated digitally. Use it to ground Part 3 of the project (the Etimad procurement lifecycle). NOTE: the /en-us landing redirects to an SSO login (login.etimad.sa) for account-based services; public tenders can still be browsed via the platform's tenders search without signing in. English UI available; much underlying content and notices are in Arabic — flag Arabic-language content."},{"title":"Etimad Platform — e-services overview","provider":"Saudi Ministry of Finance","url":"https://www.mof.gov.sa/en/eservices/Pages/Etimad.aspx","type":"official webpage","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source — official description","notes":"Read MoF's own description of Etimad's modules (budget, tenders/procurement, contracts/awards, payments, employee financial rights) — confirmed live and all five modules described. Use to confirm the platform's scope and role before mapping the procurement lifecycle. If the link shifts, search the mof.gov.sa site for 'Etimad'."},{"title":"Budget Statement & Budget Performance Reports (2017–present)","provider":"Saudi Ministry of Finance","url":"https://www.mof.gov.sa/en/financialReport/Pages/default.aspx","type":"official reports / data","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source — real fiscal data","notes":"Use the annual Budget Statement and quarterly performance reports (the page lists 2017 through 2025/2026) as a real-world reference for how KSA presents public finances and transparency disclosures under Vision 2030. Pull realistic SAR magnitudes for the project. Reports are bilingual; some detailed annexes are Arabic-only — flag Arabic content."},{"title":"The Saudi Arabian Public Sector's Journey to Accrual Accounting: Lessons Learned and Key Insights","provider":"IFAC (International Federation of Accountants)","url":"https://www.ifac.org/knowledge-gateway/discussion/saudi-arabian-public-sector-s-journey-accrual-accounting-lessons-learned-and-key-insights","type":"article / case study","cost":"Free","role":"Reputable secondary — reform narrative","notes":"Best free overview of the cash-to-accrual transition, the MoF Accrual Accounting Center's role, the phased approach, and implementation lessons. Read first to frame outcomes 1-3. English."},{"title":"Leading the Implementation of IPSAS in Saudi Arabia (ME PoV, issue 37)","provider":"Deloitte Middle East","url":"https://www.deloitte.com/middle-east/en/our-thinking/mepov-magazine/game-changer/leading-implementation-of-ipsas-saudi-arabia.html","type":"professional article","cost":"Free","role":"Reputable secondary — practitioner view","notes":"Practitioner perspective (interview with the President of the MoF Accrual Accounting Center) on adopting IPSAS in KSA: project structure, asset registers, opening balances, and operational/IT/HR challenges. Use for the implementation-challenges outcome and to inform the conversion worksheet. English. (Confirmed live; an older mirror also exists at www2.deloitte.com/xe/en/... if the primary link moves.)"},{"title":"IPSAS — International Public Sector Accounting Standards (standards & resources)","provider":"IPSASB / IFAC","url":"https://www.ipsasb.org/publications","type":"standards / reference","cost":"Free (standards available to download)","role":"Primary technical reference — the standards being adopted","notes":"Reference the actual IPSAS being adopted by KSA — especially the Conceptual Framework, IPSAS 17 (Property, Plant & Equipment), and Cash Basis IPSAS — when building the accrual entries and drafting the PP&E disclosure note in Part 4. The free Handbook of IPSAS Pronouncements is downloadable from this site; some downloads route through a free login/permissions step. If the path shifts, search 'IPSASB handbook pronouncements'. English."},{"title":"SOCPA — Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (home)","provider":"SOCPA","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/","type":"official body website","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source — exam/standard-setter context","notes":"Confirm SOCPA's mandate and its supporting/technical role in the public-sector reform, and how this contrasts with the IFRS-as-endorsed-by-SOCPA framework used in the private-sector modules. NAME NOTE: SOCPA now stands for 'Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants' (renamed from 'Certified Public Accountants') — same acronym. Site is primarily Arabic with an English (en-us) toggle — flag Arabic-language content; use the English toggle where available."}],"project":"Mini accrual-conversion case for a fictional Saudi government entity (\"General Directorate of Roads — Eastern Region\"). You are given a one-year cash receipts-and-payments summary in SAR. (1) Build a conversion worksheet that moves it to an IPSAS-aligned accrual basis: recognize year-end receivables and payables, capitalize a road-maintenance machine and book straight-line depreciation, accrue unpaid salaries and a utilities bill, and recognize a government grant/appropriation under accrual rules. (2) Present both a cash-basis statement and an accrual statement of financial performance side by side, and write a 4-6 line memo explaining the three biggest differences and why accrual gives \"a more vibrant view of financial position.\" (3) Map one procurement transaction (a SAR 2,000,000 paving contract) through the Etimad lifecycle — tender published, bid awarded, contract signed, milestone invoice, payment released — and show the accrual journal entries at each stage versus the single cash entry the old system would have recorded. (4) Draft a short IPSAS-style PP&E disclosure note (cost, accumulated depreciation, depreciation method, useful life, net carrying amount) for the machine.","milestoneCheck":"You can take a Saudi government entity's cash-basis figures, convert them to an IPSAS-aligned accrual basis with correct recognition of receivables, payables, PP&E, and depreciation; explain in plain language why the MoF reform matters for Vision 2030 transparency; trace a procurement transaction through Etimad with the matching accrual journal entries; and produce a defensible IPSAS-style disclosure note — while clearly distinguishing public-sector IPSAS from the IFRS/SOCPA private-sector framework.","flags":["VERIFIED — all 8 resources load, are free, and sit on canonical current URLs (checked June 2026); no resources dropped or downgraded.","FACT CONFIRMED — Royal Decree No. 13059 is the correct reference mandating the cash-to-accrual conversion; multiple sources (MoF, IFAC, Deloitte) corroborate it. CLARIFICATION ADDED to summary: the decree was issued 16 Rabi al-Awwal 1438H (≈ Dec 2016) and the conversion program ran from 2017 — wording adjusted to 'the conversion program began in 2017' to avoid implying the decree itself was dated 2017.","FACT CONFIRMED — the MoF 'Accrual Accounting Center' (established under paragraph 5 of RD 13059, sometimes rendered 'Accrual Accounting Conversion Center'; led by President Abdullah Al-Mehthil) leads the IPSAS transition. The phrase 'a more vibrant view of financial position' is authentic MoF/IFAC reform language, retained in the project deliverable.","FACT CONFIRMED — KSA has adopted accrual-basis IPSAS without amendment; IFAC's 2024-era materials describe implementation as substantially/fully completed. The module's 'phased transition' framing remains historically accurate; instructors may note the reform is now in a maturity/consolidation phase rather than early rollout.","FACT CONFIRMED — Etimad (portal.etimad.sa) is the live MoF digital finance/procurement platform (launched 2017–2018) covering budget, tenders/procurement, contracts/awards, payments, and employee financial rights, per the MoF e-services page. CAVEAT: portal.etimad.sa/en-us redirects to an SSO login (login.etimad.sa) for authenticated services; public tenders are browsable via the platform's tenders search without a login — added to the resource note.","SOCPA NAME CONFIRMED CURRENT — 'Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants' is the correct present-day name (renamed from 'Saudi Organization for Certified Public Accountants'); the site retains the SOCPA acronym and offers an English (en-us) toggle. SOCPA's supporting/technical role in the public-sector reform is corroborated.","NO TAX/RATE CLAIMS PRESENT — this module makes no statements about VAT (15%), zakat (2.5%), corporate income tax (20%), ZATCA (formed 2021), the Companies Law (effective Jan 2023), or GOSI rates, so none required correction here; those facts are unaffected by this module.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY (low) — IPSASB free-access page (ipsasb.org/publications) loads but routes some downloads through a login/permissions gate; the freely downloadable Handbook of IPSAS Pronouncements and individual standards (Conceptual Framework, IPSAS 17, Cash Basis IPSAS) remain available from the same site. If the /publications path shifts, search 'IPSASB handbook pronouncements' for the current download page."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["5.1"]},{"id":"SA.9","title":"SOCPA Fellowship & Professional Certification Roadmap","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"This module maps the professional credential landscape for accountants working in Saudi Arabia, centered on the SOCPA Fellowship (\"الزمالة\") — the qualification that lets you sign audit opinions and practice as a Certified Public Accountant in KSA. It covers fellowship eligibility, the six-subject exam (Financial Accounting; Managerial & Governmental Accounting; Auditing; Zakat & Tax; Business Environment; Regulations), the 75% MCQ / 25% essay format, and the 2025 reform (publicly announced August 2025) that opened the Fellowship to applicants worldwide with an English-language sitting beginning with the third 2025 session (September 2025). It also explains how international credentials (US CPA, ACCA, CMA/IMA, ICAEW) are recognized for SOCPA associate membership and valued by Saudi employers, including the SOCPA-ACCA exemption partnership.","whyItMatters":"In Saudi Arabia only a SOCPA-registered fellow can sign statutory audit reports and represent clients on zakat/tax matters, so the Fellowship is the gatekeeper credential for public practice and senior finance/audit roles.","outcomes":["Describe SOCPA's role and the difference between Associate, Professional, and Full (Fellowship) membership (within SOCPA's five membership categories), and explain which category authorizes signing audit reports in KSA","List the SOCPA Fellowship eligibility requirements (accounting bachelor's, recognized diploma ≥2 years, or administrative-science degree with ≥15 accounting credit hours) and the document-attestation steps for foreign degrees","Identify the six Fellowship exam subjects and the 75% multiple-choice / 25% essay format, and explain the four-year window rule for passing all subjects","Explain the 2025 reform (publicly announced August 2025) opening the Fellowship to applicants worldwide and the English-language sitting beginning with the third 2025 session (September 2025)","Compare how US CPA, ACCA, CMA/IMA, and ICAEW are recognized for SOCPA associate membership and describe the SOCPA-ACCA exemption arrangement (SOCPA Fellowship members exempt from up to 7 of ACCA's 13 papers, completing the remaining 6)","Build a personalized credential roadmap that sequences a target qualification (SOCPA Fellowship and/or an international credential) against your degree, experience, and career goal in KSA"],"estimatedHours":"8-10","resources":[{"title":"SOCPA Fellowship Authority — General Rules","provider":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Fellowship-Authority/General-Rules.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"official primary source / regulations","cost":"Free","role":"Primary authority on Fellowship eligibility, exam rules, and the four-year subject-validity window","notes":"Read FIRST for the governing rules and the four-year window. CAUTION: at verification (June 2026) the English-language version of this page still displayed the PRE-reform structure (five subjects: Accounting, Auditing, Zakat & Tax, Jurisprudence, Business Law; 60% MCQ / 40% essay). For the current six-subject / 75-25 format use the August 2025 news announcement (below). Switch to lang=ar-sa for the authoritative Arabic version, which may be updated sooner."},{"title":"SOCPA Opens Its Fellowship to Professionals Worldwide (August 2025 announcement)","provider":"SOCPA Media Center","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Media-Center/News/2025/4018.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"official primary source / news","cost":"Free","role":"Confirms the 2025 reform: global eligibility, the six subjects, and English-language sitting from the third 2025 session (September 2025)","notes":"The single best source for what changed in 2025. Article dated Aug 13, 2025. Use it to verify the six subject names (Financial Accounting; Managerial & Governmental Accounting; Auditing; Zakat & Tax; Business Environment; Regulations) and the September 2025 English-exam start. The 75/25 split is reported by reputable trade press (The Accountant / Yahoo Finance) rather than stated verbatim on this page."},{"title":"Apply for the Fellowship Exam (E-Services)","provider":"SOCPA E-Services portal","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Sites/E-Services/Ex/9.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"official primary source / application portal","cost":"Free to view (exam fees apply to register)","role":"Shows the real application steps, sitting calendar, and fee structure a candidate must follow","notes":"Use to see the live registration workflow, sitting dates, and fees (page lists SAR 1000 first attempt / SAR 500 retake plus SAR 300 per module; verify at registration). Viewing is free; actual exam registration requires payment. NOTE: this page references a 21+ accounting-credit-hour threshold for a related-field bachelor's, distinct from the 15-hour administrative-science pathway — confirm which clause applies to your degree."},{"title":"SOCPA Membership Categories & Associate Membership","provider":"SOCPA","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Membership/Associate-Membership.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"official primary source","cost":"Free","role":"Defines the five membership tiers (Associate, Professional, Full, Student, Honorary) and the approved-professional-certificate pathway used to recognize international credentials","notes":"Use to map US CPA / ACCA / CMA / ICAEW onto SOCPA membership. The page links to a 'Certificates' list of approved bodies and notes foreign certificates must be attested and recognized by the Ministry of Education. Confirm the current approved-bodies list via the linked document rather than memory."},{"title":"SOCPA and ACCA Sign a Partnership Agreement","provider":"SOCPA Media Center","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Media-Center/News/2022/3523.aspx?lang=en-us","type":"official primary source / news","cost":"Free","role":"Documents the SOCPA-ACCA arrangement: exemptions, joint certificates, and training cooperation","notes":"Article dated Mar 9, 2022. The page itself says 'some of the ACCA exam papers' without a number; the concrete figure (SOCPA Fellowship members exempt from 7 of ACCA's 13 papers, completing the remaining 6) is confirmed by ACCA's AB Magazine and the SOCPA 2021 exemptions news (socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Media-Center/News/2021/3393.aspx). Cross-check the live count on ACCA's exemptions calculator."},{"title":"Building the Profession in Saudi","provider":"ACCA — AB (Accounting and Business) Magazine","url":"https://abmagazine.accaglobal.com/global/articles/2021/sep/acca/building-the-profession-in-saudi.html","type":"reputable free secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Context on how international credentials and SOCPA fit together within Saudi's Vision 2030 profession-building agenda; corroborates the 7-of-13 ACCA exemption figure","notes":"Sep 2021 issue. Good narrative background on why employers value both SOCPA and global credentials. Secondary source — use for context, not for current exam rules."},{"title":"A Practical Guide to the SOCPA Certification","provider":"Wafeq (Saudi accounting-software knowledge base)","url":"https://www.wafeq.com/en/learn-accounting/accounting-certifications/a-practical-guide-to-the-socpa-certification","type":"reputable free secondary source","cost":"Free","role":"Plain-language walkthrough of SOCPA pathways, costs, and preparation tips to orient a beginner before reading the primary rules","notes":"Accessible on-ramp; confirms the 15-accounting-hour administrative-science pathway and the SAR 300 annual membership / SAR 500 foreign-certificate verification fees. IMPORTANT: this guide still describes the OLD five-subject exam structure, so always verify subject count, format, dates, and fees against the SOCPA August 2025 announcement and E-Services portal. A parallel Arabic version exists on Wafeq."}],"project":"Build a one-page \"SOCPA Credential Roadmap\" for a chosen persona working in KSA. Pick ONE: (a) a Saudi accounting graduate with no professional credential, or (b) an expatriate who already holds a US CPA or ACCA. For your persona: (1) Determine which SOCPA membership category they qualify for today and the exact eligibility clause that applies (cite the General Rules page, and the Arabic version where the English page lags). (2) List the documents and attestation steps needed (degree attestation by Saudi embassy/culture office for foreign qualifications; Ministry of Education recognition). (3) Map the six Fellowship exam subjects and mark which ones the persona is strongest/weakest in, then draft a realistic study sequence across at least two sittings given the 75/25 MCQ-essay format and the four-year subject-validity window. (4) If the persona holds ACCA/CPA, quantify the cross-credential benefit (e.g., SOCPA Fellowship members exempt from up to 7 of ACCA's 13 papers) and decide whether pursuing SOCPA Fellowship, the international credential, or both gives the best KSA career return. (5) Conclude with a dated 18-month action timeline (registration windows, English vs. Arabic sitting choice, target exam sessions). Cite at least three SOCPA primary-source URLs.","milestoneCheck":"Learner can (1) state, with the correct eligibility clause, which SOCPA membership category a given candidate qualifies for and what authorizes signing audit reports in KSA; (2) name the six Fellowship exam subjects and the 75% MCQ / 25% essay structure plus the four-year subject-validity rule; (3) explain the 2025 global-access/English-sitting reform and its start date (English sitting from the third 2025 session, September 2025; publicly announced August 2025); and (4) correctly describe how a US CPA, ACCA, or CMA is recognized for SOCPA membership and quantify at least one concrete cross-credential exemption (e.g., 7 of 13 ACCA papers) — and has produced the one-page roadmap with three or more cited SOCPA primary-source URLs.","flags":["DATE CORRECTED: bundle said 'April 2025 reform' in summary, outcome 4, and the 4018 resource title; corrected to August 2025. The 'Opens Its Fellowship to Professionals Worldwide' news article (socpa.org.sa .../2025/4018) is dated Aug 13, 2025, and all SOCPA press/social coverage (X, LinkedIn, SPA, trade press) is August 2025. No evidence of an April 2025 announcement was found.","CONFIRMED: English-language sitting begins with the third 2025 session (September 2025); the exam continues to be offered in both Arabic and English thereafter. Verified via SOCPA News 4018 + Yahoo Finance/The Accountant.","CONFIRMED: six exam subjects (Financial Accounting; Managerial & Governmental Accounting; Auditing; Zakat & Tax; Business Environment; Regulations) — verified via SOCPA Aug 2025 announcement and reputable trade press.","CONFIRMED: 75% MCQ / 25% essay format — verified via reputable secondary press (The Accountant / Yahoo Finance). NOTE the SOCPA News page does not state the split verbatim, and the General Rules English page still shows the legacy 60/40 split.","SOURCE-LAG FLAG: the General Rules page in English (lang=en-us) still displayed the PRE-reform structure at verification (five subjects: Accounting, Auditing, Zakat & Tax, Jurisprudence, Business Law; 60% MCQ / 40% essay). Resource note updated to direct learners to the August 2025 announcement for the current six-subject/75-25 format and to check the Arabic (lang=ar-sa) page.","CONFIRMED: four-year subject-validity window — General Rules page states a passed subject is cancelled if all subjects are not passed within four years of passing the first.","CONFIRMED + CLARIFIED: SOCPA-ACCA exemptions = 7 of ACCA's 13 papers (members complete the remaining 6). The 2022 partnership news page (3523) only says 'some'; the numeric figure is corroborated by ACCA AB Magazine and SOCPA 2021 news (2021/3393). Outcome 5 wording tightened from 'up to 7 of ACCA's papers' to '7 of 13'.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY (credit hours): bundle/Wafeq cite a ≥15 accounting-credit-hour administrative-science degree pathway (corroborated by Wafeq), but the SOCPA E-Services exam page references 21+ accounting credit hours for a related-field bachelor's. These appear to be two different clauses; the exact current threshold per pathway should be confirmed on the live General Rules (Arabic) page before relying on either figure. Added a note to the E-Services resource.","CONFIRMED: five SOCPA membership categories (Associate, Professional, Full, Student, Honorary); outcome 1 reworded to reflect that Associate/Professional/Full sit within five tiers.","RESOURCES: all 8 resources verified to exist and to be free to view (exam/membership fees apply only at registration, already disclosed). No dead links, no items downgraded, none dropped. SOCPA News page IDs and E-Services path are current/canonical.","NOTE: this module contains no VAT/zakat/CIT/ZATCA/GOSI rate claims to verify; 'Zakat & Tax' appears only as an exam subject name, not as a rate. No rate corrections were needed."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["6.1","6.2"]},{"id":"SA.10","title":"Arabic-Language Resources for Saudi Accountants","track":"Saudi (SOCPA) Track","summary":"A curated roundup of the best FREE Arabic-language resources for Saudi and Gulf accounting. It points learners to SOCPA's official Arabic IFRS and audit-standard translations, ZATCA's Arabic zakat/VAT/e-invoicing (FATOORAH) guides, and reputable free Arabic YouTube channels and MOOC platforms that teach accounting fundamentals and IFRS. This is an overlay module: a learner first reads the global English fundamentals in Module 0.1, then layers the correct local Arabic terminology (الزكاة، ضريبة القيمة المضافة، وعاء الزكاة) on top so they can read primary Saudi sources and work in an Arabic-first environment.","whyItMatters":"Saudi accounting is practiced and regulated primarily in Arabic: the SOCPA Fellowship exam was historically Arabic-only, with an English option added only from the third 2025 sitting (September 2025); the legally authoritative versions of the VAT and zakat regulations are the Arabic texts (English ZATCA documents are explicitly \"unofficial translations\"), and day-to-day work — ledgers, tax returns, audit files, client communication — happens in Arabic. A learner who knows only English IFRS terms will struggle to read a ZATCA assessment, file an Arabic-language إقرار, or sit the SOCPA exam. Mastering the local Arabic terminology is essential for anyone planning to work in or qualify within the Kingdom.","outcomes":["Map 30+ core accounting, zakat and VAT terms between English and their official Arabic equivalents as used by SOCPA and ZATCA","Navigate SOCPA's Arabic IFRS and audit-standard publications and locate the Arabic version of a specific standard","Read and extract rules from a ZATCA Arabic guide (دليل) on VAT, zakat, or e-invoicing without relying on the unofficial English translation","Follow Arabic-language YouTube and MOOC instruction on accounting fundamentals and IFRS, recognising spoken Arabic technical vocabulary","Compute a VAT return at the current 15% standard rate and record zakat (2.5% of the zakat base) and VAT journal entries using Arabic account names","Identify which Saudi source is legally authoritative (Arabic original) versus a convenience translation"],"estimatedHours":"12-18 hours","resources":[{"title":"SOCPA — Accounting Standards & IFRS Publications (Arabic/English portal)","provider":"Saudi Organization for Chartered and Professional Accountants (SOCPA)","url":"https://socpa.org.sa/Socpa/Professional-standards/Accounting-standards.aspx","type":"official standards portal","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for the Arabic versions of standards","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026). ARABIC-LANGUAGE (toggle lang=ar-SA; English view is lang=en-us). Official home of SOCPA's Arabic IFRS translations and Saudi-endorsed standards. SOCPA publishes the full updated IFRS edition annually (2024 edition effective 1 Jan 2024) and has endorsed IFRS 18 and IFRS 19 for Saudi implementation. Use it to download the Arabic text of a specific IFRS and to learn the official Arabic name of each standard; the Arabic translation of the international quality-control, auditing and assurance standards is also published here."},{"title":"ZATCA — Guidelines and Manuals (Arabic guides / الأدلة الإرشادية)","provider":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/en/HelpCenter/guidelines/Pages/default.aspx","type":"official guidance library","cost":"Free","role":"Primary source for zakat, VAT and e-invoicing rules","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026). ARABIC-LANGUAGE is the authoritative version (switch site to العربية; English PDFs are explicitly 'unofficial translations'). Use for the Arabic VAT guide, zakat guidelines, and the FATOORAH (e-invoicing) manuals: Phase 1 (Generation) was effective 4 December 2021 and Phase 2 (Integration) has rolled out in waves from 1 January 2023. The standard VAT rate is 15% (effective 1 July 2020, up from the original 5% of January 2018). Read the Arabic VAT guide for the mock-return project."},{"title":"ZATCA — Official website & e-services (Arabic)","provider":"Zakat, Tax and Customs Authority (ZATCA)","url":"https://zatca.gov.sa/","type":"government portal / e-services","cost":"Free","role":"Live terminology and filing-screen vocabulary","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026). ARABIC-LANGUAGE interface available. ZATCA was formed by Council of Ministers approval on 4 May 2021 merging the General Authority of Zakat and Tax (GAZT) with the General Authority of Customs. Browse the Arabic site, FAQs, and e-service screens to learn the exact Arabic field names used on a real VAT/zakat return (الإقرار، وعاء الزكاة، التسجيل الضريبي). Note: zakat is levied at 2.5% of the zakat base (وعاء الزكاة)."},{"title":"دليلك لفهم المحاسبة — Hossam Saad (YouTube)","provider":"Hossam Saad (independent educator)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@hossam_saad","type":"video course / YouTube channel","cost":"Free","role":"Arabic fundamentals taught from scratch","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026) — channel title 'دليلك لفهم المحاسبة - حسام سعد'. ARABIC-LANGUAGE. Teaches accounting fundamentals through an understanding-first method. Use after Module 0.1 to hear the English concepts you already know explained in spoken Arabic vocabulary."},{"title":"AccFlex (اكفليكس) — IFRS & Accounting Course Playlists (YouTube)","provider":"AccFlex ERP","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@accflex","type":"video course / YouTube channel","cost":"Free","role":"Arabic IFRS standard-by-standard explanations","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026) — direct channel handle @accflex (channel ID UCifd04e9Koxyj5z5Qmw5SrQ); replaced the prior YouTube-search URL with the canonical channel link. ARABIC-LANGUAGE (some bilingual). Free walkthroughs of individual IFRS/IAS standards (IAS 1, 2, 7, 8, 16, IFRS 3, etc.) with worked examples. Good for hearing each standard's Arabic name and terminology; treat the SOCPA Arabic text as the authoritative reference."},{"title":"Edraak — Arabic Online Courses (إدراك)","provider":"Queen Rania Foundation","url":"https://www.edraak.org/","type":"MOOC platform","cost":"Free","role":"Structured Arabic business/accounting courses","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026). ARABIC-LANGUAGE MOOC platform (non-profit, launched 2014 by the Queen Rania Foundation on edX/Open edX technology). Browse the business/accounting catalogue for free structured Arabic courses on accounting and financial fundamentals — confirm a specific accounting course is currently listed before relying on it, as the catalogue rotates. Companion Arabic MOOC platform Rwaq (rwaq.org) is also free and worth checking for accounting offerings."},{"title":"IFRS Foundation — Saudi Arabia Jurisdiction Profile","provider":"IFRS Foundation","url":"https://www.ifrs.org/content/dam/ifrs/publications/jurisdictions/pdf-profiles/saudi-arabia-ifrs-profile.pdf","type":"reference / jurisdiction profile","cost":"Free","role":"Confirms how IFRS and Arabic translation operate in KSA","notes":"VERIFIED LIVE (June 2026) — PDF downloads (approx. 124 KB). English-language reference about the Arabic regime. Authoritative confirmation that Saudi Arabia requires IFRS as endorsed by SOCPA and that SOCPA produces the official Arabic translations. Use to understand the structure before diving into the Arabic SOCPA texts. Note: IFRS Foundation jurisdiction profiles are updated periodically and may lag the very latest SOCPA endorsements — cross-check current status on the SOCPA portal."}],"project":"Build a bilingual (Arabic-English) accounting toolkit grounded in Saudi practice. Step 1: Compile a glossary of 30 core terms mapped to their official Arabic equivalents as used by SOCPA and ZATCA — e.g. زكاة (zakat), ضريبة القيمة المضافة (VAT), وعاء الزكاة (zakat base), فاتورة ضريبية (tax invoice), الإقرار الضريبي (tax return), معايير المحاسبة الدولية / IFRS, مكافأة نهاية الخدمة (end-of-service benefit). Step 2: Using ZATCA's Arabic VAT guide, prepare a one-month mock VAT return for a small Riyadh trading company at the current 15% standard rate: classify three sample sales and two purchase invoices, compute output VAT (ضريبة المخرجات) and input VAT (ضريبة المدخلات), and state the net payable/refundable. Step 3: Write the journal entries for the VAT and a zakat provision (zakat is levied at 2.5% of the zakat base / وعاء الزكاة) using Arabic account names alongside English, citing which ZATCA/SOCPA Arabic source informed each treatment.","milestoneCheck":"You can (1) produce a 30-term Arabic-English glossary of accounting/zakat/VAT vocabulary using SOCPA and ZATCA wording, (2) open SOCPA's Arabic standards portal and ZATCA's Arabic guidelines page and cite the correct Arabic source for a given rule, and (3) complete the mock VAT return at 15% with correctly labelled Arabic journal entries (ضريبة المخرجات / ضريبة المدخلات) and a stated net payable.","flags":["All 7 resources verified LIVE and FREE as of June 2026; none dropped or downgraded.","URL FIX: AccFlex resource changed from a YouTube search-results URL to the canonical channel handle https://www.youtube.com/@accflex (channel ID UCifd04e9Koxyj5z5Qmw5SrQ) for a stable direct link.","FACTS CONFIRMED: VAT standard rate 15% effective 1 July 2020 (from 5% since Jan 2018); zakat 2.5% of the zakat base; ZATCA formed 4 May 2021 by GAZT + Customs merger; SOCPA Fellowship English-language option added from the third 2025 sitting (Sept 2025); FATOORAH e-invoicing Phase 1 effective 4 Dec 2021, Phase 2 in waves from 1 Jan 2023. All matched the bundle.","ENRICHMENT: Added explicit zakat 2.5% rate to project/outcomes/whyItMatters and clarified the SOCPA-exam phrasing (Arabic-only historically; English from Sept 2025) for precision.","CIT 20% and Companies Law (effective Jan 2023) were in the verification checklist but are not referenced by this Arabic-resources module, so no change was needed; for the record, both are current (corporate income tax on foreign-owned shares is 20%; the new Companies Law took effect 19 Jan 2023).","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY (Edraak): could not confirm a specific accounting course is currently in the live catalogue (catalogue rotates) — kept as a general platform link with a caveat to verify a current course. Rwaq (rwaq.org) listed as a free companion alternative.","RESIDUAL UNCERTAINTY (IFRS profile PDF): file downloads and exists but its text could not be machine-extracted to confirm the exact wording on Arabic translation; IFRS jurisdiction profiles can lag latest SOCPA endorsements — added a cross-check caveat.","SOCPA standards portal base .aspx URL is canonical and live; language is controlled by the lang query parameter (ar-SA for Arabic, en-us for English)."],"overlaysGlobalModules":["0.1"]}]},"projects":[{"title":"Full-Cycle Bookkeeping: One Month for a Fictional Small Business","level":"beginner","afterModules":["m1-accounting-equation","m2-debits-credits","m3-journal-entries","m4-ledgers-trial-balance"],"description":"You are the bookkeeper for 'Bayside Bikes,' a fictional retail/service sole proprietorship. Starting from an opening trial balance, you process one full month (~25-40 source transactions: cash sales, credit sales, supplier bills, payroll, owner draws, loan payment, rent, utilities, equipment purchase). You record each transaction in a general journal, post to T-accounts/general ledger, and run an unadjusted trial balance. This is the foundational drill that proves you can take a raw business event and turn it into a balanced, posted, double-entry record without a software safety net.","deliverable":"A workbook (Excel/Google Sheets) containing: (1) a general journal with dated, referenced entries; (2) posted general ledger / T-accounts; (3) an unadjusted trial balance that balances to the penny; (4) a one-page narrative explaining 3 judgment calls you made (e.g., expense vs. capitalize, timing of revenue recognition).","skills":["Double-entry bookkeeping","Journalizing transactions","Posting to ledgers","Preparing a trial balance","Source-document interpretation","Chart of accounts design"],"resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting (OpenStax)","provider":"OpenStax / Rice University","type":"textbook","cost":"free","role":"primary","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","notes":"Ch. 3-4 cover the full accounting cycle with practice problems; use the end-of-chapter comprehensive problems as transaction sources."},{"title":"AccountingCoach (bookkeeping & debits/credits explainers + quizzes)","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"course","cost":"freemium","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/","role":"supplement","notes":"Free Q&A, visual tutorials, and self-tests; PRO tier optional and not required."},{"title":"David Krug / Notepirate / Tony Bell full accounting-cycle YouTube walkthroughs","provider":"YouTube (Accounting Stuff, Tony Bell)","type":"video-series","cost":"free","role":"supplement","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingStuff","notes":"Search 'full accounting cycle example' for end-to-end worked problems to model your project on."}]},{"title":"Month-End Close: Adjusting Entries, Closing Entries & the Three Statements","level":"intermediate","afterModules":["m4-ledgers-trial-balance","m5-accruals-deferrals","m6-adjusting-entries","m7-financial-statements"],"description":"Continuing the 'Bayside Bikes' books from Project 1 (or a supplied unadjusted trial balance), you run a real month-end close. You book the full set of adjusting entries (depreciation, accrued wages, accrued interest, prepaid expense expiry, unearned revenue earned, supplies used, bad-debt estimate), produce an adjusted trial balance, then prepare the closing entries and a post-closing trial balance. From the adjusted numbers you build a properly classified Income Statement, Statement of Owner's Equity, and Balance Sheet that articulate (net income flows to equity; ending equity flows to the balance sheet). This proves you understand accrual accounting and the close, not just data entry.","deliverable":"A close package: adjusting-entry journal with a one-line rationale per entry, adjusted trial balance, closing entries, post-closing trial balance, and the three linked financial statements (with a visible check that the balance sheet balances and ties to the statement of equity). Include a short 'close checklist' you followed.","skills":["Accrual accounting","Adjusting & closing entries","Depreciation methods","Financial statement preparation","Statement articulation","Month-end close procedures"],"resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1 (OpenStax) Ch. 4-5","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","cost":"free","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","role":"primary","notes":"The 'completing the accounting cycle' and adjusting-entry chapters map exactly to this project."},{"title":"MIT OpenCourseWare 15.501 Introduction to Financial and Managerial Accounting","provider":"MIT OCW","type":"mooc","cost":"free","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-501-introduction-to-financial-and-managerial-accounting-spring-2004/","role":"supplement","notes":"Lecture notes and problem sets on accruals and statement construction."},{"title":"AccountingCoach: Adjusting Entries & Closing the Books","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"article","cost":"free","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com/adjusting-entries/explanation","role":"reference"}]},{"title":"Build the Three Statements in Excel From a Trial Balance","level":"intermediate","afterModules":["m7-financial-statements","m8-statement-of-cash-flows","m9-excel-foundations"],"description":"Given a raw, unstructured adjusted trial balance (a flat list of accounts and balances), you build a fully formula-driven three-statement model in Excel/Sheets with zero hard-coded outputs. You map each TB line to a statement line via lookups, build a classified Income Statement and Balance Sheet, and — the hard part — derive the Statement of Cash Flows using the indirect method purely from the two-period balance sheet movements and the income statement. The model must include a balance-sheet check cell, clean formatting, and an inputs/calcs/outputs separation. This is the single most-tested skill in finance/accounting hiring screens.","deliverable":"An Excel/Sheets file where changing any trial-balance input correctly flows through to all three statements; the balance sheet ties out (check cell = 0), and the indirect cash flow statement's ending cash equals the balance sheet cash. Include a documentation tab listing assumptions and the TB-to-statement mapping.","skills":["Financial modeling","Indirect method cash flow construction","Excel (SUMIF/XLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH)","Model structure & error-checking","TB-to-statement mapping","Statement linkage"],"resources":[{"title":"Wall Street Prep / CFI 3-statement modeling free guides & templates","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI)","type":"article","cost":"freemium","url":"https://corporatefinanceinstitute.com/resources/financial-modeling/3-statement-model/","role":"primary","notes":"Several free templates and step-by-step articles; paid certification optional."},{"title":"ExcelIsFun & Leila Gharani Excel-for-accounting playlists","provider":"YouTube","type":"playlist","cost":"free","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@LeilaGharani","role":"supplement","notes":"Lookup functions, dynamic arrays, and dashboard formatting."},{"title":"SEC EDGAR Financial Statement Data Sets","provider":"U.S. SEC","type":"practice","cost":"free","url":"https://www.sec.gov/dera/data/financial-statement-data-sets","role":"practice","notes":"Pull a real company's tagged numbers to use as an alternate trial-balance source."}]},{"title":"Budgeting & Variance Analysis Model for a Small Business","level":"intermediate","afterModules":["m10-managerial-accounting","m11-cost-behavior-cvp","m9-excel-foundations"],"description":"Step into the management-accounting seat. For a fictional product business you build a master budget: a sales budget, production/purchases budget, cost-of-goods and operating-expense budgets, and a 12-month cash budget with a revolving financing line. You then layer in a flexible budget and perform variance analysis — comparing actual results to both static and flexible budgets, decomposing the difference into price/rate vs. volume/efficiency variances, and flagging which variances are material and likely controllable. The deliverable proves you can support decisions, not just record history.","deliverable":"An Excel/Sheets budgeting model with driver-based assumptions, a 12-month cash budget, a flexible-budget variance report (favorable/unfavorable with $ and %), and a one-page management memo recommending two corrective actions based on the largest variances.","skills":["Master budgeting","Flexible budgets & variance analysis","Cost-volume-profit analysis","Cash flow forecasting","Scenario/driver modeling","Management reporting & memo writing"],"resources":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 2: Managerial Accounting (OpenStax)","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","cost":"free","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-managerial-accounting","role":"primary","notes":"Budgeting and standard-costing/variance chapters provide formulas and practice data."},{"title":"Saylor Academy BUS105 Managerial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","type":"mooc","cost":"free","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/BUS105","role":"supplement","notes":"Free self-paced course; optional low-cost proctored exam for a certificate."},{"title":"Edspira managerial accounting & variance videos","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","cost":"free","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","role":"supplement"}]},{"title":"Bookkeeping & KPI Dashboard in Power BI / Google Sheets","level":"intermediate","afterModules":["m4-ledgers-trial-balance","m7-financial-statements","m9-excel-foundations","m12-data-tools-bi"],"description":"Turn a year of transaction-level data into a self-service finance dashboard. Starting from a messy CSV general-ledger export (hundreds of rows), you clean and model the data (Power Query / Sheets), build a date table and a chart-of-accounts dimension, and create measures for revenue trend, gross margin, expense breakdown, cash position, AR aging, and a few KPIs (current ratio, burn rate, top customers/vendors). You design an interactive one-page dashboard with slicers that a non-accountant owner could actually read. This proves the modern, employable overlap of accounting + data.","deliverable":"A published Power BI report (.pbix) or interactive Google Sheets/Looker Studio dashboard with: a cleaned data model, at least 6 measures/KPIs, an AR-aging visual, and drill-down by month/account/customer — plus a short written 'data dictionary' and refresh instructions.","skills":["Data cleaning (Power Query)","Dimensional data modeling","DAX / spreadsheet measures","Financial KPI design","Data visualization","Self-service BI / reporting"],"resources":[{"title":"Microsoft Learn — Power BI Data Analyst learning paths","provider":"Microsoft","type":"course","cost":"free","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/powerplatform/power-bi","role":"primary","notes":"Power BI Desktop is free; full guided modules from import to publish."},{"title":"Enterprise DNA / Guy in a Cube Power BI YouTube channels","provider":"YouTube","type":"playlist","cost":"free","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@GuyInACube","role":"supplement"},{"title":"Kaggle public financial/transaction datasets","provider":"Kaggle","type":"practice","cost":"free","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets","role":"practice","notes":"Search 'general ledger', 'accounts receivable', or 'sample superstore' for realistic transaction CSVs to model."}]},{"title":"Financial Statement Analysis of a Real Public Company's 10-K","level":"advanced","afterModules":["m7-financial-statements","m8-statement-of-cash-flows","m13-ratio-analysis"],"description":"Pick a real public company, pull its most recent Form 10-K (and the prior year) from SEC EDGAR, and perform a full financial-statement analysis. You build a clean spreadsheet of 2-3 years of the income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow statement; compute and trend the full ratio set (liquidity, solvency/leverage, activity/efficiency, profitability/DuPont, and per-share/market ratios); perform horizontal and vertical (common-size) analysis; and benchmark against one industry peer. Crucially, you read the MD&A and footnotes to explain *why* the ratios moved — revenue recognition policy, debt covenants, segment shifts, one-time items. This is what an equity/credit analyst actually does.","deliverable":"A 6-10 page analyst report (PDF) plus the supporting Excel model: common-size statements, a multi-year ratio table with a DuPont decomposition, peer benchmark, a red-flags/earnings-quality section drawn from the footnotes, and a clear investment- or credit-style conclusion with caveats.","skills":["Ratio & DuPont analysis","Horizontal/vertical (common-size) analysis","Reading 10-K MD&A and footnotes","Earnings-quality / red-flag detection","Peer benchmarking","Analytical report writing"],"resources":[{"title":"SEC EDGAR full-text search & company filings","provider":"U.S. SEC","type":"tool","cost":"free","url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar","role":"primary","notes":"Free source for every 10-K, 10-Q, and 8-K; use the 'Financial Report' R-tables or XBRL viewer to speed up data extraction."},{"title":"CFI Financial Statement Analysis & Ratio guides","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute","type":"article","cost":"freemium","url":"https://corporatefinanceinstitute.com/resources/accounting/analysis-of-financial-statements/","role":"reference"},{"title":"Aswath Damodaran 'Foundations of Finance' / valuation lectures & data","provider":"NYU Stern (free site + YouTube)","type":"video-series","cost":"free","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/","role":"supplement","notes":"Free industry-average ratio datasets and lectures for benchmarking context."}]},{"title":"Prepare a Sample Individual + Small-Business Tax Return From Source Documents","level":"advanced","afterModules":["m14-intro-to-taxation","m15-individual-income-tax","m16-business-entity-tax"],"description":"Work a realistic tax-prep engagement for a fictional taxpayer who is also a self-employed sole proprietor. From a packet of source documents (W-2, 1099-NEC, 1099-INT/DIV, business income and expense logs, mileage, home-office data, mortgage interest, charitable receipts), you prepare a complete individual return: Form 1040 with Schedule C (business profit/loss), Schedule SE (self-employment tax), Schedule 1, and either standard vs. itemized (Schedule A) with a comparison. You reconcile the books to the tax return (book-to-tax differences) and document the law/instruction citation behind each judgment call. This proves you can go from shoebox to a defensible, signed-ready return.","deliverable":"A completed return package using current-year IRS forms (filled by hand/PDF, no paid software required): 1040 + Schedules C, SE, 1, and A; a standard-vs-itemized comparison; a book-to-tax reconciliation worksheet; and a workpaper index citing the relevant IRS instruction/publication for each significant position.","skills":["Individual income tax (Form 1040)","Schedule C / self-employment tax","Itemized vs. standard deduction analysis","Book-to-tax reconciliation","Tax research & citation","Source-document organization / workpapers"],"resources":[{"title":"IRS Forms, Instructions & Publications (1040, Sch C, SE, A; Pub 17, Pub 334, Pub 535)","provider":"Internal Revenue Service (IRS)","type":"reference","cost":"free","url":"https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions","role":"primary","notes":"All forms and the plain-English Pub 17 (individuals) and Pub 334 (small business) are free PDFs."},{"title":"IRS Link & Learn Taxes / VITA training (Pub 4491)","provider":"IRS","type":"course","cost":"free","url":"https://apps.irs.gov/app/vita/","role":"supplement","notes":"Free volunteer-prep training with practice scenarios and answer keys — ideal as your fictional fact pattern source."},{"title":"Tax Foundation & IRS Free File Fillable Forms","provider":"Tax Foundation / IRS","type":"tool","cost":"free","url":"https://www.irs.gov/e-file-providers/free-file-fillable-forms","role":"practice","notes":"Free fillable PDFs to assemble the return without commercial software."}]},{"title":"Mini Audit & Internal-Controls Walkthrough Engagement","level":"advanced","afterModules":["m7-financial-statements","m17-auditing-assurance","m18-internal-controls"],"description":"Act as a staff auditor on a focused engagement for a fictional company. You document and evaluate the internal control over a key cycle (e.g., the revenue/cash-receipts or purchasing/disbursements cycle): produce a narrative and flowchart, identify the control activities, and map risks to controls (a risk-control matrix). You then design and execute a control walkthrough and a substantive test on a provided sample (e.g., test a sample of sales invoices for the existence/occurrence and accuracy assertions, vouch and trace, recalculate), document tickmarks and exceptions, evaluate a possible control deficiency for severity, and draft an audit workpaper plus a management-letter point. This proves audit reasoning: assertions, risk, evidence, and conclusions.","deliverable":"An audit workpaper set: a process narrative + flowchart, a risk-control matrix mapping assertions to controls, a completed test-of-controls/substantive worksheet with tickmark legend and noted exceptions, a deficiency-severity evaluation, and a one-page management letter recommending control improvements.","skills":["Internal control documentation & evaluation","Audit assertions & risk assessment","Walkthroughs & tests of controls","Substantive testing (vouch/trace/recalculate)","Sampling & exception evaluation","Audit workpaper & management-letter writing"],"resources":[{"title":"AICPA Audit & Assurance resources + COSO Internal Control framework summary","provider":"AICPA / COSO","type":"reference","cost":"free","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com/topic/audit-assurance","role":"primary","notes":"Free overviews of the COSO five components and assertions; use to structure the risk-control matrix."},{"title":"PCAOB Auditing Standards (AS 2110 risk, AS 2201 ICFR, AS 2301)","provider":"PCAOB","type":"reference","cost":"free","url":"https://pcaobus.org/oversight/standards/auditing-standards","role":"reference","notes":"Authoritative, free standards on risk assessment, controls, and evidence."},{"title":"OpenStax / Saylor BUS302 Auditing-adjacent materials & university OCW audit cases","provider":"Saylor Academy / university OCW","type":"mooc","cost":"free","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/","role":"supplement","notes":"Free case studies and lecture notes to model an engagement fact pattern and sample population."}]},{"title":"Capstone: Forensic Investigation & Reconstruction From Incomplete Records","level":"advanced","afterModules":["m6-adjusting-entries","m13-ratio-analysis","m17-auditing-assurance","m18-internal-controls"],"description":"The integrative final. A fictional small business hands you a shoebox: bank statements, partial invoices, a fraud tip, and no proper books. You reconstruct the accounting records from incomplete information (using the bank statement, gross-margin, and net-worth methods), perform a full bank reconciliation, build the financial statements, then run analytical and forensic procedures — Benford's Law on disbursements, ratio anomalies, a fictitious-vendor and lapping test — to quantify a suspected misappropriation. You conclude with a defensible estimate of the loss and recommended controls. This single project forces you to chain bookkeeping, statements, analysis, and audit/forensic skills end to end.","deliverable":"An investigation report (PDF) plus supporting workbook: reconstructed journals and statements, a completed bank reconciliation, the analytical/forensic test workpapers (including a Benford's analysis chart), a quantified loss estimate with methodology, and a remediation memo of internal-control fixes that would have prevented the scheme.","skills":["Records reconstruction from incomplete data","Bank reconciliation","Forensic analytics (Benford's Law, net-worth/gross-margin methods)","Fraud scheme identification","Loss quantification","Integrative reporting across the full accounting cycle"],"resources":[{"title":"ACFE Fraud Resources & Fraud Tree (occupational fraud taxonomy)","provider":"Association of Certified Fraud Examiners (ACFE)","type":"reference","cost":"free","url":"https://www.acfe.com/fraud-resources","role":"primary","notes":"Free Report to the Nations and scheme taxonomy to design a realistic fraud fact pattern."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting Vol. 1 (OpenStax) — bank reconciliation & incomplete records sections","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","cost":"free","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","role":"reference"},{"title":"Benford's Law tutorials + sample disbursement datasets","provider":"YouTube / Kaggle","type":"practice","cost":"free","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets","role":"practice","notes":"Use a public transactions dataset and a spreadsheet to run a first-digit Benford test; many free walkthroughs explain the method."}]}],"certifications":[{"name":"Intuit Academy Bookkeeping / QuickBooks Badge","body":"Entry-level, vendor-backed bookkeeping credential. Intuit Academy offers a genuinely free self-paced bookkeeping program (16 modules) culminating in a badge exam; the same content is mirrored as the 'Intuit Academy Bookkeeping Professional Certificate' on Coursera, which is free to audit (the shareable certificate requires the ~$39/month subscription). Covers the accounting cycle, recording transactions, adjusting entries, financial statements, and basic analysis. There is no formal QuickBooks 'certification' here per se, but the badge signals employability for junior bookkeeping roles and pairs naturally with QuickBooks software practice.","region":"Global (US-centric content; badge issued in the U.S.)","whoItsFor":"Career-changers and absolute beginners who want a fast, free, recognizable first credential before committing to a heavier cert (NACPB/AIPB) or a degree.","prereqs":"None. No degree or experience required.","costRange":"Free (Intuit Academy badge) to ~$39/month if you want the verified Coursera certificate; auditing the Coursera course is free.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","The Accounting Cycle & Adjusting Entries","Financial Statements","Bookkeeping Software (QuickBooks)"],"freePrep":[{"title":"Intuit Academy Bookkeeping (free program + badge)","provider":"Intuit Academy","type":"course","url":"https://academy.intuit.com/programs/intuit-bookkeeping-certification","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free self-paced modules and badge exam in the U.S."},{"title":"Intuit Academy Bookkeeping Professional Certificate","provider":"Coursera (Intuit)","type":"mooc","url":"https://www.coursera.org/professional-certificates/intuit-bookkeeping","cost":"free-to-audit","role":"primary","notes":"Audit all course content free; paid only for the shareable certificate."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Volume 1: Financial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","cost":"free","role":"reference"},{"title":"AccountingCoach (explanations + quizzes)","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"practice","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com","cost":"freemium","role":"practice","notes":"Core explanations and basic quizzes are free; PRO bundle is paid-optional."},{"title":"Accounting Stuff (debits/credits, double-entry basics)","provider":"YouTube (Accounting Stuff)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingStuff","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"NACPB Certified Public Bookkeeper (CPB)","body":"US professional bookkeeping license from the National Association of Certified Public Bookkeepers. Earned by passing three 50-question exams — Bookkeeping, QuickBooks, and Payroll (75% to pass each) — plus an experience requirement. A strong, recognized US bookkeeping credential that signals readiness to run a small-business books end-to-end. Distinct from (and lighter than) the CPA.","region":"United States","whoItsFor":"Bookkeepers seeking a formal US license and small-practice owners who want a credibility marker with clients.","prereqs":"Complete NACPB courses in accounting, payroll, and QuickBooks (or waive via accredited transcripts) + ~1 year / 2,000 hours of supervised bookkeeping experience (or 3 months via the CPB program). 24 hours CPE/year to maintain.","costRange":"Exam fees ~$240 (members) to ~$300 (non-members) for all three parts; additional membership/course costs if not waived.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","The Accounting Cycle & Adjusting Entries","Payroll Accounting","Bookkeeping Software (QuickBooks)","Financial Statements"],"freePrep":[{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Vol. 1 (Financial)","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","cost":"free","role":"primary"},{"title":"BUS103: Financial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","type":"course","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/BUS103","cost":"free","role":"primary"},{"title":"AccountingCoach (payroll & bookkeeping topics)","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"practice","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com","cost":"freemium","role":"practice"},{"title":"CPB exam overview & requirements (official syllabus)","provider":"NACPB","type":"article","url":"https://www.nacpb.org/certification/bookkeeping-certification","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Official exam structure, pass marks, and requirements."},{"title":"Edspira (financial & payroll accounting playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"AIPB Certified Bookkeeper (CB)","body":"The American Institute of Professional Bookkeepers' CB designation — the other major US bookkeeping credential alongside NACPB's CPB. A four-part national exam covering adjusting entries, error correction, payroll, depreciation, inventory, internal controls and fraud prevention. Parts 1 and 2 are taken at a test center; Parts 3 and 4 are open-book take-home tests bundled with the workbooks. Well-regarded by employers.","region":"United States","whoItsFor":"Working bookkeepers who want a rigorous, employer-recognized US credential and are willing to document real experience.","prereqs":"Recommended: be a working bookkeeper or have ~1 year of college accounting. Must document 2 years full-time (or 3,000 hours part-time) bookkeeping experience within 3 years of passing. Adherence to a code of ethics + CPE to maintain.","costRange":"Self-study workbooks ~$254 (member) to ~$314 (list); plus registration and test-center fees. The official prep materials are not free (only the published syllabus is).","mapsToModules":["The Accounting Cycle & Adjusting Entries","Payroll Accounting","Inventory & Cost Flow","Depreciation & Fixed Assets","Internal Controls & Fraud Prevention"],"freePrep":[{"title":"CB exam content & requirements (official)","provider":"AIPB","type":"article","url":"https://aipb.org/certification-program/","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free syllabus/exam breakdown; the workbooks themselves are paid."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Vol. 1 (Financial)","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-financial-accounting","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Covers inventory, depreciation, adjusting entries tested on the CB."},{"title":"AccountingCoach (inventory, depreciation, payroll)","provider":"AccountingCoach","type":"practice","url":"https://www.accountingcoach.com","cost":"freemium","role":"practice"},{"title":"Edspira (inventory/depreciation/internal control playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"ACCA Foundations in Accountancy (FIA) / Certified Accounting Technician (CAT)","body":"ACCA's on-ramp suite for those without a degree. Builds from Recording Financial Transactions (FA1) and Management Information (MA1) up through Business & Technology (FBT), Financial Accounting (FFA) and Management Accounting (FMA), plus Foundations in Professionalism. Awards stackable diplomas and the CAT qualification, and provides exemptions into the full ACCA Qualification. On-demand computer-based exams. A globally portable entry path.","region":"Global (UK-headquartered; strong in UK, EU, Africa, Middle East, South/SE Asia)","whoItsFor":"School-leavers and beginners without university access who want an internationally recognized, exemption-yielding route toward full ACCA.","prereqs":"Open entry — no formal academic prerequisites for the Foundations level. Registration + annual subscription fee required.","costRange":"Per-exam CBE fees paid to test centers plus ACCA registration/annual subscription; varies by country. Generally low hundreds of GBP across the suite.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","Managerial / Cost Accounting","Business & Technology / Economics","Financial Statements","Business Law & Ethics"],"freePrep":[{"title":"ACCA FIA syllabus, study guides & specimen exams","provider":"ACCA Global","type":"article","url":"https://www.accaglobal.com/fia","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Official syllabi and free specimen/CBE practice exams."},{"title":"OpenTuition ACCA/FIA free lectures & notes","provider":"OpenTuition","type":"course","url":"https://opentuition.com/fia/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Long-running free ACCA/FIA prep (lectures, notes, forums)."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Vol. 1 & 2","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"supplement"},{"title":"BUS105: Managerial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","type":"course","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/BUS105","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"CPA — Certified Public Accountant (US)","body":"The gold-standard US accounting license. Under the 2024+ CPA Evolution model the exam is three Core sections — Auditing (AUD), Financial Accounting & Reporting (FAR), Regulation/Tax (REG) — plus one Discipline of your choice: Business Analysis & Reporting (BAR), Information Systems & Controls (ISC), or Tax Compliance & Planning (TCP). Licensure is state-by-state. Opens audit sign-off, public accounting, controller/CFO tracks.","region":"United States (state boards; widely respected internationally)","whoItsFor":"Those targeting public accounting, audit, US tax, or corporate finance leadership who can meet the 150-hour education rule.","prereqs":"Bachelor's degree + 150 total semester hours (specific accounting/business credits vary by state); 1+ year of supervised experience for licensure (not for sitting). This self-study path builds the knowledge base but does NOT satisfy the 150-hour or experience requirements.","costRange":"Roughly $1,000–$1,500 in exam, application and registration fees for all four sections (state-dependent), before any review course.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","Intermediate / Advanced Financial Accounting","Auditing & Internal Controls","Taxation (US Federal)","Managerial / Cost Accounting","Business Law & Ethics","Financial Statement Analysis"],"freePrep":[{"title":"AICPA Uniform CPA Examination Blueprints (official)","provider":"AICPA-CIMA","type":"article","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free PDF blueprints for every Core & Discipline section. Search for: 'AICPA CPA Exam Blueprints'."},{"title":"AICPA CPA Exam sample tests / released questions","provider":"AICPA-CIMA","type":"practice","url":"https://www.aicpa-cima.com","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free official sample test interface. Search for: 'CPA Exam sample test'."},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Accounting Vol. 1 & 2","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"primary"},{"title":"15.501 Introduction to Financial and Managerial Accounting","provider":"MIT OpenCourseWare","type":"course","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/search/?q=financial%20accounting","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Search for: 'MIT OCW 15.501 financial accounting'."},{"title":"Farhat's Accounting Lectures (FAR/AUD/REG topic videos)","provider":"YouTube (Farhat Lectures)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","cost":"free","role":"supplement"},{"title":"Edspira (intermediate accounting & auditing playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"CMA — Certified Management Accountant (IMA)","body":"The Institute of Management Accountants' globally portable credential focused on corporate/management accounting and financial strategy. Two exam parts: Part 1 (Financial Planning, Performance & Analytics) and Part 2 (Strategic Financial Management). Emphasizes budgeting, cost management, internal controls, performance measurement, decision analysis, corporate finance and risk — i.e., the FP&A / controllership skill set rather than audit/tax. CMA vs CFA context: the CMA is the management-accounting/FP&A credential (internal decision support, costing, corporate performance), whereas the CFA (CFA Institute) targets investment management, equity/fixed-income valuation, and portfolio management for buy/sell-side finance. Choose CMA for industry finance/controllership; CFA for asset management, research, or investment banking.","region":"Global (US-origin IMA; very strong in the Middle East, India, China)","whoItsFor":"Industry accountants and finance professionals on the FP&A, cost accounting, controller, or CFO track who want a global credential without the 150-hour CPA rule.","prereqs":"Bachelor's degree (any field) from an accredited institution OR an approved professional certification, plus 2 years of continuous relevant experience (can be completed within 7 years after passing). IMA membership required.","costRange":"Roughly $1,100 (students) to ~$1,600 (professionals) all-in for IMA membership, one-time entrance fee, and both exam parts.","mapsToModules":["Managerial / Cost Accounting","Budgeting & Performance Management","Internal Controls","Corporate Finance","Financial Statement Analysis","Decision Analysis & Risk Management"],"freePrep":[{"title":"CMA Content Specification Outlines & Candidate Handbook (official)","provider":"IMA","type":"article","url":"https://www.imanet.org/ima-certifications/cma-certification","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free official exam content outlines and handbook. Search for: 'IMA CMA Resource Guide'."},{"title":"Principles of Accounting, Vol. 2: Managerial Accounting","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/details/books/principles-managerial-accounting","cost":"free","role":"primary"},{"title":"BUS105: Managerial Accounting","provider":"Saylor Academy","type":"course","url":"https://learn.saylor.org/course/BUS105","cost":"free","role":"primary"},{"title":"Farhat's Accounting Lectures (managerial/cost playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Farhat Lectures)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","cost":"free","role":"supplement"},{"title":"Corporate Finance / Valuation lectures & spreadsheets","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","type":"course","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"For Part 2 corporate-finance/valuation topics."}]},{"name":"ACCA — Association of Chartered Certified Accountants","body":"A globally recognized chartered accountancy qualification structured in three levels — Applied Knowledge, Applied Skills, and Strategic Professional — plus an Ethics & Professional Skills module and a Practical Experience Requirement (PER). Built around IFRS and international standards, making it especially relevant outside the US (and in IFRS jurisdictions like Saudi Arabia and the wider GCC). Confers the 'ACCA' designation; widely portable across employers and countries.","region":"Global (UK-origin; dominant in UK, EU, Africa, GCC/Middle East, South & SE Asia)","whoItsFor":"People wanting an internationally portable, IFRS-based chartered qualification — particularly outside the US, or in multinationals and IFRS-reporting markets.","prereqs":"Minimum entry varies (school qualifications); degree holders and the FIA route earn exemptions. Requires 36 months of relevant experience (PER) and the Ethics module for membership. Registration + annual subscription.","costRange":"Per-exam fees plus registration/annual subscription; full journey typically runs into the low-to-mid four figures (GBP) over several years, excluding tuition.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","IFRS / Financial Reporting","Managerial / Cost Accounting","Auditing & Assurance","Taxation","Corporate Finance","Business Law & Ethics","Financial Statement Analysis"],"freePrep":[{"title":"ACCA syllabus, study guides, past papers & specimen exams (official)","provider":"ACCA Global","type":"article","url":"https://www.accaglobal.com","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free official syllabi and past/specimen exams per paper."},{"title":"OpenTuition ACCA free lectures, notes & mock exams","provider":"OpenTuition","type":"course","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Comprehensive free ACCA prep across all papers."},{"title":"IFRS Foundation educational materials & standards","provider":"IFRS Foundation","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ifrs.org","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free registered access to IFRS Accounting Standards and educational resources."},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Accounting Vol. 1 & 2","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"EA — Enrolled Agent (US Tax)","body":"The IRS's own credential and the highest designation the IRS awards — an EA has unlimited rights to represent taxpayers before the IRS. Earned by passing the three-part Special Enrollment Examination (SEE): Individuals; Businesses; and Representation, Practices & Procedures. No degree required, making it the most accessible US tax credential. Note: effective March 1, 2026 the SEE is administered by PSI Services (previously Prometric).","region":"United States (federal tax practice)","whoItsFor":"Tax preparers and anyone wanting federal tax-representation rights without a CPA license or accounting degree.","prereqs":"No education or experience prerequisite — just a PTIN and passing all three SEE parts (or qualifying IRS work experience). Background/tax-compliance check applies.","costRange":"$317 per part (three parts) at scheduling; plus the PTIN fee and a modest enrollment fee. No mandatory courses.","mapsToModules":["Taxation (US Federal — Individuals)","Taxation (US Federal — Business Entities)","Tax Practice, Representation & Ethics"],"freePrep":[{"title":"SEE Candidate Information Bulletin (official syllabus)","provider":"IRS / PSI Services","type":"article","url":"https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/enrolled-agents","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free official content outline; from 1 Mar 2026 see PSI's site. Includes a free on-site 'Test Drive'."},{"title":"IRS Publication 17 (Your Federal Income Tax) + form instructions","provider":"IRS","type":"textbook","url":"https://www.irs.gov/forms-pubs/about-publication-17","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free, authoritative primary source for individual tax (Part 1)."},{"title":"IRS Publications 334, 535, 541, 542 (business tax)","provider":"IRS","type":"reference","url":"https://www.irs.gov/forms-instructions-and-publications","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free business-entity tax references for Part 2. Search the pub number."},{"title":"IRS Circular 230 (Regulations Governing Practice)","provider":"IRS","type":"reference","url":"https://www.irs.gov/tax-professionals/circular-230-tax-professionals","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Core source for Part 3 (representation & ethics)."}]},{"name":"CIA — Certified Internal Auditor (IIA)","body":"The only globally recognized designation for internal auditors, from the Institute of Internal Auditors. Three-part exam: Part 1 Essentials of Internal Auditing; Part 2 Practice of Internal Auditing; Part 3 Business Knowledge for Internal Auditing. Built on the Global Internal Audit Standards (formerly the IPPF). Signals competence in governance, risk management, control, and the audit process.","region":"Global","whoItsFor":"Internal auditors, risk and controls professionals, and accountants moving into governance/assurance roles.","prereqs":"Bachelor's degree (or qualifying education/experience combination) + internal-audit experience (e.g., ~1–2 years depending on education), a character reference, and IIA standards adherence. Education and experience can be staged.","costRange":"Roughly $740–$1,000 for IIA members (application + three parts) up to ~$1,500 for non-members.","mapsToModules":["Auditing & Internal Controls","Governance, Risk & Compliance","Financial Accounting Fundamentals","IT & Information Security Basics","Financial Management & Business Acumen"],"freePrep":[{"title":"CIA exam syllabi / content outlines (official)","provider":"The IIA","type":"article","url":"https://www.theiia.org/en/certifications/cia/","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free official three-part content outlines and exam info."},{"title":"Global Internal Audit Standards (foundational framework)","provider":"The IIA","type":"reference","url":"https://www.theiia.org/en/standards/2024-standards/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free download; the backbone of Parts 1 & 2. Search for: 'IIA Global Internal Audit Standards'."},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Accounting Vol. 1 & 2","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"For Part 3 financial/managerial accounting topics."},{"title":"Edspira (internal controls, governance, finance playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"CFE — Certified Fraud Examiner (ACFE)","body":"The Association of Certified Fraud Examiners' specialist anti-fraud credential. The exam has three sections — Fraud Schemes & Financial Crimes (rebranded from Financial Transactions & Fraud Schemes), Fraud Investigations & Legal Issues (law), and Fraud Prevention & Deterrence — each requiring 75% to pass. Combines accounting, investigation, law, and criminology. Highly valued in forensic accounting, investigations, and compliance.","region":"Global","whoItsFor":"Auditors, accountants, investigators, and compliance professionals specializing in fraud detection, deterrence, and forensic accounting.","prereqs":"Associate ACFE membership required. A points-based eligibility system (education + fraud-related experience): minimum 40 points to sit, 50 to be certified, plus at least 2 years of relevant professional experience for certification.","costRange":"CFE Exam application ~$480 (covers first attempt at each section) + ACFE membership dues; retakes ~$110 per section. Official prep materials (Fraud Examiners Manual/prep course) are paid-optional.","mapsToModules":["Internal Controls & Fraud Prevention","Forensic & Investigative Accounting","Business / Commercial Law","Financial Statement Analysis","Auditing & Internal Controls"],"freePrep":[{"title":"CFE Exam structure, sections & eligibility (official)","provider":"ACFE","type":"article","url":"https://www.acfe.com/cfe-credential/about-the-cfe-exam","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free official breakdown of sections, eligibility points, and format."},{"title":"Report to the Nations (occupational fraud research)","provider":"ACFE","type":"reference","url":"https://www.acfe.com/fraud-resources/report-to-the-nations","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free flagship fraud study; useful context for prevention/deterrence."},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Accounting (controls, transactions)","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"supplement"},{"title":"Edspira (internal controls & financial statement fraud playlists)","provider":"YouTube (Edspira)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"CPA Canada (note — successor to legacy CGA/CMA/CA)","body":"Context note: Canada unified its three legacy designations (CGA — Certified General Accountant, CMA-Canada, and CA) into a single 'CPA' designation around 2012–2015. The legacy CGA route no longer exists; today's path is the CPA Professional Education Program (PEP) plus the Common Final Examination (CFE) and 30 months of practical experience, administered provincially. Do not confuse Canada's CPA with the US CPA — they are separate bodies and credentials, though both are IFRS-aware (Canada uses IFRS for public companies, ASPE for private). This self-study curriculum maps to the prerequisite/foundational knowledge, not the proprietary PEP modules.","region":"Canada (provincial CPA bodies; CPA Canada national)","whoItsFor":"Anyone pursuing professional accounting in Canada, or learners who encounter the obsolete 'CGA' term and need the current pathway.","prereqs":"Undergraduate degree with specific prerequisite coursework, completion of CPA PEP, passing the Common Final Examination (CFE), and 30 months of qualifying experience. (Prerequisites can be met via CPA preparatory courses.)","costRange":"Several thousand CAD across PEP modules, the CFE, and dues — set provincially. The proprietary materials are not free.","mapsToModules":["Financial Accounting Fundamentals","IFRS / Financial Reporting","Managerial / Cost Accounting","Auditing & Assurance","Taxation (Canada)","Corporate Finance"],"freePrep":[{"title":"CPA Canada certification pathway (official overview)","provider":"CPA Canada","type":"article","url":"https://www.cpacanada.ca/en/become-a-cpa","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free authoritative description of the current (post-CGA) pathway."},{"title":"IFRS Foundation standards & educational materials","provider":"IFRS Foundation","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ifrs.org","cost":"free","role":"reference"},{"title":"OpenStax Principles of Accounting Vol. 1 & 2","provider":"OpenStax","type":"textbook","url":"https://openstax.org/subjects/business","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Prerequisite financial/managerial accounting knowledge."}]},{"name":"IFRS Certificate (ACCA CertIFR / DipIFR; ICAEW IFRS Programme)","body":"Standalone International Financial Reporting Standards credentials for professionals who need IFRS competence without a full chartered qualification. ACCA offers the Certificate in International Financial Reporting (CertIFR — introductory, online assessment) and the more advanced Diploma in IFR (DipIFR, for experienced practitioners). ICAEW offers an IFRS Learning & Assessment Programme. Especially relevant in IFRS-reporting regions (EU, GCC, Saudi Arabia). These are paid assessments, but the underlying standards and much study material are free via the IFRS Foundation.","region":"Global (IFRS jurisdictions; not the US, which uses US GAAP)","whoItsFor":"Accountants and finance staff in IFRS-reporting countries (or multinationals) who need a focused, recognized IFRS credential.","prereqs":"CertIFR: open entry, no prerequisites. DipIFR: typically 2–3 years of relevant accounting experience or a recognized qualification. ICAEW programme: open but aimed at practitioners.","costRange":"ACCA CertIFR ~£190 (assessment only) to ~£295 (with materials); DipIFR exam fee similar. ICAEW IFRS programme is materially more expensive (around US$2,000). The certificate exams are not free.","mapsToModules":["IFRS / Financial Reporting","Intermediate / Advanced Financial Accounting","Financial Statement Analysis","Consolidations & Group Accounts"],"freePrep":[{"title":"IFRS Accounting Standards + free educational materials","provider":"IFRS Foundation","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ifrs.org","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free registered access to the actual standards and supporting resources."},{"title":"ACCA CertIFR / DipIFR syllabus & specimen (official)","provider":"ACCA Global","type":"article","url":"https://www.accaglobal.com/gb/en/qualifications/glance/certifr.html","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free syllabus and exam info; the assessment itself is paid."},{"title":"OpenTuition DipIFR free lectures & notes","provider":"OpenTuition","type":"course","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/dipifr/","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free DipIFR lectures and notes."},{"title":"Farhat's Accounting Lectures (IFRS topic videos)","provider":"YouTube (Farhat Lectures)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@AccountingLectures","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]},{"name":"SOCPA — Saudi Organization for Chartered & Professional Accountants (Saudi note)","body":"Saudi Arabia's professional accountancy body (under the Ministry of Commerce) and the national standard-setter. Key point for this curriculum: Saudi Arabia has adopted IFRS Accounting Standards as issued by the IASB for publicly accountable entities (effective 2017) and IFRS for SMEs (2018), with limited local additions — so IFRS-based study transfers directly. SOCPA runs the Fellowship examination (accounting, auditing, Zakat & tax, fiqh/jurisprudence, and business law) for the SOCPA designation, and also offers a standalone Professional Certificate in IFRS. The Saudi-specific layers to add on top of an IFRS foundation are Zakat & tax (ZATCA) and Saudi commercial/Sharia law.","region":"Saudi Arabia (GCC relevance)","whoItsFor":"Accountants practicing in Saudi Arabia/the GCC who need the local professional designation, and IFRS learners who want to localize for the Saudi market.","prereqs":"Fellowship: relevant degree and experience plus passing SOCPA's multi-subject Fellowship exam (rules set by SOCPA). The IFRS professional certificate is more accessible. Exact requirements are governed by SOCPA regulations.","costRange":"Set by SOCPA (exam and membership fees in SAR); the Fellowship and IFRS certificate exams are paid. Underlying IFRS study can be done with free resources.","mapsToModules":["IFRS / Financial Reporting","Auditing & Assurance","Zakat & Tax (Saudi/ZATCA)","Business & Commercial Law","Financial Accounting Fundamentals"],"freePrep":[{"title":"SOCPA professional exams & IFRS certificate info (official)","provider":"SOCPA","type":"article","url":"https://socpa.org.sa","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Official exam descriptions and standards adoption. Search for: 'SOCPA Professional certification Exam in IFRS'."},{"title":"IFRS Accounting Standards (as adopted in KSA)","provider":"IFRS Foundation","type":"reference","url":"https://www.ifrs.org","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"KSA follows full IFRS, so the standards apply directly."},{"title":"Saudi Arabia financial reporting framework summary","provider":"IAS Plus (Deloitte)","type":"article","url":"https://www.iasplus.com/en/jurisdictions/asia/saudi-arabia","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free overview of Saudi IFRS adoption and local additions."},{"title":"OpenTuition DipIFR / ACCA free lectures","provider":"OpenTuition","type":"course","url":"https://opentuition.com/acca/dipifr/","cost":"free","role":"supplement"}]}],"tooling":[{"name":"Spreadsheets Mastery (Excel + Google Sheets)","why":"Spreadsheets are the accountant's daily workbench: reconciliations, schedules, pivot-table analysis, lookups (XLOOKUP/INDEX-MATCH), conditional logic, and clean financial layouts. Fluency here directly drives speed and accuracy in close, audit prep, and ad-hoc analysis, and is the prerequisite skill for every other tool in this list.","resources":[{"title":"Excel help & learning (official training videos and guides)","provider":"Microsoft Support","type":"course","url":"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/excel","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Vendor-authoritative how-to articles plus the 'Excel video training' track (formulas, tables, PivotTables, charts). Always current with the latest Excel."},{"title":"Excel tutorials (Basic, Intermediate, Advanced, Formulas)","provider":"GCFGlobal (Goodwill Community Foundation)","type":"course","url":"https://edu.gcfglobal.org/en/excel/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free, structured, no-signup lessons. If link changes, search for: 'GCFGlobal Excel tutorial'. Same site also has free Google Sheets and Excel Formulas courses."},{"title":"Google Sheets training and help (Workspace Learning Center)","provider":"Google","type":"course","url":"https://support.google.com/docs/topic/9054603","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Official Sheets cheat sheets and tutorials. If link shifts, search for: 'Google Sheets Workspace Learning Center'. Essential because many SMB/B2B finance teams run on Sheets."},{"title":"ExcelIsFun (Mike Girvin, Highline College)","provider":"YouTube (ExcelIsFun)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/user/ExcelIsFun","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Thousands of free, accounting-relevant Excel lessons including full 'Excel Basics' and data-analysis playlists. Deep coverage of formulas and PivotTables."},{"title":"Microsoft Learn — Excel training paths","provider":"Microsoft Learn","type":"course","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/m365/","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Free interactive learning paths. Browse all learning paths and search 'Excel'. Good for guided, modular skill-building."}]},{"name":"Bookkeeping Software (QuickBooks Online + Xero)","why":"QuickBooks Online and Xero are the two dominant SMB/cloud ledgers most accountants and bookkeepers actually operate. Both vendors give accountants a genuinely free accountant edition plus free, certification-grade training, so this is the highest-ROI free credential an accountant can stack to be employable and client-ready.","resources":[{"title":"QuickBooks ProAdvisor Academy — free certification & training","provider":"Intuit QuickBooks","type":"mooc","url":"https://quickbooks.intuit.com/accountants/training-certification/certification/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free with a free QuickBooks Online Accountant account. Includes QBO certification courses/exams and CPE-eligible webinars."},{"title":"Intuit Bookkeeping (foundational bookkeeping certification)","provider":"Intuit QuickBooks","type":"course","url":"https://quickbooks.intuit.com/proadvisor-academy/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Now-free bookkeeping certification (formerly a paid Coursera course) requiring no prior QuickBooks knowledge. Good entry point for fundamentals. Search for: 'Intuit Bookkeeping certification ProAdvisor Academy'."},{"title":"Xero advisor certification & Xero learning","provider":"Xero","type":"mooc","url":"https://central.xero.com/s/certifications","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free, multi-level certification (L1 associate ~1-2 hrs). On-demand e-learning + assessment. Direct learning portal: learning.central.xero.com."},{"title":"Xero Central — help & learning library","provider":"Xero","type":"reference","url":"https://central.xero.com/","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Searchable task-level guides for every Xero workflow (bank rec, invoicing, payroll basics, reports). Useful day-to-day reference alongside the certification."},{"title":"QuickBooks official YouTube tutorials","provider":"YouTube (Intuit QuickBooks)","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@QuickBooks","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Short task-based walkthroughs of QBO features. Good for quick how-do-I answers without logging into a course."}]},{"name":"Data & Analytics (Power BI, SQL, Python/pandas)","why":"Modern accounting is increasingly data-driven: pulling and cleaning data from ERPs, building dashboards instead of static reports, and automating repetitive reconciliations. Power BI handles visualization/reporting, SQL lets you query the source ledgers directly, and a little Python/pandas automates analysis at scale — the core toolkit of the analytical finance professional.","resources":[{"title":"Power BI training (learning paths)","provider":"Microsoft Learn","type":"course","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/powerplatform/power-bi","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free official paths: 'Get started building with Power BI', 'Prepare data for analysis', 'Model data', and 'Prepare and visualize data' (DP-605 / PL-300 aligned)."},{"title":"Kaggle Learn — Python, Pandas, and Intro to SQL","provider":"Kaggle (Google)","type":"course","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/learn","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free hands-in-browser micro-courses (1-7 hrs each), free completion certificates. Take 'Python' -> 'Pandas' -> 'Intro to SQL' in order."},{"title":"SQLBolt — interactive SQL lessons","provider":"SQLBolt","type":"practice","url":"https://sqlbolt.com/","cost":"free","role":"practice","notes":"Zero-setup, in-browser SQL exercises that build SELECT/JOIN/aggregate fluency fast. Ideal first SQL exposure for non-programmers."},{"title":"Mode SQL Tutorial (Basic + Intermediate analytics SQL)","provider":"Mode","type":"course","url":"https://mode.com/sql-tutorial/","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, business-analytics-oriented SQL tutorial with an embedded query editor. Strong on the kinds of aggregation/reporting queries finance uses."},{"title":"Intro to SQL — querying and managing data","provider":"Khan Academy","type":"course","url":"https://www.khanacademy.org/computing/computer-programming/sql","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, beginner-friendly SQL course with interactive challenges. Good conceptual grounding in relational data."}]},{"name":"Financial Modeling Basics","why":"Beyond recording history, accountants are increasingly asked to project it: budgets, forecasts, three-statement models, and DCF/valuation support for planning and deals. Learning to build clean, linked, assumption-driven models in Excel turns an accountant from a reporter of the past into a partner in forward-looking decisions.","resources":[{"title":"Damodaran Online — valuation lectures, spreadsheets & data","provider":"Aswath Damodaran, NYU Stern","type":"course","url":"https://pages.stern.nyu.edu/~adamodar/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free full valuation/corporate-finance webcasts (YouTube), downloadable DCF/WACC Excel models, and annually updated datasets. The gold-standard free valuation resource."},{"title":"A Simple Model — free financial modeling course","provider":"ASimpleModel.com","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.asimplemodel.com/","cost":"free","role":"primary","notes":"Free, build-it-yourself video course on the three-statement model and DCF, with downloadable templates. Excellent for absolute beginners to modeling."},{"title":"Financial modeling, DCF & three-statement explainer videos","provider":"Edspira (Michael McLaughlin) — YouTube","type":"video-series","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@Edspira","cost":"free","role":"supplement","notes":"Free, accountant-friendly explanations of DCF, NPV/IRR, WACC, and statement linkages. Search the channel for 'financial modeling' / 'DCF'."},{"title":"Free finance & modeling foundation courses","provider":"Corporate Finance Institute (CFI)","type":"course","url":"https://corporatefinanceinstitute.com/collections/","cost":"freemium","role":"supplement","notes":"CFI offers several genuinely free courses (e.g., accounting/finance fundamentals, Excel) with free account; advanced FMVA content is paid. Search for: 'CFI free courses'."},{"title":"Finance Theory I (15.401) — lecture notes & videos","provider":"MIT OpenCourseWare","type":"course","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15-401-finance-theory-i-fall-2008/","cost":"free","role":"reference","notes":"Free university-level grounding in time value of money, DCF, and valuation theory that underpins modeling. Rigorous reference, not a click-along Excel course."}]}],"career":{"paths":[{"role":"Bookkeeper","description":"Records day-to-day financial transactions, reconciles bank and credit-card accounts, manages accounts payable/receivable, runs payroll, and produces month-end reports for small businesses. The most accessible entry point into accounting and the easiest path to freelance income.","modulesNeeded":["Accounting Fundamentals (the accounting equation, debits/credits)","Recording Transactions & the General Ledger","Adjusting Entries & the Accounting Cycle","Bank & Account Reconciliation","Accounts Payable / Accounts Receivable","Payroll Basics","Sales & Payroll Tax Basics","Accounting Software (QuickBooks Online / Xero)"],"certs":["QuickBooks Online ProAdvisor (free)","Xero Advisor Certification (free)","NACPB Certified Bookkeeper (CB)","AIPB Certified Bookkeeper"],"startingSignal":"You can take a shoebox of receipts and bank statements and produce a clean, reconciled set of monthly books with an accurate trial balance, P&L, and balance sheet in QuickBooks or Xero without help. At that point you can apply for bookkeeping roles or take on your first freelance client."},{"role":"Staff Accountant","description":"The standard first salaried 'accountant' job inside a company or accounting firm. Handles journal entries, month-end close, reconciliations, accruals, supporting schedules, and feeds into the financial statements under a senior or controller.","modulesNeeded":["Full Accounting Cycle","Adjusting & Closing Entries","Financial Statement Preparation (Income Statement, Balance Sheet, Cash Flow)","Accruals, Deferrals & Prepaids","Fixed Assets & Depreciation","Inventory Accounting","Intro to US-GAAP","Spreadsheet/Excel Skills"],"certs":["CPA (long-term, usually requires a degree + 150 credits)","Intuit/Xero software certs","Microsoft Excel certification (helpful, not required)"],"startingSignal":"You can independently take a company from unadjusted trial balance through adjusting entries, a full month-end close, and a complete set of GAAP-style financial statements. You understand why each number lands where it does, not just the mechanics. Ready to apply for staff/junior accountant roles."},{"role":"Management / Cost Accountant","description":"Works inside a company (not for external reporting) to analyze costs, build budgets, set product/standard costs, compute variances, and give managers the numbers they use to make decisions. Heavy in manufacturing, retail, and operations-driven businesses.","modulesNeeded":["Managerial/Cost Accounting Foundations","Cost Behavior (fixed/variable/mixed) & CVP Analysis","Job-Order & Process Costing","Standard Costing & Variance Analysis","Budgeting & Forecasting","Activity-Based Costing","Contribution Margin & Break-even","Decision-Making (make-or-buy, special orders)"],"certs":["CMA (Certified Management Accountant) — the flagship cert for this track","CPA (optional)"],"startingSignal":"You can build a budget, compute standard costs for a product, and explain a set of price/quantity/efficiency variances to a non-accountant manager in plain language. Ready to apply for cost accountant, FP&A, or financial/management analyst roles."},{"role":"Auditor (External / Internal)","description":"Examines financial records, internal controls, and processes to verify accuracy and compliance. External auditors work at firms attesting to client financials; internal auditors work inside an organization assessing controls and risk.","modulesNeeded":["Financial Accounting & Full Cycle","Financial Statement Preparation & Analysis","Internal Controls (COSO framework)","Audit Fundamentals (assertions, evidence, sampling)","US-GAAP","Ethics & Professional Responsibility","Fraud & Risk Awareness"],"certs":["CPA (effectively required for external audit and signing opinions)","CIA (Certified Internal Auditor) for internal audit","CISA (for IT/systems audit)"],"startingSignal":"You understand internal controls, can trace a transaction from source document to financial statement, and can describe how you'd test an assertion with evidence. Note: external audit is hard to enter without a degree and CPA path; internal audit and entry audit-support roles are more accessible. Ready to apply when you can walk through a control test end to end."},{"role":"Tax Preparer / Enrolled Agent (EA)","description":"Prepares individual and business tax returns and advises on tax matters. An Enrolled Agent is federally licensed by the IRS with unlimited rights to represent taxpayers — and notably does NOT require a college degree, making it one of the best credentialed paths for self-taught learners.","modulesNeeded":["Accounting Fundamentals","Individual Income Tax Basics (Form 1040, income, deductions, credits)","Business & Entity Taxation (Schedule C, partnerships, S-corps)","Payroll & Self-Employment Tax","Sales/Use Tax Basics","Recordkeeping & Documentation"],"certs":["IRS Enrolled Agent (EA) — pass the 3-part SEE exam, no degree required","AFSP (Annual Filing Season Program) as an entry step","PTIN (required to prepare returns for pay)","CPA (alternative, degree-based)"],"startingSignal":"You can accurately prepare a realistic individual return (with a Schedule C, common credits, and deductions) by hand or in tax software, and explain the result. Get a PTIN, prep returns during a season (often via a storefront firm like H&R Block to build volume), and study for the EA exam. You can freelance/seasonally prepare returns once you hold a PTIN."},{"role":"Financial Analyst / FP&A","description":"Builds financial models, forecasts, and budgets; analyzes performance, variances, and KPIs; and supports business and investment decisions. Bridges accounting knowledge with finance and Excel modeling. A common step toward corporate finance.","modulesNeeded":["Financial Accounting & Statement Analysis","Reading the Three Statements & How They Link","Ratio & Trend Analysis","Budgeting & Forecasting","Managerial Accounting / CVP","Time Value of Money & basic Valuation","Advanced Excel / Financial Modeling"],"certs":["FMVA (Corporate Finance Institute) — modeling-focused","CFA (investment/markets-focused, rigorous, multi-year)","CMA (management-accounting angle)"],"startingSignal":"You can build a linked three-statement model in Excel, run a variance analysis against budget, and turn the numbers into a clear recommendation. Ready to apply for FP&A, financial analyst, or business analyst roles — a strong portfolio model often matters more than a cert here."},{"role":"Controller (track)","description":"A senior leadership destination, not an entry role. The controller owns the entire accounting function: close, financial statements, internal controls, compliance, payroll, AP/AR, and the team. Reached after years as a staff/senior accountant or accounting manager.","modulesNeeded":["The entire curriculum — Financial + Managerial + Tax foundations","Financial Statement Preparation & Consolidation","Internal Controls & Compliance","Budgeting, Forecasting & Cash Management","US-GAAP (deep)","Payroll, AP/AR & Close Management","Accounting Systems / ERP"],"certs":["CPA (strongly expected for controller roles)","CMA (common alternative/complement)","Often a bachelor's/master's in accounting"],"startingSignal":"This is a 5-10+ year trajectory, not an apply-now target. You're on track once you can own a full month-end and year-end close, produce GAAP financials a CPA would sign off on, and supervise others. Aim first at staff -> senior -> accounting manager; controller follows experience plus (usually) the CPA."},{"role":"Forensic Accountant","description":"Investigates fraud, embezzlement, financial disputes, and economic damages; reconstructs records and often serves as an expert witness or supports litigation. A specialization built on top of a solid audit and accounting base — not an entry-level role.","modulesNeeded":["Full Financial Accounting & Cycle","Internal Controls & Audit Fundamentals","Fraud Schemes & Red Flags","Financial Statement Analysis","Ethics & Investigations","Documentation & Evidence Handling"],"certs":["CFE (Certified Fraud Examiner) — the core forensic cert","CPA (strongly preferred, often required)","CFF (Certified in Financial Forensics, CPA add-on)"],"startingSignal":"This is a mid-career specialization. You're ready to move toward it once you have solid audit/accounting experience and can spot control weaknesses and fraud red flags, then pursue the CFE. Most people enter via audit or accounting roles first rather than starting here."}],"faq":[{"q":"Do I need a college degree to work in accounting?","a":"For many roles, no. Bookkeeping, tax preparation, accounts payable/receivable, and payroll work are open to self-taught people who can demonstrate skill — and the IRS Enrolled Agent license requires no degree at all. However, a degree (and specifically 150 college credit-hours) is required to become a licensed CPA in nearly every US state, and external audit and many corporate-controller roles effectively expect a degree. Think of it this way: a degree is optional for getting into accounting, but it's the gatekeeper for the CPA and the highest-prestige tracks."},{"q":"Is this free curriculum enough to sit the CPA exam?","a":"It will teach you a large share of the technical content the CPA exam tests (especially the FAR financial-accounting section), but the curriculum alone does not make you eligible to sit. CPA eligibility is set by state boards and almost always requires a bachelor's degree plus 150 total credit-hours, with a minimum number of accounting and business credits. So use this curriculum to learn and to prepare, but you'll still need accredited college credits to qualify, and most candidates also use a dedicated CPA review course (Becker, Wiley, etc.) before testing."},{"q":"Does this teach US-GAAP or IFRS?","a":"This curriculum is grounded in US-GAAP, because that's the standard used by US companies and tested on the US CPA exam. The good news is that the fundamentals — debits and credits, the accounting equation, the accounting cycle, and how the financial statements link — are identical under both frameworks. IFRS (used across Europe, much of Asia, and many multinationals) differs mainly in specific treatments: inventory (IFRS bans LIFO), asset revaluation, development costs, and presentation. Once you know GAAP, learning the IFRS differences is an add-on, not a restart. If you plan to work internationally, plan to study those differences separately."},{"q":"How long does it take to become job-ready?","a":"For bookkeeping, a focused learner studying 8-10 hours a week can be ready to take freelance clients in roughly 3-6 months. Staff accountant readiness is more like 6-12 months of study plus ideally some practice. The Enrolled Agent path is typically 6-12 months of study to pass all three exam parts. Credentials like the CMA or CPA take 1-3+ years including eligibility and exams. These are study timelines, not guarantees of a job — hiring depends on your portfolio, networking, and local market too. Be honest with yourself: consistency over months beats cramming."},{"q":"How do I practice without a job?","a":"Practice is the difference between knowing accounting and being hireable. Options that work: (1) keep a full set of books for a fictional small business for several months, including month-end close; (2) volunteer to do books for a nonprofit, church, family business, or a friend's side hustle; (3) use the free trial/educational versions of QuickBooks Online and Xero and complete their sample-company exercises; (4) do the IRS VITA program to get real, supervised tax-return experience for free; (5) build a portfolio of completed financial statements and reconciliations you can show employers. Real, messy data beats clean textbook problems."},{"q":"Can I freelance or do bookkeeping on the side?","a":"Yes — bookkeeping and tax prep are two of the most freelance-friendly corners of accounting. Many people start part-time alongside another job. To bookkeep for pay you mainly need competence, software access, and clients; getting QuickBooks ProAdvisor or Xero certified (both free) helps with credibility and referrals. To prepare tax returns for pay you legally need an IRS PTIN. Be careful about scope and titles: you generally cannot call yourself a 'CPA,' sign audit opinions, or perform attest services without the license. Also get basic professional liability (E&O) insurance and a written engagement letter before taking real clients."},{"q":"What's the difference between a bookkeeper, an accountant, and a CPA?","a":"A bookkeeper records and organizes transactions and keeps the books accurate and reconciled — the day-to-day data layer. An accountant takes that data and interprets it: adjusting entries, financial statements, analysis, tax, and advice; the role usually implies more education and judgment. A CPA (Certified Public Accountant) is a state-licensed accountant who has met the education, exam, and experience requirements and can do things others legally cannot — most importantly, sign audit/attest reports. Roughly: bookkeeper records, accountant interprets, CPA attests and signs."},{"q":"Which certification should I start with?","a":"Match the cert to your target role and circumstances. If you have no degree and want income soonest: free QuickBooks/Xero certs plus a bookkeeping credential (NACPB CB or AIPB), then the EA if you like tax. If you want corporate/cost work: aim at the CMA. If you can get a degree and want the top of the field: the CPA. Avoid collecting certs for their own sake — one credential tied to a role you can actually perform is worth more than three vague ones. Start with the cheapest, most directly job-relevant cert and earn money before investing in the expensive ones."},{"q":"Will AI replace accounting jobs?","a":"AI and automation are genuinely reshaping the field, and it's dishonest to pretend otherwise. The most exposed work is the repetitive, mechanical data-entry layer: transaction coding, basic reconciliation, and routine bookkeeping are increasingly automated. But demand is growing for people who can do what AI can't reliably do alone: judgment, exception-handling, advising clients, interpreting results, controls and fraud detection, and standing behind numbers professionally. The practical takeaway: don't bet a career only on raw data entry. Learn to use the tools (AI-assisted software is a force multiplier), and push your skills up the value chain toward analysis, advisory, tax strategy, and controls — those are getting more valuable, not less."},{"q":"Is accounting a good career if I'm not a 'math person'?","a":"Yes. Accounting is far more about logic, rules, organization, and attention to detail than about advanced math — the actual arithmetic is addition, subtraction, multiplication, and percentages, all done by software. If you can balance a budget, follow a structured process carefully, and enjoy things reconciling neatly, you have the right aptitude. The people who struggle aren't bad at math; they're usually impatient with detail. Comfort with logic and consistency matters more than mathematical talent."},{"q":"Do I need expensive software to learn and work?","a":"No. You can learn the fundamentals with pen, paper, and a spreadsheet (Excel or free Google Sheets / LibreOffice), and that core skill of building statements manually is exactly what employers test. For software, QuickBooks Online and Xero both offer free certification programs and trial/educational access, which is enough to become proficient before a client ever pays you. You don't need to buy a full paid subscription until you have real clients or a job that provides it."},{"q":"What entry-level job should I target first, realistically?","a":"For most self-taught learners, the realistic first paid steps are bookkeeper, accounts payable/receivable clerk, payroll clerk, or seasonal tax preparer — not 'accountant' or 'auditor' on day one. These roles get you real transactions, real deadlines, and a reference. From there you move up to staff accountant, then senior, then specialize (cost, FP&A, audit) or pursue a credential. Trying to skip straight to controller or external auditor without a degree, experience, or CPA usually leads to frustration; climb the ladder one verifiable rung at a time."}]},"sequencing":"A few modules are best interleaved rather than taken in strict numeric order:\n• Statement of Cash Flows deep dive (1.7) — right after 1.2 (the four statements).\n• Managerial & Cost (1.6) — can be taken early (after 1.3) to break up the financial-reporting stretch.\n• Investments & Equity-Method (1.8) — a hard prerequisite for Consolidations (2.1); don't skip it.\n• Deferred-tax accounting (1.10) — follows 1.5 and pairs with tax compliance (4.1).\n• Ethics (4.4) — seed it early (right after 0.1) and reinforce during Auditing (2.4).\n• Governmental & Nonprofit (5.1) — an elective here, but core for the US CPA (FAR): CPA-track learners should do it before the capstone.","stats":{"modules":45,"resources":315,"projects":9,"certs":14,"tracks":8}};
